window.AKK_STREET_SMART_HEIRESS_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_STREET_SMART_HEIRESS_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1: For 20 Bucks, I Transmigrated into a Book","paragraphs":["\"Twenty bucks. Street fight on Xinsheng Street. You in or not?\"","Seeing Qi Meili's message, He Huanhuan shot up out of bed.","Twenty bucks! That was a lot!","She immediately typed back: \"When?\"","Xinsheng Street was in the county seat, and it would take her three hours to walk there.","\"Three in the afternoon. Just tell me, are you coming or not?\"","\"Sister's in! Wait for me!\"","She got up and put on her shoes right away. It was already eleven-thirty—if she didn't leave now, she wouldn't make it in time!","\"I'm off to make some money!\"","She shouted into the empty room and set off without hesitation.","At two fifty-eight, Qi Meili stood on the street corner, tapping her foot anxiously. \"What the hell is He Huanhuan doing? She said three o'clock—why isn't she here yet?\"","If it weren't for the fact that this girl was a real pro at cursing people out, she wouldn't have bothered waiting for her!","Just as she finished speaking, a familiar figure appeared in the distance.","Zhao Xiaojuan quickly grabbed Qi Meili and rushed over. \"She's here! Sister Huan's here!\"","If He Huanhuan didn't show up, Zhao Xiaojuan would have felt completely unsure of herself.","He Huanhuan had a foul mouth, and most people couldn't out-insult her.","The three gathered, and Qi Meili looked annoyed. \"Why are you so late? Where's your sense of honor?\"","Showing up late for a fight was seriously embarrassing!","He Huanhuan waved her hand, unable to speak. Damn it, she was dying of thirst!","She stood there for a moment to catch her breath, then held out her hand to Qi Meili. \"Twenty bucks. Transfer it to me.\"","Qi Meili was even more annoyed. \"You think I'd stiff you?\"","He Huanhuan shot her a look. \"Cut the crap. You're the worst at paying up. No money, and I'm heading back.\"","She turned to leave, and sure enough, Qi Meili panicked. \"Don't go! I'll transfer it right now!\"","\"Come on, I never said I wouldn't pay... What kind of person are you? And we're supposed to be sisters!\"","Grumbling, Qi Meili sent her a red envelope. He Huanhuan opened it and saw: 13.52.","\"What's this supposed to mean? You messing with me?\"","It was supposed to be twenty!","Qi Meili looked guilty. \"That's all the money I have!\"","And even that she'd stolen from her dad!","He Huanhuan shook her leg. Well, she was already here...","\"You owe me seven bucks! Remember to pay me back!\"","\"Fine!\"","Money collected, time to fight!","Qi Meili led the two of them charging toward the malatang shop on Xinsheng Street. \"That bitch stole my boyfriend! Sister Huan, curse her out for me!\"","They pushed open the door, and before she'd even laid eyes on anyone, He Huanhuan's curses were already flying. \"You motherfcker! So you're the one stealing my sister's man? Your mother—\"","Before she could even get her footing, a big liquor bottle came flying straight at her head!","Her eyes rolled back, and she passed out on the spot!","Damn it!","This gig was a total loss!","She didn't have health insurance!","When she opened her eyes again, she found herself lying on a clean white hospital bed. The huge room had only her bed in it.","Shit. They played dirty.","Putting her in a private room—how many fights would she have to pick to pay that off?","That was totally ruthless!","She got out of bed, planning to sneak away.","Before her feet could touch the floor, the door to the room suddenly opened. Caught off guard, she turned her head and met the gaze of an elderly man.","The old man was wearing a cream-white Tang suit, with a gentle, refined air—he looked like the kind of traditional Chinese doctor who charges a fortune!","Without a second thought, He Huanhuan rolled her eyes and collapsed back onto the bed.","She was dead. Don't call her.","\"Miss, since you're awake, please come home. The master and madam have been waiting for you for a long time.\"","Huh?","What the hell?","She cracked one eye open just a slit. The old man looked at her with a kind, affectionate face. \"Miss, I know you must be in a lot of pain right now. But what's done is done. The master and madam will make it up to you.\"","She blinked. What was this old guy rambling about?","She didn't understand a single word.","'Master and madam'? Were they shooting a TV drama?","But then a sharp pain shot through her head, and a foreign consciousness rushed into her body like a cyclone.","\"I'm sorry. I was in so much pain. I just wanted to end it—I didn't think it would drag you into my body... I'm sorry...\"","A voice full of guilt echoed in her mind. He Huanhuan did a full-body shake like she was doing calisthenics. \"What the hell! Back off, back off! I don't want any part of this! Stay away from me!\"","\"Huh?\"","The tearful voice choked mid-sob. \"What do you mean? What's 'stay away'? Do you want to ride a horse or something?\"","\"You don't know what 'stay away' means?\"","He Huanhuan sat bolt upright. \"Then what the hell are you?\"","The voice started crying again. \"I'm He Huanhuan...\"","\"Like hell you are!\"","He Huanhuan was furious. \"You're stealing my name? Believe I'll slap your mouth shut?\"","......","The voice in her head suddenly got a lot weaker. \"I really am He Huanhuan...\"","\"You're my grandson!\"","She bared her teeth and spewed curses, scaring the old man in the Tang suit into backing away. \"Doctor! Call the doctor! The young lady has gone mad!\"","After sniffling for a while, the voice in her head finally managed to explain things.","He Huanhuan had transmigrated into a book—a story about a swapped-at-birth rich and poor daughter.","That voice in her head was the unlucky real daughter, whose parents—who had just recently passed away—suddenly turned out to be her adoptive parents. Her biological parents had forcibly taken her back.","A luxurious estate. Endless money.","Strangers she had to call 'Mom' and 'Dad.' And the fake daughter who targeted her...","Everything about her new home made her feel inferior, timid, and miserable.","In the end, crushed by all that pressure, she died of depression.","She thought it would be an escape. But when she opened her eyes, she was back on the day her biological parents first claimed her.","The tide of pain wrapped around her like a net she couldn't break free from. She couldn't escape.","She couldn't take it anymore, so she chose to end her own life.","This whole game of fake and real daughters—she was done playing.","But she never expected that her choice would harm a stranger.","She watched He Huanhuan's soul get pulled into her body, unable to do anything to stop it.","Just thinking about He Huanhuan having to endure all her pain made her feel worse than death itself!","He Huanhuan picked her nose. \"You're already dead—how can you feel worse than death? You're so illiterate, you know that?\"","......","\"I'm sorry. I didn't mean to do this. I didn't think it would turn out like this.\"","She shrank into a foggy little ball, looking like she could dissipate at any moment.","He Huanhuan raised a hand. \"Hey, I got a question.\"","\"Ask anything! If I know it, I'll tell you!\"","She could feel she didn't have much time left. She wanted to help He Huanhuan as much as she could.","She had to tell her what the Gu family was really like—and the heart-wrenching tactics they used.","So she wouldn't have to suffer through all of it.","He Huanhuan opened her eyes wide with wisdom and asked, \"What's this 'real daughter fake daughter' stuff?\"","......","The little foggy figure nearly scattered into nothing. \"It means I was originally the Gu family's daughter, but we were swapped at birth, and they only found out recently...\"","\"Oh, that! Swapped babies!\"","He Huanhuan sat cross-legged. \"You rich people and your fancy terms. 'Real daughter fake daughter'—it's just a baby mix-up! No big deal!\"","The foggy figure froze. \"No big deal?\"","He Huanhuan nodded. \"No big deal at all! Haven't you watched TV? There are shows where people marry the wrong wife! They just swap back and still get married—it's all small stuff!\"","\"If this is small stuff, then what's the big deal?\"","He Huanhuan frowned. \"There is one big thing. Kind of urgent.\"","\"What?\"","\"That 13.52 I earned hasn't been spent yet! Can you spend it for me? I worked hard for that money—I walked three hours for it!\"","“......”"]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2: Dazzling Debut","paragraphs":["“I’m sorry... I can’t help you...”","If she had the ability to do so, how could she have ended up in this situation?","“Hey, you. Why do you keep saying sorry? Makes me want to punch you.”","He Huanhuan gave her a disdainful glance. “You’ve just been holding back too much. From now on, stick with me, and I’ll show you how to rule Xin Sheng Street.”","She gave a faint smile. “Alright. From now on, I’ll stick with you.”","She would worry about the future later. The most important thing now was to warn her about Gu Chacha’s tricks.","“You have to be careful of Gu Chacha. All her kindness is fake. She...”","Before she could finish telling the old stories, her soul could no longer hold on and instantly scattered.","“Hey? Sis?”","She called out several times, but got no response.","Seems like she was really gone.","He Huanhuan sighed. “Hey, sis. Next life, remember to watch more TV! Take things easier. If worst comes to worst, come find me. I’ll take you on a hell of a ride.”","Just as she sent off that bitter spirit, she turned around to face an old man in a Tang suit.","The old man rushed over with a doctor and nurses, his face full of worry as he checked on her. “Miss, are you feeling uncomfortable anywhere? Does your heart hurt?”","He Huanhuan nodded. “Yeah, it hurts. Every time I think about my thirteen bucks, my heart aches.”","“Huh?”","The old man didn’t understand, but he knew how to fix problems.","“How about I transfer you some money?”","He Huanhuan shot upright. “I misspoke earlier. It’s twenty. Transfer me twenty.”","The old man looked baffled. Twenty?","“I’ll give you two hundred. No, as long as you feel better, I’ll give you two thousand.”","After all, the boss would reimburse him. Two thousand? Hell, he’d give twenty thousand if it meant she was okay.","He Huanhuan glanced at the old man, then at the doctor, and sprang up like a rocket. “Are you trying to steal my kidneys, huh? Two thousand? That’s enough to buy my life!”","No, her life was bought for just 13.52 bucks!","In the end, she only got a twenty-buck transfer. As soon as the money hit her account, He Huanhuan was miraculously cured.","She jumped up and hooked her arm around Old Tang’s neck. “Hey, Old Man! What’s your name? When are we going home?”","The affectionate gesture caught Old Tang off guard. “Everyone at home calls me Old Tang. You can call me Old...”","“Old Man! Let’s go! Time to head home!”","He Huanhuan bolted. She had to run.","What if they asked her to pay the bill? She’d just gotten that twenty bucks. No way was she losing it.","As she rushed through the hospital lobby, she caught a glimpse of her reflection in the glass.","A small, palm-sized face with big, sparkling eyes.","A head of jet-black, glossy hair that made the face in the glass look pale as snow.","He Huanhuan stopped and grinned at the glass. The reflection grinned back.","She flexed her arm. The reflection did the same.","Her porcelain-white arm was completely clean—no tattoos.","“Ahhhhh!!”","Hearing her hysterical scream, Old Tang rushed over with the others. “Miss! What’s wrong? Did someone bully you?”","He Huanhuan pointed at the reflection, looking at Old Tang in disbelief. “Is that me?”","Old Tang smiled warmly. “Yes. The moment I saw you, I knew it was you! You look exactly like the madam did when she was young.”","His face was full of affection, but He Huanhuan nearly fainted!","Where was her rainbow-colored hair?","Where were her full-body tattoos?","Gone? All that money she’d earned crying at funerals? Gone like smoke!","Old Tang gently urged her. “Miss, shall we head back? The master and madam are waiting at home.”","He Huanhuan immediately pulled out her phone and started searching for group deals. “No way, no way. I need to prepare before I go.”","All her armor was gone. This was like walking around naked!","Old Tang thought she wanted to buy gifts for her family and looked at her even more fondly.","“Miss, we’re all family. No need to be so polite.”","“Shut up!”","Inside the Gu family estate, five people were waiting in the living room, growing more anxious by the minute.","“Why isn’t she here yet? Did something happen?”","Jiang Yulan stood up nervously. Just thinking about finally meeting her biological daughter after twenty lost years made her heart race uncontrollably.","Every word of concern she spoke fell on Gu Chacha’s ears like an open insult.","Gu Chacha clenched her teeth silently, forcing a smile as she stood up and took Jiang Yulan’s arm. “Mom, don’t worry. If something really happened, Uncle Tang would have called.”","“Right, right...”","Jiang Yulan nodded absently, but her heart was still restless. “But why has it taken so long for them to come back?”","“Maybe...”","Gu Chacha’s eyes flickered. She spoke softly, “Maybe Sister doesn’t like me being here... I’ve lived the life that was meant for her for twenty years... It’s only natural she’s upset...”","Dressed in a pure white princess dress, her dark, grape-like eyes blinked, and instantly, two streams of tears rolled down her cheeks.","She looked utterly pitiful!","It softened Jiang Yulan’s heart completely. She held Gu Chacha’s hand tightly, pulling her close. “Chacha, don’t worry. This isn’t your fault. Huanhuan won’t be unreasonable.”","“Mom...”","The mother and daughter embraced, eyes red, as if He Huanhuan had reached across the room and slapped them both.","“Master, Madam, Uncle Tang has arrived with the young miss. The cars have entered the estate.”","The head of security announced it. The whole family stood up at once.","Gu Chengye was the first out the door, taking long strides to greet her.","The cold, gleaming extended Maybach slowly pulled up. The door opened...","Jiang Yulan rushed forward, her voice choked with tears. “Huanhuan...”","A blindingly colorful feathered headdress rolled out of the car—red, orange, yellow, green, blue, purple...","Everyone was stunned. Where did that ridiculous thing come from?","It rolled once, then slowly lifted, revealing a face strikingly similar to Jiang Yulan’s.","Jiang Yulan’s eyes immediately welled up. “Huanhuan...”","He Huanhuan was pale. She swallowed hard, but it didn’t help. “Ugh!”","Jiang Yulan sobbed. “Huanhuan, I’m your mother.”","“Ugh!”","Gu Chengye: “Huanhuan, I’m your father.”","“Ugh!”","Gu Jingchen stepped forward. “I’m your eldest brother.”","Gu Jinghan followed. “I’m your second brother.”","He Huanhuan: “Ugh!”","She was dry-heaving so violently that the whole family gathered around her, worried.","Her mother frowned. “Why is she throwing up so badly?”","Her father asked Old Tang. “What happened?”","Old Tang shook his head bitterly. “Miss seems to...”","“Could Sister be...”","Gu Chacha gestured vaguely at her belly. Throwing up like that—had she been messing around and gotten herself knocked up?","At that, the couple’s faces turned grim instantly.","Unacceptable! Huanhuan was only twenty!","“Ugh!!”","A thunderous retch later, her insides finally settled, and the flush faded from her face.","He Huanhuan straightened up, kicked the car tire angrily, and turned to glare at Gu Chengye. “You’re my dad?”","Gu Chengye nodded. “Huanhuan, you...”","“Aren’t you supposed to be rich? Why didn’t you buy a decent car? I almost threw up all over myself! Are you doing this on purpose?”","Her eyes went wide as saucers, leaving Gu Chengye completely baffled.","A stretched Maybach was... a crappy car?","Then what counted as a good car?","The girl had endured way too much hardship in her first two decades of life, so treating herself to a decent car wasn't asking too much.","In a gentle tone, he asked, \"Huanhuan, tell me, what kind of car do you think is a good one? Daddy will buy it for you.\"","He Huanhuan put her hands on her hips. \"A BYD, of course!\"","Back in the day, the first time she'd landed a gig as a professional mourner—that very first job—had earned her two hundred bucks, and oh, how that went to her head!","That day, she couldn't even be bothered to walk home. She'd tossed down thirty whole bucks to get a cab.","That cab was a BYD, and she didn't get carsick at all.","With a disgusted look at the three men of the Gu family, she said, \"Three grown men and you can't even scrape together enough for a single BYD? And you still have the nerve to call yourselves high-society?\""]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3: How to use a smart toilet","paragraphs":["A thunderous question left five people speechless.","Gu Jingchen racked his brains for a moment before asking incredulously, \"Are you talking about the BYD I’m thinking of?\"","He Huanhuan gave him a once-over. This guy wasn’t bad-looking, but he wasn’t exactly sharp.","\"Is there another BYD in the world?\"","Apparently not.","Gu Jinghan pointed at the stretched Maybach behind her. \"Do you know what kind of car this is?\"","He Huanhuan curled her lip in disgust. \"Looks like a stretched hot dog. What car it is ain’t my damn business.\"","What a wild attitude. Gu Jinghan couldn’t help but give her a thumbs-up.","\"Huanhuan, your hair...\"","Jiang Yulan wanted to ask what was going on with He Huanhuan’s hair.","It was a mess of colors, nothing like a proper young lady.","\"Pretty cool, right?\"","He Huanhuan touched her hair contentedly. These bright shades? Totally her vibe!","She pulled the leftover hair dye from her pocket and asked Jiang Yulan, \"You like it? If you do, I’ll do yours too. It’ll look awesome!\"","Jiang Yulan glanced at the dye—its packaging was flimsy, the colors on it faded and blurry.","The moment it came near, a harsh, cheap fragrance hit her nostrils.","The sickly sweet smell was overpowering, making her nose sting.","Good heavens!","Would putting this stuff on her head make her sick?","Forget about being polite; she was ready to drag He Huanhuan to the hospital for a full checkup.","\"Where did you buy this? Is it safe? Is it made properly? Does it meet EU standards?\"","He Huanhuan patted her chest confidently. \"Totally safe! One tube cost me ten bucks!\"","If Old Tang hadn’t been with her, she wouldn’t have splurged on this brand.","She’d originally wanted the five-buck kind, but Old Tang absolutely refused, so she reluctantly went for the ten-buck one.","\"Ten bucks?\"","Gu Chacha frowned and stepped back several paces. Ten-buck hair dye—was that even fit for human use?","\"Sis, why would you buy such cheap dye? If others find out, they’ll think our family’s gone bankrupt...\"","Jiang City was small. If other families heard that their daughter used ten-buck hair dye, they’d assume they were in financial trouble.","As she spoke, Gu Chengye’s face indeed turned cold.","\"Throw it away right now. Don’t use such cheap stuff ever again. You’re dragging down the Gu family’s reputation!\"","\"Throw it away?!\"","He Huanhuan howled. \"I’ll throw you out if you’re not careful!\"","She had dyed her hair eighteen different colors. Eighteen tubes. One hundred and eighty bucks!","And she’d only used them once. Throw them away? Was he asking for a fight?","\"What did you say?\"","Her insolent tone made Gu Chengye’s face freeze.","He had run the family business for decades. No one had dared talk to him like that in years!","\"Huanhuan, apologize to your father quickly. Say you didn’t mean it.\"","Seeing her husband angry, Jiang Yulan tugged at He Huanhuan, urging her to apologize.","He Huanhuan ignored her completely.","She clutched the hair dye and asked Gu Chengye, \"Do you know how hard it is to earn a hundred and eighty?\"","She shook her leg like a tough street kid and tapped her head. \"A thick beer bottle smacked right on the skull—you know how much that pays?\"","\"Twenty bucks!\"","\"To make a hundred eighty, I gotta take nine beer bottles to the dome! And you want me to throw this away? I’ll bash you with a beer bottle if you keep at it!\"","\"What did you say?\"","Gu Chengye’s heart clenched. \"You’ve been taking beatings for money?\"","A beer bottle to the head for just twenty bucks?","His daughter, Gu Chengye’s daughter, had been living like this?","For twenty years!","His eyes reddened. \"Huanhuan, your father... you’ve suffered...\"","\"Pfft!\"","He Huanhuan waved her hand. \"That’s nothing!\"","Gu Chacha glanced at her two brothers. Sure enough, guilt flashed across their faces.","What a He Huanhuan!","What a shameless, pitiful wretch!","So all her scheming had just paved the way for her?","She dug her nails into her palm and suppressed her resentment.","\"It’s all my fault. If it weren’t for me... my sister wouldn’t have endured so many years of hardship...\"","She apologized with teary eyes, drawing her family’s attention away from He Huanhuan.","She looked at He Huanhuan pitifully and asked, \"Sis, do you resent me a lot?\"","Jiang Yulan took the bait and immediately let go of He Huanhuan to hold her hand and comfort her.","\"Chacha, how could this be your fault! It was your mother and I who weren’t careful enough back then, causing Huanhuan to suffer so much...\"","\"But Mom, my sister has suffered so much, while I’ve lived in comfort at home...\"","She kept glancing at He Huanhuan as she spoke. She was sure He Huanhuan would get angry.","If she just lost her temper and lashed out...","To her surprise, He Huanhuan ignored her completely and turned to walk into the house. \"Which room is mine?\"","Jiang Yulan immediately followed. \"It’s on the first floor. It was sudden, so your mother quickly cleared out a room. Just make do for now...\"","\"Oh my gosh!!!\"","He Huanhuan whirled around, her eyes sparkling as she asked Jiang Yulan, \"Is this our house?\"","Jiang Yulan smiled and nodded. \"Yes, it’s ours.\"","\"Oh my gosh!!!\"","He Huanhuan asked again in disbelief. \"And I’m living here from now on?\"","Even Gu Chengye laughed. \"Silly girl, you’re a daughter of this house. If you don’t live here, where else would you go?\"","\"Sis, are you...\"","\"Where’s my room? Take me to see it!\"","He Huanhuan grabbed Jiang Yulan and dashed back inside!","Her room was at the far end of the first floor. The Gu family estate had two main buildings.","One was the main building where the family lived, and the other was the servants’ quarters.","The main building had five floors. The first floor was the living room and a casual lounge for family gatherings.","The second floor was where Gu Chengye and his wife lived.","The third floor belonged to Gu Chacha alone.","The fourth floor was Second Brother Gu Jinghan’s space.","The fifth floor was Eldest Brother Gu Jingchen’s space.","Each person enjoyed a luxurious five hundred square meters.","And He Huanhuan had been assigned a guest room on the first floor.","Technically a guest room, but people like them rarely hosted overnight guests. If Gu Chacha’s friends came, they’d stay on her floor with her.","So the guest room had sat unused for years, only cleared out in the last two days.","Gu Chacha smirked and followed them to the first-floor guest room.","The room was barely fifty square meters, and the bathroom didn’t even have a bathtub.","She couldn’t wait to see He Huanhuan’s face when she opened the door. She’d be so disappointed, right?","Disappointed? Then throw a fit! Go crazy!","Let her lose her temper until Mom and Dad got sick of her!","The door slowly creaked open, and Gu Chacha’s anticipation rose. She kept her eyes locked on He Huanhuan.","Here it comes, here it comes...","He Huanhuan’s expression changed. She was about to explode, she was going to...","\"Oh my gosh!!!\"","He Huanhuan darted into the room like a shot. \"This huge room! And it’s all mine?\"","She launched herself onto the bed, rolling back and forth. \"Such a big bed! I get to sleep alone? So luxurious!\"","Without waiting for a reply, she leapt up again and sprinted to the bathroom. \"Oh my god! A smart toilet!!\"","A multicolored head popped out, her rosy little face looking at them: \"How do you use a smart toilet?\"","Gu Jingchen's lashes instantly grew damp—his own sister didn't even know how to use a smart toilet!","He gently turned his head away, trying to secretly wipe his tears.","But He Huanhuan caught his little move at a glance: \"Oh, come on! If you don't know, you don't know! Why cry? Let's learn together!\"","She smiled brightly and reached out to Gu Jingchen: \"Come over, let's learn together.\"","\"Okay.\"","Gu Jingchen stood up and walked into the bathroom. He crouched down beside her, seriously studying how to use the smart toilet."]},{"number":4,"title":"Chapter 4: Omakase","paragraphs":["Gu Jinghan immediately followed up: \"I can't do it either. I'll learn along with you.\"","The three of them crouched attentively in front of the round toilet bowl. He Huanhuan pointed at the English words on the side of the toilet and guessed: \"This is the flush button.\"","Gu Jingchen said: \"...That's the brand name.\"","He Huanhuan frowned: \"They print the brand name in such a random spot? That’s pretty insecure. Don’t buy from them in the future—if a brand lacks confidence, how good can it be?\"","Gu Jinghan’s eyes went wide again. What solid logic! Awesome!","The three chatted animatedly, the atmosphere warm and harmonious. Gu Chacha was so jealous her eyes turned red.","Her two older brothers had always been cold and aloof. From childhood to now, they had never been this gentle with her!","Why, just because He Huanhuan showed up, did they suddenly love her so much?","It wasn’t fair to her!","Thinking of He Huanhuan’s country-bumpkin appearance, a sudden idea flashed through her mind.","\"Mom, Dad, it’s rare that big sis and her two brothers get along so well. We have to celebrate!\"","Putting on an overly cheerful expression, she suggested to Gu Chengye and his wife,","\"Let’s not eat at home today! There’s an omakase place that just opened at Dongcheng’s Ancha Plaza. Fufu says it’s really good. How about we go there tonight?\"","She cozied up to Gu Chengye, acting spoiled: \"Dad, big sis has been through a lot. Let’s help her experience all the things she’s never seen before, bit by bit, okay?\"","Gu Chengye was deeply moved: \"Alright! Let’s show Huanhuan all the new things she’s never seen!\"","\"Big sis! Dad’s taking us out for omakase tonight! Let me pick out an outfit for you!\"","Gu Chacha grabbed her hand affectionately and led her up to the third floor—her own private floor.","She wanted to show her how well the true children of the Gu family lived. What kind of life she herself had enjoyed for the past twenty years.","She was sure that Huanhuan would feel hurt, bitter, and envious...","But He Huanhuan wasn’t the least bit envious. After all, she wasn’t the real heiress—why would she compare herself?","When they reached the third floor, He Huanhuan’s eyes nearly popped out: \"You live in a place this big all by yourself?\"","Gu Chacha smiled lightly: \"Mom and Dad say that girls need to be raised in luxury so they won’t be tricked by men when they grow up.\"","\"Wise!\"","He Huanhuan gave a thumbs-up in approval. Raising kids with luxury was the right way.","A child raised in abundance wouldn’t have a poor heart.","Like her, for instance.","Her grandparents had treated her so well. If she craved spicy hot pot in the middle of the night, her grandpa would take her to the county town on his bike first thing in the morning.","Look how well that turned out for her—she was thriving!","Her reaction stunned Gu Chacha. Wasn’t she angry?","This entire floor of the house should have been He Huanhuan’s!","But He Huanhuan wasn’t mad at all. She just asked, \"Aren’t we picking out clothes? Where’s your closet?\"","Gu Chacha forced a smile: \"In the dressing room.\"","\"Oh my god! You have a dressing room?\"","He Huanhuan’s eyes lit up instantly.","Right! Rich people all had dressing rooms!","She was going to take a good look so she could brag to Qi Meili and the others when she got back.","You country bumpkins—ever seen a smart toilet? Ever seen a five-hundred-square-meter villa? Ever seen a dressing room?","Your big sister has!","Just thinking about how clueless they’d look made her want to laugh.","Her delighted expression baffled Gu Chacha. What was she so happy about?","Suppressing her anger, she opened the door to the dressing room. A warm golden light flickered on, revealing rows of little dresses inside the cabinets.","She led He Huanhuan inside and pointed to the second row of dresses: \"Big sis, these are ones I used to wear. Pick whichever you like, and I’ll give it to you.\"","She was offering her cast-offs.","This should drive her crazy, right?","She stared intently at He Huanhuan. Sure enough, Huanhuan frowned!","She was angry! She was about to blow up!","\"Why are they all dresses?\"","He Huanhuan scratched her head: \"Dresses look nice, but they’re not convenient for a fight!\"","\"Huh?\"","The unexpected response made Gu Chacha’s eyes go wide: \"Fight? Fight who?\"","\"Sigh, you wouldn’t understand.\"","He Huanhuan rummaged through the clothes but couldn’t find any athletic pants, so she grabbed a short skirt instead.","Long skirts weren’t good for running away. A short skirt might show a little something, but it was way faster.","After changing, the whole family set out for dinner.","He Huanhuan got terribly carsick, so none of the family cars worked for her.","In the end, Uncle Tang drove her to the Japanese restaurant on the electric scooter that the security captain used for patrols.","By the time she arrived, the others had already booked a private room and were seated, waiting for the food to be served.","He Huanhuan had no idea what they were eating tonight. As soon as she sat down, she saw the head chef walk in.","When she saw his kimono, she blurted out, \"So this is a little Japanese devil’s place?\"","......","The chef was silent.","Gu Chacha laughed and said, \"Big sis, this is omakase. Haven’t you had it before?\"","He Huanhuan looked confused: \"Isn’t that English? Isn’t he a Japanese devil?\"","......","Gu Chacha glanced at Old Mr. Gu. His face had already darkened.","She faintly curled her lips, sat up straighter, smiled at He Huanhuan, and explained,","\"Big sis, omakase comes from the Japanese word おまかせ in Roman script. It means ‘to entrust.’ In the culinary world, it refers to letting the chef decide the menu based on that day’s ingredients.\"","He Huanhuan suddenly understood: \"So they don’t stock up on ingredients? Then their prices must be cheap, right?\"","The chef: ...... Is that really how you interpret omakase?","But the people in the private room were important guests.","The chef forced a smile: \"Ma’am, our ingredients are flown in fresh from Japan every day.\"","So, it’s very expensive.","He Huanhuan didn’t catch the subtext. She just wondered, \"Wouldn’t it be fresher to buy them at the local market? No need for a plane ride.\"","......","The chef’s face went dark.","Gu Chengye’s face went dark too. How embarrassing!","Gu Chacha stepped in with a smile: \"Big sis, Dad’s treating us today, so let’s just enjoy the meal happily~\"","What she really wanted was for Dad to be unhappy.","Every bit of money in the family was in Dad’s hands.","As long as Dad didn’t like He Huanhuan, she wouldn’t get anything good.","And in Dad’s eyes, she herself would always be the gracious, considerate daughter.","All the money and resources that could go to a daughter would be hers alone.","The courses came one by one, and He Huanhuan’s face darkened with each one.","She used to think from TV that Japanese food was something fancy!","But it was all raw!","When another plate of raw fish was served, He Huanhuan finally couldn’t take it anymore: \"I’m not eating anymore!\"","Jiang Yulan quickly leaned in and asked her, \"Huanhuan, what’s wrong?\"","\"I don’t like eating raw things. They taste awful and make me feel sick.\"","He Huanhuan wiped her mouth with disgust and asked the chef, \"Don’t you have anything cooked?\"","The chef felt like he was having a heart attack. The restaurant’s specialty was raw fish!","If you don’t eat raw food, why come here?","But he kept his smile: \"Today we have freshly picked silver-colored red strawberries from Hokkaido, with a sugar content of 18 degrees. It took ten years to develop this variety.\"","He Huanhuan looked at him like he was crazy: \"Isn’t that still raw?\"","The chef: ...... You want cooked strawberries too?","But they still managed to get on the table—strawberries the size of a palm, arranged in neat little square wooden boxes, looking absolutely gorgeous.","He Huanhuan picked one up and took a bite. Juice burst everywhere, and the rich aroma of strawberry instantly filled her entire mouth.","\"They really are good,\" she said.","Much better than the ones she bought for ten yuan a catty.","She reached for another to eat, but noticed that everyone else had stopped using their chopsticks.","She asked, \"These strawberries are so tasty, why aren't you all eating?\"","Gu Chacha smiled and replied, \"Sister, we're full.\"","Only nine strawberries had been served in total. If they ate them all, wouldn't that make them look like nouveau riche?","But she wasn't about to remind He Huanhuan.","\"Then give them all to me.\"","Sure enough, He Huanhuan moved the remaining two strawberries in front of herself.","She had just looked it up online—these things cost over a hundred yuan each. No wonder they tasted so good.","Gu Chengye's face instantly turned as black as charcoal. \"What kind of behavior is that! Put them back!\""]},{"number":5,"title":"Chapter 5: Let the Room","paragraphs":["The chopsticks slammed heavily onto the table. Gu Chengye's face darkened as he interrogated her, \"Don't you know any dining etiquette? Put the strawberries back!\"","He Huanhuan wasn't afraid of him at all. Her eyes widened even more, and she slammed the chopsticks even harder. \"Who do you think you're scolding? What's wrong with me eating a couple of strawberries? Did I break the law?\"","Jiang Yulan quickly stepped forward to pull her. \"Huanhuan, don't argue with your father. Just say you're sorry, and that'll be enough...\"","\"Sorry my ass!\"","He Huanhuan's fiery temper couldn't be held back at all.","She pushed herself up from the table and strode over to Gu Chengye, glaring at him. \"Old man, what were you yelling at me for?\"","\"Sister, don't be mad at Father.\"","Gu Chacha quickly walked over and explained gently, \"Sister, in a family like ours, going out to eat can't be like those nouveau riche types...\"","\"What's wrong with being nouveau riche?\"","He Huanhuan let out a mocking laugh. \"Eating all the strawberries makes someone nouveau riche? What kind of family are you? A family that glorifies waste?\"","\"Sister, that's not it...\"","She reached out to pull He Huanhuan's arm. Huanhuan, annoyed by her whining, waved her hand to shake her off.","But unexpectedly, Gu Chacha suddenly fell to the ground, crying pitifully, \"Sister, don't be angry...\"","\"He Huanhuan! Have you lost your mind?\"","Gu Chengye's fury erupted, and he banged the table so hard it rattled.","\"Why did you push Chacha?\"","He Huanhuan shot him a glare. \"I didn't push her.\"","Gu Chengye pointed at her furiously. \"I saw it with my own eyes! And you still dare to lie?\"","Huanhuan's anger flared up instantly. \"Damn it! Are you blind? I said I didn't push her!\"","\"I saw it!\"","Gu Chengye had truly seen it. From where he stood, it really looked like He Huanhuan had shoved Gu Chacha down.","His heart ached with disappointment—how could his daughter, lost for twenty years, be such a rude and uneducated child?","His trembling finger pointed at He Huanhuan, as if he wanted to jab it straight into her heart. \"At such a young age, lying through your teeth! Who do you think you are?!\"","Before he could finish, Huanhuan grabbed his finger and bent it back.","She bared her teeth at him. \"Are you sick? I said I didn't push her!\"","His finger was bent nearly to the back of his hand, and Gu Chengye was in so much pain he almost lost his voice. \"Let go!\"","Huanhuan glared at him and emphasized, \"Let go my ass! I didn't push her!\"","\"Huanhuan, you can't hit your father!\"","Jiang Yulan was terrified. Her face pale, she rushed over to pull Huanhuan away, but Huanhuan shoved her off!","\"Ah!\"","Huanhuan was strong. Jiang Yulan couldn't keep her balance and staggered backward several steps before collapsing onto her two sons.","Leaning against them, she asked in a hurt voice, \"Huanhuan, why did you push your mother?\"","He Huanhuan grabbed Gu Chengye and pointed at Jiang Yulan. \"See that? That's me actually pushing someone!\"","\"I see, I see... now let go!\"","By then, Gu Chengye couldn't care less about that. He just wanted to save his index finger!","Cold sweat dripped from his brow.","\"Weakling!\"","Huanhuan snorted disdainfully before releasing him.","She looked down at Gu Chacha. \"Tell me yourself—did I push you just now?\"","Gu Chacha felt a strange twinge in her finger, then quickly stood up and explained to Old Mr. Gu, \"Father, Sister didn't push me. I lost my balance.\"","She gently massaged Old Mr. Gu's finger. \"Father, Sister didn't mean to hit you. Please don't be mad at her, okay?\"","Her big eyes blinked up at him.","It calmed his raging heart just a little. \"You're too kind-hearted, child. That's how we raised you.\"","\"What the hell—you're a Green Tea!\"","He Huanhuan suddenly shouted. \"Holy crap! A real-life Green Tea!\"","...","Gu Chacha blinked. \"Sister, what are you talking about? I don't understand...\"","He Huanhuan clapped excitedly. \"That's exactly it! So authentic! Say more stuff like that!\"","She pulled out her phone, opened the video recorder, and started directing Gu Chacha. \"Come on! Say it into my camera! More of that Green Tea talk!\"","In her circle of friends, they swore like sailors and dragged each other's ancestors into it within three sentences.","She'd never seen such a fresh Green Tea before!","She had to film this—to show Qi Meili and the others what it looked like.","But as she started recording, she remembered she'd been pulled into a book.","Even if she went back later, the footage wouldn't come with her.","Whatever.","She'd just have to describe it herself.","She put her phone away, pinched her voice, and mimicked Gu Chacha: \"Father~ Sister didn't mean to hit you~\"","Then she looked earnestly at Gu Chacha and asked, \"Did I nail it? Any tips on how to improve? Give me some pointers?\"","...","Her gaze swept to Old Mr. Gu, and she beamed. \"Don't trust the Green Tea. I hit you on purpose just now.\"","...","Behind them, Gu Jinghan silently gave her a thumbs-up. Damn, what a warrior!","Beating up the old man, talking back to the Green Tea.","An all-around fighter!","Gu Chacha's face nearly cracked. \"Sister, what are you doing?\"","She blinked, and her eyes instantly welled up. \"Father...\"","Gu Chengye's rage surged higher. He bellowed furiously, \"He Huanhuan!\"","Huanhuan snapped her legs together, stood up straight, and shouted with perfect clarity, \"Sorry, Old Geezer! Sorry, Green Tea!\"","...","Her voice was so deliberately drawn-out it only made things worse.","That wasn't a genuine apology at all!","It was pure provocation!","\"You, you, you!\"","Gu Chengye was so angry he couldn't speak. \"What kind of behavior is this? How is this like a girl? Is this how the He family raised you?\"","He Huanhuan was jiggling her leg and smirking. \"I was twelve years old, wailing for money at funerals. What did you expect me to be? I'm already damn impressive that I turned out like this!\"","\"Twelve? Wailing at funerals?\"","Gu Chengye froze. \"Why were you wailing at funerals?\"","Huanhuan's leg jiggled faster. \"To earn money! How else was I supposed to eat? Were you going to give me money?\"","Gu Chengye couldn't believe it. \"Aren't He Hongying and her husband both working? How could you have no money for food?\"","He'd done his research. He Hongying and her husband were both wage earners. Their income, though not high, was enough to raise a child.","He Huanhuan couldn't be bothered to make up a lie. \"How the hell should I know? I never saw a cent of it!\"","The truth in her expression was too real for Gu Chengye to doubt.","He couldn't help but believe her—that this kid really did make money by wailing at funerals, scraping by on that to grow up.","He didn't dare to think about how she would've survived without that money.","Oh, wait. She could survive.","She could also take beatings for money, let people smash bottles over her head—twenty bucks a pop.","His towering rage instantly fizzled out, replaced by wave after wave of guilt. He opened his mouth. \"Huanhuan... I'm sorry, I failed you...\"","\"No, it's my fault!\"","Gu Chacha cut him off, sobbing. \"It's my fault I took the Gu family's daughter's place for twenty years! I made Sister suffer so much! It's all my fault!\"","Her face was streaked with tears, eyes red and swollen.","Old Mr. Gu's heart ached for her, and he turned to comfort her. \"How is this your fault? You were just a child. You knew nothing...\"","Gu Jinghan rolled his eyes behind the two of them. Here we go again.","She had said this dozens of times over the past few days—couldn’t she come up with something new?","“You rolled your eyes!”","He Huanhuan suddenly pointed a finger at him. “Did you just roll your eyes or not?”"]},{"number":6,"title":"Chapter 6: Han Mo","paragraphs":["Gu Jinghan's heart skipped a beat as he quickly denied it: \"Don't talk nonsense! I did not!\"","He Huanhuan immediately mimicked his eye-roll from earlier: \"You just did it like that. I saw it.\"","Gu Jinghan was speechless. She really nailed the imitation!","\"Jinghan?\"","Old Mr. Gu looked at his second son: \"Why are you rolling your eyes at your sister?\"","Gu Jinghan pursed his lips at Gu Chacha: \"She's been saying the same stuff for days, hasn't she? I'm sick of hearing it, Dad. Aren't you?\"","\"Jinghan.\"","Old Mr. Gu called his name in a warning tone.","Gu Jinghan couldn't help rolling his eyes again: \"If you're really sorry, do something about it!\"","\"Right!\"","He Huanhuan chimed in loudly.","Gu Jinghan felt emboldened: \"What's the point of just saying you're sorry without actually doing anything?\"","He Huanhuan nodded again: \"Right!\"","Tears streamed down her face as Gu Chacha said pitifully: \"I don't know what I can do... I'm too young. I have nothing...\"","Hearing that, Old Mr. Gu's heart ached for her. Chacha was only twenty; what could she possibly do?","Gu Jinghan shot her a glance: \"Why don't you let her have the third floor?\"","\"Second Brother!\"","Gu Chacha shrieked. How could she possibly stay in a guest room? It was so small! So shabby!","\"No way!! Are you letting me stay on the third floor? That's way too luxurious!\"","He Huanhuan's voice boomed out like a megaphone, drowning out Gu Chacha's screams.","She rushed over to Gu Jinghan and asked: \"Oh my god! Are you a genius? How did you come up with that?\"","The corners of Gu Jinghan's mouth lifted: \"Our house has always had one person per floor!\"","He Huanhuan turned to Old Mr. Gu: \"Dad, can I stay there?\"","She didn't ask Gu Chacha; she only looked at Old Mr. Gu.","Of course, she wasn't stupid. She could clearly see that Gu Chacha was trying to butter up their father.","So naturally, she'd direct the question to the person who actually had the say!","Her eyes were bright and full of anticipation as she looked at Old Mr. Gu.","For some reason, Old Mr. Gu nodded: \"Of course you can. You're a child of the Gu family. You can stay wherever you want.\"","Gu Chacha panicked. If He Huanhuan was on the third floor, where would she go?","She looked at Old Mr. Gu with tear-filled eyes: \"Dad, do you not like me anymore?\"","Old Mr. Gu patted her hand: \"How could I? You're my good daughter.\"","\"Then...\"","\"So you'll definitely understand your father!\"","Gu Jinghan cut her off abruptly: \"Our house is only so big, and we can't just build another floor overnight. Chacha, you're so filial. You wouldn't make things hard for Dad, would you?\"","If it's about playing innocent, who can't do that!","\"Of course not! It's just...\"","Her mind racing, Gu Chacha scrambled to save face: \"It's just that I have so many things. I'm worried the guest room won't fit everything.\"","Yes! That was it!","The guest room was so small, and she had so much stuff. How could it possibly all fit?","She blinked, letting out a deliberately troubled sigh: \"I have way too much stuff...\"","Gu Jinghan barely held back another eye-roll: \"You just don't want to move. You're faking it!\"","He Huanhuan agreed: \"Because she's a green tea [a dramatic, manipulative type]. They're all like that.\"","The two high-fived in sync, making Gu Chacha so furious that tears streamed down her face again.","\"I'm not! I'm willing! It's just that I have too much stuff...\"","\"Put your things you don't need on the fifth floor. I still have plenty of space there.\"","Gu Jingchen suddenly spoke up, offering a solution.","\"Big Brother?\"","Gu Chacha couldn't believe that her eldest brother would side with He Huanhuan against her.","She looked at him with reddened eyes: \"Big Brother, how can you...\"","He was always so cold and rarely played around with her.","But ever since she was little, whenever she asked for something, he would give it to her.","That third floor was hers!","She had designed every detail with care. How could her big brother just make her move out?","Her heart was filled with grievance, and this time, she was genuinely about to cry.","But Gu Jingchen looked straight at her: \"Since you said you wanted to make up for it, you have to follow through. You have to take responsibility for your words.\"","He wasn't a fool. He could see through Gu Chacha's hypocrisy.","Over the past two years, he had been busy with the company and had spent less time with her.","He didn't realize when she had picked up this manipulative act.","And then there was that fake fall to frame Huanhuan.","In that case, let her give up the third floor.","He had to make sure she faced the consequences of her mistakes so she would learn her lesson and correct her bad habits.","Gu Jingchen's ambiguous words made Gu Chacha feel a pang of guilt.","She didn't dare say another word and could only agree reluctantly: \"Alright, I'll stay in the guest room. As long as Dad is happy, I'm happy.\"","But inside, her anger boiled uncontrollably. He Huanhuan! I'll make her pay!","Seeing her agree to give up the room, Old Mr. Gu beamed with approval and patted her affectionately: \"Chacha has always been the most understanding one.\"","Gu Chacha nearly choked on her words. She didn't want to be understanding! She wanted the third floor!","She...","She nodded through her tears: \"As long as my sister and Dad are happy, Chacha is happy...\"","\"Happy, very happy!\"","Old Mr. Gu smiled and pressed the service bell: \"Waiter, the bill, please!\"","The door opened, and the server said politely: \"Mr. Gu, the bill for this room has already been settled.\"","Old Mr. Gu turned around in surprise: \"Settled?\"","The server nodded: \"Mr. Han Mo is in the room next door. He took care of it.\"","Old Mr. Gu raised an eyebrow: \"Han Mo is here too?\"","As if hearing Old Mr. Gu's voice, footsteps echoed in the hallway.","A young man appeared at the door, looking to be in his twenties.","He was tall, with long legs, and a tailored black suit made his figure look even more striking.","His sharply defined eyebrows gave him a serious demeanor. Standing at the door, he greeted Old Mr. Gu respectfully:","\"Uncle Gu, what a coincidence. I didn't want to interrupt your family reunion, so I didn't come over earlier. As an apology, I took the liberty of settling your bill. I hope you don't find my manners lacking.\"","His humble attitude pleased Old Mr. Gu, who smiled and pulled him inside: \"You young man, always so polite.\"","Leading him over to He Huanhuan, Old Mr. Gu introduced her: \"This is my daughter, Huanhuan.\"","Han Mo offered a polite smile: \"Hello.\"","He Huanhuan nodded: \"And hello to you.\"","She thought the pleasantries would stop there.","But Han Mo followed up: \"Are you settling into Jiangcheng okay?\"","He Huanhuan just nodded without a word.","She didn't even know this Han Mo. What was there to say?","She didn't have anything to say, but Han Mo had plenty to ask.","He looked at her and asked: \"Sorry I missed the family dinner today. Are you free tomorrow? I'd like to take you out to eat.\"","He Huanhuan's eyes went wide: \"Do we even know each other? Why would you want to take me out to eat?\"","Before Han Mo could answer, Old Mr. Gu chuckled and accepted on her behalf:","\"Huanhuan just arrived in Jiangcheng and doesn't have many friends yet. Xiao Han, if you have time, after the meal, why not show her around town a bit?\"","Han Mo nodded: \"Sure. I'll pick you up at the Gu residence at ten tomorrow morning.\""]},{"number":7,"title":"Chapter 7: Fiancé","paragraphs":["After saying that, he politely greeted Old Mr. Gu and then left.","He Huanhuan was left completely bewildered, while Gu Chacha's expression was extremely sour.","He Huanhuan had no idea what was going on. \"Who is he? Why’s he inviting me to dinner?\"","Gu Jinghan leaned in gossipily and whispered in her ear, \"That’s your fiancé.\"","\"What the hell?\"","Gu Jinghan, never one to avoid stirring things up, cheerfully told her Han Mo's identity.","The Han family and their Gu family were among the top wealthy clans in Jiangcheng.","Real estate in Jiangcheng was basically divided between the two families.","In recent years, the local government had been planning to shift the development focus to the eastern part of the city, which made the relationship between the two families a bit delicate.","All the land in the eastern part belonged to the Gu family.","If the Han family wanted a piece of the pie, they had to play nice.","Han Mo was the embodiment of the Han family’s willingness to cooperate.","Back when they were younger, Old Mr. Gu and Han Mo’s father had joked about arranging a marriage during a drinking party.","Last year, both families took that joke seriously and officially betrothed the two of them.","Gu Jinghan glanced at Gu Chacha, whose face was turning uglier by the second. \"So yeah, Han Mo is basically our family’s future son-in-law.\"","Gu Chacha’s fiancé, in other words.","Wait, so why was he asking her to dinner?","He Huanhuan wanted to ask more, but Gu Jinghan pushed her toward the door. \"Let’s go downstairs for a stroll. I’ll buy you some new clothes, how about it?\"","He Huanhuan’s attention was instantly hijacked. \"Only a fool would say no.\"","Meanwhile, in the parking lot, Han Mo sat in his car reviewing his work schedule for the next few days.","His slender fingers swiped across the tablet as he coldly instructed, \"Clear my schedule after ten tomorrow.\"","The young man in the driver’s seat hesitated for a moment, then turned to ask, \"Are you really going to have dinner with that Gu family girl?\"","Han Mo looked up at him. \"What about it?\"","\"Is their family really planning to swap the person you’re supposed to marry?\"","Han Mo’s gaze dropped back to the screen, his voice flat. \"I asked her out right in front of Gu Chengye. He told me to show her a good time around Jiangcheng. What do you think that means?\"","The young man bristled. \"But this is way too reckless! You’ve already been involved with Gu Chacha for two years, and now they just swap her out?\"","\"Chen Yu.\"","Han Mo suddenly looked up and stopped him mid-rant. \"You know what I need. Who that person is doesn’t matter to me.\"","His expression was calm, but his dark pupils held an unshakable resolve.","Chen Yu opened his mouth to argue, the words piling up inside him.","In the end, he swallowed them all and simply replied, \"Alright.\"","At nine-fifty the next morning, a car arrived at the Gu residence on time.","A door to a guest room on the first floor cracked open. Gu Chacha hid behind it, watching Han Mo carry gifts up to the third floor.","She’d thought the marriage alliance was clearly between her and Han Mo. So why, as soon as He Huanhuan showed up, did it become hers?","Yesterday, right in front of the whole family, Han Mo had been fawning all over He Huanhuan, and her father didn’t say a word.","Everyone just acted like she didn’t exist!","Why?","She had been the daughter of this household for twenty years!","He Huanhuan was just some country bumpkin who showed up out of nowhere!","Bitterly, she sat down on her bed. Her third-floor room was no longer hers, and now her fiancé was about to become He Huanhuan’s, too.","What next? Her parents? Her black card?","Her hands clenched unconsciously as she picked up her phone and called her best friend Song Zhuo.","When the call connected, she choked up tearfully. \"Fufu, I feel so awful...\"","Up on the third floor, Han Mo handed a gift bag to He Huanhuan. \"I wasn’t sure what you’d like, so I had the store send over their latest bestsellers. Hope you like them.\"","He Huanhuan took the bag and peeked inside. It was a handbag with some English words on it she couldn’t read.","\"Louis. Isn’t that a jeans brand?\"","Back when she was with Qi Meili, that friend had a boyfriend who constantly bragged that his jeans were some big-name brand.","It was something-something-ouis.","Total poser. He was with Qi Meili for two weeks and never even treated them to a bowl of hotpot. Just kept showing off.","He Huanhuan blinked her ignorant eyes and asked Han Mo, \"Do jeans brands make handbags now?\"","Han Mo was silent.","Maybe this newly returned heiress of the Gu family wasn’t quite... normal.","He couldn’t help but frown. \"This is Louis Vuitton.\"","He Huanhuan finally realized her mistake. It wasn’t a jeans brand.","She pulled the bag out. It was brown, covered in \"LV\" patterns.","\"Oh my god! It's that one—the famous one!\"","Recognizing the logo, she suddenly got it. This was the big luxury brand everyone talked about!","She turned the bag over in her hands, examining it from every angle. \"Damn! So this is what LV looks like?\"","This was an education!","She was even touching an LV now!","\"How much did this bag cost?\"","She asked Han Mo, whose frown deepened. \"You don't know?\"","He Huanhuan shook her head. \"No. First time touching one today.\"","A glimmer of understanding flashed in Han Mo's eyes. It seemed the Gu family's real daughter hadn't lived a very good life before this.","Well then... winning her over should be easier, right?","He looked at her. \"What do you want for lunch?\"","\"Spicy hotpot!\"","She’d picked a fight on Qi Meili’s behalf just to get a bowl of spicy hotpot.","But she never got that hotpot, and then she died and transmigrated into a novel.","Her first meal here was some cold and greasy Japanese food.","Now just thinking about spicy hotpot made her mouth water.","Caught off guard, Han Mo stammered, \"Spicy... hotpot?\"","\"Yeah, that’s all I want. So are you buying or not?\"","He Huanhuan had made up her mind. If he didn't treat her to hotpot, she wasn’t going anywhere with him.","No more of that awful Japanese food—she’d had enough.","\"Fine.\"","Han Mo nodded without a second thought.","His goal today was to show the Gu family his willingness to cooperate.","If he wanted a piece of the eastern city real estate deal, he had to get involved in the planning.","That would give him more leverage in the boardroom and eventually, the power to kick Han Xuan out for good.","As they walked out and headed downstairs, he opened the car door for her like a gentleman. \"Please.\"","He Huanhuan made a face like she’d bitten into a lemon. \"Why do you also drive such a crappy car?\"","What was it with rich people and cheap cars?","Han Mo froze. \"Crappy car?\"","He wasn’t the type to flaunt, but for people in their circle, a car was more than transportation.","It was also a status symbol.","A Mercedes V-class was hardly a clunker.","Still, he immediately apologized. \"I’m sorry, I was in a hurry this morning and didn’t switch cars. What do you prefer? I’ll remember for next time.\"","If He Huanhuan weren’t so set on getting her hotpot, she wouldn’t even bother dealing with him.","She raised her hand and waved. The head of the security team, catching on immediately, drove an electric scooter over. \"Miss, the battery’s fully charged. You’re good to go.\"","He even thoughtfully handed her two helmets.","He Huanhuan put on a helmet and handed the other to Han Mo. \"I’ll drive today. Next time, bring a BYD or I’m not going anywhere with you.\"","\"Huh?\"","Han Mo was taken aback. Drive a what?","Old Tang floated over just in time and whispered in his ear, \"Miss gets really carsick. She can’t ride in fancy cars—only a BYD works for her.\"","Ah, that explained it.","Han Mo took the helmet and put it on, nodding. \"After lunch, we’ll go buy one.\""]},{"number":8,"title":"Chapter 8: Spicy Hot Pot","paragraphs":["Sitting on the back seat of the electric scooter, He Huanhuan excitedly let out a howl: \"Spicy hot pot! Here I come, sis!\"","The electric scooter zoomed off with a whoosh, and Han Mo was yanked backward by inertia.","The strong wind whistled past his ears. He struggled to sit upright and leaned over to He Huanhuan's ear to ask, \"Are you speeding?\"","But he heard He Huanhuan excitedly reply with a question, \"Is there a speed limit for electric scooters?\"","Can't you just ride it as you like?","...","He wanted to get off.","He Huanhuan's second personality was completely out of control, and her singing drifted in the wind: \"Oh ho~ Ho ho~ Spicy hot pot~ So hot~\"","Han Mo folded his arms across his chest, and his heart felt like it was being tossed up into the sky and then slammed back down to the ground.","He thought that maybe he could find other ways to kick Han Xuan out of the company.","Maybe he could take it one step at a time. It didn't seem that urgent...","After a wild ride, they arrived at a bustling residential area. He Huanhuan really couldn't understand why rich people would choose to live in such a remote place.","It was so inconvenient to go out.","If it were up to her, she'd definitely choose to live in a lively neighborhood.","You could go out and have a meal right away. How convenient!","She picked a popular roadside stall and took off her helmet, about to go in.","\"You want to eat here?\"","Han Mo glanced at the storefront and frowned so hard that he could have pinched He Huanhuan to death on the spot.","It was small, shabby, and the hygiene was questionable.","Could he just not go in?","\"Then don't eat,\" said He Huanhuan.","The enticing smell wafted out from the store in waves. She didn't have the time to pay attention to him at all.","If she didn't eat soon, her saliva was really going to start spraying out!","She went in, grabbed a basket, and started piling it up with food. When she weighed it, it came to twenty - eight yuan.","All of He Huanhuan's current assets were twenty yuan transferred by Old Tang.","Plus the original body's savings: three yuan and fifty cents.","She wondered how the original \"sister\" had managed to live like that. All her assets combined were only three yuan and fifty cents.","Poorer than her!","It was okay for He Huanhuan not to have money since she was a minor, but the original \"sister\" was already twenty!","How could she be poorer than her?","It wasn't even enough for a meal of spicy hot pot!","She waved to the outside and shouted, \"Aren't you treating me to dinner? Come in and pay the bill!\"","She couldn't afford it herself.","Han Mo stepped into the spicy hot pot shop. With each step he took, the floor clung to his soles, making a \"patter\" sound as he moved.","It made him want to turn around and leave right away.","But he couldn't. He was already here.","Since he had chosen this path, he had to see it through.","He consoled himself that it was all for the sake of his career.","After he kicked Han Jie out of the company, after he took over the entire company, after he...","His long eyelashes drooped, covering his jet - black pupils and also hiding his thoughts.","It was all worth it. It was all worth it.","He grimaced and picked up a plastic basket, selected some vegetables that looked relatively fresh, and took them to the cashier to pay the bill together.","He Huanhuan asked him, \"I thought you weren't going to eat?\"","Even a fool could tell how disgusted he was.","He Huanhuan didn't like to play tricks on people. If he didn't like it, he could just wait outside for her to finish eating, right?","Han Mo forced a smile and said, \"Suddenly want to give it a try.\"","The food in the street stall was served very quickly. Not long after paying the bill, their number was called.","A large plastic bowl was placed in front of him. Countless thoughts flashed through Han Mo's mind.","Was it made of PP material?","Could it withstand high temperatures?","Was it disinfected daily?","...","He expressionlessly picked up the bowl and followed He Huanhuan to a corner, sitting on a red plastic stool.","His high - end suit was a complete mismatch for this noisy and greasy little shop. His straight back and extremely cold face made the people in the shop keep turning to look at him.","Wearing a suit and eating spicy hot pot. What a pretentious guy!","He Huanhuan lowered her head and stuffed a big mouthful of food into her mouth. The rich sesame paste and thick chili oil instantly filled her mouth!","So delicious!","She took a big bite and satisfied her craving.","Only then did she have the time to notice Han Mo. Seeing his extremely stiff sitting posture, she couldn't help but persuade him, \"Why don't you wait outside? I can finish your portion.\"","Han Mo shook his head and refused. \"Eating at a roadside stall once in a while can also add some flavor to life.\"","He Huanhuan scoffed, \"Don't you know that you're really ruining my appetite like this?\"","A good dining companion was quite particular. It wasn't just about having good - looking looks.","You had to be able to enjoy the same kind of food and talk about it too.","Obviously, Han Mo didn't meet the necessary criteria for a good dining companion.","Looking at the bowl of spicy hot pot in front of him, he simply couldn't bring himself to eat it.","But today's meal wasn't just about eating for him. It was more of a job.","It was a very important job that needed to be taken seriously.","He took a deep breath, picked up his chopsticks as if going to his death, and stuffed a chopstick full of greens into his mouth.","The over - powering taste of the sauce instantly filled his entire mouth.","He Huanhuan looked at him expectantly and asked, \"How is it? Is it delicious?\"","Of course, it wasn't delicious.","The inferior taste of the sesame paste and the cloying chili oil completely masked the original flavor of the food.","He glanced at the people carefully selecting their food in front of the food cabinet. With such strong - flavored sauce, everything would taste the same after being cooked.","Was there any point in choosing?","\"Not bad. It's edible,\" he murmured, giving the most insincere answer.","He Huanhuan pouted. She knew he couldn't be her dining companion.","She reached her chopsticks into his bowl and scooped up all the vegetables in one go and stuffed them into her mouth.","Han Mo was completely stunned. \"What are you doing?\"","Why did she take the vegetables from his bowl, and they were the ones he had already started eating?","He Huanhuan waved her hand in disgust. \"Go wait outside. It annoys me to see you sitting here.\"","It was really ruining her appetite!","For just that one chopstick of vegetables, if she didn't eat them for him, he could sit there all day.","After saying that, she ignored Han Mo and lowered her head to focus on eating her own bowl.","The plastic chopsticks were still in his hand. Han Mo stared at the plastic bowl in front of him for a long time.","In the end, he didn't say a word and silently got up and walked out of the door.","He didn't go far. He just stood there stiffly, enduring the gazes of passers - by.","He Huanhuan looked outside when she was halfway through eating. He was standing there motionless.","When she was almost finished, she looked out again. He still had his back straight, standing with his back to the door.","She gobbled up the remaining food in a few mouthfuls, wiped her mouth, and walked out. \"I've finished eating. Let's go home.\"","She thought that this encounter had ended in a complete failure.","They could just go back to their own homes and find their own families.","She didn't want to play this game of two women vying for one man with Gu Chacha.","It was so low - class.","She was a new - era woman. She could play with men, but it would be too demeaning to fight with another woman over a man.","She put on her helmet and was about to ride home when she didn't expect Han Mo to say as he sat behind her, \"Let's go to the 4S store.\"","\"What for?\"","\"Aren't you carsick? Let's go buy a BYD.\"","\"Huh?\"","He Huanhuan was confused. They had already finished eating the spicy hot pot. Why was he still talking about buying a car?","She turned to look at Han Mo. \"Are you still trying to date me?\"","Han Mo nodded. \"There's an engagement between the Han and Gu families. That's an unchangeable fact.\"","\"Then just marry Gu Chacha! Weren't you two the ones originally arranged?\"","He Huanhuan couldn't understand. Since they were the ones originally arranged, then they should get married.","Why drag her into this?","Was he just bored?","\"You'll have to ask Uncle Gu about that. It was his arrangement,\" said Han Mo, reaching out to turn her head back. \"Let's go. Let's go to the 4S store to buy a car. I'll drive you around from now on.\"","He refused to experience the thrill of riding an electric scooter again."]},{"number":9,"title":"Chapter 9: Born with a Destiny of Poverty","paragraphs":["Han Mo's attitude was very firm, so He Huanhuan had no choice but to bike him to the 4S store.","It had to be said, riding an electric scooter to buy a BYD—the vibe really matched.","Inside the 4S store, the salesperson's eyes lit up the moment he saw Han Mo.","This guy looks rich, go for it!","He swooped over instantly. Good service could at least sell him a Bao. Maybe if luck struck, he could even sell a U!","\"Sir, miss, do you have any prior knowledge of BYD? What series are you interested in? Do you have a rough budget? Need me to make a recommendation?\"","The salesperson's mouth went a mile a minute, staring at the two of them.","He Huanhuan pointed at Han Mo. \"He's buying. Ask him.\"","Han Mo glanced at the salesperson. \"Nothing too expensive. Something around five hundred thousand will do.\"","Whoa! A big spender!","Five hundred thousand and not too expensive!","The salesperson's grin stretched ear to ear. \"Bro! Then I have to recommend our Bao 8 top trim. Full comfort, only four hundred thousand out the door.\"","He pulled out a tablet, ready to give Han Mo a thorough rundown of the car's specs.","Unexpectedly, Han Mo just pulled out a black card. \"Run it.\"","\"Huh? That casually?\"","The salesperson was stunned. Had he even woken up from his nap yet?","A miracle customer? Did he even deserve this?","Shouldn't he be haggling aggressively down? Shouldn't he be chasing after an employee discount? Shouldn't he demand freebies? Shouldn't he make me kick back my commission to him?","He gaped at Han Mo, refusing to take the card for a long moment.","Han Mo frowned in displeasure. \"Is there a problem?\"","\"No, no...\"","The salesperson shook his head furiously, took the card respectfully, and asked cautiously, \"Just swipe it? Don't you need a test drive?\"","The guy decided too fast; he wasn't used to it.","This actually reminded Han Mo—he bought the car to take He Huanhuan out, so she'd better sit in it first to see if she gets carsick.","He looked down at He Huanhuan. \"Want to give it a try?\"","\"Sure!\"","They followed the salesperson to the display car. He opened the doors for them enthusiastically. \"Our Bao 8 uses...\"","\"Blergh!\"","As soon as her head poked into the car, that dizzy, nauseous feeling hit her in a second.","\"No... blergh... this car... I... blergh... can't sit in it... blergh...\"","The salesperson wanted to slap himself. Why did his dead mouth have to say test drive? Just swipe the card, damn it!!","His commission!","His face grimacing, he helped He Huanhuan out. \"Um, would you like to try another model? We have other series...\"","Thankfully, the customer didn't just turn and leave.","He nervously took them to try the U series. Inevitably, the moment her head went in...","\"Blergh!\"","The salesperson smiled. He knew it. Heaven doesn't pity the working stiff!","After trying several high-end series, He Huanhuan's face went pale, and she waved her hand. \"No more, I'm done testing. My throat hurts...\"","Han Mo was puzzled. \"Your housekeeper said you don't get carsick in BYDs.\"","He Huanhuan groaned weakly, \"How should I know? I used to ride BYDs when I took ride-hailing cars, and I didn't get carsick at all!\"","A faint spark of hope flickered in the salesperson's dead heart. \"Miss, could the car you sat in have been a Qin, Song, Yuan, or Han?\"","He Huanhuan shook her head. \"No idea. I just know it was a BYD.\"","She was only twelve then, riding for the first time. She was terrified of looking clueless.","Before the car came, she'd kept searching online how to open the door. She hadn't paid any attention to the model.","\"Miss, can we try one more time?\"","The salesperson stared at He Huanhuan with hopeful little eyes. \"Last time. If it doesn't work, we're done. Deal?\"","A hundred thousand—fine, just let him close one deal!","He gritted his teeth and took her straight to the Qin, the go-to ride-hailing car.","And honestly, as soon as He Huanhuan sat in it, it felt like being home!","No dizziness, no dry heaving, no discomfort at all!","That soft, squishy seat! That charming leather smell!","So comfortable!","She sat there happily. \"If you'd brought me to try this one earlier, none of this hassle would've happened!\"","This was exactly the ride-hailing car she'd taken!","Hehe, so cozy!","The salesperson wept inside. His commission! His miracle customer!","He'd never be a blabbermouth again!","A four-hundred-thousand car or a hundred-thousand car—it made no difference to Han Mo. This car was bought to pick up He Huanhuan. He wouldn't drive it himself anyway.","As long as she was happy riding it, the money was well spent.","Taking the black card again, the salesperson kept his mouth shut.","Just swipe the card. Don't say a word.","As he turned, he heard He Huanhuan ask, \"Hey, if we buy a car here, do you get any gifts?\"","Great!","He knew it. A rich guy who buys a cheap car still turns into a high-maintenance customer!","He was wrong. So wrong.","He should never have been assigned to sell this cheap car.","Because of selling this cheap car, his guilty conscience made his mouth run off.","Now, thanks to his loose lips, he'd lost his big sale!","He turned around with a bitter face. \"Miss, our car doesn't come with any free gifts...\"","He Huanhuan crossed her arms. \"That's nonsense. When my grandma bought a three-wheeler, they gave her eggs! A store this big doesn't give anything?\"","Stubborn customer!","The salesperson braced himself and started the tug-of-war with He Huanhuan.","The salesperson emphasized, \"Our car's selling point is affordability and value. But since you bought so decisively, I can apply for a free seat cushion for you.\"","He Huanhuan reached for the card. \"A hundred-thousand car and you only throw in a seat cushion? Your store is pretty stingy! We're not buying!\"","The salesperson clutched the black card tightly. \"Alright alright... I'll throw in a free dash cam too. But this is coming out of my own pocket. Please don't tell other customers, or it'll make things hard for me...\"","\"That sales line is way too clichéd. Who'd believe that!\"","......","Han Mo's brows furrowed again.","Only after He Huanhuan had wrangled a whole set of freebies from the salesperson did Han Mo get a chance to ask her, \"Why did you ask for all these things?\"","Why bother with free cheap stuff?","\"Wouldn't you have to spend money on them otherwise? Why pay when you can get them free?\"","He Huanhuan glared at him. \"Don't you throw these away! If I find out you did, I swear I will too, believe me!\"","\"...Fine.\"","Since he'd become an adult, a full ten years, he'd met countless people.","Men and women alike.","All of them schemed to squeeze money out of him. He Huanhuan was the first person crazy enough to save him money.","He glanced at the goofily grinning girl beside him, silently pulled out his phone, and opened the chat with Chen Yu:","[Those new summer runway pieces. Buy them and have them sent to Gu Chacha.]","The other side typed back a string of question marks.","[Why? Didn't Gu Chengye want you to get close to the real daughter?]","His fingers paused on the screen for a moment, then firmly typed a line: Too many variables. She's not easy to handle.","He needed the two families' collaboration to go smoothly. As the bond for this partnership, his fiancée—","Needed to be easy to coax, easy to deal with, easy to communicate with.","He Huanhuan clearly didn't qualify.","And Gu Chacha, the fake daughter raised in the Gu family—","Money was her lifeblood.","Pampering her came down to just spending money."]},{"number":10,"title":"Chapter 10: Old Gu's Arrangement","paragraphs":["Chen Yu quickly replied with an okay.","After a moment, he couldn’t help asking another question: “But how do we explain things to Gu Chengye?”","Han Mo’s eyes flickered, and his gaze inadvertently swept over He Huanhuan.","【Gu Chacha will handle her dad.】","Gu Chacha was the kind of person raised on luxuries since childhood, a proper heiress.","If her haute couture arrived even half a day late, she’d throw a month-long tantrum.","For her birthday, she’d make a big production of dragging a group of people to France for Michelin-star dining.","She dressed herself in wealth and glamour every day, snapped countless photos, posted them on social media, and basked in the adoration of netizens.","This kind of lifestyle was built on a mountain of money.","Among the second-generation rich kids in Jiang City, she was known for being extraordinarily generous.","And the Han family was among the wealthiest—he was her best option.","As long as Gu Chacha wasn’t stupid, she’d fight for him.","【Okay.】","Chen Yu worked fast. Before the women even got home, a gift had already been delivered to Gu Chacha’s room.","A massive gift bag sat piled in front of her bed, and Gu Chacha was so furious her eyes turned red.","This Han Mo!","Yesterday, he had the nerve to ask He Huanhuan out right in front of her, and now he was sending her gifts? What was he playing at?","She couldn’t help herself and dialed Song Zhuo again: “... Fufu, what do you think he means?”","Song Zhuo shrieked on the other end: “Oh, my girl! What else could it mean? Where a man puts his money, there his heart lies!”","“So you’re saying...”","Gu Chacha’s eyes narrowed slightly. “His choice is me?”","“Otherwise? It’s not like he fell head over heels for that country bumpkin at first sight, is it?”","On the phone, Song Zhuo’s shrill voice dripped with coldness: “Chacha, people like us don’t believe in true love. Who’s the better choice? There’s no way Han Mo doesn’t know that.”","Gu Chacha nodded silently. Yes, compared to He Huanhuan, she was clearly the superior choice.","She had grown up in this circle; she knew the rules of the game.","Fawning, testing, and cutting others out—she could do it all with ease.","What did He Huanhuan have to compete with her?","“But I’m worried Dad won’t like it...”","She couldn’t help hesitating. She could tell her father wanted He Huanhuan and Han Mo to marry for a strategic alliance.","If she acted rashly, would she make him angry?","“Then don’t fight for it,” Song Zhuo said, her voice full of disdain. “Sis, you can’t have it both ways. Do you want to please your dad or land a rich husband? The choice is yours; I can’t help you with that.”","With that, she hung up without hesitation.","The busy tone buzzed on the other end, and a restless irritation crept up in Gu Chacha.","She sat on the bed for a while, then got up and went to the kitchen to wash a bowl of blueberries herself. She carried it to the second floor.","Old Mr. Gu wasn’t at the office today and was resting at home.","She knocked on the study door: “Dad, can I come in?”","The study door opened, and Old Mr. Gu asked with a smile, “Why aren’t you out hanging out with your friends?”","The smile was as warm and affectionate as always.","Gu Chacha’s nose instantly stung. Everything seemed the same, so why did she suddenly feel like she was no longer the daughter of this house?","Without needing any acting skills, her eyes reddened on the spot: “Dad...”","“Why are you crying?”","Old Mr. Gu quickly pulled her into the study, sat her down, and asked with concern.","Holding the bowl of blueberries, Gu Chacha’s tears fell freely: “I thought you didn’t want me as your daughter anymore...”","Old Mr. Gu fondly stroked her head: “Silly child, how could that be!”","He gestured with his hands to show size: “When you were little and didn’t want to sleep, I’d hold you every day and rock you to sleep. I brought you up until you were this big—how could I not want you?”","He gently took her hand and recounted bits of her childhood stories one by one.","“Remember when you first learned how to spend money and used my card at Gucci to buy a belt, saying it was for me...”","Old Mr. Gu’s face was full of pride: “You’ve been good since you were little. Out of all the kids, you’re the one I love the most.”","Gu Chacha had long forgotten these old stories. Hearing her father describe them so vividly now,","a huge wave of bitterness rushed to her eyes, and tears streamed down uncontrollably: “Then why did you make Han Mo get in touch with sister? He’s my fiancé...”","“Silly child...”","Old Mr. Gu hadn’t expected her to be upset over this.","He patted her head with his big hand and asked, “Do you like Han Mo?”","Gu Chacha shook her head. That man Han Mo was incredibly dull.","Ever since last year, they’d have dinner once a week and a movie every two weeks, like clocking in for work.","Old Mr. Gu asked her, “Then what’s got you so unhappy?”","“I...”","She hesitated. “But he’s such a good match for marriage, isn’t he? That’s what you told me, Dad.”","She hadn’t wanted this arranged marriage at first.","She wasn’t bad-looking, and she had no time for Han Mo!","She was too busy chasing after celebrities!","Last year, she became obsessed with a newly debuted idol and flew all over the world chasing after him.","Then, out of nowhere, her family arranged a marriage alliance for her, and she threw a huge fit at home.","It wasn’t until Old Mr. Gu cut off her credit cards that she resigned herself to accepting the arrangement.","She remembered him saying at the time that male stars under the spotlight couldn’t afford to keep her.","How much money could they possibly make?","A group of a dozen people splitting a concert’s earnings? Each person might get a million or so—enough for a few days of her spending?","Han Mo was her best bet.","This man would spend money to support her, keep her in luxury and comfort.","She had barely convinced herself of this when Old Mr. Gu handed Han Mo over to He Huanhuan?","So what was she? A clown?","She fumed silently, but Old Mr. Gu pretended not to notice and said with a smile, “Chacha, the Han family has messy relationships, and you’re a bit headstrong. Honestly, the Hans aren’t a good fit for you. Last year, I had no choice but to let you bear the burden. Now that Huanhuan is here, you don’t have to suffer. Isn’t that better?”","“No! It’s not!”","Gu Chacha pouted defiantly: “Dad, you’re just stringing me along! You’re obviously playing favorites with sister!”","What nonsense about her not having to suffer?","Her father just wanted to use her arranged marriage to make it up to He Huanhuan.","Hearing this, Old Mr. Gu didn’t get mad. He just sighed deeply: “Chacha, Huanhuan isn’t like you. She grew up in a small place and hasn’t seen much of the world. It’s hard to find a good match for her.”","The Han family still needed the land he controlled. If he told Han Mo to marry Huanhuan, the Hans wouldn’t refuse.","Other families wouldn’t be so easy to deal with.","Their circle was the most snobbish; they wouldn’t easily accept Huanhuan.","Chacha was different. She had been in this circle all her life, and she had plenty of options.","If not Han Mo, there would be someone else.","So Old Mr. Gu was determined to pair Han Mo with He Huanhuan.","Seeing his firm stance, Gu Chacha didn’t argue further.","She knew her father well enough—once he decided something, it was hard to change.","“Dad, I understand,” she said, lowering her head in obedient agreement.","Her long lashes covered her eyes, but they also hid her true thoughts.","Everyone had to fight for their own fate. She and He Huanhuan were not loving sisters."]},{"number":11,"title":"Chapter 11: Han Mo Sends You","paragraphs":["When He Huanhuan came back, she found Old Mr. Gu sitting in the living room, smiling at her.","Seeing her come in, Old Mr. Gu immediately stood up and asked her, \"Huanhuan, what do you think of Han Mo?\"","He Huanhuan nodded. \"Not bad.\"","He wasn’t a bad guy. Even though he didn’t like spicy hot pot, he still forced himself to eat it.","Even though he didn’t like her, there was no disdain in his eyes when he looked at her.","To be honest, Han Mo’s annoyance with her was less than Gu Chacha’s.","So really, he was fine.","Old Mr. Gu latched onto the opportunity. \"How about I give him to you as a husband?\"","It sounded like he was handing out a gift.","He Huanhuan wrinkled her nose and refused. \"No way.\"","She had seen Qi Meili date. When things were good, it was all \"honey, I love you so much,\" disgustingly clingy.","When things turned sour, it was \"get lost, you ugly bastard, go far away and never come back.\"","Just watching it gave her a headache.","Actually dating one herself?","Sorry, she wasn’t into Old Geezers.","Her current body was twenty, sure, but she herself was a solid seventeen.","Who wanted to date a twenty-seven-year-old Old Geezer?","He probably already had that old person smell!","Old Mr. Gu asked gently, \"Why not? Did Han Mo upset you?\"","He Huanhuan shot him a look. \"Old Man, are you working for the matchmaker god or something? How old am I? You’re already rushing me into marriage? Ever heard of late marriage and late childbirth? You’re so uneducated...\"","Even if she was borrowing this body and was twenty this year,","that wasn’t even marriage age, was it?","She figured people shouldn’t even think about marriage until at least thirty.","Let her think about it for another ten years first!","She turned and headed upstairs, but Old Mr. Gu chased after her, pleading, \"Huanhuan, think it over. Everyone has to get married eventually. Since you have to, why not pick the most suitable person at the best time? Think about it...\"","In short, Han Mo was just that \"most suitable person.\"","He Huanhuan couldn’t be bothered. She stepped into the elevator and shut the door on him.","When the elevator reached the third floor and the doors opened, a flashy man was standing there.","Gu Jinghan posed with exaggerated style and said, leaning on his brow, \"Dear little sister, I heard you just got nagged about marriage by Dad?\"","He Huanhuan glanced at him. \"What’s with the drama? Are we that close?\"","Gu Jinghan didn’t care. He slid right next to her and asked, \"You know, after you left today, Gu Chacha went straight to Dad’s study?\"","He Huanhuan shot him a look. \"I was gone. How the hell would I know?\"","\"Guess what she wanted from Dad?\"","\"What?\"","Gu Jinghan pinched her cheek teasingly. \"I’m asking you!\"","\"I don’t feel like guessing.\"","He Huanhuan sprawled out on the bed like a starfish. She didn’t care what Gu Chacha was up to.","After all, she wasn’t the real Gu heiress—she was just borrowing the identity.","Who knew if she’d wake up tomorrow and be back to her old life?","Gu Jinghan leaned over to the bed. \"She wants to steal Han Mo from you.\"","\"Take him.\"","No need to steal; she’d give him away for free.","\"Dad won’t let her.\"","He Huanhuan shot upright. \"Why? Is he crazy?\"","She didn’t want him, Gu Chacha did—what a perfect arrangement!","Why couldn’t he just do the right thing?","Gu Jinghan leaned in mysteriously and whispered Old Mr. Gu’s exact words to her.","\"Damn it! He called me tacky!\"","He Huanhuan was furious. Where was she tacky? She’d always been the most stylish among the alternative girls!","She rolled up her sleeves, ready to charge downstairs and confront Old Mr. Gu, but Gu Jinghan grabbed her. \"Idiot, Dad was just bluffing Gu Chacha! Can’t you tell?\"","What tacky or not?","She was found and brought back as the Gu family’s daughter—she was the Miss Gu now.","Families like theirs, when they arranged marriages, thought about future business growth, cooperation, and a thousand other things.","But they never cared about whether the kid was tacky or had grown up in the countryside.","Especially not for a girl like He Huanhuan.","\"Why are you talking like that? What’s wrong with a girl? Damn it! What’s wrong with a girl?\"","She couldn’t stand his words. What was wrong with a girl? Girls could fight just as hard!","Without hesitation, she slapped Gu Jinghan. \"What’s wrong with a girl? Bothering you somehow? Damn it, pulling out some misogyny on me?\"","\"Hey! No! That’s not what I meant!\"","Gu Jinghan dodged and explained, \"You and Chacha can’t get involved in company business, so you’re no different. That’s what I meant!\"","Only those with shares and a say in the company became special.","Like their big brother, Gu Jingchen.","Like Han Mo of the Han family.","He pointed at himself. \"I’m on the same level as you two right now.\"","Dad thought he was unreliable and wouldn’t let him handle business.","If any family wanted their daughter to marry into theirs, Dad would throw him out as bait too.","People who didn’t work, just spent money—their only use in the family was as marriage ties, to help develop business.","So as long as they stayed alive, they’d already done their part, ha.","Whether they were tacky or not, worldly or ignorant—none of that mattered.","This explanation finally made He Huanhuan understand a little.","\"But why is Han Mo being pushed into marriage? Isn’t he capable?\"","She was confused. Wasn’t Han Mo the one handling their companies’ collaboration?","Wasn’t he pretty competent? Why was his family sending him off to arrange marriage?","\"Ah, him!\"","Gu Jinghan sighed dramatically. \"Got interested in him?\"","Huh, Han Mo was something else!","One dinner out, and he’d already won her over?","That was a skill worth learning. He might need it himself one day.","If he had to marry for business anyway, why not pick someone pleasing and win them over ahead of time? Then he’d— heh heh heh...","He Huanhuan watched him go from a sleazy grin to an even sleazier one.","\"Can you talk like a normal person or not?\"","\"Ahem...\"","Gu Jinghan tried to be serious. \"He’s twenty-seven. His mom’s been gone less than ten years, and his brother is only five years younger. Figure it out yourself.\"","The Han family started as a mom-and-pop shop, working it up from a small factory to a big company.","But the moment Han Mo’s mom closed her eyes, his dad brought in the mistress—along with her grown son.","Han Mo had just turned eighteen. Still reeling from his mom’s death, his dad packed him off to study abroad.","By the time he came back, the company had become his dad’s alone.","Everyone his mom had promoted was kicked out, and the shares and inheritance she’d left for Han Mo were seized by his dad.","\"Look at him—spends all day busy at the company, but he’s on a fixed salary.\"","Gu Jinghan clicked his tongue. \"That dad of his is ruthless.\"","Otherwise, why would Han Mo, like a dog, sweet-talk Gu Chacha and then turn around to sweet-talk He Huanhuan?","Who would want to live like that?","They were all rich second-generation kids too, damn it!","\"He’s after that piece of land Dad owns. Otherwise, why would Dad just hand him over to you like a giveaway?\"","Only by securing the deal with Old Mr. Gu could Han Mo finally get some real say in the Han Group."]},{"number":12,"title":"Chapter 12: Gu Chacha Goes on a Blind Date","paragraphs":["Gu Jinghan nudged her with his elbow. \"So now you understand why Dad insisted on sending Han Mo to you?\"","\"Why?\"","He Huanhuan stared at him with wide, innocent eyes. How was she supposed to know?","He hadn't said anything, had he?","Gu Jinghan shook her shoulders in frustration at her naivety. \"It's about bloodline! You’re the real daughter of the Gu family. Of course, it has to go to you!\"","What was an arranged marriage really about?","It was about bloodline, of course!","The vast plots of land in the eastern part of the city were all in their hands. Why would they let the Han family get a foothold for nothing?","Naturally, it was because they had to bring a worthy son-in-law along for mutual development!","The development of an entire region wasn't something that could be done in a year or two.","Plans spanned at least a decade, sometimes decades longer, involving enormous economic entanglements.","Gu Jinghan cupped He Huanhuan's face and looked her in the eyes. \"You little fool, think about how much money our family would have to split off?\"","\"No matter how much Dad likes Chacha, he would never give Han Mo to her.\"","His expression suddenly turned dead serious. \"Han Mo can only be yours.\"","\"Damn...\"","This was a world He Huanhuan had never encountered before. She was a bit dazed and couldn't help asking, \"How much money are we talking? Is it a hundred million?\"","She had seen rich people showing off on short videos where they casually mentioned 'one small goal'—a hundred million.","She figured that given how serious Gu Jinghan sounded, it had to be at least a hundred million, right?","In truth, she had no real concept of what a hundred million meant.","For someone poor like her:","A hundred thousand was a car.","A million was an apartment.","Ten million was a luxury mansion.","But a hundred million?","Sorry, her imagination failed her.","Gu Jinghan pinched her nose. \"Silly girl, we’re talking about tens of billions...\"","\"Damn, am I really that valuable?\"","\"You bet you are!\"","Gu Jinghan smirked teasingly. \"Just wait. Gu Chacha is definitely going to come after you next.\"","Han Mo was someone Chacha wouldn't easily give up.","In the circle of wealthy second-generation heirs, there weren't many as generous as Han Mo.","Most of them couldn't even cover their own startup costs with the money their families gave them, so where would they find the cash to spoil a woman?","Once Gu Chacha met a few of those heirs, she’d realize just how good Han Mo really was.","As it turned out, the very next day, Gu Chacha found out exactly how good Han Mo was.","That guy Song Zhuo, after learning that Chacha had lost her arranged marriage, scrambled to find her a new prospect overnight.","\"Their family is loaded!\"","Song Zhuo’s voice was practically vibrating with excitement over the phone. \"You absolutely have to lock this down! If you snag him, you’ll be untouchable in the Gu family!\"","These days, having money wasn't enough—his family had been 'red' for generations!","Gu Chacha sounded unenthusiastic. \"If it’s so great, why don’t you go for it yourself?\"","Talk was cheap. If it were really that good, Song Zhuo would have kept it for herself.","Song Zhuo grumbled in frustration. \"Damn, you think I didn’t try? He’s not into my type!\"","She had already made her own attempt!","And been flat-out rejected!","That admission actually made Gu Chacha believe her a little more.","\"Fine, set up a time for me. I’ll go check him out.\"","In the circle of heiresses at Jiang City, Gu Chacha’s looks were more than presentable.","Her eyes were naturally upturned, long yet not narrow.","They were stunning fox eyes.","But her pupils were round, which took away from the sharpness and gave her a softer appearance.","Song Zhuo moved fast—one call and she booked a lunch meeting for the next day.","The next day, Gu Chacha dressed in an apricot-colored dress, looking gentle and sweet.","She arrived at the Western restaurant as agreed, and the hostess led her into a private room.","Inside, a man in an old suit sat frowning as he flipped through the menu.","When she walked in, the man nodded at her. \"Liang Ye.\"","\"Gu Chacha.\"","As soon as she sat down, Liang Ye handed her the menu. \"Take a look at what you'd like to eat.\"","She casually ordered two dishes. Today's main focus wasn't really about eating—it was...","\"Make it two checks. She pays for what she ordered.\"","Hmm?","Gu Chacha froze. \"What did you say?\"","Liang Ye glanced up at her. \"I always split the bill when I eat with a woman. Do you mind?\"","\"Always split it?\"","Gu Chacha was a bit confused. \"Even when you're dating?\"","\"Split it.\"","\"What about marriage? Even after marriage?\"","Liang Ye nodded. \"Naturally. Men and women are equal. I refuse to spend money on women. I also look down on those who try to latch onto wealth. I assume you're not that kind of person, right?\"","His gaze landed on her, waiting for a reply.","She forced a smile onto her face. \"Of course not...\"","She knew it! That bastard Song Zhuo would never actually set her up with a decent match!","So this was the catch!","When the food arrived, she poked at it listlessly with her chopsticks, unable to eat.","Originally, she had thought that without Han Mo, she could always find someone else.","But yesterday, when she went through the eligible bachelors in Jiang City...","One by one, they were all even worse than Han Mo.","She'd heard that the second-generation heir of the Xu family had opened a coffee shop as a startup at the start of the year—spending ten million on the interior alone.","The steps leading into the shop were imported straight from France.","After six months in business, he hadn't even made a thousand in revenue.","If she ended up with someone like that...","Her dowry wouldn't even be enough to cover his losses!","She'd hoped that Fufu could hook her up with someone reliable—ha!","Call it being cheap, why dress it up as splitting bills? Who was he trying to fool?","\"Why aren't you eating?\"","Seeing her poke at the food for ages without taking more than two bites, Liang Ye couldn't help but ask.","She smiled and shook her head. \"I don't have much of an appetite. I can't eat.\"","\"Then I'll help you finish it.\"","Without waiting for a response, Liang Ye reached over, took the dish in front of her, and polished it off in three or four bites.","It happened too fast—she couldn't react in time.","\"Th-That was my dish.\"","Liang Ye nodded. \"You said you didn't have an appetite, right? It's wasteful to leave it.\"","\"But we're splitting the bill!\"","She paid for that food!","Liang Ye smiled. \"I know. So, you're welcome.\"","You're welcome, my ass!","Was he acting like he was doing her a favor?","Gu Chacha could barely keep the smile on her face. She took a deep breath. \"Mr. Liang, I think we might not be very compatible...\"","\"Why?\"","Liang Ye looked at her, puzzled. \"I actually have a good impression of you. I think we should keep seeing each other. If you don't mind, I could visit your parents tomorrow. If everything goes smoothly, we could get engaged by the end of this month...\"","His lips kept moving, spouting terrifying words.","Gu Chacha suddenly realized—that damn Fufu! She was just foisting her problem onto Gu Chacha!","Under the table, her fingers flew across her phone, typing frantically: \"Song Zhuo! You did this on purpose! You set me up!\"","A reply came from the other side in no time: \"Sorry! If I didn't, I'd be the one getting engaged to him! Chacha, save your bestie—his family is really loaded! I swear!\"","\"What good does being loaded do? He won't spend a cent on her! He's making me split the dinner bill!\"","\"Then just pawn him off on someone else! He's not picky!\"","\"You—\"","She had just typed the word \"you\" when a flash of a colorful figure crossed her mind. The corners of Gu Chacha's mouth curled up involuntarily.","She rested her chin on her hands and looked at Liang Ye. \"Mr. Liang, actually, I have a pretty good impression of you too. But you might not know, I'm not really the child of our family...\"","With tears in her eyes, she recounted her background. \"Sigh... I feel like I'm not good enough for you...\"","\"That's true.\"","Liang Ye nodded. \"Based on what you're saying, you are indeed a bit lacking for someone like me.\"","Gu Chacha barely stopped herself from cursing. You stingy jerk! How dare you say that!","But on the surface, she still put on a sad expression. \"Compared to my older sister, I'm really not worthy of you...\"","Liang Ye glanced at her face—it was very beautiful.","He felt a little reluctant, but considering her background, he decided to prioritize the bigger picture. \"Does your sister have a boyfriend? If not, you can introduce us.\"","Gu Chacha quickly shook her head. \"My sister is virtuous and pure, she has no boyfriend!\""]},{"number":13,"title":"Chapter 13: Need a Driver","paragraphs":["In the evening, the family gathered for dinner.","Gu Chacha glanced at He Huanhuan and asked casually, \"Big Sister, I heard things are going well with Han Mo?\"","Hearing her words, Gu Jinghan immediately started making exaggerated faces at He Huanhuan.","Ha! Didn't he say it before?","Gu Chacha was definitely going to stir things up with her!","He Huanhuan couldn't be bothered with him. She looked up and asked Gu Chacha, \"Who told you that? Who the hell is spreading rumors about me? Speak up! Who's making up lies about me?\"","Her eyes were wide with anger, staring intently at Gu Chacha, making the latter falter mid-sentence: \"Uh, I just guessed it myself... Big Sister, don't be mad...\"","He Huanhuan shot her a disdainful glance. \"Don't overthink it. My business is none of yours.\"","......","What was she being so arrogant about?","Gu Chacha suppressed her rising anger and turned to Old Mr. Gu. \"Dad, guess who I ran into today?\"","Old Mr. Gu played along. \"Who?\"","\"Liang Ye!\"","Gu Chacha smiled lightly. \"He heard about Big Sister's situation and felt really sorry for her. He said she must have had a hard time in the past...\"","\"Liang Ye? Which Liang?\"","At the mention of the surname Liang, Old Mr. Gu's expression shifted instantly.","His eyes locked onto Gu Chacha as he pointed mysteriously toward the ceiling. \"Are you talking about that Liang?\"","Gu Chacha winked and smiled. \"It was set up through Fufu~\"","The moment he heard it was through Song Zhuo's introduction, Old Mr. Gu knew it was definitely that Liang family.","The Song family had quite the connections in that regard.","He immediately forgot about dinner and hurriedly pressed Gu Chacha, \"He asked about Huanhuan? What did he say?\"","But Gu Chacha didn't elaborate. She only vaguely replied, \"He just said he felt bad she had a tough time and mentioned that if she's free, they could have a meal together.\"","\"He must eat! He absolutely must eat!\"","Old Mr. Gu, having imagined something in his head, was suddenly flushed with excitement.","He shot up from his seat, trotted over to He Huanhuan, and grabbed her hand. \"Huanhuan, you need to take this meal seriously, understand?\"","\"Why?\"","He Huanhuan hadn't followed their exchange at all. What were they even talking about?","Why was pointing at the ceiling making him so worked up?","Old Mr. Gu pointed upward again. \"That's the Liang family!\"","His excitement was like a eunuch in a Qing dynasty drama.","\"They're like royalty!\"","\"She's like a princess!\"","......","He Huanhuan couldn't help but chuckle, imagining Old Mr. Gu making exaggerated gestures with a lispy tone.","Gu Chacha, sitting across the table, watched He Huanhuan laugh carefreely.","She sneered inwardly. A country bumpkin playing all high and mighty.","Hearing that the Liang family had ties to the upper echelons of power, she was still laughing all the same.","But she was desperate to get rid of Liang Ye, and she secretly hoped He Huanhuan might actually hit it off with that weirdo...","That would work out conveniently for her.","The Liang family had undeniable, solid influence, but Liang Ye himself was just too stingy. She couldn't stand it.","Still, if the two families could become connected through marriage, hers would benefit.","Even the development of East City would give Old Mr. Gu more say.","It wasn't as if Old Mr. Gu was genuinely kind and wanted to mentor young people!","Old Mr. Gu: Who's old? Who's unkind? Watch your words!","East City was such a huge area that the Gu family couldn't take it all for themselves.","But since the land was in their hands, Old Mr. Gu had absolute authority over who got to join in.","If He Huanhuan successfully won over Liang Ye, the Gu family could easily latch onto the Liang family.","Then everything their family did would be much smoother.","For families like theirs, convenience meant making money faster and more aggressively.","Without He Huanhuan in the picture, she could go ahead and marry Han Mo...","Then Han Mo could follow along with her dad and make money off the Liang connection.","Meanwhile, He Huanhuan would have to struggle, splitting everything fifty-fifty with Liang Ye!","Thinking about that, her gaze toward He Huanhuan softened noticeably. \"Big Sister, Mr. Liang is a handsome man. I'm sure you'll like him~\"","\"You're definitely up to no good.\"","He Huanhuan turned to Gu Jinghan. \"Did she look this fake when she schemed against you?\"","Gu Jinghan nodded through tears. \"Yes!!\"","Every time she smiled at him like that, something bad happened to him!","\"Second Brother!\"","\"Jinghan!\"","Old Mr. Gu's disapproving gaze swept over, and Gu Jinghan instinctively shrank back.","Damn Gu Chacha!","Even smiling at Huanhuan still got him in trouble!","The date with Liang Ye was set for the next day. If it weren't so late, Old Mr. Gu would've wanted them to have dinner that very night.","What about Han Mo?","Sorry, kid, his daughter was marrying up now~~","That evening, Gu Chacha lay in bed and texted Han Mo: Want to have dinner together tomorrow?","After a while, he replied: Are you sure it's okay?","A contemptuous smile curled at her lips. He couldn't stand He Huanhuan but didn't want to offend Old Mr. Gu.","Men. Useless, every single one.","Her slender fingers tapped the screen: Big Sister has a date with that Liang family guy tomorrow, so I'll be bored. Don't you want to take me out?","He replied instantly: Liang Ye?","She smirked. Yep.","With her confirmation, he practically responded in seconds: What are we eating?","French cuisine.","Okay.","Setting down her phone, Gu Chacha lay down lightly.","Tomorrow was bound to be interesting.","She set the meeting for He Huanhuan at ten in the morning. At nine-thirty, He Huanhuan pushed her electric scooter out, ready to go.","Old Mr. Gu rushed out to persuade her. \"Let Old Tang drive you. Riding an electric scooter doesn't look good.\"","He couldn't let Liang Ye's son think he didn't care about Huanhuan or didn't want the marriage. That would be a huge loss!","He Huanhuan frowned in disgust. \"Drive me? I've been back for days, and you haven't even bought a BYD yet. Now you're acting fake?\"","Han Mo couldn't stand her and still bought a car right after that cheap hotpot meal!","That was what you call showing attitude!","Old Mr. Gu laughed sheepishly. \"I've been busy and forgot. I'll buy one tomorrow, I promise!\"","Busy his foot. He just hadn't bothered.","For the past two years, all the tedious company work had been dumped on Gu Jingchen, and Old Mr. Gu rarely went into the office.","He just hadn't taken He Huanhuan's motion sickness seriously.","Too lazy to call him out on it, He Huanhuan stubbornly pushed her scooter forward.","She wasn't about to suffer for someone else's pride!","Just as she put on her helmet, a deafening roar came from behind the house.","Then a flash of bright red shot straight toward He Huanhuan and Old Mr. Gu!","\"Move!\"","Gu Jinghan shouted from his motorcycle. \"This thing won't stop! Get out of the way!\"","\"Oh crap!\"","He Huanhuan jumped off her scooter and pulled Old Mr. Gu aside.","\"Boom!\"","Her little electric bike was sent flying!","So was Gu Jinghan in his red motorcycle suit.","He ended up planted face-first in a flowerbed, dizzily pulling off his helmet while still grinning.","\"Pretty cool bike, huh? I'll take you for a ride.\"","......","Did she look like she wanted to die?","\"Miss, Master Han has arrived.\"","A report crackled through the wireless intercom at the gate, and He Huanhuan was surprised. Han Mo?","What was he doing here?","The BYD she had personally picked slowly pulled into view. The window rolled down to reveal Han Mo's cold, expressionless face.","His intense gaze fell upon her. \"I heard you have a date today?\"","He Huanhuan nodded. \"Yeah, what’s up?\"","Han Mo got out of the car, walked over to her, and opened the door for her. \"Maybe you need a driver.\""]},{"number":14,"title":"Chapter 14: Psycho Girl Cures the Miser","paragraphs":["The passenger door opened in front of her, and He Huanhuan immediately recognized the seat cushions as the free ones she'd wrangled from the salesperson.","The car charms dangling from the rearview mirror were also her doing—cheerful little God of Wealth pendants she'd grabbed on a whim.","The whole car reeked of trying to win her over, and she was genuinely puzzled.","She looked up at Han Mo. \"Do you even know what I'm about to do?\"","Han Mo nodded. \"Yeah, I know.\"","\"And you're still giving me a ride?\"","Han Mo gave a soft laugh. \"You get carsick, don't you? I happened to be free today, so I figured I'd drop you off on the way.\"","What the hell!","The guy was a total simp!","He Huanhuan gave him a thumbs-up. \"You're something else.\"","Rich as hell and still acting like a lapdog—impressive!","\"Big Sister~ Don't blame Han Mo. I'm the one who told him to come~\"","Gu Chacha's syrupy voice floated out from inside the house.","She was wearing a snow-white long dress, her hair curled into elegant waves.","Her smile was just as sickly sweet as she wrinkled her nose at He Huanhuan. \"Big Sister, I told him you had a date today, so he came on purpose~\"","\"Fine.\"","A ride beat biking any day, so He Huanhuan bent down and slid into the passenger seat.","When she spotted that cheap BYD, the smile on Gu Chacha's face froze for a second.","Had Han Mo actually gone and bought this budget car?","She shot a glance at Han Mo, who walked over to the rear door expressionlessly and opened it for her. \"After you.\"","Polite, and utterly distant.","Gu Chacha's eyes darkened. A piece-of-junk car like this, and she was supposed to sit in the back?","She looked down at He Huanhuan. \"Big Sister, it seems you're sitting in the wrong spot.\"","The passenger seat was reserved for the fiancée. And she was on her way to meet Liang Ye for a blind date—how could she sit there?","He Huanhuan didn't budge an inch. \"What's wrong with where I'm sitting?\"","These seat cushions were hers, begged for with her own mouth. She'd sit wherever she damn well pleased!","If she knew how to drive, she'd have hijacked the whole car by now!","\"But the passenger seat is...\"","Gu Chacha started to argue, then bit her tongue just in time.","She couldn't say it. If she did, she'd lose.","Sure, Han Mo was a catch, but she wasn't about to let him lead her around by the nose.","She couldn't let him think she was desperate for him.","She glanced at Han Mo, standing there like a wooden post, not saying a word to defend her.","Fuming, she climbed into the backseat. The cheap leather smell hit her nostrils instantly, making her dizzy and sick.","She snapped irritably, \"Why'd you buy such a crap car?\"","He Huanhuan swayed happily in the passenger seat. \"What's crap about it? It's brand new!\"","Gu Chacha frowned in discomfort. If she'd known she'd have to suffer this pointless poverty, she'd have driven herself!","But the car had already left the Gu mansion, and it'd be awkward to turn back now.","She had a ten o'clock appointment with Liang Ye, and being late wouldn't do.","When they pulled up to the agreed-upon coffee shop, Liang Ye was already there, two cups of coffee set on the table, waiting.","The car stopped at the entrance, and the three of them got out.","Seeing Gu Chacha, Liang Ye stood up and waved.","Halfway through the gesture, his hand froze awkwardly in midair.","That gaudy bouquet standing beside Gu Chacha—was that the real rich daughter they'd mentioned?","That rainbow of a head stepped into the shop, step by step, and his gaze followed it helplessly.","Red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, violet, pink...","How could one person cram so many colors onto their head?","It was so distracting he didn't even register what He Huanhuan's face looked like.","Not until she was standing right in front of him, boldly giving him a once-over. \"You're Liang Ye?\"","He nodded, dazed. \"Yeah.\"","He had imagined this real heiress might look dowdy, or maybe be too timid to present herself.","But definitely not this aggressive... like some street-smart tough girl.","Exactly!","Street-smart tough girl vibes!","He’d seen videos of that type online, and she was the spitting image.","He had heard those girls were totally wild, ready to throw a punch if they got upset.","He swallowed hard and nodded gently. “Yeah, that’s me.”","Gu Chacha smiled sweetly as she greeted him. “Mr. Liang, I’m entrusting my Big Sister to you now, you’d better not bully her, okay~”","Liang Ye forced a bitter smile. “Do you think I could?”","Just look at the two of them—who’s really going to mess with who?","“Oh, of course you wouldn’t~”","Gu Chacha gave him a playful slap, then naturally linked her arm through Han Mo’s. “Mr. Han, didn’t you promise to treat me to French food? I’m getting a little hungry~”","“Alright.”","Han Mo nodded at the two of them and led her out the door.","The coffee shop was suddenly left with just those two.","Liang Ye felt a bit tense—he couldn’t shake the feeling that He Huanhuan might jump up and whack him at any moment.","He sat down with his legs pressed together, playing it safe, and pointed to the coffee cup in front of He Huanhuan. “I ordered that for you.”","The straw was ridiculously thin, so He Huanhuan found it annoying and just popped the lid open to take a sip.","No sooner had the coffee touched her lips than Liang Ye said, “That one costs thirty-eight yuan.”","“Pfft, pfft, pfft...”","She brought the cup to her mouth, then spat all the coffee back into it.","With a sour face, she looked at Liang Ye. “I didn’t drink it.”","Since she got home, no one had mentioned giving her any pocket money.","They kept piling activities on her every day, keeping her so busy she never thought about asking for cash.","Her entire net worth was still twenty-three dollars and fifty cents—and not a cent more.","There was no way she could afford this coffee.","She slid the coffee cup back toward Liang Ye, palms up. “Here, take it back.”","Liang Ye was utterly stunned. In all his years of blind dates, he had never met such a... such a crazy girl!","He lowered his voice and snapped, “You drank some!”","He Huanhuan opened her mouth wide. “Don’t you frame me! I didn’t take a single sip!”","“You did! And you spit it back!”","Liang Ye was losing his mind staring at that cup. She actually spit back into it!","How was he supposed to drink that now?","What a waste!","He Huanhuan shrugged defiantly, her hands open. “I didn’t drink it, so I’m not paying.”","“You—!”","Liang Ye’s face turned red with anger!","He hadn’t dealt with anything like this since he became an adult.","Usually, he’d suggest splitting the bill, and the girls would meekly pay their share.","He glanced at the coffee, then at the fierce-looking He Huanhuan.","His stinginess won out over his vague fear, and he stood right in front of her, demanding money. “Thirty-eight. Give it to me.”","He Huanhuan’s eyebrow twitched. “You want to die?”","Liang Ye insisted, “Everyone has to pay for what they consume. You drank it, so you pay.”","“Crazy!”","He Huanhuan didn’t want to argue anymore and got up to leave.","But he grabbed her arm. “You just drank it—why won’t you admit it? If you drank it, you pay.”","For crying out loud!","Was he really dead set on taking her twenty-three fifty?","Her temper shot straight through the roof. She shoved him down into his seat!","With one hand, she pried open his mouth; with the other, she grabbed the coffee cup and started pouring.","“Drink it, dammit!”","“Gulp-gulp-gulp... gulp-gulp-gulp...”","Liang Ye was completely broken. This was the coffee she had spat back into!","But He Huanhuan was incredibly strong, pressing him down so much that he couldn’t struggle free.","After forcing half a cup of coffee down his throat, she finally let go of her grip on him.","Wiping the corner of his mouth casually with her thumb, He Huanhuan reached out and patted his face: “Now you’ve drunk more than I have. Still going to charge me?”","Liang Ye looked aggrieved: “Yes...”","He had been forced—he didn’t want to drink it...","His chin was gripped hard again: “Then you drank my saliva—shouldn’t you pay up?”","Liang Ye’s face turned bright red: “You forced me...”","He Huanhuan squeezed him and played dirty: “Just tell me, did you drink it or not?”","Liang Ye nodded, his face still red—he had indeed drunk it...","He Huanhuan pulled out her payment QR code with a flourish: “Half a cup of saliva, thirty-eight bucks. Scan it.”","“How is it that much...”","Liang Ye felt it was unfair—there was still more than half left in the cup!","“Scan it!”","A sharp glare shot his way, and he obediently scrolled the money over like a timid little wife.","With the payment in, He Huanhuan turned to leave.","“Where are you going?”","Liang Ye stood up to chase after her, then ran two steps back hurriedly to carefully pick up the remaining coffee.","“Where are you going, huh?”"]},{"number":15,"title":"Chapter 15: Chosen Wife","paragraphs":["After walking out of the coffee shop, the familiar BYD was long gone. He Huanhuan turned and walked toward the side of the road.","Having just swindled thirty-eight bucks, she could afford to take a cab.","She pulled out her phone, ready to check how much it would cost to get home.","Liang Ye rushed out holding coffee, chasing after her: \"Where are you going?\"","\"Home.\"","Liang Ye ran up beside her, panting: \"Aren't we going to eat together?\"","He Huanhuan lowered her phone and looked at him in disbelief: \"Are you sick? Us? Eat together?\"","She had just tricked him with that spit-laced coffee and swindled him out of thirty-eight bucks.","And now they were supposed to eat together?","Was he out of his mind?","Liang Ye bit his lip, a flush of unnatural red appearing on his face: \"You didn't even drink the coffee, and we didn't eat a single meal during the blind date. If I go home like this, my brother will scold me.\"","Because he was cheap and insisted on splitting the bill on blind dates, his family had already chewed him out endlessly.","If they found out today he hadn't even managed to split the bill and had driven the girl away, he really would get cursed out when he got home.","He stuck close to He Huanhuan: \"How about we split a meal, okay? Once we finish, I can at least have something to report when I get home.\"","He Huanhuan gave him a look like she'd grown a second head: \"Are you sick, or am I sick?\"","Why would she eat with him?","With that money, wouldn't she rather get a bowl of spicy hotpot?","Too lazy to deal with him, she opened her phone to call a car. After entering her destination, a glaring eighty-seven bucks popped up.","She almost fainted on the spot.","Eighty-seven!","Damn Old Mr. Gu!","Why did he have to buy a house in such a remote place?","Putting away her phone, she forced a smile and turned to Liang Ye: \"Splitting the bill is fine, but I get to decide where we eat.\"","Liang Ye's eyes lit up: \"Deal!\"","It didn't matter where they ate—it was all on his brother's card anyway, not his money.","He Huanhuan patted his shoulder: \"After we eat, you drive me home.\"","Liang Ye frowned: \"Can't you take a cab yourself?\"","\"What's the big deal if you give me a ride?\"","He Huanhuan was speechless. If she could afford a cab, would she be asking him to drive her?","Use your eyes!","Even Han Mo was better than this.","Liang Ye looked at her pitifully: \"I don't have a car.\"","\"Huh?\"","He Huanhuan was shocked: \"Why don't you have a car?\"","Wasn't he a second-generation rich kid? How could a second-generation rich kid not have a car?","How was he supposed to show off then?","The answer: he didn't show off.","Which flashy member of the rich second generation would split the bill on a date?","This question hit Liang Ye right where it hurt. His eyes lit up instantly, and he started rambling excitedly to He Huanhuan about his philosophy.","\"A car hits the road costing how much? Even a cheap one costs at least one or two hundred thousand, right?\"","\"I live in the city center. My monthly cab fare doesn't exceed five hundred. You do the math: with one hundred thousand, how many years can I take cabs?\"","He pumped his fists excitedly: \"Twenty years! Twenty whole years!\"","...","\"Do you even know how to be a rich kid?\"","He Huanhuan had never seen a rich second-generation kid so messed up. He wouldn't even buy a car for a hundred thousand.","Unbelievable!","Know how to be a rich kid?","If he didn't, let her do it!","She forgot she was the one who threw up every time she got into a luxury car.","Those two were six of one, half a dozen of the other.","Seeing how worked up Liang Ye was, He Huanhuan didn't need to guess—there was no way this guy would spend the money to drive her home.","Let him just die from being stingy.","Fine, fine. She'd head to the spicy hotpot place first.","She opened the map and picked a shop nearby.","Liang Ye still followed her every step, dead set on splitting a meal with her.","Spicy hotpot was the kind of thing where everyone picked their own stuff. If he wanted to follow, He Huanhuan couldn't be bothered to stop him.","Entering the shop, she skillfully grabbed herself a bowl and went to pay.","Only after paying did she notice Liang Ye staring at her with shining eyes, as if she were some kind of rare treasure.","Her heart skipped a beat. Damn, she had a bad feeling about this!","Sure enough, Liang Ye came closer, eyes full of hearts: \"You're so good at saving money! Let's get married!\"","Huh?","He Huanhuan's jaw almost dropped. What had she even done?","All she did was eat some spicy hotpot.","\"Do you have a disorder?\"","How many times had she said that today?","Liang Ye looked at her blissfully: \"You only spend twenty bucks on a meal. You're perfect for me! Really!\"","In all these years of blind dates, today was the cheapest he'd ever spent!","Before, when he ate out, the women would pick those high-end places.","Michelin three-star, private chef reservations...","Every meal would cost a few thousand.","He Huanhuan only spent twenty bucks on a meal!","That was so economical! She was the wife he'd been searching for!","He blinked, gazing at her deeply: \"I can eat spicy hotpot with you every day.\"","He Huanhuan: \"Split the bill?\"","\"Mm-hmm!\"","\"Mm-hmm, my ass.\"","He Huanhuan flipped him off: \"I'd rather eat with Han Mo than with you.\"","Han Mo at least paid for her meals!","\"Han Mo?\"","Liang Ye was annoyed: \"Isn't he off eating French food with your sister? He and I aren't from the same world. You and I are the perfect match.\"","He slurped a loud mouthful of noodles from his spicy hotpot—delicious! Why had he never discovered such cheap goodness before?","\"Look how much I'm enjoying this.\"","He showed off to He Huanhuan: \"I bet that Han Mo could never eat spicy hotpot.\"","People like Han Mo—one look and he knew, same stubborn attitude as his own brother.","Guys like that would never eat spicy hotpot with He Huanhuan.","But he was different. He just hadn't known about this cheap delicacy before.","Now that he did, he could eat it for life!","He winked at He Huanhuan: \"Eat it with you for life~\"","...","He Huanhuan felt that even spicy hotpot had lost its appeal.","She lowered her head, wolfed down the rest of her bowl, and quickly made her escape.","Liang Ye was even more satisfied. Wow, she didn't waste food either!","That was his wife!","He hurriedly finished his own bowl and followed her out.","He Huanhuan walked for a whole street, and he followed every step of the way.","Annoyed beyond belief, she finally turned around: \"Why are you following me?\"","Liang Ye smiled shyly: \"I'm on a date with you~\"","Street-strolling—the cheapest kind of date. He loved it.","He Huanhuan was completely done. If she had money, she would have hailed a cab and left on the spot.","But she didn't, so she could only stomp away on foot.","She walked. She walked. She walked like a madwoman.","For a whole hour, Liang Ye still followed her with a grin.","Even more, the surprise in his eyes was so full it was about to spill over.","He praised her happily: \"You've got great stamina~ Let's get married?\"","People with good health rarely got sick. Not getting sick meant saving money.","Saving money meant... she was his wife!","...","He Huanhuan was out of ideas.","She slumped her face by the roadside, and out of the corner of her eye, she saw a distant electric scooter slowly approaching.","The rider was a young, handsome guy. She quickly waved: \"Hey, handsome! Can you give me a ride?\"","The young guy saw her face and hesitantly rode over: \"Where are you going?\"","He Huanhuan plopped down behind him: \"Anywhere, just get me out of here!\"","She had to shake off that idiot Liang Ye!","\"Free ride?\"","Liang Ye's world was blown open by He Huanhuan: \"That's how you can get a ride?\"","Wow, what kind of extravagant life had he been living before?","\"I want a ride too!\"","He happily ran over, trying to squeeze in behind He Huanhuan.","Disgusted, He Huanhuan frantically tapped the young guy: \"Quick, quick, quick! Go, go!\"","The electric scooter zoomed off in an instant, leaving Liang Ye feeling wronged as he chased after it. \"I haven't even gotten on yet!\""]},{"number":16,"title":"Chapter 16: Spicy Hot Pot and French Cuisine","paragraphs":["Inside the pale gray dining room, a slender chandelier cast a soft beam of light.","The aroma of butter lingered around her, and Gu Chacha cut a piece of steak before bringing it to her mouth.","\"What do you think my sister is doing right now?\" she asked with a smile, looking at Han Mo.","Han Mo sat at the other end of the table, his face hidden in the dim light. Gu Chacha couldn't make out his expression at all.","\"Let's just eat,\" he replied, his voice cold and detached, as if he had no interest whatsoever in the topic.","Gu Chacha let out a light laugh. \"That Master Liang isn't exactly generous. I wonder if my sister can handle him.\"","In her opinion, the two of them were perfectly matched—a country bumpkin and a stingy weirdo. What a perfect pair!","She set down her knife and fork, turning her gaze to Han Mo. \"HanMo, do you think they’ll end up together?\"","Or rather, did he want them to?","She thought Han Mo understood what she was getting at.","The Liang family and her father—what they represented—she believed Han Mo would grasp.","Han Mo held the steak knife in his hand, cutting into the meat slowly and deliberately, one slice after another.","Only after the meat was fully separated did he lift his head to look at her. \"You can never be sure with feelings. Maybe they will.\"","Gu Chacha gave a sweet smile. \"I hope my sister finds her true love too.\"","Han Mo raised his glass, toasting her from across the table. \"Here’s to her.\"","The smile on Gu Chacha’s face widened. \"Let’s toast to her together.\"","After the meal, she grabbed her small bag and said cheerfully to Han Mo, \"I’ve got an afternoon tea date with Fufu, so no need to drive me.\"","She had no intention of riding in that cheap car of his.","Han Mo nodded in agreement. \"Okay.\"","In the basement parking lot, he sat in his car for a long time before finally picking up his phone and opening the chat with He Huanhuan.","[How was the coffee?]","The reply came quickly: [Screw good! He made me split the bill! 38 bucks! Where am I supposed to get 38?]","A faint smile tugged at his lips as he pictured her hopping mad.","[You didn’t drink it?]","[I did, but I spat it back out. Then he tried to scam me, so I poured the cup of coffee into his mouth and charged him 38 for saliva fee! Haha!]","His eyes narrowed in annoyance as his fingers flew across the screen.","[Are you two still together?]","[Nope! The guy’s crazy! We were eating malatang just fine when he suddenly said I’m marriage material. I—]","Clearly, He Huanhuan needed to vent.","Large chunks of text came flooding in, detailing everything that had just happened to him.","Bony fingers tapped thoughtfully on the steering wheel, his gaze fixed on their chat log for a long time without moving.","Second Young Master Liang had taken a liking to her.","The Liang family, the Gu family, the eastern part of the city...","[Where are you? Need a ride home?]","[Yes!]","When the electric scooter stopped in front of the coffee shop, He Huanhuan was stunned.","She poked the young guy and asked, \"Are you heading to the coffee shop?\"","The kid nodded. \"I have a meeting with someone here.\"","\"Seriously? So I just wasted an hour walking for nothing?\"","He Huanhuan was speechless. A full hour of speed-walking was exhausting!","The young guy scratched his head apologetically. \"Where are you headed? If you’re not in a hurry...\"","Before he could finish, He Huanhuan’s phone lit up.","It was Han Mo.","Without a second thought, He Huanhuan started chatting with him.","After playing the sympathy card, Han Mo predictably offered to pick her up.","Cab fare saved!","If Liang Ye knew, he’d probably think she was even more suited to be his wife.","He Huanhuan grinned, closed her phone, and said goodbye to the young guy. \"Have a good date. You’re too handsome to be messing with people’s feelings.\"","With that, she turned and walked off, leaving him standing there alone.","\"It's not a date... it’s a job interview...\"","He wanted to say that after the interview, he could have given her a ride home...","At the designated intersection, the familiar car was already parked by the roadside.","Han Mo stood by the car door in a black suit, his long legs slightly bent, staring at the ground, lost in thought.","She walked over and snapped her fingers in front of him. \"What are you pondering?\"","Han Mo looked up and gave a faint smile. \"Nothing much. Just waiting for you.\"","He opened the car door to let He Huanhuan in.","As the car slowly drove toward the Gu family estate, Han Mo glanced at her from the corner of his eye.","She sat in silence, staring out the window.","She was usually so loud, rarely this quiet.","Even her multicolored hair seemed calmer.","\"What are you looking at?\"","He Huanhuan rested her chin on her hand. \"Why do rich people insist on living in such remote places?\"","A sudden laugh broke from him—only she would ask that.","His tense mood relaxed, and he smiled as he explained, \"The suburbs offer better privacy.\"","\"Downtown is too crowded and noisy. The suburbs are quieter, and the air is better.\"","\"Besides, the neighborhood we live in is full of influential people from the city...\"","\"Stop!\"","He Huanhuan yawned in boredom. All he was talking about was the class divide!","She wasn’t stupid—she got it.","The car pulled into the Gu family’s estate. She pushed open the door to leave but was stopped by Han Mo. \"The day after tomorrow is my father’s birthday party. Do you want to come with me?\"","\"Me?\"","He Huanhuan pointed at herself. \"Shouldn’t you be inviting Gu Chacha?\"","Hadn’t they just had dinner together today?","What was he playing at?","Han Mo didn’t answer. He just smiled at her. \"Would you like to come?\"","\"No.\"","He Huanhuan refused without hesitation. \"I feel like you’re up to something shady, so I’m not going.\"","Han Mo gazed at her silently, his jet-black eyes seeming to hold countless emotions—or perhaps nothing at all.","\"Why are you staring at me like that!\"","She slammed the car door roughly. \"I’ll think about it!\"","\"I’ll pick you up the day after tomorrow.\"","Before she could respond, the car sped off, leaving a fuming He Huanhuan punching the air in frustration.","\"Damn it! He just flirted with me!\"","This was the downfall of good looks!","Her phone chimed. She opened it to find Han Mo had transferred her some money.","One, two, three, four, five zeros.","[Why are you sending me money?]","[For a cab.]","She rolled her eyes, then her fingers danced across the screen: [So you’re not my driver anymore, huh?]","The chat showed \"typing...\" then stopped, then \"typing...\" again.","[Next time you go out, remember to call me.]","He Huanhuan’s lips curled triumphantly. Flirting, huh?","Two could play that game.","She pocketed the money and headed home in high spirits.","As expected, Old Mr. Gu was waiting in the living room. The moment he saw her, his eager eyes zeroed in. \"How was it? What did you think?\"","He Huanhuan waved dismissively. \"No good. He’s stingy as hell.\"","She plopped onto the couch and recounted Liang Ye’s insistence on splitting everything to the couple.","Jiang Yulan frowned after listening. \"Is this Second Young Master Liang a bit too cheap?\"","\"Cheap?\" Old Mr. Gu cut her off irritably. \"That’s being smart with money! That’s how a man should live!\"","...","With that attitude, he’d have made a perfect eunuch in the old days.","\"So what if they split things!\" Old Mr. Gu declared confidently. \"With Dad’s money, I’ll cover every penny you spend after you get married!\"","He vowed passionately, practically itching to marry her off to the Liang family.","He Huanhuan realized that the Liang family must be a big deal among the wealthy elite.","But that had nothing to do with her. She didn’t like Liang Ye, and she had no intention of marrying him."]},{"number":17,"title":"Chapter 17: Liang Zheng","paragraphs":["At the Liang residence, Liang Ye was also being interrogated.","His elder brother Liang Zheng gave him a cold look: \"Weren't you supposed to be meeting the young lady from the Gu family today? How come you only spent two amounts? And both under a hundred?\"","Liang Ye nodded happily: \"That's because we went to eat malatang! One serving for twenty yuan is enough to fill you up!\"","...","This hopeless fool!","Liang Zheng really wanted to crack open his head and see what was inside!","Was the family not giving him enough money, or was he, as the elder brother, mistreating him?","Liang Zheng asked him helplessly: \"Do you have a problem with me?\"","He truly didn't know what to do with this younger brother anymore.","Buying him a car? He didn't want it, said it was less cost-effective than taking a taxi.","Living in the family home? He refused, insisted on staying in a rundown old apartment in the city center, saying it was convenient and the property fees were cheap.","Now word outside was that he, the elder brother, was ruthless and couldn't tolerate his own brother.","He had nowhere to vent his grievances!","He seriously suspected that this younger brother was born by their parents just to torment him.","To his surprise, Liang Ye actually nodded: \"Yeah, a little. Brother, you're too wasteful. You're the only one home, why do you need so many lights on? Isn't that wasting electricity?\"","With that, he zipped around the house and turned off all the unnecessary lights.","Only the small desk lamp in front of his brother remained.","...","What a disaster!","The brother closed his eyes and took a deep breath.","Forget it, forget it. It wasn't like this was the first day. He'd just kick him out later.","\"Why did you take the girl to eat that stuff called malatang? Didn't I say all dating expenses should go on my card?\"","At this, Liang Ye's face instantly turned red: \"It was her idea to take me!\"","He even twisted his body a little unconsciously.","His brother couldn't help closing his eyes again. No need to ask—this blind date was definitely a bust.","If the girl had any interest in him at all, would she take him to eat malatang?","Twenty yuan per person wasn't even enough to cover an hour of parking.","Oh, right, his brother didn't even own a car.","His brother waved him off in resignation: \"Go on back. I'll find someone else to set you up with.\"","Given their family's standing, there would always be people willing to arrange introductions.","Unexpectedly, Liang Ye beamed and waved his hand: \"Brother, no need to refuse. I've already found my soulmate!\"","\"Who?\"","Liang Zheng couldn't help frowning. He didn't even dare imagine what kind of person his brother's soulmate might be.","\"The true daughter of the Gu family, He Huanhuan!\"","Speaking of He Huanhuan, a shy blush rose on his face: \"Brother, you have no idea how interesting she is. She doesn't even take a taxi when she goes out—she hitches rides. She's so good at saving money...\"","...","He might have known.","His brother raised a hand to stop his gushing: \"Get along well with the girl. Once you're in a stable relationship, bring her home to meet us.\"","He knew the Gu family. Their eldest son was quite capable, and several projects he had initiated were developing very well.","As long as there was one child who could handle things, the family could be maintained.","The Gu family had Gu Jingchen. As for them...","He looked at his brother twisting like a pretzel and sighed again.","He had heard that the Xu family's kid had started a business this year, burning through one or two million of the family's money, and it went under in less than six months.","At least his brother had no bad habits. Supporting him for a lifetime would be easy enough.","His tone softened a bit: \"There's a birthday banquet at the Han family the day after tomorrow. Remember to invite that girl to go with you.\"","Liang Ye beamed: \"Mm-hmm! She'll definitely come with me!\"","After having his brother's driver drop him off at his rundown apartment in the city center, the first thing he did when he got home was call He Huanhuan.","Beep beep beep, beep beep beep...","Beep beep, beep beep beep...","Beep, beep, beep...","She hung up faster each time. Liang Ye opened her contact photo and sent her a message: Want to go to Han family's birthday banquet together the day after tomorrow?","No reply.","He asked again. Still no answer.","Could it be that she hadn't seen it?","He thought for a moment and sent her a red envelope.","The red envelope was instantly accepted. Overjoyed, he said: He Huanhuan, come to the Han family's together the day after tomorrow!","A glaring exclamation mark suddenly appeared—he was dazed and confused. What happened?","At the Gu residence, He Huanhuan had just finished her shower when her phone rang.","She took one look. Liang Ye.","She immediately hung up. He called again, and she hung up again...","Until he sent a red envelope. Her hand betrayed her, and she tapped it open without thinking.","0.01 yuan.","...","Delete! She had to delete him right this instant!","She slept right through till morning. Half-awake, she went downstairs to eat.","Just as she stepped out of the elevator, she heard Old Mr. Gu's giddy laughter coming from the living room.","\"Hehehe... you two get along so well... Oh my, that's wonderful!\"","Fawning. Totally fawning.","Curious, she walked over and immediately spotted Liang Ye sitting on the sofa. Surrounding him were one, two, three, four, five people chatting with him...","Even Big Brother Gu Jingchen was there. Was this really necessary?","\"Huanhuan, look who's here!\"","When he saw her, Old Mr. Gu's face instantly bloomed into a doting smile: \"Little Ye's been thinking about you. Calling about Lan's birthday banquet would've been enough, but he came in person to invite you to the Han family's! Look, he even brought you a gift!\"","Him? Bringing a gift?","A 0.01-yuan gift?","As if reading her mind, Gu Chacha smiled sweetly: \"Sister, Second Young Master Liang was very thoughtful—he gave you a very special handmade gift~\"","That smile of hers clearly had ill intentions.","She stepped closer to take a look. Oh my, what a big heart!","And it was made from folded cardboard.","...","Even kindergarteners don't give out stuff like this anymore, do they?","\"You folded this?\"","Liang Ye nodded shyly: \"Mm-hmm! For you!\"","The big heart was forcefully shoved into her hands, and only then did she see the words printed on its tip.","\"Lunar New Year's Gift? Community Committee Donation?\"","Liang Ye grinned sheepishly: \"That's right. I work at the community committee. Got in on my own merit through the exam!\"","He edged closer to He Huanhuan: \"So you care about my job? Does that mean you can add me back?\"","...","He Huanhuan tossed the heart back at him: \"We're not happening. Stop thinking about me, sis.\"","\"Huanhuan!\"","\"Sister!\"","Before Liang Ye could even say anything, Old Mr. Gu and Gu Chacha both cried out at the same time!","Old Mr. Gu's face turned pale: \"Huanhuan! Aren't you fully awake yet? You and little Ye are such a perfect match!\"","Gu Chacha nodded in agreement: \"Exactly! Sister, Second Young Master Liang likes you so much! You can't let his true feelings go to waste!\"","He Huanhuan let out a mocking laugh: \"True feelings? What true feelings?\"","She glanced at Gu Chacha: \"Didn't you two go on a blind date the day before yesterday? Looked to me like he was pretty sincere with you too. Why don't you get together with him?\"","\"Sister!\"","Gu Chacha shrieked. She wouldn't stoop to Liang Ye's level!","\"Chacha.\"","Gu Jingchen suddenly called out to her, the displeasure in his eyes unmistakable: \"Marriage is no trivial matter. This is Huanhuan's own business. Don't butt in.\"","After scolding Gu Chacha, he turned to He Huanhuan and said gently: \"This family never raised you, so you owe us nothing. You are free.\"","He Huanhuan had been back in this house for less than a week, and she had no obligation to repay the family.","These words were spoken to He Huanhuan but were more a warning to Gu Chacha.","Don't try playing any little games—he wouldn't allow it.","\"Big Brother...\"","Gu Chacha was unwilling. She wanted to defend herself a little.","Then, out of the blue, He Huanhuan said, \"I agreed to go with Han Mo to his dad's birthday banquet. He'll pick me up the day after tomorrow.\"","\"What did you say???\""]},{"number":18,"title":"Chapter 18: Did you two kiss","paragraphs":["Gu Chacha looked at her in disbelief: \"Han Mo invited you?\"","He Huanhuan raised an eyebrow provocatively at her: \"Yeah, what's the problem?\"","\"How is that possible!\"","She had clearly talked it over with Han Mo yesterday!","What on earth was Han Mo doing?","Didn't he know what the best choice was?","Was he crazy?","Anxiously, she fumbled for her phone to confront Han Mo, but unexpectedly met her brother's gaze.","Gu Jingchen simply looked at her with unwavering certainty in his eyes: \"Don't cause trouble.\"","Was she causing trouble?","What had she even done?","She just wanted to live a comfortable life, didn't she?","If He Huanhuan hadn't suddenly stolen her identity, how would she have ended up like this?","Gritting her teeth, she sat back down, her eyes churning with intense hatred she couldn't suppress.","At tomorrow's birthday banquet, all the influential people in River City would be there.","With so many people watching the two of them attending the event together, where would she put her face?","Originally, she was supposed to be the one in the arranged marriage, but as soon as He Huanhuan appeared, it went to her.","What would everyone think of her then?","It would be obvious to everyone what her status in the Gu family really was!","In that case, who would even want to arrange a marriage with her?","At this thought, the hatred in her heart surged even more violently.","Tomorrow, no one was going to steal her spotlight!","He Huanhuan, you asked for this!","She fell silent, and Liang Ye finally seized the chance to ask: \"But aren't we dating? Shouldn't you come with me instead?\"","This question left He Huanhuan stunned. She pointed at herself, then at him: \"Us?\"","\"Dating? Since when?\"","She had already deleted him; when were they ever dating?","Her question turned Liang Ye's face bright red: \"Yesterday, we... we blended our spit, went strolling together, and even...\"","Before he could finish, Gu Jinghan leapt up in shock: \"Whoa! He Huanhuan, you kissed him? Your taste is that weird?\"","He had heard of this Liang Ye before—some seriously bizarre guy.","Whenever he went out to eat, he never paid the bill, even asking to split the cost down to each bite.","How could He Huanhuan kiss a guy like that?","How disgusting!","He Huanhuan jumped even higher: \"Damn it! Stop making up lies! I did not kiss you!\"","She wished she could smash his head in: \"Get it straight! All you did was drink my spilled coffee! I never kissed you!\"","Hearing this, Liang Ye turned even redder: \"You spat it out of your mouth, and I drank it. How is that different from kissing?\"","He looked all shy and embarrassed, making Gu Jinghan's skin crawl.","\"Man, you're disgusting! You drank the coffee my sister spat out? Doesn't that gross you out?\"","Liang Ye shot a bashful glance at He Huanhuan: \"She forced me to...\"","Gu Jinghan looked at her in disbelief: \"You're into role-playing games too?\"","Hadn't she been raised in the countryside? How did she get into such fancy stuff?","He Huanhuan: ...","Her good reputation!","Even eldest brother Gu Jingchen stared at her in surprise, so she had to tell them what had happened yesterday.","After explaining, she emphasized bitterly: \"I do not do that kind of thing!\"","And even if she did, it wouldn't be with Liang Ye!","She was attracted to good looks; she only liked handsome people.","This Liang Ye—not tall, not short, not fat, not thin, not ugly, not particularly short.","In short, he was just average.","He was nothing compared to Han Mo.","Han Mo was 1.88 meters tall, broad-shouldered and long-legged, with very striking facial features.","When it came to appearance alone, Han Mo suited her taste much better.","After hearing her story, even Old Mr. Gu fell silent.","So that's what \"blended their spit\" meant?","Was this young man from the Liang family reincarnated from a beggar in his past life?","And He Huanhuan...","Old Mr. Gu coughed awkwardly: \"If he wants thirty-eight, just give it to him. Our family's not short on that kind of money...\"","He Huanhuan shot him a glare: \"Give him nothing? Where would I get the money?\"","She only had twenty-three fifty on her. How could she pay?","Besides, she hadn't even ordered that coffee. Why should she pay for it?","Old Mr. Gu glanced at his eldest son, and Gu Jingchen immediately said: \"Eldest brother will open a supplementary card for you. Spend whatever you want.\"","\"No need.\"","He Huanhuan waved her phone: \"Han Mo transferred me some money. I've got cash to spend.\"","\"Han Mo?\"","Old Mr. Gu frowned. What was that kid Han Mo up to?","He wanted He Huanhuan to form a marriage alliance with the Liang family; didn't Han Mo know about that from yesterday?","Why was he giving Huanhuan money?","He Huanhuan had mentioned Han Mo several times this morning, which made Liang Ye a bit sulky.","Even though he hated spending money, if they were really dating, he'd still be willing to transfer some cash to his girlfriend.","And from what he'd read online, a transfer of 520 was already a lot in a relationship.","He knew about the Han family; what happened with Han Mo's father had already spread throughout the circle long ago.","Brother Gu Jingchen had a very low opinion of his family.","He said the Han family had little wealth to begin with, and once the two sons started fighting over it, the Han family would inevitably be in turmoil.","He had also heard that Han Mo wasn't valued much in the Han family.","If he wasn't valued, how much money could he possibly give He Huanhuan?","At most, 520.","That much, he could afford too.","So he asked confidently: \"How much did he give you?\"","He Huanhuan held up one finger, and he immediately felt smug.","Only a hundred, huh?","\"I'll transfer you two hundred...\"","\"A hundred thousand.\"","\"How much?!\"","His voice cracked in shock. Was Han Mo crazy?","They weren't even in a relationship yet, and he was already sending that much?","How much family fortune did he have to squander like this?","His hand trembled as he reached for his phone. A hundred thousand!","He would never, ever transfer that much, not even if he were killed!","His lips moved several times, but in the end, he gritted his teeth and managed an envious compliment: \"Well... he's pretty generous...\"","He Huanhuan glanced at him: \"Still more generous than thirty-eight, anyway.\"","\"But we strolled together...\"","Liang Ye looked wronged. Money was so vulgar. Wasn't strolling together much more romantic?","He Huanhuan was speechless: \"Who went strolling with you? You were the one who insisted on following me.\"","\"But we really did...\"","He was about to continue, but He Huanhuan was already shaking her fist: \"If you keep yapping, I'll beat you up!\"","He immediately shut his mouth.","After all those years of splitting everything equally, his survival skill depended entirely on knowing when to back off.","He Huanhuan glared at him with disdain: \"We're not going to happen, so stop thinking about me.\"","\"You—!\"","Liang Ye never expected it to end this way. He had searched online yesterday.","The internet said: if a girl deletes you, she's angry; give her a gift to cheer her up.","The internet had lied to him!","He turned and walked away in indignation, but after a few steps, he came back and took the big heart with him.","His love deserved someone who would cherish it!","Hmph!","\"What a child!\"","Old Mr. Gu gave He Huanhuan a helpless look, then got up and chased after him.","Even if things didn't work out, he couldn't afford to offend the Liang family!","\"Young Master! Wait...\"","When he got to the door, he found Liang Ye standing out there, waiting.","He didn't have a car and needed time for a ride-hailing order.","Old Mr. Gu promptly arranged: \"Old Tang, take the Young Master back!\"","\"Sure!\"","Old Tang immediately pulled the car around, which instantly lifted Liang Ye's spirits.","Another taxi fee saved!"]},{"number":19,"title":"Chapter 19: Impossible to Give Him","paragraphs":["Probably realizing that there really was no chance between the two of them, Liang Ye didn't bother her at all for the next two days.","Not only him, even Gu Chacha had calmed down a lot, stopping her sarcastic remarks.","It wasn't until the day of the birthday party, with the event check-in time set between six and seven in the evening, that things started moving.","At half past five, Han Mo's car pulled up exactly on time at her doorstep.","Wearing a suit of smoke-gray, standing in front of the little car He Huanhuan had picked out, he somehow made even that vehicle look far more upscale.","He Huanhuan was still sporting her flashy hairdo, but she did him the favor of wearing a short-tailed evening dress.","The hem just barely grazed the top of her thighs, leaving two long, slender legs exposed beneath the skirt.","The moment he saw her come out, something in Han Mo's gaze shifted.","In formal wear, she looked much more composed.","When their eyes met in the air, He Huanhuan clicked her heels over to Han Mo and shook her leg. \"Good-looking?\"","...","Guess that was just a false impression.","He nodded and complimented her, \"You look nice.\"","He Huanhuan grinned. \"Picked it especially for you.\"","Word had it that Han Mo and his brother didn't get along, so she chose a short gown.","Short skirt, perfect for throwing hands!","But to Han Mo's ears, her words meant something entirely different.","Today was his father's birthday, and she had accepted his invitation.","She also specifically picked out an outfit for him.","That was more than enough to show her stance.","His usually indifferent eyes flickered unsteadily, avoiding her straightforward gaze.","His large, sharp-knuckled hand tightened firmly on the car door handle as he opened it for her. \"Let's go.\"","He Huanhuan didn't notice anything off about him at all and plopped right into the seat.","Along the way, he still didn't say much.","In her eyes, he had always been a man of few words.","Less, and even less—either way, it was all the same to her.","It wasn't until the car approached the Han family estate that the last trace of hesitation in Han Mo's eyes finally vanished.","The car moved very slowly, yet with an unshakable certainty, it drove into the estate, rolling into full view of the crowd.","\"BYD? What broke-ass pauper is this?\"","\"How did security let this car in?\"","\"...\"","As the car slowly came to a halt amidst whispered murmurs, a sharply defined face emerged from the door, and the crowd was instantly stunned.","\"Han Mo driving such a cheap car?\"","\"Has the family finally had a complete falling-out?\"","\"Hey, there's someone in the passenger seat!\"","\"Holy crap, it's a mop that came to life!\"","\"...\"","The moment He Huanhuan poked her head out and got out of the car, everyone's eyes seemed to go collectively blind for a second.","\"Who's that? Never seen her before.\"","\"How come she came with Han Mo? Isn't he with Gu Chacha?\"","\"You don't know? Gu Chacha isn't really a daughter of the Gu family!\"","\"What?\"","\"...\"","Chatting away excitedly, the little scandal of the Gu family quickly spread through the crowd.","In the middle of all the chatter, the Gu family's car slowly pulled up right in front of them.","The door opened, and Gu Chacha stepped out in a floor-length ivory satin fishtail gown, a perfectly composed smile on her face.","She could feel it—everyone's eyes were on her.","Curiosity, scrutiny, schadenfreude...","All those gazes cut like knives, slicing mercilessly into her pride.","She didn't need to guess—she knew they had all found out about her real background.","She raised her chin higher and straightened her spine.","So what if there was no blood relation?","She was the child her parents had raised with their own hands. She was the Gu family's daughter!","No one was going to kick her out of this life. She wouldn't allow it.","She walked firmly beside Gu Chengye, speaking obediently to him: “Dad, do you know which piano master Uncle Han invited tonight?”","She had studied piano since childhood, and though her talent was average, she had been taught by renowned teachers for years, far surpassing those who only aimed for exam grades.","This was her honor, one that He Huanhuan could never take away.","Old Mr. Gu smiled and patted her hand: “If he hasn’t invited anyone, you can play a piece to celebrate Uncle Han’s birthday.”","“Dad~”","Gu Chacha chuckled coquettishly: “There are so many elders here tonight; I wouldn’t dare to show off!”","“How is it showing off? You’ve been learning piano since you were little...”","The two chatted and laughed as they entered, drawing glances that fiercely exchanged in the air around them.","[Looks like Gu Chacha hasn’t lost her favor, judging by Uncle Gu’s manner?]","[What’s the deal with Han Mo then?]","[Of course, he’s leaning toward his biological daughter! Blood ties are what matter most!]","Entering the first-floor hall, all the notable families in Jiang City had already arrived.","Han Changyong, with his younger son Han Xuan, greeted everyone with a beaming face.","When he saw Han Mo and He Huanhuan enter, Han Changyong’s expression flickered for a moment before quickly breaking into a smile: “Xiao Mo, who is this?”","Han Mo led He Huanhuan over and introduced her: “Dad, this is Uncle Gu’s daughter, He Huanhuan.”","He Huanhuan smiled sweetly: “Happy birthday, Uncle.”","Han Changyong warmly thanked her: “With your blessing, this uncle will surely be happy this year.”","Beside him, Han Xuan snorted: “Big Brother’s quick on the draw, huh. The Gu family’s daughter was just found, and he’s already sucking up?”","The sarcasm in his tone was thick, but Han Mo didn’t care at all.","He turned to He Huanhuan: “Tired? Want to rest a bit?”","He Huanhuan nodded: “Let’s rest—I don’t like listening to dogs bark.”","Han Xuan immediately grew furious: “Who are you calling a dog!”","He Huanhuan widened her eyes and looked at Han Mo: “What’s with all the barking again? So noisy!”","Han Mo raised his hand, lightly covering her ears: “Then ignore it.”","He gave his father a perfunctory nod: “I’ll take Huanhuan to rest over there.”","Han Changyong smiled and agreed: “Go ahead.”","Watching them leave, Han Xuan fumed: “Dad! She insulted me!”","“You deserved it!”","Han Changyong glared at his son: “Don’t you know what to say and what not to say?”","Unwilling to back down, Han Xuan retorted: “I didn’t say anything wrong.”","He was never afraid of his father, who had always favored him.","Han Changyong shot him an exasperated look: “That’s Gu Chengye’s daughter—are you clueless?”","Han Xuan curled his lip dismissively: “Isn’t he just trying to meddle in the East City development? As if he’s fit for it!”","His father had long said that everything in the family was meant for him.","It was only because he had been too young and his father’s health had been poor that he had let Han Mo take over as acting manager.","“Dad, look how greedy Han Mo is! You can’t keep him in the company anymore—he’ll steal our family business!”","Han Changyong glanced at him: “If I pull him out, who takes over? You?”","“Me! I’m up for it! I’m not useless!”","He leaned on Han Changyong, pleading with puppy-like persistence: “Dad, let me do it! I swear I’ll do a better job than Han Mo! Really!”","He begged repeatedly, but Han Changyong stood firm and refused.","It wasn’t that he favored Han Mo—he knew his own children well enough.","Han Xuan was impulsive and reckless—there was no way he’d hand over the company to him.","The moment he didn’t answer, Han Xuan immediately called out, “You’re not actually thinking of handing the company over to Han Mo, are you?”","Han Changyong sighed. “Can’t you be a little more composed?”","If he were even slightly reliable, would Han Mo have ever gotten involved in the company’s affairs?","But seeing how frantic Han Xuan was, Han Changyong couldn’t help but soften. “Don’t worry. The East City project won’t be given to him.”","He knew what Han Mo was after. Letting him into the company was one thing—getting involved in the East City project was another.","This family business was never going to end up in his hands."]},{"number":20,"title":"Chapter 20: Ballache","paragraphs":["In the side hall, Han Mo stood quietly by the window, watching the commotion outside.","He Huanhuan couldn’t quite figure him out anymore.","At first, she knew his flattery was for the East City project.","He wanted a voice within the Han Group.","When she was set up on a blind date with Liang Ye, he was all for it.","She knew he was just like Gu Chacha, hoping she’d latch onto the Liang family so they could bask in the reflected glory.","But when she ignored Liang Ye, he didn’t complain. Instead, he came back to be nice to her.","He even invited her to join him at his father’s birthday banquet.","What was he after?","She couldn’t wrap her head around it.","His father didn’t like him, and his younger brother had no respect for him.","And yet he kept at it—wasn’t his ambition obvious?","Would his father even let him stay in the company?","She stared boldly at the man by the window, until he turned and looked at her. “Why are you staring at me?”","He Huanhuan pouted. “I can’t figure you out.”","The whole estate was ablaze with lights, yet the glow only reached him from the front.","He stood by the curtain, half-hidden in the dark, and asked quietly, “What don’t you understand?”","He Huanhuan wasn’t one for beating around the bush. She stood up and asked directly, “Why did you invite me tonight? You know what Old Gu wants. Why provoke him? Why provoke your dad? You’re really weird.”","She wasn’t stupid. Han Mo’s actions were too contradictory.","He chuckled softly. “Weird? Maybe.”","Suddenly, he stepped forward, stepping into the dazzling light. “Are you afraid?”","He Huanhuan stared right back at him. “Afraid of what?”","“That I might hurt you.”","“Ha!”","He Huanhuan pointed at herself. “Hurt me? How? By throwing money at me?”","She was alone, dead broke—what harm could come to her?","That ten-thousand-yuan balance in her account was from him!","A smile tugged at Han Mo’s lips. “Maybe I really will throw money at you.”","He Huanhuan spread her arms wide. “Then you’d better hit me hard enough to kill me. If you don’t, I won’t accept it.”","“Alright.”","He nodded seriously, then pulled open the door. “Rest here. I’ll go out and take a look.”","After all, it was the Han family’s banquet. As Han Changyong’s eldest son, he had to make the rounds and socialize on his behalf.","The door closed gently, leaving the room in silence.","He Huanhuan lay back on the couch, listening to the noise outside.","She didn’t feel like going out. Forced smiles and small talk bored her to death.","She always believed she’d return to her modern world someday. All this splendor and luxury in the book? Just a fleeting dream.","Fun to play around with, but nothing to take seriously.","She wasn’t the real heiress of the Gu family, and she didn’t need to fit into this high society.","She was He Huanhuan, a penniless street girl.","In her own world, she was the scrappy kid waiting to turn eighteen so she could work off her debts.","She lay on the couch, legs crossed, enjoying a freedom that wasn’t really hers.","Just treat it like a sweet dream.","In that dream, a tall, handsome guy with long legs kept transferring her money, taking her out for spicy hot pot to cheer her up.","If Qi Meili and the others knew, they’d be green with envy!","She hummed a little tune, her thoughts drifting lazily.","She never noticed the door creak open or the slinking shadow creep inside.","The figure quietly locked the door behind him, then hunched over and edged forward.","The flickering light from the hall cast flashes across the room, lighting his way as he crept closer to the couch.","“Bang!”","In the dark, his foot caught on a trash can with a jarring clatter.","“Who’s there?”","He Huanhuan shot up, demanding.","“Don’t ask!”","The shadow lunged at her!","“Ahhh!!!”","A shrill scream tore through the room—cut short after just half a second, swallowed by the air.","The hall was loud and chaotic, no one noticed the brief cry.","“Click.”","The room’s light flicked on, casting a warm yellow glow over a pitiful, disheveled face.","He Huanhuan raised an eyebrow at the man at her feet. “Han Xuan?”","“Wah... it’s me...” Han Xuan lay at her feet, whimpering pitifully. “It hurts...”","She pressed her high heel down harder. “What were you trying to do, jumping at me like that?”","“Ahhh!!!” Han Xuan curled up in agony. “I wanted—I wanted to seduce you! If I could hook you and then land the East City project, I could kick Han Mo out of the company!”","The dim light flickered. He Huanhuan’s colorful hair swooped down as she stared coldly. “Seduce me? Or rape me?”","What decent man lunges at a girl like some perv, trying to pin her down?","If she hadn’t reacted fast, he would’ve kissed her!","Han Xuan forced a fawning smile. “Isn’t it... isn’t it kind of the same thing?”","If he could sleep with her, she’d have to obey him, right?","A girl raised in the countryside—who else would have her?","Did she really think Han Mo would want someone with a flashy dye job?","He just wanted the East City project, didn’t he?","If he’d succeeded in screwing her just now, see if Han Mo would still bother with her!","Inside, he was brimming with arrogance, but on the surface, he played the coward. “I’m sorry, I really messed up! I lost my head! Let me go...”","He Huanhuan lifted her heel slightly, and Han Xuan’s lips curled up secretly.","Typical country girl, so gullible.","A little sweet talk, and she’s convinced.","He scrambled to get up, not noticing she lowered the heel again, aiming perfectly for his thigh.","“Ahhhh!!! My balls!!!”","The scream was bloodcurdling. It cut through the room and spread across the whole hall.","“What’s that sound? What’s wrong with his eggs?”","“The cake, maybe? Isn’t it Old Han’s birthday today?”","“What happened to the cake? Why’s he screaming like that?”","“Was it smashed?”","“...”","The crowd buzzed with curiosity, but no one dared move in.","A few seconds later, another agonized howl rang out: “Help!!!.”","“That voice sounds like...”","“Isn’t that Second Young Master Han?”","Before anyone could react, Han Mo’s aura dropped to freezing. He spun around without hesitation, charging toward the room.","What was Han Xuan doing in there?","What did he plan to do to He Huanhuan?","With him leading the way, the nosy crowd followed eagerly.","With screams like that, who wouldn’t want to see what was happening?","At the door, Han Mo grabbed the handle anxiously, only to find it locked from inside.","His face darkened. He lifted his leg and kicked the door hard.","“Bang!”","The door splintered open. He rushed in, followed by dozens of curious eyes.","On the floor of the room, Han Xuan clutched his groin, drenched in cold sweat. “Take me to the hospital! Take me to the hospital! She kicked my balls! It hurts!”"]},{"number":21,"title":"Chapter 21: Protect Her","paragraphs":["Han Mo dashed forward in front of He Huanhuan, scrutinizing her intently, his expression filled with tension: \"Why is Han Xuan here? Did he hurt you?\"","He Huanhuan clapped her hands confidently: \"With him? Hurting me?\"","These tough girls, when they fought, were brutally dirty.","Men kicked, women clawed.","Aiming for wherever hurt the most.","Han Xuan’s few moves were nothing special.","On the ground, Han Xuan was still wailing in agony: \"Take me to the hospital! It hurts so much!\"","At the doorway, Han Yongchang finally heard the commotion and rushed over.","The moment he entered, he heard his son’s cries of pain, scaring him into hurrying inside: \"Xiaoxuan, what’s wrong? What happened to you?\"","\"Dad!\"","With his backer finally here, Han Xuan poured out his grievances with a full heart: \"He Huanhuan kicked me down there! Get her! Get her!\"","His emotions got the better of him, and he accidentally strained that area again, finally overwhelmed by the pain. He rolled his eyes and passed out.","\"Someone! Take the Second Young Master to the hospital!\"","A chaotic group of people rushed in and carried Han Xuan out.","That left Han Yongchang, his face full of fury, and the guests, waiting to enjoy the drama.","Han Yongchang stood up with a grim face and looked at He Huanhuan: \"Girl, you need to explain yourself to me.\"","Han Mo’s face turned colder. He stepped forward, blocking He Huanhuan: \"Shouldn’t Han Xuan be the one to explain? Why was he in that room? What was he trying to do? He...\"","\"Han Mo!\"","Han Yongchang cut him off sharply, barely containing his rage: \"That’s your brother!\"","\"Is it?\"","Han Mo sneered: \"I didn’t know my mother had two sons.\"","\"Han Mo!\"","Han Changyong could no longer hold back his anger: \"Are you asking for trouble?\"","The company’s equity was all in his hands!","Had this boy lost his mind?","Was he not afraid of being kicked out of the company?","His eyes were full of threat, but he was shocked to find no trace of fear on Han Mo’s face.","He just looked at him coldly, as if this man wasn’t his father.","As if they were two completely unrelated people.","His heart suddenly skipped a beat. He felt like things were slipping out of his control.","He suddenly couldn’t understand this son of his.","He knew Han Mo held a grudge against him, and he had always known.","He and Chen Meixin had started as a young couple, supporting each other through it all. They opened a shop, built a business, and grew it bigger and bigger, until they finally made it into the circle of the rich in River City.","Everything was good—until he went and had a child with someone else.","That crushed Chen Meixin, making her sick with grief, and she died young.","How could Han Mo not hate him?","But he had his own reasons. Once the business took off, he wasn’t the same man he used to be.","Chen Meixin didn’t see it that way. She thought that since they had climbed from poverty to wealth together, they were still the closest partners.","She was domineering and blind, with no idea what he truly needed.","He needed a woman’s admiration, not to be screamed at at home.","When they were young and poor, it was tolerable. But now he was the chairman of a public company. Why should he still take the abuse?","If she wouldn’t pamper him, someone else naturally would.","He never intended to drive her to her death, nor did he plan to bring that other woman and child into the home.","It was she who couldn’t handle the truth. That wasn’t his fault.","But that ungrateful son blamed him for everything, shifting all that hatred onto him.","So why bother playing the loving father? He wasn’t the only son he had.","All those shameful memories of poverty, of groveling, of being some man’s dog—he could just throw them away.","Father and son stood their ground, cold and stiff.","Han Yongchang would never back down. He was the superior, the father.","If he yielded, where would his dignity be?","He just couldn’t figure out why that damn boy had suddenly become so stubborn.","Hadn’t Han Mo always wanted to get his hands on Chen Meixin’s shares?","What had changed all of a sudden?","That was not a good sign.","He knew how much his son valued his mother. He didn’t believe he would throw away all his past efforts for a girl he had known for only a few days.","But the evidence was right in front of him. Han Mo was firmly shielding He Huanhuan, refusing to let him question her.","His eyes were mocking: \"Dad, are you afraid to ask Han Xuan?\"","\"Don’t you dare slander your brother!\"","In the silent room, the father and son were at daggers drawn.","The onlookers at the doorway didn’t utter a word. Hell, who would break into such a gripping scene?","What if they interrupted and the fight stopped halfway?","\"I wanted... I wanted to seduce you! If I could... the East City project... get Han Mo kicked out of the company...\"","\"Seduce me? Or rape me?\"","\"Isn’t that... isn’t that basically the same thing?\"","In the quiet room, a conversation rang out with an electronic voice overlay. The female voice was clearly He Huanhuan’s, and the male voice was unmistakably that of the recently carried-off Han Xuan.","He Huanhuan pushed Han Mo aside, her face full of disgust: \"What are you doing? You’ve wasted half my time!\"","Han Mo: \"... Where did you get that recording?\"","He Huanhuan raised her phone: \"He lunged at me first, so of course I had to keep evidence. I’m not stupid.\"","That ugly loser had bad intentions. If she was going to beat him up, she had to record his dirt first.","Otherwise, how would she prove her actions were justified?","Without that alertness, she’d have been sent to juvenile detention countless times by now.","The veteran survives a hundred battles—her trick was always hitting the record button first!","She lifted her face to look at Han Mo, glowing with triumph, begging for praise. Her rainbow-colored hair made her look wild and bold, and Han Mo’s gaze softened: \"You’re really amazing.\"","Even without him, she could take care of herself.","Truly amazing.","He Huanhuan put her hands on her hips: \"Damn right!\"","In the recording, Han Xuan’s voice was loud and clear. Every word was heard by everyone present.","Old Mr. Gu immediately stood up from behind the crowd. Just now, it was his daughter who had kicked someone’s son, and he had to keep a low profile. But now, it was Old Han’s son who had tried to do wrong by her. He had to stand up for his daughter.","He quickly pushed the people in front of him aside and joined the fray: \"Old Han, I think you need to give me an answer about this.\"","Outside the crowd, Gu Chacha bit her lip in frustration.","This He Huanhuan loved stealing the spotlight so much!","She hadn’t even started her own act yet, and this girl had already caused such a mess. How could the rest of her plan play out?","But by now, the situation was beyond her control.","All she could do was stand aside and watch how things unfolded.","Song Zhuo stood beside her, patting her hand soothingly: \"Don’t worry. I’ll make sure you get your revenge.\"","She nodded silently and turned her gaze back to the scene.","Inside the room, Old Mr. Gu stared grimly at Han Yongchang: \"Old Han, Huanhuan has suffered a lot outside before coming back to me. We’re old friends of years. Is this how you treat her?\"","\"Oh, Old Gu, I really had no idea about this...\"","The moment Old Mr. Gu stepped forward, Han Yongchang’s momentum immediately weakened.","He was still hoping for a piece of the East City pie. This was a critical moment—how could he afford to offend him?","The man who had once climbed the ladder by being another man’s dog knew exactly how to grovel when he needed to.","After apologizing to Old Mr. Gu, he immediately walked quickly over to He Huanhuan, bent down, and leaned in close to her. \"Huanhuan, my dear niece, your uncle really has no idea what's going on with Xiaoxuan. Give me some time, and I promise I'll get to the bottom of this for you!\""]},{"number":22,"title":"Chapter 22: Changing Surname","paragraphs":["His attitude was extremely sincere. He Huanhuan glanced at Han Mo, then at Old Mr. Gu.","Neither of them showed any reaction.","Damn it!","Couldn't they at least give her a hint?","In her social circle, fights only involved the individuals themselves—parents never butted in.","Han Xuan had tried to take advantage of her, and she had taught him a harsh lesson.","As far as she was concerned, that matter was settled.","But these two old men had to keep nagging, and now they were nagging without making things clear.","Was she supposed to agree or not?","Her gaze darted around the room and accidentally collided with a cold face.","Her cheap older brother, Gu Jingchen, stood by the door and silently nodded at her.","She immediately said to Han Changyong, \"Fine! Arrange it however you want!\"","Han Changyong let out a heavy sigh of relief. \"Thank you, Little Huanhuan. Your uncle appreciates your kindness.\"","Today, he had invited every notable family in the city.","If Gu Chengye insisted on making things difficult for him, he would lose a lot of face.","He quickly patted He Huanhuan and smiled as he led her out. \"Do you prefer Chinese or Western food? I've prepared both Huaiyang cuisine and French cuisine. The chefs are nationally renowned, so we have whatever you want.\"","Since no major scene had erupted, the onlookers were a bit disappointed.","But no one was foolish enough to press the matter.","Everyone present had their own conflicts of interest.","If there was excitement, they watched; if not, they were all one big happy family again.","Except for Song Zhuo.","The Song family had deep roots, and Song Zhuo was their only daughter—a pampered and genuine noble young lady.","She held a glass of red wine, stepped forward, and blocked He Huanhuan's path. \"Gu Huanhuan?\"","He Huanhuan glanced at her. \"My name is He Huanhuan.\"","Song Zhuo sneered. \"Since you've been recognized by the Gu family, why haven't you changed your surname to Gu? Or do you hold a grudge? Is that why you won't change it?\"","He Huanhuan rolled her eyes at her. \"What the hell does it have to do with you?\"","\"Big Sister, you can't speak to Fufu like that.\"","Gu Chacha immediately stepped in to stop He Huanhuan's cursing. \"Fufu says all this for our family's sake. She means well...\"","He Huanhuan looked at Gu Chacha defiantly. \"So what? Still none of her damn business.\"","\"Big Sister!\"","Gu Chacha put on a very wronged expression. \"How can you be like this?\"","She looked pitiful enough, but her voice was loud, instantly drawing everyone's attention.","\"Big Sister, Fufu only cares about us. How can you be so harsh with her?\"","She blinked, and her eyes instantly turned red.","To be fair, with her talent for crying on the spot, she could snag a decent role even in the entertainment industry.","Curious gazes quickly fixed on He Huanhuan. Ah, she was stirring up trouble again tonight!","\"What's going on? What now?\"","Old Mr. Gu had just walked away with Han Changyong to have a proper talk about sincerity.","Before they could even start, a commotion broke out.","Han Changyong seized the opportunity to steer Old Mr. Gu over. He couldn't let Gu Chengye hold the upper hand!","Taking a closer look, well, well—Gu Chengye's two daughters were having a row.","Han Changyong was instantly delighted. Guess everyone has their own family troubles!","And he had been mocked for his!","Old Mr. Gu had no choice but to step forward and ask Gu Chacha, \"Chacha, what's this about?\"","\"Dad...\"","Gu Chacha's eyes grew even redder, tears threatening to fall.","It was He Huanhuan who had spoken rudely, so why was he questioning her first?","Dad had never treated her like this before!","\"Uncle, He Huanhuan was the one who cursed at me. Why are you asking Chacha?\"","Song Zhuo stood up unhappily, confronting Old Mr. Gu.","As soon as she spoke, Old Mr. Gu's tone softened. \"Huanhuan cursed at you? Impossible. She doesn't even know you, right?\"","Song Zhuo sneered. \"I was just curious why she hasn't changed her surname to Gu since she was found. Or are you saying He Huanhuan doesn't accept the Gu family from the bottom of her heart? That's why she refuses?\"","At her words, Old Mr. Gu's attention shifted.","\"That's right! Huanhuan has been back for so long, and Dad never thought about having you change your surname to Gu.\"","Old Mr. Gu looked at He Huanhuan considerately. \"How about this: Dad will take you to change it tomorrow? What do you think?\"","\"Not happening.\"","He Huanhuan refused flatly, expressionless. \"My name is He Huanhuan, and I'm not changing it.\"","Song Zhuo's eyes were full of mockery. \"Ha! So you're not sincere at all.\"","He Huanhuan flipped her off. \"None of your damn business. You talk too much.\"","Song Zhuo curled her lips into a smile. \"You're Chacha's sister, so naturally I care about you.\"","\"Is it really care?\"","Han Mo walked over, his cold face fixed on Song Zhuo. \"You know very well whether it's care or harassment.\"","These petty tricks were obvious to anyone with eyes.","Song Zhuo smiled and nodded. \"So what if it is? Can't I ask?\"","Han Mo's gaze turned icy. \"The Gu family's matters are none of your business. I think...\"","\"And they are your business?\"","Song Zhuo's tone dripped with sarcasm. \"Han Mo, weren't you licking Chacha's boots before? Don't tell me—now that Gu Huanhuan's back, you've switched to licking hers? You're such a loyal dog, guarding your new master...\"","Before she could finish her vicious mockery, a figure suddenly darted out from behind Han Mo, moving so fast she could barely see it.","\"Slap!\"","A loud, forceful slap landed on her face, so hard it sent her tumbling to the ground!","He Huanhuan's face was full of aggression. \"I told you, my name is He Huanhuan! The hell is 'Gu Huanhuan'!\"","Song Zhuo went mad. \"He Huanhuan! How dare you hit me!\"","He Huanhuan shook her leg. \"I hit you, so what? Want to start a fight with me? Bring it on!\"","Her provocation was extreme, and the burning sting on her cheek pushed Song Zhuo's rationality out the window.","Gu Chacha crouched down worriedly, calling out, \"Fufu...\"","But a flicker of barely suppressed excitement flashed in her eyes.","If He Huanhuan had hit Song Zhuo, this would get interesting!","The Song family wasn't like the Han family—they weren't easily brushed off.","Song Zhuo was the apple of her parents' eye.","Just wait until Uncle and Aunt found out. Hmph...","She carefully helped Song Zhuo up and said softly, \"Fufu, are you okay?\"","Rage had completely burnt away all of Song Zhuo's restraint. She shoved Gu Chacha aside and lunged at He Huanhuan like a madwoman. \"You hit me! I'll kill you!!\"","\"Fufu!\"","Gu Chacha cried out in alarm, but her hands didn't exert any strength, letting Song Zhuo easily slip past her.","Because they were standing so close, Song Zhuo reached He Huanhuan in just two steps!","Then He Huanhuan pinned her to the ground with one hand!","He Huanhuan let out a cold laugh, straddling her body.","Her palm smacked heavily onto Song Zhuo's head as He Huanhuan yelled arrogantly, \"You want to hit me?\"","\"Let me go!\"","Song Zhuo was furious and struggled wildly, but couldn't escape at all.","He Huanhuan, though she looked thin and weak, had freakish strength.","She had no trouble keeping her pinned down.","\"Slap!\"","Another slap landed on Song Zhuo's head. He Huanhuan looked at her like she was an idiot.","\"Do I even know you? Why are you showing off here? Someone's using you as a pawn, and you're blazing away, huh? You dumbass.\"","Song Zhuo blushed and glared at her. \"Stop trying to drive a wedge between Chacha and me! I just don’t like you, got a problem with that?\"","She and Gu Chacha had grown up together and knew each other very well.","Even though Gu Chacha could be a bit of a schemer, they were still best friends.","She genuinely cared about her.","\"Oh, really?\"","He Huanhuan leaned down and whispered in her ear, \"If she really cared about you, she would’ve charged in and hit me by now, instead of letting me pin you down and beat you up. Idiot.\"","\"Shut up!\"","Song Zhuo’s heart couldn’t help but waver. Chacha was just timid—she wasn’t that bad!"]},{"number":23,"title":"Chapter 23: Sisterhood","paragraphs":["She and Chacha are the best of friends. Although sometimes they have small disagreements and sometimes they each have their own little thoughts.","But they are the best of friends.","The best.","Thinking this in her heart, out of the corner of her eye she caught sight of Gu Chacha rushing towards her.","She knew it! They were the best of friends!","\"Big Sister, how could you hit Fufu? You'll ruin our family!\"","Gu Chacha shrieked, but stopped a step away and didn't come any closer.","In an instant, Song Zhuo's heart sank. As friends for so many years, how could she not understand what Gu Chacha meant by that sentence.","She was targeting He Huanhuan, trying to make He Huanhuan be condemned by everyone.","This circle of theirs was very small, and tonight was He Huanhuan's first official appearance.","If her image was ruined right away, it would be even more difficult for her to fit in later.","Was that what Chacha was planning?","So that's why she just loudly scolded but didn't come to help at all.","She wasn't worried that she would be hurt by He Huanhuan because she had the Song family backing her up.","Even if He Huanhuan was reckless, others wouldn't let He Huanhuan really hurt her.","She knew that's definitely what Chacha was thinking, but she couldn't help feeling disappointed.","She was standing up for her, but how could she be so rational?","Didn't she care about her at all?","Even if she wouldn't suffer serious injuries, getting slapped still hurt!","Boundless grievance welled up in her heart, but Gu Chacha didn't notice.","She panicked and shouted at Old Mr. Gu, \"Dad! Hurry up and stop Big Sister!\"","Only then did Old Mr. Gu react. He rushed forward in a hurry, trying to stop He Huanhuan.","Unexpectedly, Han Mo suddenly stepped aside and blocked him, saying, \"Uncle, be careful.\"","Han Mo grabbed him tightly, making him unable to move an inch.","He could only sternly stop He Huanhuan, \"Huanhuan! Don't be naughty!\"","He Huanhuan pinched Song Zhuo's face and brought her lips close to her ear, saying, \"Look, no one is helping you. Your popularity is not that good.\"","\"You!\"","Those words hit the very core of Song Zhuo's heart. Her eyes instantly turned red, and she glared at He Huanhuan angrily, \"And how good are you? Do you think Han Mo is helping you for nothing? He's still doing it for...\"","\"The project in the East City!\"","He Huanhuan laughed shamelessly, \"Of course I know, but I don't need his help either. Isn't it obvious who's getting beaten here?\"","She kicked her foot, and the tip of her shoe rudely poked Song Zhuo's buttocks, \"Fufu? Is getting beaten fun?\"","In such a flippant tone, it made Song Zhuo's eyes even redder, \"Let me go! You...\"","She was so ashamed and angry that she was about to struggle wildly when she suddenly found that the restraint on her body disappeared.","He Huanhuan jumped up and casually clapped her hands, \"I'm not being naughty. She jumped up to hit me.\"","After saying that, she smiled and reached out her hand to Song Zhuo, \"Not getting up?\"","Her tone was quite natural, as if they were old friends who had known each other for a long time.","Song Zhuo was stunned. Before her mind could react, her hand had already reached out.","A strong force pulled her up, and many people surrounded them instantly.","Gu Chacha was the first one. Looking at her, her eyes were full of worry, \"Fufu, how are you? Did Big Sister hurt you? Are you feeling uncomfortable anywhere?\"","She leaned over and winked at Song Zhuo, signaling her to exaggerate the injury.","But she found that Song Zhuo was standing there blankly and didn't notice her at all.","\"Fufu!\"","\"Ah?\"","Song Zhuo came back to her senses and looked at her blankly, \"Chacha, what's wrong?\"","Gu Chacha asked again, \"Are you feeling uncomfortable anywhere in your body? Did Big Sister hurt you?\"","Song Zhuo replied blankly, \"No, I'm fine...\"","\"That's good, that's good...\"","Cold sweat almost broke out on Old Mr. Gu's forehead. He quickly broke free from Han Mo's grasp and walked to the two of them. He apologized sincerely, \"Fufu, I'm sorry. Huanhuan just came back not long ago and doesn't know any better...\"","\"It doesn't matter...\"","\"Fufu!\"","Gu Chacha suddenly interrupted Song Zhuo. She stared at Song Zhuo with wide eyes.","This wasn't what they had planned!","Why did she suddenly change her mind?","But Song Zhuo quietly avoided her gaze. For some reason, it was as if she suddenly saw Gu Chacha clearly.","All her little thoughts and tricks.","Suddenly they seemed so obvious and childish.","She didn't want to follow her arrangements anymore.","He Huanhuan hadn't offended her. Why did she have to target her?","She was the only daughter of the Song family!","Gu Chacha noticed that her expression was different, and her tone instantly softened.","She shook Song Zhuo's arm and called her softly, \"Fufu...\"","You promised to help me, right?","Wasn't it?","Unexpectedly, Song Zhuo suddenly turned to look at her, \"Chacha, why didn't you come to help me just now?\"","The sudden question caught Gu Chacha off guard. A flash of guilt flashed across her face, and she nervously asked back, \"Fufu, why do you suddenly ask this?\"","Song Zhuo stared at her intently, \"Aren't you afraid that I'll be hurt by her?\"","Gu Chacha finally realized something was wrong. She had been too obvious just now, and Fufu was unhappy.","She affectionately wrapped her arm around Song Zhuo's and coquettishly said, \"How could I not be worried about you? Don't worry. In public, she won't dare to do anything to you.\"","What an obvious perfunctory. How come she hadn't noticed it before.","One by one, past events echoed in her mind. She stood up for Chacha, then got bullied, and her family would go to the other party...","Gradually, she had no friends left.","Only Chacha was still willing to play with her, so she stood up for Chacha even more.","She used to be so stupid. How could she be so stupid?","How could she have been used by her for so long without even noticing?","She glanced at the person beside her. He Huanhuan, with a multi - colored hairstyle, was standing there looking nonchalant.","It was her.","She had whispered something in her ear just now, and suddenly her mind became clear.","What was so different about He Huanhuan?","She silently lowered her eyes and didn't echo Gu Chacha's words.","\"Fufu...\"","Gu Chacha was unwilling. She was just one step away. As long as Song Zhuo insisted that He Huanhuan had hurt her.","According to Uncle and Aunt's temper, Dad wouldn't be able to protect He Huanhuan.","But why did Fufu suddenly stop talking?","In the past, as long as she asked, Fufu would always agree to her!","She glared at He Huanhuan hatefully. Consider herself lucky.","Since Song Zhuo didn't care, this matter was easily brushed aside.","To prevent any more incidents, Han Changyong quickly ordered the kitchen to serve the dishes.","Eat quickly and go home quickly after eating.","He still had to go to the hospital to see Xiaoxuan.","The dinner went smoothly. Everyone wasn't here just for the meal.","After exchanging greetings, they just casually ate a few mouthfuls and that was it.","Only He Huanhuan was holding a plate and eating very seriously.","Gu Chacha wanted to find an opportunity to laugh at her, but she almost blinked her eyes out, and Fufu didn't cooperate with her at all.","Until Song Zhuo picked up a small piece of cake for He Huanhuan and smiled at her embarrassedly, \"This is very delicious. You can try it.\"","Gu Chacha finally realized something was wrong. Was Fufu trying to curry favor with He Huanhuan?","Why?","Was she crazy?"]},{"number":24,"title":"Chapter 24: Be Careful, Gu Chacha","paragraphs":["Gu Chacha panicked. Over the years, Song Zhuo had always treated her well.","The reason she could throw her weight around in their social circle was entirely because of Song Zhuo’s family background.","Her father Gu’s money alone wouldn’t have been enough to make those heiresses treat her so carefully.","She hurried forward and grabbed Song Zhuo’s arm: “Fufu, what are you talking about with your sister?”","Song Zhuo pulled her arm back stiffly: “I just thought the cake was good, so I recommended it to Huanhuan.”","“Huanhuan?”","Gu Chacha caught the change in her address immediately. Was she sick or something?","Hadn’t He Huanhuan just slapped her? Not only was she not angry, she was calling her Huanhuan?","Was she suffering from Stockholm syndrome?","To her surprise, Song Zhuo glanced cautiously at He Huanhuan: “May I call you that?”","Her eyes were full of anxiety, as if she was afraid He Huanhuan would refuse.","Gu Chacha nearly fainted. What was she being so nervous about?","How was He Huanhuan worthy?","“Fufu, weren’t you just saying earlier that I should change my surname to Gu? So why now...”","She deliberately brought up their earlier conflict, hoping to reignite the tension.","But Song Zhuo frowned at her instead: “Chacha, I wasn’t thinking clearly earlier. One’s surname is a personal choice. Huanhuan grew up outside the Gu family; if she doesn’t want to be a Gu, that’s her right.”","She sized up Gu Chacha: “Speaking of which, Chacha, you’re not actually a Gu by blood. Shouldn’t you consider changing your surname too? He Chacha?”","“Song Zhuo! Have you lost your mind?”","Gu Chacha shrieked: “I am the daughter of the Gu family! I won’t be a He! Why are you bullying me?”","Song Zhuo shrugged indifferently: “I was just making a casual remark. Why are you so upset?”","Gu Chacha’s eyes instantly reddened: “Fufu...”","Before she could play the victim, Song Zhuo stepped back, putting distance between them: “You’d better call me Song Zhuo. ‘Fufu’ is what my family calls me.”","Hearing this, Gu Chacha was completely shaken. She knew something was wrong. In all her life, Song Zhuo had never been this cold to her.","They had fought before, but Song Zhuo had never told her not to use her nickname.","It was a sign of closeness, and now she was taking it back.","She didn’t want to be friends anymore.","But why? She hadn’t done anything!","With red-rimmed eyes, she asked Song Zhuo: “Why? Just because I’m not a real Gu daughter? Are you going to hang out with He Huanhuan now and stop being friends with me?”","She stared pitifully at Song Zhuo, who felt her heart drop suddenly. That confused, overwhelming feeling was creeping in again.","She bit her lower lip and darted over to He Huanhuan’s side.","The gnawing feeling vanished instantly.","She found she could once again face Gu Chacha’s tears.","A thin layer of cold sweat broke out on her back. She felt as if she had just been under some sort of spell.","Her rational mind had been slowly disappearing.","It was terrifying.","She thought about how obedient she had been before—it was as if she’d been bewitched.","She never thought for herself.","Her parents had told her that Gu Chacha had ulterior motives and warned her not to be friends with her.","But she had acted like she hadn’t heard, rushing over the moment Gu Chacha called.","She rubbed her arms involuntarily and said to Gu Chacha: “That’s right. I don’t want to be friends with you anymore. Let’s just leave it at that.”","It was too scary.","She had to stay far away from Gu Chacha.","She needed to take this chance to cut ties completely.","Otherwise, she was afraid that if He Huanhuan wasn’t around one day, she would lose control again and become Gu Chacha’s lackey.","Gu Chacha’s tears fell like rain: “Fufu, we’ve been friends since we were kids. How can you do this?”","Song Zhuo, terrified, scooted even closer to He Huanhuan.","He Huanhuan gave her a strange look: “Are we that close?”","Song Zhuo forced an awkward smile: “Uh, I just lost my balance...”","Though she said that, she refused to move an inch away from He Huanhuan.","She looked firmly at Gu Chacha: “Just think of me as heartless. But being your friend has been exhausting—always helping you pick fights, acting like an idiot.”","Gu Chacha wanted to say more, but Song Zhuo waved her off, refusing to engage further.","For the rest of the time, she stuck to He Huanhuan’s side like glue.","She wasn’t about to give Gu Chacha any chance to brainwash her again.","“Why are you following me? Do we even know each other?”","He Huanhuan gave Song Zhuo an exasperated look. Following her around the hall was one thing, but the bathroom too?","Was she some kind of weirdo?","Song Zhuo wouldn’t leave the restroom. She was afraid that if she went out, she’d run into Gu Chacha.","“I...”","She tried to explain but couldn’t find the right words.","He Huanhuan rolled her eyes: “If you don’t want to be friends with Gu Chacha anymore, why don’t you just go home? What are you hanging around here for? Do you have nothing better to do?”","Song Zhuo suddenly snapped back to reality. That’s right!","She could go home!","She’d go home right now and fly abroad first thing in the morning!","She’d travel to dozens of countries and stay far, far away from Gu Chacha.","There’s no way Gu Chacha could influence her from the other side of the world.","She locked herself in the bathroom and blocked Gu Chacha on every platform—even their music app.","Only then did she calm down a little.","She glanced at He Huanhuan and decided to warn her.","After all, if it weren’t for her, she never would have woken up.","“Hey, be careful with Gu Chacha. She means you...”","Before she could finish, He Huanhuan cut in: “She has a grudge against me and wants to force me out of the Gu family?”","Song Zhuo was shocked: “You know?”","She had thought He Huanhuan was oblivious, given how clueless she seemed!","He Huanhuan barely held back another eye roll: “That little scheme of yours? Any idiot could see through it, okay?”","Who did they think she was?","She’d been hustling on the streets since she was ten!","She could see through Gu Chacha’s little tricks at a glance.","And on top of that, after transmigrating into the book, the original body’s tragic story was still fresh in her mind.","She knew perfectly well that Gu Chacha was no good.","Song Zhuo was stunned: “Then why don’t you kick her out of the Gu family?”","Gu Chacha was malicious, and she had no real blood ties to the Gus.","She couldn’t understand why He Huanhuan didn’t just send her packing.","He Huanhuan scoffed: “You think I have the power to kick her out?”","The Gu family wasn’t hers to command. She couldn’t just decide who stayed and who left.","Besides, she wasn’t the original He Huanhuan.","She just wanted to keep a low profile in this book world until this absurd universe decided to kick her out.","As for Gu Chacha? That was none of her business!","Her nonchalant attitude left Song Zhuo at a loss for words. She hesitated for a long time before adding: “Be careful. There’s something weird about her. I helped her do a lot of bad things in the past without even realizing it...”","She wasn’t sure if she should tell He Huanhuan this. What if she thought she was crazy?","But He Huanhuan took it in stride, even nodding in agreement: “Makes sense. Otherwise, how would she have been able to kill the orig—uh, kill me in the original story?”","In the original novel, there was no way Gu Chacha could have smoothly killed off the original He Huanhuan without some serious ability.","Influencing the people around her? Totally normal!","That’s how these short dramas always played out."]},{"number":25,"title":"Chapter 25: Tea, You Deceived Me","paragraphs":["Song Zhuo couldn't help but ask her, \"Aren't you scared?\"","Today was the first time she had directly experienced that feeling—the sensation of her own physical consciousness slipping out of her control.","She felt like she had become a puppet, with Gu Chacha pulling the strings.","With just one look from her, she had charged forward without hesitation, fighting for her.","It was absolutely terrifying!","He Huanhuan naturally wasn't afraid. In her eyes, this was just a novel.","Although she didn't know why she had been pulled into this book, she had lived seventeen years, and those seventeen years of life experience told her one thing.","She wasn't a lucky girl.","Heaven wouldn't just hand her good fortune for nothing—a rich family's long-lost true heiress.","For the original host, this might have been a nightmare life.","But for her, it was too lucky.","She didn't believe the damn heavens would be so kind to her. She was firmly convinced that this trip into the book was just a few days' vacation.","It was compensation from the wretched heavens for her miserable childhood.","What did she have to be afraid of?","Gu Chacha? She was nothing!","Just throwing out passive-aggressive remarks and orchestrating bullying?","In their mental world, that was all child's play.","Could spiritual bullying compare to the pain of not being able to afford food?","Back in the day, she and Qi Meili had walked twenty miles in anger, gotten into a fight, and won four yuan.","One honeydew ice cream each, then another twenty-mile trek home.","If you asked her, if the original host had just hung out with her for a few days and walked twenty kilometers a day, she absolutely wouldn't have cared about Gu Chacha's snide comments.","No time to care, really—she'd get home and go straight to bed.","Too tired!","But she wasn't going to say any of this to Song Zhuo; they weren't friends.","She just glanced at Song Zhuo. \"Don't hang around Gu Chacha anymore. You can't outplay her.\"","\"Mm-hmm!\"","Song Zhuo nodded vigorously. Once she got home, she was going to buy a plane ticket and fly abroad immediately.","She wasn't coming back until she figured out what Gu Chacha was really up to.","Soon, a knock came from outside the bathroom—it was the Song family butler coming to pick her up.","Watching Song Zhuo leave with the butler, He Huanhuan let out a soft laugh.","Gu Chacha, one of your right-hand men is gone now~","With a relaxed expression, she returned to the hall. Inside, the atmosphere was harmonious. Everyone held their glasses, clinking toasts and chatting about topics they cared about.","Meanwhile, Gu Chacha sat at the grand piano in the center of the hall, playing with graceful poise.","He Huanhuan listened to the clear, crisp notes of the piano; it sounded nice enough.","But she couldn't really tell anything more than that.","Still, looking at the people around her, most of them seemed mesmerized, so she guessed Gu Chacha must have played quite well.","When the piece ended, Gu Chacha rose elegantly and took a bow.","\"Bravo!\"","Suddenly, applause erupted beside her, along with a very young man's voice.","He Huanhuan turned to look. A man in his early twenties had appeared right next to her, standing so close that when he spoke, all eyes landed on her.","Here we go again!","She wanted to roll her eyes. Didn't Gu Chacha get tired of this?","Sure enough, after the applause died down, the man turned to her. \"Miss He Huanhuan? Chacha just played a piece for everyone. Don't you think you should perform something too?\"","Before she could answer, Gu Chacha immediately stepped in to \"save\" her. \"Xiao Rong, big sister has suffered a lot in the past. You shouldn't make things difficult for her.\"","The words seemed to rescue her, but in reality, they told everyone she was from the countryside.","Inexperienced, untalented, not worth showing off.","Such a childish trick. He Huanhuan rolled her eyes at the man. \"I can't do anything. So what?\"","The man gave her a contemptuous look. \"Not being able to do anything, and you're proud of it?\"","\"Why can't I be proud of it?\"","He Huanhuan curled her lips into a smile. \"Why can't I do anything? Because Gu Chacha and I got swapped, and she got all the good years. I was out working before I was even ten, making money crying at funerals to support the family.\"","She reached out and poked Xiao Rong. \"Tell me, how was I supposed to learn piano? Were you going to pay for my lessons?\"","\"Yo—that's not Chacha's fault! Why are you so petty!\"","Xiao Rong hadn't expected He Huanhuan to be cowed by his words; instead, she fired back with sharp-tongued defiance.","\"I'm petty?\"","He Huanhuan laughed. \"Bro, your brain is even smaller, isn't it?\"","She pointed at Gu Chacha. \"She spent twenty good years in the Gu family, while I was so poor I nearly had to beg.\"","\"Now I'm back, and she's just sitting here playing the piano like nothing's wrong.\"","\"What's the message? Is she playing for me, showing me what a good life she had?\"","\"Huh? Is that what this is?\"","She jabbed at Xiao Rong, pressing him until he was speechless.","Then she turned to Gu Chacha. \"Gu Chacha, you sent him to cause trouble for me. Is that what this is?\"","Gu Chacha burst into tears instantly. \"Sister, no, I didn't send him...\"","\"You didn't?\"","He Huanhuan pressed again. Gu Chacha nodded pitifully.","She immediately turned to Xiao Rong. \"You're a simp! You're pathetic.\"","Xiao Rong got flustered. \"I am not!\"","\"Yes, you are.\"","He Huanhuan suddenly stepped forward, grabbing Gu Chacha's arm with a smile. \"Chacha and I get along great, and yet you came to pick a fight with me. If you're not a simp, what are you?\"","She gave Xiao Rong a dismissive look. \"You can't even simp right. No wonder Gu Chacha is over here cozying up to Han Mo and ignoring you.\"","\"What did you say?!\"","Xiao Rong's face flushed with anger. Gu Chacha cozying up to Han Mo?","Hadn't she always said she couldn't stand Han Mo?","\"Chacha!\"","He questioned Gu Chacha angrily, and she panicked immediately, trying to pull her arm free from He Huanhuan's grip.","But He Huanhuan was incredibly strong—there was no escaping her.","\"No, that's not it...\"","He Huanhuan tightened her hold. \"Not what? That we don't get along? That you don't like me? That you've been targeting me the whole time? That you sent Song Zhuo and this simp to attack me?\"","Gu Chacha let out a shrill scream. \"No! I didn't!\"","He Huanhuan looked satisfiedly at Xiao Rong. \"Did you hear that? She called you a simp.\"","\"No! I—\"","Gu Chacha tried to explain, but He Huanhuan was faster. She held Gu Chacha down and said to Xiao Rong, \"Being a simp has no future. Gu Chacha likes Han Mo. You don't stand a chance.\"","\"My dad wants to give Han Mo to me as my fiancé, but Gu Chacha is trying to keep him, so she set me up with someone else. That guy, what's-his-name—\"","\"It's me!!\"","Liang Ye made a grand entrance, bounding over to He Huanhuan. \"It's me~ Huanhuan and I had a blind date. It went pretty well, you know~\"","Once he showed up, Xiao Rong was mostly convinced.","If it was the Liang family, then Han Mo naturally wouldn't measure up.","The Gu and Liang families had never had any business dealings before. Why on earth would Uncle Gu introduce He Huanhuan, this country bumpkin, to Liang Ye?","It could only be Chacha.","She really did like Han Mo.","Disappointment flooded Xiao Rong's eyes. \"Chacha, you lied to me.\"","Gu Chacha shook her head frantically. \"I didn't! How could I ever—\"","But Liang Ye cut in. \"What's this about 'didn't'? Didn't you introduce Huanhuan to me?\"","\"Shut up!\""]},{"number":26,"title":"Chapter 26: The Punishment of Hammer","paragraphs":["Gu Chacha shouted at Liang Ye to stop, but it was completely too late.","Xiao Rong had fully believed their words in his heart, a flicker of pain passing through his eyes. \"I understand. I won't bother you anymore,\" he said, then turned and walked away resolutely.","He had always believed that he and Gu Chacha shared mutual feelings.","Later, when the Gu and Han families arranged a marriage alliance, Gu Chacha told him she had no choice.","He believed her.","Marriage alliances were far too common for people like them.","They depended on their families and were also constrained by them.","If the family ordered them to marry someone, how could they rebel?","He didn't blame Chacha; he knew she had no options.","After the whole \"true vs. fake daughter\" mess surfaced, he felt even more for Gu Chacha.","How precious she was—how could that girl from the countryside bully her?","So when Gu Chacha approached him, hoping he could make things difficult for He Huanhuan at Uncle Han's birthday banquet, he agreed without a second thought.","He didn't even know that Gu's father had gifted the \"Han Mo\" (jade) to He Huanhuan.","If he had known, he would have immediately begged his family to negotiate with Uncle Gu, to let him and Chacha be together.","He didn't care whether Chacha was the true daughter of the Gu family; he didn't want to inherit the family business either.","He only wanted to be with the one he loved.","But he never expected this love to be fake.","Chacha liked Han Mo—she actually liked Han Mo.","Then what was he?","A joke?","No, maybe she was right—he was nothing but a clueless, sycophantic boot-licker.","\"Xiao Rong! Wait for me...\"","Gu Chacha chased after Xiao Rong as he left, and the drama of the birthday banquet finally quieted down.","He Huanhuan glanced at Liang Ye next to her. A smug grin was plastered all over his face.","She frowned. \"What are you smiling about?\"","Liang Ye looked shy. \"When you brought me up at that moment, I feel you still have some feelings for me. I've decided to give you another chance.\"","He Huanhuan: ...She really wanted to knock him out with a hammer!","The turbulent birthday banquet finally ended, but the judgment waiting for Han Mo was far from over.","Once all the guests had left, Han Changyong's face instantly darkened like the bottom of a pot.","\"Han Mo!\"","He demanded fiercely, \"Do you even know what you're doing? Are you just going to throw everything away?\"","He shouted hoarsely, but Han Mo stood quietly, bathed in the light as he looked at him.","His gaze was as icy as sleet, sending an involuntary shiver through Han Changyong's heart.","Hopeless—this child was hopeless.","He had long ceased to be his son; he shouldn't have held any expectations for him.","And he shouldn't give him any hope either.","He pulled out his phone and called the hospital. \"How is Xiaoxuan?\"","Hearing that Han Xuan's condition was not serious, he finally breathed a sigh of relief.","He put down the phone, his decision finally made. \"You don't need to handle company matters anymore. Xiaoxuan is old enough to take over.\"","Han Mo's expression finally shifted. A mocking gleam gradually crept into his pitch-black pupils.","So this was his dear father.","As always, he never disappointed him.","With a faint, scornful smile, he nodded. \"Fine.\"","Han Changyong was surprised. \"Don't you have anything to say?\"","He had worked so hard to get into the company back then.","And now he agreed so easily?","Han Mo let out a bitter laugh. \"To be honest, I've been sick of it for a long time. Your hypocrisy. Han Xuan's stupidity. Everything about this family—I've had enough.\"","\"Han Mo!\"","Han Changyong's face turned black. \"You're still a son of this family. You're still living off its money!\"","Did he really think he wouldn’t cut off his allowance?","Han Mo smiled even wider. “You’re wrong. I’m my mother’s son. I spend my mother’s money. It has nothing to do with you.”","“Fine, fine, fine...”","Han Changyong’s face burned red with rage. He grabbed a vase from beside him and hurled it. “If you have any balls, get the hell out of this house! Never come back! Don’t spend a single cent of my money!”","None of these words intimidated Han Mo at all. Without hesitation, he turned and walked away.","“Get out!!!”","Outside the Han family estate, Chen Yu sat quietly in the driver’s seat, waiting.","As time ticked by, his heart began to rise with anxiety.","Finally, the back door was pulled open, and Han Mo slid into the car with a cold expression.","He couldn’t help but ask, “What’s this?”","Han Mo’s lips curled slightly upward. “Kicked out.”","“Yes!”","Chen Yu pounded the car seat in excitement. “I’ve had enough of them! My dad’s been waiting for this day for years! Let’s go! Homeward!”","But Han Mo’s face was indifferent as he refused. “This is just the beginning. Let’s wait until things settle before going back.”","No need to disappoint his uncle, or anyone else.","“What are you doing?”","Chen Yu wrinkled his nose. “Even if we’re not celebrating, you could at least come home and see your uncle.”","“Next time,” Han Mo said silently from the back seat, turning his face toward the window.","Hazy streetlights glowed against the window, casting a blurry halo of light. In that dim glow, he seemed to see a sharp and capable face.","That face was full of warm smiles. “Momo, look! Mom and Dad bought you this estate! Big, right? My son was born to live in a place like this, to have a good life forever!”","“You don’t have to work hard. Mom worked hard so you could take it easy!”","“When you grow up, do whatever you want. Mom will support you!”","“Momo, I hate him! How could he do this to us? I hate it!”","“I...”","That face eventually twisted into a shape of ferocious cursing, until it vanished from this world, turned into a pile of ashes.","How could he not hate?","The betrayal of those closest to him—how could he not hate?","He wouldn’t let them off easy. He absolutely wouldn’t.","Hatred quickly flickered in his eyes, then he returned to that calm demeanor.","He asked Chen Yu, “Are the contracts and accounts all checked?”","Chen Yu nodded confidently. “Of course! I was very careful!”","Now they were just waiting for Han Xuan to enter the company.","That useless fool—he would never notice a thing.","At the hospital, Han Xuan lay on the bed, whimpering nonstop. “It hurts, it really hurts. Doctor, I think it’s broken...”","The doctor patiently explained, “Second Young Master, rest assured. They’re perfectly fine. Not broken at all.”","Han Xuan didn’t believe it. “Impossible! If they’re not broken, why does it hurt so much?”","The doctor explained more gently, “It might be because you’re quite weak.”","“You! Oh, it hurts so much...”","Amid the moaning, the ward door opened, and Han Changyong walked in.","Seeing his father, Han Xuan let out a wail. “Dad! It hurts so much! Did you hit He Huanhuan? Make her pay! Compensate me! I’m in so much pain!”","Han Changyong snorted in annoyance. “You idiot! And you have the nerve to ask for compensation? Even getting a cheap trick on camera, you fool! What good are you?”","Han Xuan was dumbfounded. “What recording? What do you mean?”","His clueless expression made Han Changyong even angrier. “You moron! A fool who can’t even form a proper sentence!”","He angrily told the story of how He Huanhuan had recorded him, and Han Xuan immediately curled up in guilt, pretending to be hurt: “Ow, Dad, I’m in so much pain...”","How was he supposed to know that He Huanhuan would actually make a recording?","His cries were obviously fake, but after all, he was his son.","Han Changyong let out a long sigh, sat down by the bed, and tried to soothe him: “I’ve told your brother to take a break. When you’re discharged from the hospital, I’ll put you in charge of the company’s affairs. You need to be careful—don’t act impulsively...”","Before he could finish his warnings, Han Xuan suddenly sat up in bed, practically ecstatic.","“Really?! Dad! You’re the best dad ever! I swear I’ll do a great job!”","Hmph!","Han Mo!","Just wait! He would definitely take over all of his projects!"]},{"number":27,"title":"Chapter 27: Change of Dynasties","paragraphs":["With a burst of renewed energy, the minor physical discomfort vanished instantly.","That very night, Han Xuan checked out of the hospital. The next morning, he was determined to head straight to the company to assume his position.","At the Han family home, Han Changyong couldn’t stop worrying. He repeated his advice again and again: “At the company, make sure to listen to the seasoned employees. Don’t be impulsive. Don’t be overbearing. Don’t—”","Han Xuan waved his hand impatiently. “Oh, come on, Dad! Don’t worry about me! I’m not a kid anymore. I know what I’m doing!”","How hard could it be to be the boss?","If Han Mo could do it, then surely he could too.","When his car pulled up to the company building, he stepped out confidently, stretching his long legs.","He strode into the building, looking every bit the part, expecting employees to greet him with cheers and applause.","But there was nothing. Absolutely nothing.","Around him, people rushed by like clock-punching cattle, hurrying to their shifts.","He frowned, displeased. “Why isn’t anyone here to welcome me?”","His assistant, Meng Yu, followed respectfully behind him. “Junior Han, our company has never had that kind of tradition.”","This isn’t some idol drama. Who’d want to play along with that nonsense?","He was just an ordinary grunt. For the salary he got, how many extra jobs did he have to juggle?","Han Xuan pouted in irritation. “Didn’t Han Mo get a welcome when he took over?”","Meng Yu nodded. “Senior Han never went in for that sort of thing.”","The mention of Senior Han triggered Han Xuan’s temper instantly. “What’s all this ‘Junior Han’ and ‘Senior Han’ nonsense? From now on, there’s only one President Han in this company! Got it?”","Meng Yu bowed his head obediently. “Understood.”","The elevator climbed to the fifteenth floor, where his new office awaited.","Han Mo’s belongings had been cleared out the night before. Polite, considerate—Han Xuan was satisfied with that.","He pushed open the office door and was greeted by a sleek, black-and-white décor.","He curled his lip in disdain. “Tacky. Get rid of it all. Replace it.”","Meng Yu hesitated. “Everything? That’ll need the finance department’s approval stamp...”","Han Xuan was a hair’s breadth from kicking him. “Are you deliberately going against me? Huh? Can’t you talk properly?”","From the moment he’d stepped out of the car, not one word from this guy had been pleasant to hear.","Why did he have to get stuck with such an idiot as his assistant?","Meng Yu stood there looking miserable. Did he want to be his assistant?","He’d been doing great in logistics before!","Nice and stable.","No idea what crack that idiot in HR was smoking when they transferred him to work for Han Xuan.","Good Lord, everyone in the company knew about the mess in the Han family.","What business was the struggle for the heir to him?","Han Mo’s competence was obvious to all. If they’d assigned him as Han Mo’s assistant, that might have been something.","But instead, it had to be Han Xuan, clearly a useless pretty boy!","If Han Xuan messed up, he’d be dragged down with him.","The thought made him want to quit on the spot.","He stood there all pitiful, and Han Xuan, disgusted by the sight of him, waved his hand dismissively. “Forget it. Just bring me all the projects Han Mo was handling.”","“Oh, okay.”","Chen Yu had worked overtime all last night to hand everything over.","Meng Yu went to fetch the files. As soon as he placed them on the desk, without even glancing at them, Han Xuan announced, “Tell everyone—all these projects are canceled.”","“Huh?”","Meng Yu was stunned. “All of them?”","These were Senior Han’s life’s work in the company over the past few years!","Han Xuan shot him a look. “You deaf?”","Meng Yu hesitated nervously. “President Han, don’t you want to look these over first?”","The company had already poured a huge amount of money into these projects. Scrapping them now would be a disaster.","Besides, several of them were investments worth nearly a hundred million. Canceling them outright?","Without consulting the board?","He tried to reason with him, but Han Xuan exploded. “What part of ‘shut up and follow orders’ don’t you get? Didn’t you hear me? I said cancel them!”","Every single project Han Mo had touched—he was going to kill them all!","He would erase every trace of Han Mo!","“But—”","Han Xuan glared at him. “One more word, and I’ll fire you on the spot!”","Meng Yu grimaced. “We need your signature to cancel...”","Honestly, he wished he’d be fired. If that happened, he’d get his severance package and be done with it. Sweet deal.","He’d assumed Han Xuan was just messing around initially.","But no, he actually meant to shut down everything.","The strangest part? Some of the project cancellations required board approval.","Yet when the termination documents were submitted, they were approved in no time.","Those old men on the board didn’t say a single word.","Meng Yu didn’t get it. Combined, this added up to hundreds of millions!","Was the company just throwing all that away?","Rich people’s world was beyond him.","But it wasn’t his problem. He was just a regular guy getting paid monthly. Why should he lose sleep over it?","In a single day, the fruits of Han Mo’s several years of hard work were wiped clean.","All projects—axed.","All the people Han Mo had trusted and promoted—suspended.","Some got severance, some got buyouts for stock options...","They were all cleared out without exception.","Meng Yu was dumbfounded by how fast it happened.","Was this what they meant by the war for the heir?","Holy crap.","Watching those people walk out of the building with cardboard boxes, Han Xuan felt an immense thrill.","He snapped his fingers triumphantly and said to Meng Yu, “See that? That’s what happens when you back the wrong person. Got it?”","Meng Yu nodded miserably. “Got it.”","All he could think was that he wanted a severance too.","Fire me, please.","But luck wasn’t on his side. He was stuck working under Han Xuan.","After vetoing ten versions of a project proposal, Han Xuan finally had fun with his choice—returned to the very first draft.","He leaned back smugly in his executive chair. Being General Manager—wasn’t that hard!","The grunts would handle all the pesky details.","His job was just to make things difficult for them.","What the hell had Han Mo been so busy with all the time?","No doubt trying to show off to Dad.","Dad had already brought the company to its peak. Their job was just to maintain it.","Maintain. How hard could that be?","Don’t go crazy with investments. Don’t mess with random projects. Simple.","For now, he was only going to back one project: East City.","East City—the Gu family.","He’d already offended He Huanhuan, so that left Gu Chacha.","At the thought of her, Han Xuan immediately pictured her haughty face.","Gu Chacha had always looked down on him. Back in that nightclub, when he’d asked her for a drink, she’d sneered and called him a bastard’s son. He remembered that to this day.","He was a bastard, was he?","She never imagined that one day he—the mongrel—would have the upper hand.","A secret excitement pulsed through him.","He’d heard that last night, Song Zhuo and Rong Yuze had both cut ties with her.","That bastard Han Mo, trying to win East City’s project, would kiss He Huanhuan’s shoes if he could.","He didn’t give a damn about Gu Chacha anymore. She must be struggling now, right?","Good. Hard times would show her who could truly be her savior in a snowstorm.","He pulled out his phone and dialed Gu Chacha.","The phone rang several times before she picked up. His voice dripped with smug delight. “Gu Chacha, dinner tonight?”","Gu Chacha’s voice was ice-cold. “I don’t think we’re close. Why would I have dinner with you?”","Han Xuan’s smile grew. “Because I can give you what you want.”","The line went silent for a long moment—long enough that Han Xuan wondered if she’d hung up.","“What time tonight?”"]},{"number":28,"title":"Chapter 28: I Can Give You What You Want","paragraphs":["Han Xuan immediately perked up. \"Eight o'clock tonight! I'll pick you up. You decide where to eat!\"","\"No need.\"","Gu Chacha refused coldly. \"Cloud Mirror Manor. See you at eight.\"","\"Fine!\"","The phone buzzed with the disconnection sound, but Han Xuan wasn't upset at all.","No matter how much she pretended, agreeing to have dinner with him meant she had already lost.","In the past, she wouldn't have given him the slightest bit of courtesy.","Having dinner with him? Not even worth considering.","Staring at the hung-up phone, a smug smile curled at the corner of his lips.","Gu Chacha, look at you now.","At eight o'clock that evening, he arrived at Cloud Mirror Manor on time.","Gu Chacha had already booked a private room and was waiting inside.","As he pushed open the door, she sat by the table, wearing a moon-white dress.","Seeing him, she gave a faint nod. \"I didn't know what you liked, so I just ordered what I enjoy.\"","He casually picked a few dishes from the menu and then dismissed the waiter.","Tonight wasn't really about eating anyway.","His gaze burned intensely as he stared at Gu Chacha. There was no denying it—Gu Chacha was genuinely stunning.","Her eyes shimmered like liquid light, her skin was snow-white, and her lips were a soft, rosy pink.","She was the top-tier beauty in that delicate flower-girl style.","He liked her. He had liked her since childhood.","Letting out a satisfied sigh, he said, \"Chacha, I never thought we'd actually sit down and eat together one day.\"","Unexpectedly, Gu Chacha smiled sweetly. \"When Han Mo and I get married, we'll have plenty of meals together, little brother.\"","\"Ha!\"","He let out a sneer. \"Chacha, are you really that clueless, or just pretending? Han Mo would happily act like a dog for He Huanhuan. How could he ever marry you?\"","Gu Chacha's smile faltered slightly. \"He's just temporarily blinded by interests. He'll realize who's truly right for him.\"","\"Is that so?\"","Han Xuan raised his phone. \"Don't you go online? Han Mo has been kicked out of the company. The person in charge now is me.\"","Gu Chacha looked at him with a contemptuous smirk. \"So what?\"","What did it matter if it was him?","He was nothing but a useless fool. When things fell apart, Uncle Han would have no choice but to call Han Mo back.","She wasn't stupid. She knew exactly who to win over.","Han Xuan pouted in displeasure. \"You look down on me.\"","The door was knocked, and a waiter stood respectfully at the entrance, holding the appetizers. \"Sir, shall we start serving the dishes?\"","He yelled furiously toward the door, \"Get out!\"","The waiter immediately lowered his head and apologized sincerely. \"I'm sorry.\"","The door closed again, and the disdain on Gu Chacha's face grew even more obvious.","\"See? You always embarrass yourself like this.\"","Losing his temper at the wrong time, every single time—it was truly degrading.","Those words hit a nerve. Han Xuan stood up angrily, strode over to Gu Chacha, and grabbed her chin.","\"Gu Chacha, you have no cards left to play. What right do you have to look down on me?\"","Gu Chacha let out a sneer. \"What I do is none of your business.\"","His fingers tightened, and his face darkened to the extreme. \"Keep pretending. You don't have a drop of the Gu family's blood. What cards could you possibly have? You bastard!\"","The blunt insult finally struck a chord in Gu Chacha. She cursed through gritted teeth, \"Shut up!\"","A provocative grin spread across Han Xuan's lips. \"Gu Chacha, since when did you become so naive? Does shutting up change the facts? Can shutting your mouth stop Han Mo from sucking up to He Huanhuan? Can it undo the fact that you've been abandoned? Huh?\"","Their gazes clashed in the air, both staring fiercely at each other, neither willing to back down.","\"What do you want?\" Gu Chacha asked coldly.","Han Xuan grinned broadly. \"Don't you think we're perfect for each other? The bastard son and the illegitimate daughter—what a match, right?\"","Gu Chacha's expression soured further. \"If you don't want to talk properly, I'm leaving.\"","She was no bastard!","She was the rightful daughter of the Gu family!","\"Alright, alright...\"","Han Xuan reached out and wiped her lips. \"Dear Chacha, why don't you consider me? I've already kicked Han Mo out of the company. All his projects have been halted. He can't stir up trouble anymore.\"","Gu Chacha sneered. \"He still has He Huanhuan. He still has my father.\"","Old Mr. Gu hadn't chosen his partner yet, so Han Mo wasn't out of the game yet.","\"That's why...\"","His fingers on her chin grew gentler, more intimate. \"We need to be together, Chacha. We have to make sure Dad completely boots Han Mo out, don't you agree?\"","Gu Chacha shot him a look of disgust. \"You?\"","She didn't think her father would ever take Han Xuan seriously, nor did she believe he had the capability to land the East City project.","The contempt in her eyes was unmistakable. Han Xuan's mouth twitched in irritation, but he quickly suppressed it.","Sitting down on the edge of the table, he said, \"Chacha, I know you look down on me. But you need to understand one thing: in my father's eyes, I'll always be his favorite son. Han Mo doesn't even come close.\"","This wasn't just arrogance. Everyone in their circle knew how ruthlessly Han Changyong treated Han Mo.","If it weren't for that, would she ever have agreed to have dinner with him?","Just looking at him made her lose her appetite.","His sleazy fingers gripped tighter, and his revolting face pressed closer to hers. \"Chacha, being with Han Mo will only get you money. With me, I can give you shares.\"","Gu Chacha looked up at him in shock. \"Are you insane?\"","\"Ha ha...\"","He laughed openly. \"That's my sincerity, Chacha. I'm serious about you.\"","As long as he could completely drive Han Mo out and secure the East City project, the whole company would be his.","If Gu Chacha was willing to be his woman, giving her a few shares was nothing.","Unlike his cold-hearted father, he was generous with women.","His face moved closer, his voice a tempting lure. \"Chacha, aren't you even going to think about me?\"","A wave of disgust churned deep inside her, but it was quickly swallowed by a greater greed.","If she could gain control, who would want to beg for money with an open palm?","She blinked, and only delight remained in her eyes. \"Han Xuan, it seems I really misjudged you before.\"","\"It's fine. There's still plenty of time for us to get to know each other again...\"","The door opened once more, and the waiter asked respectfully, dishes in hand, \"Sir, shall I serve the food?\"","Before he could finish, the guests inside had already left gracefully.","\"Forget it! Keep it all for yourselves!\"","He had more important things to do.","In the most bustling district of River City, inside the presidential suite of a five-star hotel.","The moment they entered the room, they were all over each other. Gu Chacha's face flushed as she looked at him. \"If you dare to deceive me, you know I'll...\"","He kissed her like a madman. \"Then kill me.\"","Then came the relentless closeness—taking over her body, her will, everything.","All that was left was her anxious insistence. \"I will.\"","The neon lights blazed wildly in the city, and in the room, two people with secret motives merged together.","Bound inseparably."]},{"number":29,"title":"Chapter 29: Good Night","paragraphs":["Han Xuan lay on the bed, his face full of satisfaction, watching as Gu Chacha put her clothes on one by one.","He lit a cigarette and suggested, \"It's already so late. Why not just stay the night?\"","They weren't teenagers with curfews, were they?","Gu Chacha shot him a disgusted glare. \"Are you an idiot?\"","If they spent the night out at the very beginning of their relationship, what would her father think of them? Of him?","She ordered him curtly, \"Get up. Drive me home.\"","\"Fine.\"","Han Xuan stubbed out his cigarette, put on his clothes, and followed her downstairs.","In the elevator, Gu Chacha looked at the countless glowing lights outside the window, feeling dazed.","How had her world turned upside down in just a few short days?","She had become the fake daughter who had taken over He Huanhuan's life. Her mom and dad had become He Huanhuan's parents. Her brothers had all become He Huanhuan's brothers.","Her second brother wouldn't even give her a kind look, and even her eldest brother was no longer on her side.","Not to mention that damn Han Mo. She had given him a better choice, and he just turned a blind eye!","He was still trying to win over He Huanhuan!","Why?","Why was fate treating her so unfairly?","If everyone was against her, then she wouldn't hold back.","She had no choice. She had to do what she had to do.","Suddenly, a large hand wrapped around her waist. Han Xuan pulled her close affectionately. \"What are you thinking about?\"","She wrinkled her brow in disgust. \"Can you stop being so frivolous?\"","Hearing this, Han Xuan burst out laughing. \"Chacha, we've done far more frivolous things than this. What are you shy about?\"","Gu Chacha barely kept herself from rolling her eyes. How could two brothers born from the same father be so different?","She wasn't particularly fond of Han Mo, but compared to Han Xuan, he was far more presentable.","When comparisons were made, the disgust in her heart grew until it became unbearable.","But for now, she could still tolerate it.","As long as she had something to gain, she could endure.","She slapped his hand away from her waist and snapped, \"Watch yourself. We're still in the early stages. Don't let my dad catch on.\"","Just a couple of days ago, she had cried and pleaded with her father to pursue Han Mo. She couldn't suddenly get involved with Han Xuan now.","That would be too obvious.","The car drove back to the Gu family estate. Gu Chengye and his wife were strolling in the courtyard, and when they looked up, they saw Han Xuan in the driver's seat.","Gu Chengye frowned. \"Why did Chacha go out with the second son of the Han family?\"","His old friend Han had two sons who were complete opposites: Han Mo was steady and capable, while Han Xuan was flashy and reckless. The contrast was sharp.","He had always admired Han Mo, as Chacha well knew, so why was she mixing around with Han Xuan now?","The car slowly rolled up. As the door opened, Han Xuan flashed a bright, ingratiating smile. \"Uncle and Auntie, enjoying your evening walk?\"","Gu Chengye nodded coldly, then turned to Gu Chacha with a questioning look. \"When did you two start hanging out?\"","Gu Chacha pretended not to catch the underlying concern in her father's question and answered with a smile, \"We just had dinner together. He was on the way, so he gave me a ride home.\"","Just a meal together—nothing more.","Gu Chengye nodded and said to Han Xuan, \"It's getting late, Xuan. You should head back now. Drive safely.\"","A polite dismissal.","With a cheerful grin, Han Xuan replied, \"I'll be off then. Bye, Uncle and Auntie.\"","The car quickly drove out of the Gu estate. Through the rearview mirror, Han Xuan glanced back.","In the darkness, the massive estate looked like a sleeping tiger—seemingly harmless but full of hidden aggression.","He snorted coldly. \"You old bastard. I'll make you pay later.\"","The car surged forward, speeding away into the distance.","Back in the courtyard, Gu Chengye turned to Gu Chacha, his expression darkening. \"Chacha, come with me to the study.\"","Jiang Yulan patted Gu Chacha's hand gently. \"Talk nicely to your father. Don't make him angry.\"","Gu Chacha nodded obediently and followed Gu Chengye into the study.","Once inside, Gu Chengye asked directly, \"Why are you hanging out with Han Xuan?\"","Gu Chacha looked down, silent.","Gu Chengye sighed. \"I asked you a question.\"","Gu Chacha's eyes reddened instantly. \"Is my father still willing to listen to me?\"","\"What do you mean? When have I ever refused to listen to you?\"","Her eyes grew misty. \"Father gave Han Mo to sister. What could I do? I...\"","Gu Chengye interrupted her with a tone of frustration:","\"But that doesn't mean you should get mixed up with Han Xuan! Do you know what he's like? He's nowhere near good enough for you!\"","Tearfully, Gu Chacha moved closer to sit beside him. \"Father, did you know that Uncle Han kicked Han Mo out of the company?\"","Gu Chengye was startled. \"When did that happen?\"","Was his old friend Han that foolish?","Gu Chacha lowered her voice. \"Just last night, right after the birthday party ended. Uncle Han completely removed Han Mo from the company, and this morning, Han Xuan stepped into the role.\"","\"And that's why you went to dinner with him?\"","Gu Chengye shook his head disapprovingly. \"Chacha, you've made a mistake. That boy—what can he ever accomplish?\"","Within a month at most, Old Han would have to beg Han Mo to come back.","Gu Chacha looked at him with innocent, teary eyes. \"Father, he invited me to dinner. I was curious about what happened in their family, so I went. There's nothing else to it.\"","\"Better be nothing,\"","Gu Chengye said, frowning. \"Han Mo and Huanhuan are getting along quite well. If you get involved with Han Xuan... what kind of image would that project? Do our daughters have to settle for the Han family sons?\"","He had chosen Han Mo carefully after considering everything; it wasn't a decision limited to the Han family!","He had no respect for Han Changyong.","Gu Chacha nodded obediently. \"I understand, Father.\"","\"But, Father...\"","She casually asked, \"Since Han Mo was kicked out of the company, will our family's cooperation with the Han family continue?\"","She needed to know whether her father intended to work with the Han family as a whole or just with Han Mo for the East City project.","If it was just Han Mo, then she would have to reconsider Han Xuan's value.","A one-night stand was nothing.","But if she gambled her entire future on him and it collapsed, she'd be finished.","The question seemed offhand, so Gu Chengye didn't dwell on it. He nodded and said, \"Of course, it will continue.\"","The Han family held a weak position in Jiangcheng, making them ideal partners for him.","If he chose another family, leverage in the upcoming project would be diminished.","That's why he had initially selected Han Mo as a son-in-law: the boy was smart, understood what he cared about, and handled things with tact.","Hearing his confirmation, Gu Chacha smiled lightly, She stood up. \"Father, I'm going to bed now.\"","So her father planned to cooperate with the Han family.","Then Han Mo didn't matter anymore.","As long as Uncle Han didn't involve Han Mo, he would never recover.","So what if he was trying to win over He Huanhuan? What did she have? Nothing but a shabby background?","Hmph!","Once in bed, she picked up her phone. On the chat page, there was a new conversation pinned to the top.","She opened it, tapped the screen lightly, and sent a message:","Good night."]},{"number":30,"title":"Chapter 30: Is Gu Chacha Crazy","paragraphs":["A reply quickly came from the other side of the screen: Goodnight, my baby. Did Dad say anything?","Gu Chacha rolled her eyes, put down her phone, and went to sleep.","Up on the third floor, He Huanhuan stared at the huge transfer on her phone, her brow tightly furrowed.","Han Mo had just sent her another sum of money, several times more than the previous hundred thousand.","What was he trying to do?","As soon as the thought crossed her mind, she called him immediately.","The call was answered quickly, and He Huanhuan asked impatiently, \"Why did you transfer me money?\"","The voice on the other end was calm and casual: \"Afraid you wouldn't have enough to spend.\"","\"Wait, what exactly are we to each other? Why does it matter to you whether I have enough or not?\"","He Huanhuan's tone was sharp, but Han Mo, as if he hadn't heard her, replied steadily, \"They say I'm your simp. Just think of it as an offering from a simp.\"","......","Who even gets addicted to being a simp?","After hanging up, she tossed her phone aside in irritation.","A knock came at the door, and Gu Jinghan's annoying voice sounded from outside: \"Sister Huan, did you know your simp got fired?\"","The door was yanked open, and He Huanhuan frowned at him. \"What did you say?\"","Gu Jinghan smirked slyly. \"Exclusive news: Han Mo got kicked out of his family's company. Han Xuan took his position, and on his first day, he shut down all the projects Han Mo was handling.\"","\"Is Han Xuan insane?\"","He Huanhuan didn't know much about running a company, but she knew that abruptly stopping projects midway would lose a lot of money.","\"Does their family have money to burn?\"","Gu Jinghan nodded with disgust. \"Han Xuan's been dim-witted since he was a kid, and he never grew out of it.\"","\"Alright, I've got it.\"","He Huanhuan was about to close the door, but Gu Jinghan stuck his foot in to stop her. \"Hold on, there's another bit of exclusive news—want to hear it?\"","He Huanhuan glanced at him. \"Where do you get so much exclusive news?\"","Was he some kind of paparazzo?","Gu Jinghan grinned slyly. \"Just say whether you want to hear it or not.\"","\"Spill it.\"","\"Gu Chacha and Han Xuan hooked up.\"","\"What?\"","He Huanhuan was genuinely shocked. \"Is she crazy?\"","Although Han Xuan and Han Mo were brothers, their looks weren't even close.","Han Xuan took after his father—big head, a stupid look.","A stupid, lecherous ugly bastard—how could Gu Chacha fall for him?","\"And there's more!\"","Gu Jinghan said in a gossipy tone. \"They went to a hotel to hook up!\"","\"What?\"","He Huanhuan frowned. \"How did you find out?\"","Something as private as a hotel meetup—how did Gu Jinghan know?","Gu Jinghan smirked proudly. \"That hotel is mine.\"","\"What?\"","He Huanhuan was stunned again. \"Aren't you just some trust fund kid?\"","She had always thought Gu Jinghan was just a spoiled rich kid who only knew how to spend money!","Gu Jinghan couldn't hold back his smug grin. \"Of course not! I opened it with my allowance back in college, and it actually took off!\"","He hadn't told his family. He was waiting for the right moment to shock everyone with the news.","But not only did that moment never come—he ended up catching Gu Chacha and Han Xuang at a hotel!","He winked at He Huanhuan lecherously. \"They stayed from check-in to check-out—twenty minutes total. Tsk tsk... Han Xuan's a real disappointment, kid!\"","Taking a shower alone took at least ten minutes, then there was prep work, and a smoke afterward...","The actual act probably lasted less than five minutes.","Tsk tsk...","What a failure!","He Huanhuan glared at him. \"Do we need the details?\"","It turned her off!","Gu Jinghan asked her, \"Don't you want to know why they ended up sleeping together?\"","He Huanhuan pouted. \"None of my business.\"","\"Sister Huan, it does involve you.\"","Gu Jinghan turned serious. \"She got together with Han Xuan only for the East City project. He must have promised her something tempting.\"","\"The Han family and our family—you and Han Mo, her and Han Xuan—don't you think that has something to do with you?\"","He Huanhuan dropped her eyes. \"I don't like Han Mo. I don't plan on being with him.\"","In her world, she wouldn't even turn eighteen until next month.","Right now, dating would be considered early romance!","This was a world inside a book. To her, everything here was dramatic and unrelated.","She didn't want to get involved—not with Han Mo, not with the Gu family, not with the East City project.","She just wanted to coast along.","Gu Jinghan looked at her seriously. \"Huanhuan, do you think Han Mo will let Han Xuan take everything from him? He won't give up.\"","\"As long as you live here, you can't escape these things.\"","He Huanhuan bit her lower lip, feeling annoyed.","Dragged into such a game for no reason—she didn't like it at all.","Gu Chacha was annoying, Han Mo was annoying.","And that ugly bastard Han Xuan was even more irritating.","Since she couldn't control them, she might as well just go to sleep.","She'd take things step by step. See what that guy Gu Chacha was up to, and see what that guy Han Mo wanted.","The next day, as soon as she woke up, Han Mo sent her a message.","\"Are you free today? Want to grab a meal together?\"","He Huanhuan stared at her phone for a long time before replying, \"Fine.\"","A reply came quickly from the other side: \"I'll be at your place in ten minutes.\"","Ten minutes?","That jerk wasn't waiting outside her house, was he?","She wasn't wrong. Han Mo's car was indeed parked outside the Gu family estate, waiting.","As soon as her reply came, Han Mo drove in immediately, not giving her a chance to back out.","By the time she finished washing up and getting ready, Han Mo was already chatting with Old Mr. Gu.","The two sat on the sofa, idly making small talk—about her, about the weather—but not about business.","When she came downstairs, Old Mr. Gu smiled warmly and waved her over. \"Han Mo has been waiting for you a long time. Go out and have fun with him.\"","Old Mr. Gu's smile was kind and open, making He Huanhuan wonder if he knew about Gu Chacha's plans.","Gu Chacha had been dropped off by Han Xuan last night, and Old Mr. Gu had seen it with his own eyes.","What was he thinking?","Was he weighing his options?","He Huanhuan couldn't figure it out. She just felt that rich people lived such boring lives.","Scheming and fighting over money.","But then she thought of those staggering sums and couldn't help but sigh.","Of course they had to scheme—it wasn't just tens of millions.","It was billions, hundreds of billions.","No wonder they couldn't stop.","It was like ancient princes fighting for the throne—the stakes were too high to ignore.","She was just a poor guy who had stumbled into the wrong circle, so she didn't fit in.","She quietly followed Han Mo out the door and got into the car.","As the car drove out of the estate, she remained silent.","Han Mo glanced sideways at her. \"Why aren't you talking?\"","He Huanhuan leaned her head against the window and looked at him blankly. \"Do you know that Gu Chacha and Han Xuan slept together last night?\"","\"Hmm? What did you say?\"","Han Mo looked at her in surprise, as if he hadn't understood her words.","She shrugged. \"Slept together, you know... at a hotel...\"","\"Huanhuan.\"","Han Mo stopped her from continuing, his face slightly reddening. \"I understand. That's enough.\"","No need to be so direct."]},{"number":31,"title":"Chapter 31: Don't You Have Anything You Like","paragraphs":["\"How do you know that?\"","He asked He Huanhuan. She raised an eyebrow: \"Are you saying those two are...?\"","\"At a hotel.\"","Han Mo's face reddened a bit more: \"They're at a hotel. How do you know?\"","He Huanhuan curled her lips slightly: \"I have my little birds.\"","Her tone was so certain that Han Mo knew the news was a hundred percent true.","Gu Chacha chose Han Xuan. What did Han Xuan promise her?","When it came to gifts and spending money, Han Xuan couldn't compare to him.","So it could only be...","Shares.","That fool promised Gu Chacha some shares.","Had to be it.","A faint smile curled at the corner of his mouth. He really was as stupid as ever.","If so, as a good big brother, shouldn't he give him a push?","Lost in thought, he heard He Huanhuan say: \"You look pretty sinister right now, you know that?\"","He instinctively glanced at the rearview mirror. His own face was grim, his eyes cold.","He really didn't look like a good guy.","He blinked, burying all those schemes deep in his heart.","\"Just thinking about something. Sorry.\"","He Huanhuan stared at him: \"What were you just thinking about?\"","Han Mo smiled politely: \"Work stuff.\"","But He Huanhuan pressed on: \"What work? Weren't you kicked out of the company? Do you even have a job right now?\"","Han Mo: ...","Adults always leave a little room when they talk. If someone doesn't give a direct answer, you know not to push further.","But He Huanhuan was different. Her soul was still underage.","On top of that, she was a restless spirit. Whatever popped into her head, she had to say it.","As for whether you were willing to listen or answer?","Sorry, that wasn't within her consideration.","She locked her eyes on Han Mo: \"You were just thinking about how to screw over Han Xuan, weren't you?\"","...","\"Does it matter?\"","He Huanhuan nodded: \"Of course it matters. That guy's ugly, and I can't stand the sight of him anyway.\"","Han Mo gave her a once-over. What did she mean by that?","Was she on his side?","Before he could dwell on it, He Huanhuan pressed on: \"So, how were you planning to get him?\"","Was that something you could just ask?","\"Are you still in touch with my dad? Seems like the old man's pretty friendly with you. Did you ever talk about that East City project?\"","\"The old man wouldn't back Han Xuan, would he?\"","\"Does that mean Gu Chacha and Han Xuan slept together for nothing?\"","\"Your dad dislikes you that much. Do you think you've got a shot?\"","\"Would you marry me just to get that project?\"","\"I've watched TV shows. Guys like you marry me for a project. Then, when you get older, you feel resentful and go find some young chick to fool around with.\"","\"You know 'Dwelling Narrowness,' right? That's how it goes.\"","\"Are you Song Siming?\"","...","What the hell was all that?","\"Say something!\"","Han Mo sighed helplessly: \"You could at least give me a chance to answer.\"","He thought for a moment and asked He Huanhuan: \"Do you want to marry me?\"","He Huanhuan immediately shook her head: \"It's illegal for minors to get married!\"","Han Mo frowned: \"I remember you're an adult.\"","He Huanhuan grinned: \"My soul is still under eighteen.\"","\"Fine.\"","Han Mo smiled helplessly: \"Then why did you come out with me?\"","He Huanhuan held up her phone: \"You're my sugar daddy!\"","He'd transferred her so much money!","Having dinner with him was nothing, right?","Han Mo went along with it: \"What do you want to eat? Same as before, spicy hot pot?\"","He Huanhuan shook her head: \"Not feeling it today. Let's just get some beef noodles.\"","\"Okay.\"","The car drove slowly until He Huanhuan picked a shop to eat at.","The second time stepping into a roadside joint, Han Mo was much more comfortable with it.","He ordered two bowls of noodles and sat down on the red plastic stool, waiting for the food to arrive with an easy expression.","When the steaming red noodles were set in front of him, he calmly snapped apart disposable chopsticks and started eating.","He Huanhuan deliberately wanted to see him struggle, but found him eating with complete composure.","She pouted in displeasure: \"I thought you didn't like places like this?\"","Han Mo wiped his mouth clean and smiled: \"Actually, once you accept it mentally, it's pretty tasty.\"","It was the same with them. On the surface, they seemed completely mismatched and incompatible.","But once you accepted it in your heart, they actually fit well together.","He Huanhuan, however, didn't catch a single bit of what he meant.","She wrinkled her nose in annoyance: \"That's no fun.\"","After finishing a bowl of blazingly spicy beef noodles, both of them had sweat beading on their foreheads.","Despite trying his best to hold it together, Han Mo still looked a bit frazzled.","He Huanhuan glanced at his reddened lips and finally felt a little satisfied.","She asked him: \"Want to eat together again?\"","Han Mo smiled and nodded: \"It's pretty fun. I think we could eat at a lot of roadside joints together.\"","Damn!","He Huanhuan shot him a glare: \"Who wants to eat with you? I'm way happier eating alone!\"","\"Okay.\"","He was still smiling, leaving He Huanhuan unable to figure out how to pick a fight.","She huffed, stood up, and walked out.","She didn't get in the car, just walked along the roadside instead.","Han Mo quietly followed alongside her, trailing her street after street.","Habits really were a torment. Before, she could walk for three to five hours without getting tired.","But after just a few days of the good life at the Gu family, her body had gone soft.","After only three blocks, her feet were aching.","Just two hours, and she was already tired!","She'd changed!","She wasn't the same person anymore!","An unspeakable grievance welled up inside her. She whirled around and glared at Han Mo: \"You're tired of walking, aren't you?\"","A hint of amusement flickered in Han Mo's eyes. He asked her: \"Should I be tired?\"","Her eyes grew wider: \"How would I know if you're tired or not? I'm not you!\"","Han Mo's smile deepened: \"You know. You can feel it.\"","\"I—\"","She was about to snap, but Han Mo suddenly reached out and took her hand.","\"Feel it. Do you think I'm tired?\"","The warmth of his body traveled through his fingertips and palm, rushing into her blood. Her face suddenly felt hot.","Her eyes couldn't help but dart away: \"I think you should be tired. Yeah, you're definitely tired.\"","Han Mo smiled and tightened his grip on her hand: \"Then should we take a taxi back?\"","He Huanhuan hesitated: \"But the car's still back there...\"","\"It's fine. It's not going to get stolen.\"","They hailed a ride-hailing car and sat together back to the Gu family home.","The car pulled into the estate, and He Huanhuan got out.","She should have just gone straight home, but a moment's hesitation tugged at her heart.","She looked down at Han Mo: \"Want to come up to the third floor for a bit?\"","Han Mo looked up at her: \"Am I allowed to?\"","\"Of course you are.\"","The third floor was empty. After Gu Chacha moved her things out, He Huanhuan hadn't added anything new.","Maybe because her heart didn't truly belong here, she hadn't felt the need to stake any claims.","Han Mo stepped onto the third floor with her, and seeing the stark emptiness, he couldn't help but frown: \"Don't you have anything you like?\"","Girls her age usually had so many passions.","Cute dolls he couldn't name, limited-edition blind boxes, pretty clothes, luxury bags...","But her room had nothing at all.","Like if she left someday, any trace of her could be wiped away in an instant."]},{"number":32,"title":"Chapter 32: This is the Right Way to Eat Malatang","paragraphs":["He Huanhuan shook her head. \"I don't like anything.\"","Han Mo didn't say anything, but held her hand tighter. \"There's a new mall opening in the old town. I need to check it out tomorrow. Would you come with me?\"","He Huanhuan wrinkled her nose in disdain. \"Men who are too clingy lose their charm, you know?\"","Han Mo smiled and nodded. \"Got it. I'll pick you up tomorrow morning, okay?\"","He Huanhuan gave a perfunctory nod. \"Fine.\"","The next day, when He Huanhuan came downstairs, Han Mo was still chatting with Old Mr. Gu.","A door to the guest room on the first floor cracked open slightly, and Gu Chacha stood carefully by the door, eavesdropping on their conversation.","For an entire hour, the two talked about food, fun, and various trending topics, but never about work.","She thought to herself, Dad really does only intend to cooperate with the Han family, it seems.","Although Han Mo was reliable, without the Han family, he was nothing.","Without massive financial backing, what was a little capability worth anyway?","There were so many people on this land—capability was the least scarce thing.","She gently closed the door and sat back on the sofa.","She opened her phone and sent a message to Han Xuan: Come pick me up from my place later.","Han Mo had already been cut out of the game, yet he was still so sycophantic.","Showing up every day to curry favor with He Huanhuan and her father.","That arrogant fool Han Xuan, ever since he dropped her off two days ago, had vanished without a trace.","If he wasn't even attentive in wooing her, how could he win her over?","After a long pause, the other side replied with a simple \"Okay.\"","Gu Chacha's heart suddenly felt clogged. It was supposed to be him asking her, so how had she become the proactive one now?","She couldn't help but wonder: was her choice really the right one?","Was Han Xuan truly her best option?","She had no confidence, but she also knew she didn't have many choices.","She was greedy. She wanted a lot of money.","Even more money than being the daughter of the Gu family would bring.","She wanted a wild and unrestrained life, no longer under anyone's control.","Her fists clenched unconsciously. She absolutely could not lose.","She waited quietly until He Huanhuan and Han Mo left together.","Until Dad and Mom went out to meet friends.","Only then did Han Xuan finally arrive, late.","Her anger could no longer be suppressed, and she lashed out at him: \"What were you doing? Didn't I tell you to come immediately? Why did you take so long? Do you even know what you're doing?\"","She cursed in fury, but Han Xuan wasn't the least bit angry.","He grinned, pulling her hand to his lips and pecking it several times. \"There's a reason I was late. Want to know? I'll take you to see it?\"","His expression was full of barely contained excitement and pride. Gu Chacha looked at him doubtfully. \"What mischief have you been up to now?\"","She had asked around—the projects he'd cut were costing their company at least several hundred million in losses.","Wasn't he worried at all?","If he didn't land the East City project, he wouldn't have an easy time.","Did he even know what was urgent and important?","To her surprise, Han Xuan laughed smugly. \"I know what you're worried about, but don't worry. I've gotten involved in a new project that's guaranteed to make money.\"","He leaned in close to Gu Chacha. \"I won't tell anyone else, just you.\"","His secretive demeanor piqued her curiosity. \"What project? Is it worth more than the East City project?\"","Han Xuan's smile grew even more arrogant. \"Much more.\"","Gu Chacha suddenly became interested, sitting up straight. \"What project? Is it reliable?\"","The car roared to life, and Han Xuan's unrestrained voice drifted into the air: \"I'll take you to see it right now. You're going to love it.\"","Meanwhile, in the new mall in the old town.","He Huanhuan sat bored in the conference room, not knowing why Han Mo had insisted on bringing her along.","What was up with him suddenly being so clingy?","She slumped in her chair, leg jiggling. So boring!","The conference room door suddenly swung open, and Han Mo stood smiling at the entrance. \"Bored?\"","He Huanhuan nodded. \"Extremely! Bored!\"","Han Mo asked her, \"Want to go downstairs and look around?\"","He Huanhuan glanced at him. \"Don't you have a meeting to attend?\"","Han Mo smiled and shook his head. \"Just a work handover. You know, I don't have a job right now.\"","That was true.","She had just been wondering—since he'd been pushed out, why would he still have a meeting?","They went from the eleventh floor down to the tenth, which was full of trendy lifestyle stores.","Han Mo looked down at her. \"Want to check them out?\"","He Huanhuan pursed her lips uncomfortably. \"I don't know anything about those.\"","She grew up in the countryside, where there were no such things in the county seat. She'd only seen them online.","Qi Meili and the others really liked them and would occasionally save up to buy one.","She couldn't afford a single one, so she never looked.","When Qi Meili and the others discussed them, she never joined in.","What was there to talk about?","That wasn't a world she could enter.","She only wanted to get a little older, to become an adult, so she could work in a factory.","She heard factory work paid five or six thousand a month.","Five or six thousand—that was a lot of money.","Once the family's debts were paid off, then she could talk about those things with Qi Meili and the others.","Those exquisite, trendy stores—she had never been inside one.","But Han Mo held her hand tighter. \"I don't know them either. Let's go get to know them together.\"","He firmly pulled her hand and step by step led her into the store.","They looked at everything one by one, asking the staff what blind boxes were, what figurines were, what Pop Mart was...","Her heart began to light up little by little. \"This big-eyed one is cute.\"","Han Mo smiled and said, \"Then buy it.\"","\"This one's cute too.\"","\"Buy it too.\"","\"...\"","All day long, they worked their way down from the tenth floor, floor by floor.","Every store she had never been to or dared to enter before—they visited them all.","And they bought from them all.","Everything was packed up and sent to her third-floor room, filling it up.","It was full, full of her preferences, her presence.","Making her never want to leave.","They kept at it until it got dark, and she waved her hands in exhaustion. \"No way, I really can't walk anymore.\"","After walking all day, even an energetic girl gets tired, huh?","Han Mo sat beside her and asked, \"Want to eat malatang?\"","\"Yes!\"","When your body is utterly exhausted, malatang becomes even more irresistible.","She put on a new dress she'd bought and led Han Mo into a malatang shop.","A lolita dress paired with a black suit—very jarring and conspicuous.","But neither of them cared at all.","She pulled Han Mo over to the shelves and told him, \"You know why your malatang last time wasn't good? You have to get the yellow noodles. Using the thin vermicelli won't work—it soaks up too much flavor! And also...\"","She earnestly shared her malatang experience, and Han Mo listened even more seriously.","For everything she said, Han Mo took one.","Until two plastic baskets were piled into identical little mountains.","He Huanhuan nodded with satisfaction. \"That's how you pick it—that's how it tastes good!\"","Han Mo carried the two plastic baskets to the counter to pay.","Two bowls of identical malatang were set on the table, and the two, who had been walking all day, started eating in silence.","A mouthful of yellow noodles, a mouthful of cola.","Bliss!"]},{"number":33,"title":"Chapter 33: Is Your Heart True","paragraphs":["Two bowls of spicy hot pot were soon finished. He Huanhuan happily held the Coke and drank, saying, \"Isn't this little bit incredibly delicious?\"","Han Mo wiped his mouth and nodded with a smile, \"It's quite delicious.\"","His smile was always like this, with the corners of his mouth slightly raised, a very proper smile.","There was a hint of aloofness in the politeness.","He Huanhuan glanced at him and said nothing.","After finishing the spicy hot pot, Han Mo drove her home.","This time, he still accompanied her upstairs.","The living room on the third floor was filled with the things they bought today, so many that there was hardly any space to put one's feet.","Han Mo rolled up his sleeves and said voluntarily, \"Let me help you tidy up.\"","So the two of them began to unpack those so - called blind boxes. He Huanhuan had just gotten to know them today.","Therefore, she was very happy no matter what she unpacked.","\"This is the one with big eyes!\"","\"Yes, it's quite cute.\"","\"This is the one with wings!\"","\"Yes.\"","\"....\"","After unpacking and putting all the things away, the third floor instantly felt more lively.","There were dolls in each room, the dolls that they had seen together, bought together, and unpacked together.","Looking at these dolls, the corners of Han Mo's mouth involuntarily turned up.","This third floor finally seemed like someone was really living here.","Not just staying temporarily, but completely belonging to someone.","He looked down at He Huanhuan and said, \"Then I'll go back first.\"","\"Han Mo.\"","He Huanhuan suddenly called out to him, \"Are you happy today?\"","Han Mo nodded, \"Naturally. Why do you ask?\"","He Huanhuan stared at him, with very complicated emotions in her eyes. \"Why did you take me shopping?\"","Since they started going from floor to floor, she knew that today's goal of Han Mo was this.","To take her shopping, to let her spend money.","To let her buy all the things she thought were good.","To make her happy.","This was his goal today.","But what was the real purpose behind this goal?","To please her? Or to please Old Mr. Gu?","Was the ultimate goal the project in the east city?","The two stared at each other in silence, and that aloof smile returned to his face. \"Your room is too empty. I just wanted to fill it up. That's all.\"","As for the deeper thoughts, did they matter?","Wasn't she happy?","He Huanhuan nodded, \"Okay, I got it.\"","She felt a bit unhappy, but she couldn't tell why.","Wasn't she happy today?","When she got back to the real world, when Qi Meili and the others talked about Pop Mart, she would never be at a loss for words again.","She could have a great chat with them. She could...","She plopped down on the sofa. Damn this wealth! Damn herself!","In the past, when she saw the so - called troubles of the rich on the Internet, she only thought it was so pretentious.","Extremely pretentious.","If you're rich, what else do you have to be unhappy about?","What are you pretending for?","If you're unhappy, just go to work. After working for two days, you won't have any troubles.","Now that she was really living in such a wealthy life, somehow, she was also unhappy.","She was unhappy even when someone spent money on her and someone coaxed her.","Why should she care about his ultimate purpose of coaxing her?","Did it matter?","He really spent money on her.","He helped her ask the shop assistants one by one about the differences between those dolls.","Wasn't that enough?","But she just was unhappy.","\"Ah ah ah...\"","She kicked the air in frustration. What on earth was she unhappy about?","\"Sister Huan, are you pedaling a bicycle?\"","Gu Jinghan's annoying voice sounded. He Huanhuan glared at him angrily, \"What are you doing here?\"","Gu Jinghan grinned and came closer, asking, \"Are you unhappy?\"","He Huanhuan's attitude got even worse, \"None of your business!\"","Gu Jinghan had a really thick skin and kept chasing after her, asking, \"Why? Tell me. Maybe I can help you.\"","He Huanhuan glanced at him. His slovenly appearance made him seem very unreliable.","But she was really unhappy, so she told him what had happened today.","She couldn't help but ask, \"You said, for the project in the east city, he could go to such lengths. What kind of person is he? How could he be like this!\"","But there was a big smile on Gu Jinghan's face. \"Oh, he's really putting a lot of effort into it. Isn't that great!\"","In their circle, arranged marriages were the norm.","People would tacitly act out a play with each other. On festivals, you'd give me a gift, and I'd accompany you home to pretend to be affectionate...","This was already considered quite cooperative.","Gu Jinghan really admired Han Mo for being able to do this.","He propped his chin up and reflected, \"No wonder I can't get close to the eldest sister. I'm still not putting in enough effort.\"","He Huanhuan almost rolled her eyes to the sky. Was this guy here to help her solve her doubts?","He was here to learn!","Did he pay the tuition? And he just started learning?","Was he a sponge?","She kicked Gu Jinghan angrily, \"Get out of here! I'm annoyed just looking at you!\"","What a nuisance!","Gu Jinghan left with a grin. But when he reached the door, he suddenly said seriously, \"Huanhuan, have you ever thought that your unhappiness is because you care. You're starting to care whether his heart is sincere or not.\"","\"What do you mean?\"","Her heart skipped a beat. She looked up at Gu Jinghan, but Gu Jinghan started joking again, \"It means you've grown up. Growing up is great! When you grow up, you can have an arranged marriage~\"","\"Get out!\"","After driving Gu Jinghan out, He Huanhuan lay on the bed angrily.","Involuntarily, Gu Jinghan's words flashed through her mind.","Did she care whether his heart was sincere or not?","She couldn't help but shake her head, trying to shake these thoughts out of her mind.","How could she care about this?","Wasn't Han Mo just trying to please her to please Old Mr. Gu?","She had always known this!","Why should she care about this?","Wasn't she just getting along with him because he was generous and willing to coax her?","What was there for her to be unhappy about?","Right!","There was nothing for her to be unhappy about!","She was just here on vacation to relax. When she got back to the real world, she would almost be an adult.","Then she would have to start working to earn money to pay off debts.","Putting all those meaningless thoughts aside, she lay in bed and told herself.","Just have fun and don't think too much.","All of this here has nothing to do with you.","You're just a sassy girl.","At Chen Yu's place, Han Mo was standing on the balcony making a phone call. The person on the other end of the phone spoke with a thick accent. \"We've made contact. The progress is very smooth. He's very excited and didn't suspect a thing.\"","Han Mo nodded, \"Good. Give him more commission and let him taste the sweetness.\"","The person on the other end hesitated, \"But...\"","\"I'll cover the extra money.\"","\"Okay!\"","After hanging up the phone, Chen Yu walked up to him and handed him a glass of wine. \"It's starting?\"","He tightened his grip on the glass and nodded, \"It should have started a long time ago.\"","Chen Yu looked at him and asked, \"Are you really not going to marry that He Huanhuan?\"","He glanced at Chen Yu coldly, \"My business has nothing to do with others.\"","Chen Yu hesitated, \"But you've tried so hard to please her...\"","Since he had gone to so much trouble to please her, why not just marry her?","Then Old Mr. Gu would trust him more, and it would be more convenient for him to act!","He tightened his grip on the glass even more and looked down towards the east.","The night had completely hidden it. No one knew what kind of hustle and bustle it would become.","\"Chen Yu.\"","He said in a low voice, \"Hatred has nothing to do with marriage.\"","His parents' marriage was a joke. He wouldn't let his own marriage become a joke either.","He could stay single for the rest of his life.","But he would never marry someone he didn't love just for revenge and torture each other."]},{"number":34,"title":"Chapter 34: The Pianist","paragraphs":["Chen Yu naturally understood his meaning from what he said.","He had witnessed the aunt's suffering with his own eyes.","But he couldn't help asking, \"Since that's the case, why did you do that?\"","Why go to such lengths to ingratiate yourself with He Huanhuan?","Was it really necessary to go that far?","This would all be over soon, wouldn't it?","The answer that came was a long silence.","\"Since I've started it, I have to do it properly.\"","He emphasized coldly, \"I've always been serious about everything I do, haven't I?\"","He couldn't afford to lose. He couldn't let his mother die so humiliatingly.","He had to take back what belonged to his mother, and being serious was only natural.","The tips of his fingers gripping the wine glass turned white from the strain as he downed the drink in one gulp.","\"No more waiting. Let's begin.\"","Chen Yu raised an eyebrow at him. \"That soon?\"","He replied in a low voice, \"I don't want to wait anymore.\"","He had waited long enough, long enough to lose all patience.","A reckless face flashed through his mind, and he wanted to be reckless too.","Let's begin. He truly couldn't wait a moment longer.","In the following days, Han Mo clocked in like he was going to work.","Every morning, he would arrive early at the Gu residence, spend an hour chatting with Old Mr. Gu on the first floor,","then take He Huanhuan out to eat, drink, and have fun, letting her do whatever she wanted.","The theme was pure indulgence.","Until half a month later, in the top-floor office of the Han Group, Meng Yu stood before the desk with a grim face. \"President Han, a few of the projects you suspended before—they're coming to hold us accountable...\"","Han Xuan snorted coldly. \"Let them come. Don't bother with them.\"","Meng Yu's face grew even more pained. \"We'll have to pay compensation.\"","Han Xuan laughed scornfully. \"Do you think I'm stupid?\"","Pay just like that?","These projects would drag on for at least a year or two before anything got settled.","Let them drag on. Stall for a year first.","As for a year later...","Hmph, by then, he wouldn't be the same person he was now.","Meng Yu handed over the documents, trying to explain. \"But—\"","\"Don't you get tired of nagging?\"","Han Xuan shot him a glare. \"Can't you understand what I'm saying? Can't you handle such a small task?\"","\"But—\"","Before he could explain, Han Xuan waved his hand impatiently. \"Get out. Don't bother me.\"","With his attitude so hostile, Meng Yu had no choice but to leave, feeling utterly dejected.","Standing at the office door, Meng Yu's head throbbed with worry.","Did this spoiled brat even know what he was doing?","The projects that Senior Han had managed—back then, to secure them smoothly, the company had already prepaid the penalties!","The moment Han Xuan took over, he suspended all those projects, which meant paying out those penalty fees!","That was real money!","Didn't he care?","It added up to several hundred million!","As far as he remembered, that was about all the liquid cash the company had on hand.","If it all got drained away...","God!","Meng Yu took a deep breath. He wanted to quit.","Could someone just fire him already?","He wanted that severance package!","Han Xuan knew nothing of all this. No one had even mentioned it to him.","He sat in his office, staring anxiously into space.","He was waiting for a call. Once that call came, his life would turn around!","\"Ring, ring, ring~~\"","The phone rang, and his eyes lit up instantly!","He gripped the phone tightly and swiped to answer with urgency. \"Hello? Hello?\"","The voice on the other end, like music to his ears, delivered the news he had been waiting for.","\"Really?\"","He couldn't contain his excitement. \"When do we sign?\"","The accented Chinese voice replied coldly, \"Anytime, but you'll need to fly over here. Our people can't go to you.\"","\"Fine! I'll go tomorrow!\"","Hanging up, he immediately called Gu Chacha. \"Chacha, come with me to Southeast Asia tomorrow.\"","Gu Chacha hesitated. \"Tomorrow? Is it that urgent?\"","Han Xuan laughed triumphantly. \"They agreed to our terms! What do you think—urgent or not?\"","Gu Chacha sat up in surprise. \"Really?\"","\"A hundred percent real!\"","That evening, the two of them went back to the same hotel and booked the same presidential suite.","Clothes were strewn everywhere. The thick smell of smoke mixed with the aroma of liquor as they danced drunkenly on the carpet.","Han Xuan slurred, wrapping his arms around Gu Chacha. \"Chacha! I'm going to make you a pianist! Even Lang Lang will have to call you a master!\"","A pianist. A world tour.","An international reputation. Piano master Gu Chacha.","Her vision grew blurry, but her heart pounded faster and faster. She clung to Han Xuan. \"I know you can do it. I believe in you.\"","Wait until tomorrow. Just wait until tomorrow.","After a night of indulgence, they caught the early flight to Southeast Asia the next morning.","At ten o'clock, He Huanhuan woke up on time and went downstairs.","Downstairs, Han Mo and Old Mr. Gu had already moved on to talking about Labubu...","Han Mo explained earnestly, \"Labubu is very popular among young people lately. It's...\"","Old Mr. Gu listened even more attentively, nodding occasionally. \"Young people always like trendy things. I'm old, can't keep up with the fads anymore.\"","\"Not at all.\"","Han Mo smiled. \"You have experience and a steady eye. We still have a lot to learn from you.\"","His words pleased Old Mr. Gu so much that his eyes crinkled with laughter.","\"You really know how to talk, kid. At my age, having a bit of experience is normal, hahahaha...\"","He Huanhuan was speechless. Had Han Mo been a traitor in a past life or something?","He was way too good at flattering people.","When she came downstairs, Han Mo stood up with a smile. \"You're up?\"","She nodded and walked over to him. \"What are we doing today?\"","She was getting numb from all the spending.","She seriously wondered if she'd be able to adapt to a poor life again after returning to the real world.","Money really corrupted people!","She thought today would be another day of having fun spending money.","But instead, Han Mo drove her to a desolate place surrounded by dry reeds stretching as far as the eye could see.","She looked at him, puzzled. \"What's this? Are you planning to kill me and dump the body?\"","She had come out with him directly—the police wouldn't even need to investigate to nail him.","Han Mo smiled and handed her a sandwich. \"Breakfast.\"","As she bit into the sandwich, a plane flew far overhead, passing rapidly across the sky.","Han Mo stood silently, watching the plane grow smaller and smaller until it disappeared.","\"He Huanhuan,\" he called softly.","He Huanhuan looked at him, sandwich in mouth. \"What's up?\"","Their eyes met, and Han Mo asked seriously, \"You're annoyed by me, aren't you?\"","All that fake concern, all those rejected favors.","She must be utterly fed up with him, right?","He Huanhuan took a big bite of her sandwich. \"Why would I be annoyed by you?\"","Without him, her days would be just as boring. Maybe even more so.","Plus, she wouldn't have had the chance to spend money so freely. Without him footing the bill, she wouldn't have been reckless enough to shop like a madwoman.","After all, her poverty mindset hadn't worn off yet.","She was certain—she wasn't annoyed by him.","But Han Mo acted as if he hadn't heard her, muttering to himself, \"It'll all be over soon. You won't have to be bothered by me anymore.\"","He Huanhuan was exasperated. Hadn't she just spoken perfectly clear Mandarin?","Hadn't she just said she wasn't annoyed?","Why was he acting like she had thoroughly despised him?","She shoved the last bite of the sandwich into her mouth, then suddenly reached out and grabbed his face between her hands. \"I said I'm not annoyed by you. Don't be so insecure, okay?\""]},{"number":35,"title":"Chapter 35: He Huanhuan, Are You Cheating","paragraphs":["After standing outside for a while, her hands had grown a little cold.","She pressed her cool hands against his cheeks, freezing him in place.","\"I really don't find you annoying, you hear me?\"","She repeated herself, her eyes full of sincerity.","Han Mo nodded involuntarily. \"I understand.\"","Of course he knew. Although she seemed hot-tempered, deep down she was a kind-hearted person.","The first time they ate malatang, he had felt quite repulsed.","She had noticed the moment she saw it, and without a word, she ate his bowl of malatang for him.","She knew he was trying to get along with her; if she had asked him to, he would have finished the bowl no matter how much he disliked it.","But she didn't. She just told him to wait outside.","He lowered his eyes and said nothing more.","The plane had taken off; everything was on track.","He wouldn't have to bother her anymore. All he had to do now was wait.","But the words lingered on his lips for a long time, until finally he said, \"Want some malatang?\"","He Huanhuan gave him a speechless glance. \"You did that on purpose, didn't you?\"","If there was malatang, why had she been eating a sandwich?","After the sandwich, how could she still eat malatang?","Han Mo chuckled. \"It's okay. Let's just walk around first. We can eat when we're hungry.\"","When he said walk, he meant walking.","The two of them strolled silently down the road, as if someone were chasing them.","After an hour of walking, He Huanhuan couldn't take it anymore. \"I actually don't love walking that much...\"","Back when she walked for hours every day, she had no choice—she couldn't afford a cab, so her legs were all she had.","Now that we're both doing better, can we please stop walking?","She puffed out her cheeks and glared at Han Mo, but he simply took her hand and asked, \"Hungry? Want some malatang?\"","The sudden hand-holding caught He Huanhuan off guard.","Hold on, that was way too natural, wasn't it?","This...","\"Yeah, let's eat.\"","Hand in hand, they walked into the malatang shop, only to run into an acquaintance.","\"Let go of her hand!\"","Liang Ye shouted, his mouth still full of food.","He stared at their linked hands, utterly crushed. \"He Huanhuan, how could you cheat on me?\"","The other customers in the shop pricked up their ears.","A live cheating scene!","They even forgot their food, instantly zeroing in on He Huanhuan and Han Mo.","One look at Han Mo, then another at Liang Ye, and their sympathies leaned toward Han Mo. With someone that handsome, was it really her fault for cheating? Who could resist a face that good and a figure that stunning?","He Huanhuan shot Liang Ye a disgusted look. \"When was I ever with you?\"","She grabbed two plastic baskets and started picking her ingredients. She always chose the same favorites, quickly finished, and handed them to Han Mo to pay.","She plopped down beside Liang Ye and asked, \"What are you doing here?\"","Liang Ye sniffled. \"This is the place you took me to! You forgot?\"","He gazed at her with puppy-dog eyes. \"Every time I miss you, I come here for a meal. Miss you, eat one, and after I eat, I miss you even more...\"","He Huanhuan couldn't help rolling her eyes. \"You come here because it's cheap, right?\"","\"Hehehe...\"","Liang Ye laughed guiltily. \"That's part of it too~\"","Cheap and tasty—it was addictive.","He would eat it every day if he could.","He picked up a chopstickful of yellow noodles and ate it with obvious relish, looking completely ordinary.","Nothing like a rich second-generation heir.","After paying, Han Mo brought the number tag and sat down next to He Huanhuan.","Liang Ye immediately scowled. \"You eat malatang too?\"","Wasn't Han Mo the type to take girls to fancy French restaurants to show off?","Malatang—was that even something he understood?","Han Mo sat up straight. \"Can't I eat it?\"","Liang Ye sneered. \"Do you even know how to appreciate malatang, Mr. Spoiled Rich Boy?\"","The title \"Mr. Spoiled Rich Boy\" was dripping with sarcasm, making Han Mo laugh. \"Second Young Master Liang, compared to you, the Han family is hardly worth mentioning.\"","The Han family had pulled themselves up from rags, but the Liang family was old money—genuine blue blood.","Liang Ye calling him a rich boy? How ridiculous.","Liang Ye frowned. \"But I don't waste money. My heart is ordinary. I'm just an ordinary person!\"","He lived in an old, run-down apartment in the city center and relied on cabs for transport.","Well, no, now he relied on bumming rides.","He ate cheap food and did grunt work.","He wasn't some Second Young Master!","He was just as ordinary as ordinary could be.","Han Mo snorted. \"Keep telling yourself that, Second Young Master Liang.\"","\"You!\"","Liang Ye was furious. He turned to He Huanhuan. \"See how classless he is? You can't be with him.\"","He Huanhuan shot him another glare. \"When did I ever say I was with him?\"","And besides, why couldn't she be with him?","Old Mr. Gu had given Han Mo to her, so she could be with him or not as she pleased.","Liang Ye didn't believe her. \"You two were holding hands just now, and you say you're not together?\"","He Huanhuan smiled sweetly. \"My hand was itchy. He was scratching it for me.\"","Liang Ye was speechless: Did she think he was that much of an idiot?","He looked at her, wounded. \"We've exchanged saliva before. You can't just be a heartbreaker...\"","\"Exchanged saliva?\"","Han Mo's brow instantly furrowed. He turned to He Huanhuan. \"You two have kissed?\"","Liang Ye grinned triumphantly. \"Even more intimate than kissing!\"","She had drunk the coffee he spat out!","That was way more meaningful than a simple kiss!","He Huanhuan: ...Planet Earth, just end it already. I'm tired.","She really couldn't be bothered to explain, but if she didn't, there was no telling what crazy things Liang Ye would blurt out next.","\"That day you sent me to the blind date, remember? He ordered coffee...\"","Liang Ye nodded sweetly beside her. \"That's right... that's right. Huanhuan, you remember so clearly. You really do have me in your heart!\"","Han Mo listened with a deepening frown. \"You call that exchanging saliva?\"","Wasn't it just drinking someone else's spit?","Liang Ye insisted it was saliva exchange.","It was love!","The love between him and He Huanhuan.","He glared fiercely at Han Mo. \"Don't you dare try to ruin the bond between us. Take back your dirty money. Huanhuan doesn't need your cash.\"","......","He Huanhuan wanted to cuss. Who said she didn't need that money?","For crying out loud!","She needed money like crazy!","She was a slave to cash!","\"You're such a pain in the...\"","Before she could finish, Han Mo took her hand again.","Right in front of Liang Ye.","He sat back comfortably on the big red plastic stool and shot Liang Ye a blatantly provocative look. \"You say I'm ruining your relationship? I spent over two weeks at the Gu residence and never saw you there once.\"","Liang Ye said matter-of-factly, \"Of course I wasn't at the Gu house. The cab fare there is too expensive—I couldn't bring myself to spend it.\"","......","\"Then what kind of relationship did you and Huanhuan ever have?\"","Liang Ye smiled dreamily. \"I send her friend requests every day! And in those request notes, I wrote all sorts of sweet words~\"","......","Both of them fell silent.","So did the eavesdropping customers in the shop.","You can't even be WeChat friends, and you're calling her a cheater?","What kind of weirdo was this?"]},{"number":36,"title":"Chapter 36: I Like Beautiful Women","paragraphs":["With Liang Ye around, the two of them ate in much greater silence.","It wasn’t that they were worried about him overhearing—it was that he talked way too much.","The moment Han Mo opened his mouth to say, “Later, do you want to—”","Liang Ye immediately cut in: “Later, what are you two up to? Take me with you! I’ve got the day off, and I’m free anyway. I was feeling kinda bored this morning...”","He Huanhuan gave him a sweet smile. “We’re planning to go shopping. Are you going to pay for me?”","He shut up at once. “Uh, yeah, I think I have to go back to the neighborhood committee for some overtime this afternoon...”","He Huanhuan raised an eyebrow at Han Mo. See? That’s how you handle him.","Han Mo smiled and gave her a little nod. You’ve got experience.","Their silent exchange made Liang Ye’s teeth ache with jealousy.","A few days apart, and now they could send each other telegrams with their eyes.","Hmph!","This Han Mo—jobless as he was—still couldn’t stay in his lane!","If he wasn’t careful, Liang Ye might get competitive and start spending money on He Huanhuan too!","He, he, he... he’d buy her...","Damn it!","He couldn’t bear to part with his money!","He sulkily finished his spicy hot pot, then shot Han Mo a dirty look. “Save your money, alright? Is your family loaded or something?”","Han Mo nodded. “Okay.”","Damn!","He clearly wasn’t taking it seriously!","Liang Ye fumed inwardly.","This man was such a poser. If he ended up spending all that money and He Huanhuan still didn’t end up with him, just wait—he’d regret it!","He stomped off in a huff. “I’m going back to work overtime!”","The two watched him leave. He Huanhuan was baffled. “His family is that rich, so why is he so stingy?”","Han Mo explained quietly, “I heard he was raised by his grandparents.”","The older generation in his family had lived through the hardships of war and the turbulent years that followed.","As a result, they were extremely frugal.","Without realizing it, those habits passed down to the kids.","When Liang Ye was little, these traits weren’t so obvious.","He was just more careful with money and didn’t like waste.","His parents thought it was a good thing and praised him plenty.","But as he grew up, his eccentricities started to show.","He refused to live in the family estate, and he hated when the driver picked him up from school.","If any classmate saw that, he’d be overcome with embarrassment.","He’d want to dig a hole and crawl into it.","As soon as he graduated college, he moved straight into a run-down old apartment in the city and happily played the part of an ordinary broke guy.","He Huanhuan was speechless. Life! It was truly absurd.","Some people went crazy trying to become rich but failed, while others were born into wealth and didn’t want it.","What a damn joke.","If they didn’t want to be rich, they could let her take over!","She sure knew how!","After finishing the spicy hot pot, she thought Han Mo would keep taking her shopping.","But to her surprise, he actually drove her straight home?!","What did that mean?","Was her free shopping spree over?","As she got out of the car, she looked at Han Mo. “Don’t you have anything to say to me?”","Han Mo had been off today—strange since this morning.","He reached out and patted her head. “I might be a bit busy tomorrow. Let me take the day off.”","His tone and expression were no different from usual, but He Huanhuan suddenly felt it.","Han Mo wasn’t coming back.","This weird relationship between them was about to end.","She couldn’t help frowning, a complicated surge of emotion welling up inside her.","She watched Han Mo get into the car, ready to leave.","“Han Mo!”","She yanked open the car door and looked at him in the driver’s seat. “You...”","“What’s wrong?”","He looked up at her.","But she abruptly closed the door again. “Nothing. Drive safe.”","She silently cursed herself. What was she doing?","This was a book world, after all!","How could she feel attached to a character in a book?","She lay down on the bed, not wanting to get up at all.","Her mind was swirling with complex emotions—her own scrutiny of this world, of herself.","And a vague uncertainty about the future.","At first, she had only thought this was a dream, a beautiful one at that.","When the dream ended, she would still be that free-spirited girl He Huanhuan.","He Huanhuan, waiting to come of age.","But the longer she stayed here, the more real everything became.","She turned her head toward the bedside table. Three Labubu dolls sat there, grinning mischievously at her.","Han Mo had taken her to buy those.","Her gaze drifted to the wardrobe, stuffed full of all kinds of clothes.","All of them had been bought over these days, piece by piece, as Han Mo took her to try them on.","There were pretty Lolita dresses, casual jeans, and elegant halter maxi dresses.","Anything she thought looked good, he bought for her.","She suddenly realized how full her room had become.","When had it started filling up?","She couldn’t remember. Every day, they bought a little more, added a little more, until the room was suddenly packed.","But the person who had helped fill that room might never come again.","She lay flat on her back and laughed out loud.","“Damn! Rich people sure know how to play the game.”","At that moment, somewhere in Southeast Asia, Gu Chacha and Han Xuan sat in a second-floor office, watching the people downstairs twitch as electric shocks hit them.","“Don’t worry, our standards here are strict. If performance doesn’t meet the target, they get a lesson,” said the dark-faced middle-aged man, sizing up Gu Chacha. “Don’t be scared. You won’t get shocked.”","Gu Chacha couldn’t help shrinking back. She didn’t like the way he looked at her.","Like a sticky snake, cold and oppressive.","But Han Xuan didn’t notice a thing. He pulled her close, looking openly at the man. “Of course I trust you. Otherwise, we wouldn’t have come.”","He rubbed his thumb and forefinger together. “Aren’t we signing the contract? I can’t wait!”","The man glanced at Gu Chacha again, then broke into a big smile. “We’ll sign the contract, of course. But since we’re helping Miss Gu arrange her tour, would you mind playing us a tune?”","His oppressive gaze fixed on her, making her skin crawl.","She frowned, about to refuse, but Han Xuan beat her to it. “Of course she can! Gu Chacha’s piano was taught by a world-class master!”","“Han Xuan!”","She shoved him in annoyance. She didn’t want to play.","She had come to help him sign the contract and discuss the tour details.","She wasn’t a cheap performer.","Han Xuan bent down and kissed her. “Just one piece, okay? Let them see what we’ve got. Be good, won’t you?”","“But...”","She hesitated for a moment, but ultimately couldn’t withstand that oppressive stare and nodded.","Cheerful, flowing piano notes rang out across the compound, mixing with the wails of those people.","Beautiful and despairing.","Gu Chacha sat upright at the piano, playing with total focus.","She was starting to regret it. This place was too dangerous. She shouldn’t have come.","She shouldn’t have put herself in harm’s way.","The dark-faced man walked over and leaned close to her. “Miss Gu, do you know? You’re very beautiful. Very beautiful.”","Gu Chacha’s body tensed even more. Her eyes desperately darted to the side.","Where was Han Xuan?","What was he doing?","“Don’t be afraid,” the man chuckled softly. “I won’t hurt you. I like beautiful things. Especially beautiful women.”"]},{"number":37,"title":"Chapter 37: Personal Piano Recital","paragraphs":["When he said that, Gu Chacha grew even more anxious.","How terrifying it was to be liked by him!","She wanted to go back to her home country—now, immediately, right this second!","Just as she was about to break down, the man suddenly straightened up and put on a very proper expression. \"That was wonderful piano playing. Surely anyone who loves art would appreciate it.\"","He reached out and touched the piano's body. \"Such beautiful music deserves a world tour performance. Don't you think?\"","A world tour performance?","Gu Chacha's heart stirred, and all her fear and panic instantly vanished.","She looked up sharply at the man. \"You agreed?\"","The man laughed boldly. \"Miss Gu, you deserve it.\"","Of course she knew she deserved it, but...","She offered him a gentle smile. \"Thank you for your appreciation. I won't let you down.\"","His smile widened. \"Miss Gu, you just focus on performing well. That'll be enough.\"","They stayed in Southeast Asia for three days. By the time they returned home, a flood of articles about her had suddenly appeared online.","Articles introducing her family, her piano teacher, her awards.","She became popular overnight. Some netizens bought into it, envying her perfect life—beautiful, wealthy, elegant. What window had God closed for her?","Others were skeptical, saying they had never heard of her before and that she was just another privileged elite trying to cash in on ordinary people.","But whether people bought it or not, in just a few days, her reputation was out there.","That was enough.","Her first piano concert in Jiangcheng was quickly put together.","After being away for a few days, aside from a few perfunctory calls pretending to care, there was nothing else waiting for her at home.","Once the concert plans were confirmed, she rushed back to the Gu family home with Han Xuan.","At the Gu residence, Jiang Yulan was sipping tea and sighing to Gu Chengye:","\"What do you think Chacha is up to now? I've been calling her these past few days, but she hardly picks up, and when she does, she hangs up after a few words...\"","After all, she had raised Chacha herself. Even knowing now that she wasn't her biological daughter, her love hadn't changed.","Twenty years of care had long been ingrained in her bones.","How could it just disappear overnight?","But the girl was sensitive—any careless word could make her cry.","A few days ago, she said she was in a bad mood and wanted to travel, so Jiang Yulan hadn't dared to ask too many questions.","She could only call her now and then to make sure she was safe.","But lately, it seemed Chacha had lost patience with her, cutting calls short after just a few sentences.","Worry had finally pushed Jiang Yulan to ask Gu Chengye today, \"Do you think Chacha resents me? Losing the child back then really was my fault...\"","\"What nonsense are you saying!\"","Gu Chengye patted her hand. \"What happened back then was entirely an accident. You didn't know. How could it be your fault?\"","\"Chacha is just in a bad mood. Let her think things through. She'll come around.\"","Just as the couple were talking, Gu Chacha walked in with Han Xuan.","Seeing them, she beamed brightly. \"Mom! Dad! Have you had lunch yet?\"","She looked cheerful and radiant, which left Jiang Yulan puzzled. \"Not yet... Chacha, you...\"","The girl had been so downcast before. How had her mood suddenly improved so much?","Gu Chacha laughed, stepped forward, and looped her arm through Jiang Yulan's. \"Mom, Han Xuan and I ordered some dishes. Let's all have a nice family lunch today!\"","\"Huh?\"","Jiang Yulan instinctively looked at Gu Chengye. Old Mr. Gu’s face was expressionless as he stared at the two of them. \"You two came here together?\"","Gu Chacha pretended not to read his expression and replied with a smile, \"I was in a bad mood a few days ago, so Han Xuan took me out to relax for a few days.\"","Old Mr. Gu's brow furrowed deeper, his eyes filled with displeasure. \"You two went out together?\"","He remembered telling Chacha that Han Xuan wasn't acceptable.","He shot her a sharp look. \"Chacha, have you forgotten what I told you?\"","Gu Chacha ignored him, sitting down beside him with a smile. \"Dad, I have great news to share today~\"","Gu Chengye's face remained stern. \"What great news?\"","Gu Chacha playfully wrinkled her nose. \"Can't say yet. I'll announce it at lunch when everyone's here~\"","With that, she cheerfully bounded upstairs like a little songbird to find He Huanhuan and Gu Jinghan.","Gu Jingchen was already at the office, so she called him and insisted he come home for lunch.","Her seriousness made everyone curious. What was this great news that had transformed her into such a bright and cheerful person?","Hadn't she been relentless in targeting He Huanhuan just a while ago?","How had it all suddenly blown over?","The sudden display of family harmony was so abrupt.","Gu Jinghan whispered to He Huanhuan on the sly, \"You don't think she's going to announce that she's marrying Han Xuan at lunch, do you?\"","He Huanhuan frowned. \"Can't be. The old man wouldn't agree to that.\"","Anyone could see that Old Mr. Gu disliked Han Xuan. Why would Gu Chacha provoke him like that? There was nothing to gain.","Suddenly, He Huanhuan remembered seeing a video of Gu Chacha on her phone last night.","She leaned closer to Gu Jinghan and murmured, \"You don't think Han Xuan paid for her promotion to become an influencer, and that's why she's fully committed to him?\"","She quickly dismissed the idea herself. Even if Han Xuan pushed her into becoming an influencer, what did it matter?","Ordinary social media influencers didn't make much money—barely enough for Gu Chacha to buy a few bags.","Why would she risk upsetting Old Mr. Gu for that?","The two could only guess and wait for lunch.","At eleven thirty, their eldest brother Gu Jingchen arrived home, and lunch officially began.","As soon as everyone was seated, Gu Chacha eagerly raised her glass. \"I'd like to toast all of you—to my past foolishness and the trouble I've caused...\"","Her words were considerate and mature, making Jiang Yulan's eyes tear up. \"Chacha, you will always be my good daughter.\"","She knew it—Chacha was always the sensible one!","Gu Chacha glanced at Jiang Yulan, her face full of smiles. \"Mom, don't cry. Smile! Be happy for me.\"","\"After all, I'm about to hold my own personal piano concert~\"","\"What?\"","Jiang Yulan couldn't quite process it. \"Piano concert? What piano concert?\"","Gu Chacha grinned proudly. \"A piano concert, Mom. By the end of this month, I'm going to have my very own solo piano concert. You'll all have to come and support me~\"","Gu Chengye frowned slightly. \"Where did you get the money?\"","In Jiangcheng, putting on a solo concert cost at least one million yuan.","Not that it was a huge sum, but solo concerts of this kind hardly made any ticket revenue.","Over a million would go in without making a splash.","Where had she gotten the money?"]},{"number":38,"title":"Chapter 38: Do You Accept This Son-in-Law","paragraphs":["\"Uncle, don't worry. I'll take care of the money!\"","Han Xuan said with great generosity, \"Jiang City is just an appetizer. In the future, Chacha's concerts will be held all over the country—no, all over the world!\"","His words were outrageously arrogant, and Gu Chengye's brow furrowed even tighter on the spot.","\"Where are you getting the money from?\"","Since when did Han Changyong have this much money?","He had no idea.","Han Xuan raised an eyebrow with a smug air. \"Uncle, just rest assured. I have a friend who works in investments. He really loves art and has great faith in Chacha!\"","He smiled and looked at Gu Chacha. \"Isn't that right, Chacha?\"","Gu Chacha nodded cheerfully. \"Yes, he's fully sponsoring my concert tour.\"","Old Mr. Gu stared at Gu Chacha and asked, \"Who is that person? What's his name? What does he do? Why is he sponsoring you?\"","No one willingly makes a losing deal unless there's profit to be gained.","A global tour costs an enormous amount of money.","What was that person after?","Could Chacha afford to satisfy his greed?","All eyes fell on Gu Chacha, and Gu Jingchen's gaze was equally demanding.","Gu Chacha couldn't help but feel a surge of annoyance inwardly. The Gu family wasn't short on money.","Yet over the years, her father and her older brother had never thought to support her career.","Not a tour—not even a single solo concert had they ever considered arranging for her.","Had they ever thought about her future?","Not at all.","Now that she'd found her own path, they came asking how she got there.","They asked if that man was reliable...","Did it matter?","Whether he was reliable or not, she had already made her choice. There was no turning back.","And she didn't want to turn back. She wanted to rise above; she wanted to become a world-renowned pianist.","She wanted to completely break free from this family's constraints. She didn't want to be just a daughter of this family!","She lowered her head and didn't directly answer Old Mr. Gu's question. Instead, she smiled and asked him, \"Dad, aren't you happy for me?\"","Gu Chengye's face was cold. \"Dad really wants to be happy for you, but you need to give Dad peace of mind.\"","Gu Chacha kept her head down and said nothing. Old Mr. Gu was about to press further, but Han Xuan cut in while jiggling his leg.","\"Oh, Dad, don't worry! That's my friend—completely reliable! There's absolutely no problem!\"","The word \"Dad\" made Gu Chengye's face instantly darken. \"Xiaoxuan, what did you call me?\"","\"Dad!\"","Han Xuan stood up with a grin, pulled Gu Chacha into a hug, and announced to everyone, \"Chacha and I are together now. From now on, we're family!\"","His flippant attitude made all present frown. Old Mr. Gu's face was as dark as dripping ink.","He looked at Gu Chacha with a gloomy expression. \"Chacha, is that true?\"","Gu Chacha pursed her lips and smiled. \"Dad, Han Xuan is a good person, and he treats me well. We'll be happy together.\"","She blinked and looked at Old Mr. Gu eagerly. \"Dad, you'll support us, right?\"","The muscles in Old Mr. Gu's cheek twitched. He gritted out through clenched teeth, \"This is your own choice. Dad naturally respects that.\"","But support and blessings—absolutely not.","Yet Han Xuan seemed completely unaware of the underlying tone. He grinned and asked Old Mr. Gu, \"Dad, since we're family now, how about bringing me in on the East City project?\"","Even He Huanhuan was stunned. She leaned over to Gu Jinghan and asked loudly, \"Is this how you rich folks negotiate projects?\"","Gu Jinghan rubbed his ears. \"At that volume, do you really need to whisper?\"","Was she trying to deafen him?","\"Haha...\"","Old Mr. Gu let out a dry laugh and took the chance to explain to He Huanhuan, \"Today is a family dinner, so naturally we won't discuss work matters.\"","He then dropped the smile and said to Han Xuan, \"I'm old now. About company matters, you'll have to talk to Jingchen later.\"","Han Xuan immediately zeroed in on Gu Jingchen. \"Brother, you've got to let me in on the fun.\"","Gu Jingchen didn't even lift his eyes. \"If you want to get involved, send me the proposal through my secretary. I'll take a look when I have time.\"","The coldness was palpable.","Han Xuan gritted his molars. \"Fine.\"","What a Gu family. What a Gu Jingchen. They looked down on him like this, did they?","Just wait.","Once he made it big, they'd all come begging him to include them!","A flicker of resentment quickly rose in his eyes. His movements became noticeably rougher as he sat down.","The chair scraped against the floor with a harsh screech, showing his displeasure.","But Gu Jingchen acted as if he hadn't heard a thing, sitting expressionlessly as he ate.","After a few bites, he wiped his mouth, stood up, and said, \"You all keep eating. I'm heading back to the company.\"","Without waiting for Han Xuan to respond, he turned and left.","Han Xuan grew even more resentful. His brow almost pressed down to his eyes. He stood up as well. \"I think I've had enough too. I'm off.\"","Without waiting for the Gu couple to say a word, he turned and left too.","Old Mr. Gu's face darkened once more.","He gripped his chopsticks and let out a heavy sigh. \"Chacha, is this your choice?\"","Someone with no manners at all—what did she see in him?","Gu Chacha gave an awkward smile. \"Dad, Han Xuan was really looking forward to today's family dinner. It's just that you...\"","Her gaze swept over everyone present, her eyes full of grievance.","This was her first time formally bringing her boyfriend home for a meal, and what kind of attitude did they show?","None of them took this seriously. They weren't warm to Han Xuan at all.","Was this how they treated a prospective son-in-law?","Of course Han Xuan would be upset.","\"You!\"","Old Mr. Gu was furious. How could she not understand why he was so upset?","If she'd just brought home a reliable boyfriend, would he have acted like this?","He took a deep breath, struggling to calm down, and spoke patiently to Gu Chacha. \"I don't know why you chose Han Xuan, but that man won't amount to anything. You'd better break it off with him as soon as possible.\"","\"Dad!\"","Gu Chacha glared at Old Mr. Gu in displeasure. \"Why don't you have faith in me? Is it because I'm not really a child of this family? Because I don't carry your blood? Is that why you dislike me so much?\"","This was her first time bringing up this matter herself, and it was over a man like that.","Old Mr. Gu felt a sharp pang in his heart. \"Child, what nonsense are you talking! You grew up right under your father's eyes. How could your father not love you? It's Han Xuan who...\"","He wanted to explain, but Gu Chacha wouldn't listen.","She was full of hope for that bright future ahead, and she didn't want anyone to ruin her good mood.","She slapped her chopsticks heavily onto the table. \"Dad, I am determined to be with Han Xuan. I'll only ask you one thing: Are you willing to accept him as your son-in-law?\"","\"Chacha?\"","Gu Chengye looked at his daughter in disbelief. His most well-behaved daughter was actually threatening him over a man like this?","Gu Chacha straightened her back, sitting stiffly on the chair. \"Dad, will you accept him or not?\"","Gu Chengye took a deep breath and clenched his fists. \"If you insist on being with him, how could your father not accept it?\"","After all, she was a daughter raised by him and Yulan with their own hands."]},{"number":39,"title":"Chapter 39: Got It","paragraphs":["Seeing him concede, Gu Chacha immediately pressed further: “Dad, could you let Han Xuan in on the East City project?”","“Chacha!”","Gu Chengye’s brows furrowed tightly: “Do you even know what you’re saying?”","Gu Chacha bit her lower lip: “Dad, just bring Han Xuan along. He’ll perform well.”","Gu Chengye looked at her: “Do you really think he will?”","Gu Chacha nodded eagerly: “He definitely will. Dad, please give him a chance.”","“Hmph...”","Gu Chengye let out a laugh: “Chacha... you child has no heart...”","“Dad...”","Gu Chacha tried to persuade him further, but Gu Chengye waved her off: “Tell Han Xuan to contact your brother.”","Gu Chacha’s eyes lit up instantly: “Dad! Does that mean you agreed?”","She jumped up in delight: “I’ll go tell Han Xuan right now! He’ll be so happy!”","She ran out cheerfully, only to find that Han Xuan hadn’t left at all.","He was leaning against the car, smoking one cigarette after another.","Gu Chacha strutted over, snatched the cigarette from his mouth, and tossed it away: “It stinks. Don’t ever smoke in front of me again.”","Her tone was light and joyful, making Han Xuan raise an eyebrow: “It worked?”","Gu Chacha’s smile widened: “Dad said to go find big brother. Remember to be a bit more humble with him.”","Han Xuan frowned: “Why do I have to deal with your brother too?”","Gu Chacha grabbed his arm and coaxed him: “The company’s under big brother’s management now, so you’ll have to interact with him sooner or later!”","Han Xuan curled his lip: “But I really can’t stand his attitude! Just like Han Mo—such a poser!”","Still, being able to join the East City project lifted his mood considerably.","Opening the car door, he raised an eyebrow at Gu Chacha: “Want to go to the usual spot to celebrate?”","Their gazes met in the air, and Gu Chacha smiled shyly: “Sure~”","At the dinner table, the four of them sat in silence.","He Huanhuan kept helping herself to dishes, utterly unbothered.","“Sigh...”","Old Mr. Gu sighed: “How did Chacha turn out like this?”","She used to be the most sensible little darling—when did she stop being so warm?","He didn’t know that Gu Chacha had never truly been warm.","Her coquettishness, her thoughtfulness—everything came from her own needs.","Back then, it was to spend the family’s money and enjoy the privileges they gave her.","Later, it was to edge out He Huanhuan and keep playing the part of the good daughter.","So she never lost her temper; she was considerate, filial, gentle, and sweet.","And Gu Chengye was the pillar of the family.","He held the family’s financial lifeline.","Naturally, he was also the first person Gu Chacha had always tried to please.","But in recent days, Gu Chacha had found a new direction—someone willing to spend money to support her and pay for her life.","So she no longer wanted to carefully appease Old Mr. Gu like before.","Old Mr. Gu let out a dejected sigh, and Jiang Yulan sighed along with him.","Gu Jinghan and He Huanhuan couldn’t sympathize at all.","Ever since He Huanhuan arrived at the Gu family, Gu Chacha had targeted her countless times—picking fights, being sarcastic, trying to embarrass her...","Not hitting her was already He Huanhuan’s idea of being polite.","As for Gu Jinghan, he had never liked this younger sister.","He disliked her from the bottom of his heart.","The moment Gu Chacha spoke, he found it unbearable.","He didn’t even know why himself.","Oh no, he knew it now—because this person was not his sister at all!","Gu Chacha was very sensitive by nature and had known since she was young that Gu Jinghan didn’t like her.","So once she was old enough to understand things, she realized her second brother wasn’t someone she needed to win over.","Since they weren’t allies, that made them opponents.","From childhood on, she’d used her sweet and innocent act to set Gu Jinghan up countless times.","She’d made him take the blame for her and get beaten more than once.","Their relationship could only be described as hostile, like fire and water.","So the two of them just ate in silence, completely unable to share Old Mr. Gu’s feelings.","Jiang Yulan wiped her eyes and asked Gu Chengye, “So you’ve decided to let Jingchen take Xiaoxuan on the project?”","Gu Chengye sighed. “What can I even say about that girl?”","After sighing, he stood up and went back upstairs to the second floor to rest.","As for whether he’d take Han Xuan along or not, he never answered.","Meanwhile, at the hotel, Han Xuan and Gu Chacha were already busy at work.","Gu Jinghan’s phone vibrated. He stared at the screen for a long time without saying a word.","“What the hell?”","He Huanhuan glanced at him. “What’s wrong?”","Gu Jinghan frowned. “Why do they keep going to my place to hook up?”","“They’re there again?”","Gu Jinghan nodded. “They’re there again!”","Who would’ve thought that guy Han Xuan, with his lack of skill, would have such a big appetite for it?","He leaned in close to He Huanhuan and asked, “Do you think Dad actually gave in just now?”","He Huanhuan shook her head. “No idea, but it’s none of my business.”","The family business wasn’t under her control anyway, so who got that lousy project didn’t matter to her.","Gu Jinghan smirked. “You really don’t care? Then why’d you interrupt just now when Han Xuan was asking Dad?”","Talking to him in that loud whisper—wasn’t that just to help Dad change the subject?","He Huanhuan defended herself. “I just can’t stand that guy Han Xuan!”","Gu Jinghan teased her with a grin. “Can’t stand him, or do you have a thing for his brother?”","Han Mo had always wanted to be involved in the East City project—that was exactly why the two families had gotten into an arranged marriage in the first place.","Gu Jinghan glanced at He Huanhuan; he didn’t believe she hadn’t been thinking about it just now.","He Huanhuan was silent. She didn’t even know why she’d done that.","Her mind hadn’t finished processing when the words had already come out.","Maybe she just felt Han Xuan wasn’t worthy.","That guy—he didn’t look reliable at all.","Why should he get the project?","Han Mo was obviously a better fit, wasn’t he?","He worked so diligently, and his attitude was always proper.","He...","Anyway, he was more suitable than Han Xuan.","But she knew that Han Mo had already been kicked out of the company. He didn’t have the ability to partner with Old Mr. Gu on his own.","Even if she wanted to help him, it was useless.","Sigh...","She let out a silent sigh. Han Mo, Han Mo—what are you up to?","Three days. They hadn’t seen each other for three days.","No meetings, no chats, nothing at all.","She felt an emptiness in her heart, a strange emotion she’d never experienced before.","It was probably just habit—getting used to him showing up on time every day to take her out and have fun.","Used to the two of them eating, drinking, and messing around with those little trinkets together.","Then buying them all and stuffing them into her room until it was full.","She picked up her phone and opened their chat. The last message was from three days ago.","Han Mo had sent: “I’m home.”","She hadn’t replied.","She tapped the input box, her fingers hovering over the keyboard: “What are you doing?”","She thought about it, then deleted it.","Damn it, why couldn’t she bring herself to send it?","This wasn’t her personality at all.","She was supposed to be the most straightforward person!","Talk to whoever she wants to talk to, delete whoever she doesn't like.","That was the real her!","She pressed her lips together, tapped away at the keyboard, and finally hit send.","[Got it.]"]},{"number":40,"title":"Chapter 40: You Two Don't Look Like a Match","paragraphs":["The input indicator showed \"What's wrong?\" for a second.","He Huanhuan suddenly felt emboldened and dialed his number directly!","Why was she even hesitating?","It was clearly Han Mo's fault—how could he just drop his ingratiating act halfway through?","Didn't he care about her feelings?","Unprofessional!","The phone rang once, and a familiar voice came through, calm with a hint of concern: \"What's wrong? Is something the matter?\"","He Huanhuan pouted: \"I can only call you if something's wrong? Can't I call you for no reason?\"","Her tone carried an unconscious intimacy, and Han Mo let out a soft chuckle.","\"Of course you can. What are you up to?\"","\"Just finished eating.\"","Mentioning food, she got excited and asked, \"Guess who I had lunch with today?\"","On the other end, Han Mo's voice turned cold: \"Liang Ye?\"","He Huanhuan scoffed in disgust: \"Please! Why would I eat with him?\"","\"Really?\"","His voice relaxed again. \"Then who was it?\"","He Huanhuan gossiped: \"Gu Chacha brought Han Xuan home to announce their relationship!\"","\"Them?\"","Han Mo didn't seem surprised, which annoyed He Huanhuan.","If he wasn't surprised, how could she take credit?","She wrinkled her nose and asked, \"You're not surprised?\"","\"Surprised. Extremely surprised, of course.\"","\"More than that!\"","He Huanhuan sat up excitedly: \"Han Xuan tried to pressure the old man into letting him join the East City project during dinner, but I steered the conversation away!\"","She was amazing, right? She was good to him, right?","Come on, praise her!","Han Mo chuckled lightly: \"Thank you.\"","He Huanhuan was instantly satisfied: \"No big deal! You've been so good to me, so it's only right that I'm good to you!\"","Han Mo smiled and responded, \"Mm.\"","Then came a long silence. He Huanhuan knew she should hang up, but she didn't want to.","She couldn't help feeling annoyed—she'd taken the initiative to call him, and all he did was grunt!","Her tone turned sharp: \"If you've got nothing to say, I'm hanging up!\"","She was about to end the call angrily when she heard Han Mo ask, \"I heard Gu Chacha is planning a solo concert?\"","He Huanhuan was puzzled: \"How did you know?\"","\"They've been contacting venues for the last couple of days. The owner is a friend of mine.\"","He Huanhuan drew out her words: \"I see... Then why did he tell you? Is it because she's your former fiancée?\"","For some reason, Han Mo's heart suddenly filled with a strange guilt.","The feeling of being interrogated for no clear reason made his emotions complicated.","Guilt mixed with a trace of delight...","He coughed awkwardly: \"That's not it. She and Han Xuan went together. My friend thought it was odd, so he told me...\"","\"Oh, I see...\"","He Huanhuan fiddled with the strap of her clothes: \"Speaking of which, I don't know any of your friends, but they all know about Gu Chacha...\"","This damned guilt!","Han Mo coughed again: \"If you want to meet him, I can take you to see him tomorrow. He doesn't have much to do anyway...\"","He Huanhuan's lips curled up involuntarily: \"Forget it. We'll all be there for Gu Chacha's performance anyway.\"","Han Mo immediately asked, \"When is her performance? Let's go together?\"","He Huanhuan couldn't help asking again, \"You're that eager to go see her perform?\"","The line went quiet again. He Huanhuan's heart tightened, afraid of hearing something she didn't want to.","\"Forget it, forget it! We'll talk about it later!\"","She hung up hastily and flopped onto her bed.","Damn it!","She felt like she'd lost somehow.","As for who she'd lost to, she couldn't quite say...","Ahhh...","So annoying!","Meanwhile, Han Mo stared at their closed chat window.","After a moment's thought, he typed and sent: \"It's not that I want to go see her.\"","Her phone buzzed. He Huanhuan opened it and read the message.","\"Ahhhh!!\"","She couldn't help screaming again, then jumped up and dashed to Gu Jinghan's room.","\"Second Brother!\"","\"What?\"","Gu Jinghan frowned, sitting in front of his computer. He would give anything to install a bug in the presidential suite!","He was dying to know what Gu Chacha and Han Xuan were up to.","But he couldn't. It was illegal!","Ahhhh!","He wanted to scream too. Why did they have to stay in his hotel?","Couldn't they go somewhere else?","It was testing his moral limits!","He'd endure it!","He Huanhuan plopped down beside him: \"Why are you looking at bugs?\"","Gu Jinghan gritted his teeth: \"I want to put one in the presidential suite to spy on Gu Chacha and Han Xuan...\"","He Huanhuan frowned: \"Wow, that's so creepy?\"","Gu Jinghan could tell from her expression what she was thinking. He rolled his eyes helplessly: \"I don't want to eavesdrop on that! I just want to know what they're plotting!\"","\"And! I haven't bought one! I'm just thinking about it!\"","He reluctantly closed the webpage. Forget it, he wouldn't do anything illegal.","Besides, he really didn't want to hear them being lovey-dovey.","No matter how short the time, he couldn't stand it!","He glanced at He Huanhuan: \"What do you want?\"","He Huanhuan suddenly became shy: \"Tell me, what do you think Han Mo is thinking?\"","She really wanted to know Han Mo's feelings—about her.","But she couldn't ask. She couldn't just go up to him and say, \"Hey, how do you feel about me?\"","Qi Meili had a lot of relationships, but she moved fast.","She'd meet someone in the morning, get together by noon, share a bowl of spicy noodles in the evening, and break up by night.","The speed was too fast for He Huanhuan to use as a reference.","So she came to Gu Jinghan instead: \"Do you think he's only being nice to me because of the old man's project?\"","Gu Jinghan put on a serious face: \"What else? It's not like he likes you or anything...\"","......","He Huanhuan punched him in the stomach: \"What's wrong with me? Am I not worthy of being liked?\"","Gu Jinghan clutched his stomach and groaned: \"You are, you are... But what does he like about you? You two don't seem like a good match...\"","\"Thump!\"","Another punch hit his back. He Huanhuan turned and stormed off: \"You don't know anything!\"","She shouldn't have come to him!","She stomped back to the third floor, but Gu Jinghan's words kept echoing in her head. Not a good match?","Were they not?","She stood in front of the mirror. In the reflection, she had a small face, big eyes, and fair skin.","Wasn't that a good match?","Her gaze fell on her rainbow-colored hair, and she hesitated.","Was this what made them mismatched?","Should she dye it black?","Her heart ached. When she was young, she was thin and weak, often bullied.","It was Qi Meili who took her to dye her hair and get tattoos, bringing her into a group of \"tough girls.\"","After that, no one dared bully her.","She'd never dyed her hair black since.","She loved her rainbow hair—it made her look fierce.","She loved that feeling."]},{"number":41,"title":"Chapter 41: No One Watches the Concert","paragraphs":["She studied her brightly colored hair seriously in the mirror. There were so many hues, and they were so dazzling.","It was clearly very pretty!","What didn’t match?","Thinking this to herself, her gaze couldn’t help but fall back onto the hair, lingering for a long time.","Gu Chacha’s solo recital was organized very quickly. In just three or four days, her performance was about to begin.","The day before the concert, she came back to deliver tickets to everyone.","Ever since she had publicly announced her relationship with Han Xuan last time, she had stopped living at home.","That guest room was way too small. She didn’t want to stay there anymore.","She specially took two tickets and handed them to He Huanhuan. “Big sister, bring Han Mo to come watch too~”","He Huanhuan reached out and took the tickets. “Alright.”","She opened her phone and searched for Gu Chacha’s recital. To her surprise, all the tickets were sold out.","Since when had she become so popular?","She continued searching for Gu Chacha and found a bunch of videos praising her.","Each video was more or less the same—calling her a winner in life, the beautiful pianist who had chosen to coast on a silver platter from the start.","And the comments under those videos were all similar too—“So jealous,” “Jealous,” “So jealous”...","She felt something was off but couldn’t figure out what.","She sneakily showed her phone screen to Gu Jinghan and whispered, “What do you think is going on with her?”","Gu Jinghan glanced at it and said, “Bots.”","At a glance, it was obvious. These were all paid bots.","He Huanhuan was confused. “But her tickets are all sold out.”","It couldn’t be that they had bought them themselves, could it?","What would be the point of that?","Did they just enjoy burning money for fun?","Gu Jinghan frowned. He didn’t understand it either.","No matter how rich someone was, they wouldn’t waste money like this. How much wealth did one need to be able to squander it so recklessly?","Where had Han Xuan found such a friend?","Someone this impressive?","He thought for a moment and sent a message to Gu Jingchen to ask: Big Brother, do you know where Han Xuan got the sponsorship for Gu Chacha?","After a long while, Gu Jingchen replied: No idea.","He immediately followed up: Big Brother, can you ask around?","Another long pause, then Gu Jingchen replied again: No time.","...","He should’ve known!","If Big Brother wouldn’t help him, he’d ask someone else!","He sidled up to He Huanhuan and said fawningly, “Huan-jie, why don’t you go ask Han Mo and see if he knows?”","He Huanhuan shot him a look. “Can’t you ask yourself?”","Even before she finished speaking, she had already opened her chat window: Do you know if Gu Chacha’s recital was sponsored by someone Han Xuan found?","The other side quickly replied: I know.","She asked again: Do you know who that person is?","There was a brief pause before the other side answered: Why are you asking?","She replied: I’m just curious.","For some reason, she didn’t want to say that Gu Jinghan was the curious one.","After another moment, the reply came through: I heard it’s a friend from overseas. I don’t know the specifics.","She showed the phone to Gu Jinghan.","“A friend from overseas?”","Gu Jinghan mused. “Han Xuan did spend two years in Europe, but his school was pretty mediocre. He probably doesn’t have any seriously impressive friends...”","Besides, Han Xuan was reckless and impulsive.","Who would want to be friends with someone like that?","And to sponsor Gu Chacha with so much money for a global solo recital? That wasn’t a small sum!","But he really wasn’t that close to Han Xuan, and they didn’t share any mutual friends.","So he put these thoughts aside for the moment, planning to see for himself when Gu Chacha’s recital came the next day.","Logically speaking, the person who had invested all that money would want to show up and watch her perform.","The next day, Han Mo’s car arrived at the Gu Manor on time.","He Huanhuan, dressed in a little black dress, ran downstairs. “Han Mo!”","Her eyes sparkled as she looked at him. “Do I look good today?”","She had specially chosen a black dress woven with colorful threads, thinking it would match her dyed hair better.","And Han Mo always liked to wear dark suits, so wouldn’t they look good together?","Filled with these little thoughts, she looked at him expectantly.","Han Mo glanced at her little black dress and nodded. “You look good in anything.”","...","Oh, come on!","He had no idea what she had done!","He Huanhuan pouted unhappily. “What do you know?! You have no taste!”","Han Mo was taken aback. Had he said something wrong?","Surely not?","Hadn’t he just complimented her beauty?","Gu Jinghan floated by sarcastically. “Is that how you compliment someone? ‘You look good in anything’? She looks bad in long dresses. How can you be so dismissive!”","...","No wonder Big Brother couldn’t get with Sister Huanhuan.","Who would want to hear that they looked bad in long dresses?","The recital was set to start at three in the afternoon. As family members, they arrived at half past two.","When they reached the backstage prep room, Gu Chacha’s makeup was heavier than usual. Seeing them, she broke into a smile.","“Mom, Dad, I’ll be going on stage soon~”","After today’s performance, she would officially be a pianist in the truest sense of the word!","Jiang Yulan looked at her exquisite appearance, her eyes welling up with emotion. “Chacha, you are your mother’s pride.”","She still remembered how tiny she had been as a child.","How quickly time had passed, and now she had grown into a young woman!","Gu Chacha stood up and hugged Jiang Yulan. “Mom, I know you love me very much. I’ll play well and step onto the international stage one step at a time.”","When that time came, her relationship with the Gu family would no longer be what it was now.","A faint smile curled at the corner of her mouth, as if she could already see Gu Chengye and Jiang Yulan carefully trying to pacify her.","He Huanhuan—what would become of you then?","You’d turn into the family’s marriage-bargaining chip, forced to marry some unreliable trust-fund brat and become their baby-making machine...","But she—she would become a world-renowned artist.","That was the difference between them.","She cast a brief glance at Han Mo. Ha, he wasn’t even worth mentioning in her thoughts.","Once her project with Han Xuan took off, Han Mo would have no chance to make a comeback.","Uncle Han (Han’s father) had never liked him anyway.","What awaited him was nothing but poverty and misery.","Thinking of this, her smile grew wider. “Make sure to watch my performance carefully~”","Watch me step by step, leaving all of you behind.","The recital was about to begin, so they couldn’t linger backstage any longer. They quickly made their way to their seats.","Once she sat down, He Huanhuan was stunned to find that the entire hall was nearly empty.","She clearly remembered checking the ticket platform the day before—all the tickets had been sold out.","But now, with the performance about to start, the hall was so empty...","Was this right?","She leaned close to Han Mo and asked, “Do you think something is off here?”","After hearing her words, Han Mo looked down at her. He hesitated for a moment before explaining, “It’s probably Han Xuan’s friend who bought up all the tickets.”","If they truly wanted to push Gu Chacha into being a pianist, they would have to invest money.","In the beginning, with no fame, no one would buy her tickets.","They would have to buy up the tickets themselves, to make it look like a sellout.","Then, after a few recitals, they could buy her some awards, flood the internet with press releases, and officially establish her reputation.","After that, they could arrange a tour.","He Huanhuan nodded along. “Oh, I see. So that’s why there’s no one here.”","Han Mo nodded but didn’t say anything more. What he didn’t add was that to push someone like this with so much money, it would take ten to twenty years to break even.","No investor would be so foolish as to pour money into a lost cause like this."]},{"number":42,"title":"Chapter 42: Just send the commission to them","paragraphs":["But He Huanhuan didn’t know any of this. She simply assumed Gu Chacha was lucky—lucky enough to stumble upon an investor who truly appreciated her and was willing to spare no expense to support her.","She closed her eyes and listened to Gu Chacha’s piano piece, then couldn’t help sighing: “Why doesn’t anyone invest in me?”","She had skills too!","She... she...","She was great at walking!","That probably wouldn’t cut it, though—there was no room for performance.","It wasn’t like she could just walk in circles around the hall for everyone to see.","Okay, how about this: she was really good at cursing people out!","Right, she could cuss like a champ.","Every time Qi Meili offended someone, Huanhuan was the one who argued them into submission.","Otherwise, she wouldn’t have ended up transmigrating into this book.","“You want to hold a concert too?”","A low voice came from Han Mo beside her. Huanhuan shook her head without a second thought. “What could I even perform?”","It wasn’t like she could just stand on stage and swear, right?","She could definitely do the swearing part, but she was afraid of getting beaten up.","A concert lasted an hour and a half. But before half an hour had even passed, Huanhuan had already fallen asleep.","She sprawled lazily in her chair, her head resting on Han Mo’s shoulder, sleeping like a log.","In a corner, a lean figure held up a phone and snapped a series of candid shots of the two.","Han Mo glanced at the person, who grinned back and shook the phone in his direction.","Han Mo looked at the photos on his phone. In the images, he sat completely relaxed in his seat, his shoulder leaning toward Huanhuan to let her rest more comfortably.","Ha! Han Mo, you’ve fallen for her!","You don’t even realize it yourself, do you?","Only when the performance ended did He Huanhuan wake up.","She clapped enthusiastically. “Great playing!”","Gu Jinghan teased her and said, “Great how? As a lullaby?”","He’d even heard her snoring!","Huanhuan nodded seriously. “Being able to hypnotize people is impressive in itself, no? Do you have any idea how many people toss and turn every night, unable to fall asleep?”","Gu Jinghan was speechless. She actually had a point.","Standing on stage, waiting for her family’s praise, Gu Chacha was seething with rage.","Were you this desperate for attention, He Huanhuan?","Today was supposed to be her moment!","“Daddy...”","She was about to pull everyone’s attention back when Han Mo beat her to it. He turned to Old Mr. Gu and said, “Uncle, I’d like to take Huanhuan out for a stroll. Is that alright?”","Old Mr. Gu beamed. “Of course! Young people love to have fun! Go on!”","The moment they left, Gu Jinghan made up an excuse and slipped away too.","Gu Jingchen didn’t even need an excuse—he had barely squeezed these two hours out of his schedule anyway.","The entire hall instantly emptied, leaving only her, Han Xuan, and the couple Gu Chengye and his wife.","Jiang Yulan, however, was full of relief as she came up to praise Gu Chacha. “Chacha, your piano skills keep getting better and better. Mom is so proud of you.”","Gu Chacha forced out a fake smile. What use was her praise?","Jiang Yulan was nothing but a useless stay-at-home wife—she had neither a say in the household nor any control over money.","In the past, since she was her mother, Gu Chacha had been willing to humor her.","But now that they shared neither blood nor any kind of transactional relationship, she couldn’t be bothered to waste even a shred of consideration on Jiang Yulan.","She turned to Gu Chengye with a sweet smile. “Dad, how did you like my performance tonight?”","Gu Chengye nodded and smiled. “Dad doesn’t understand music, but you looked every bit like an artist sitting up there.”","Yet the smile didn’t reach his eyes. He asked her, “Didn’t Han Xuan come to accompany you today?”","Hadn’t they said they were together?","How could he miss her very first concert?","Gu Chacha smiled sweetly. “He went to the back to take a call. He’ll be here soon.”","Old Mr. Gu frowned. “Calling that investor of yours?”","He looked around. The Golden Stream Hall was the top-tier concert venue in Jiang City, offering a full-service package. A single event there couldn’t have cost less than three million yuan.","And this was just Chacha’s first solo recital. Was that person really willing to throw that much money around?","Who the hell was he?","He pulled out his phone and sent a text to Gu Jingchen: Look into Chacha’s investor. Find out what their background is. Any red flags?","After all, Chacha was still his daughter. He could ignore everything else, but he had to ensure her safety.","Gu Jingchen replied almost instantly: Got it.","He put his phone away just as Han Xuan walked in after ending his call.","He approached them with a beaming smile. “Dad! How’d the performance go? Did I steer Chacha wrong?”","Gu Chengye nodded stiffly. “You’ve got the right intentions. But you need to know...”","He wanted to warn Han Xuan to be careful.","But Han Xuan wasn’t in the mood to listen. He cut him off midsentence:","“Dad, when does big brother have time? We need to get that East City project moving! I’ve got all the funds ready—just waiting to team up with big brother for a big success!”","The arrogance in his tone made Gu Chengye frown. Setting aside the Han family themselves, even his own Gu Corporation wouldn’t dare claim to have all the necessary funding lined up and be ready to go big.","The East City project was a massive regional development initiative. This wasn’t some small investment worth hundreds of millions—it was a long-term, decade-plus investment plan involving trillions.","What the hell was this kid so cocky about?","He shot Han Xuan a look. “Didn’t realize you had that kind of financial muscle.”","Han Xuan smirked proudly. “No way. It’s my friend. He was worried I’d fall short on funds, so he offered to lend me some to keep things moving.”","That friend again?","Who was this friend that would fund a concert and also lend him money to invest in East City?","If he had that much money, why wasn’t he doing it himself?","Gu Chengye felt increasingly uneasy, but he knew that Chacha and Han Xuan were riding high and wouldn’t appreciate him raining on their parade.","So he forced himself to stay quiet, made a bit of small talk with the two, and then headed home.","As Old Mr. Gu and the others left, Gu Chacha leaned lazily against Han Xuan. “I’m exhausted today!”","Han Xuan eagerly massaged her fingers. “Who told you to have such a gift? From now on, I’ll just live off my wife!”","“Hmph!” Gu Chacha pouted playfully. “You’re just trying to slack off!”","Han Xuan pulled her into a tight embrace. “Do you really think I’ve been slacking off? Don’t you know me by now?”","Half an hour later, Gu Jinghan’s phone buzzed with a ding.","He picked it up and groaned, “Damn it. Are there no other hotels in Jiang City?”","Did they absolutely have to push his buttons?","Did it have to be like this?","Gritting his teeth, he opened a shopping app and bought the most expensive bug he could find.","Screw it! He wouldn’t put it in the room—he’d install it outside the hallway door!","What if they happened to stand in the hallway and chat?","What if they let slip something crucial?","He wasn’t short on cash anyway. He’d buy it, install it!","One way or another, he’d dig up every bit of gossip there was to find!","Somewhere in Southeast Asia, a dark-skinned man stood in front of floor-to-ceiling windows, waiting.","When the phone rang, he picked it up briskly. “Boss, all thirty million have been transferred in.”","The man raised an eyebrow. “Cleaned?”","“Clean as can be.”","The man flashed a wicked grin. “Good. Send them their commission now.”","Inside a penthouse suite, two figures began rolling together wildly, tangled in a heated frenzy."]},{"number":43,"title":"Chapter 43: Performance in the Dark Night","paragraphs":["Three minutes later, the two of them lay on the bed, sweaty and flushed.","Gu Chacha reached out and pushed Han Xuan. \"Ask him quickly, is tonight okay like this?\"","Han Xuan looked down at her, a greasy smirk curling at the corner of his mouth. \"What? Can't wait?\"","Gu Chacha couldn't help but roll her eyes at him. \"You're so annoying. I'm just worried—what if it doesn't work?\"","Han Xuan wasn't worried at all. The guy had been introduced to him by a friend, and they'd worked together more than once before.","He leisurely reached for his phone. \"Relax, they're professionals at this. Plenty of experience.\"","When he opened his phone, a transfer notification popped up.","A string of six zeros gleamed brightly on the screen.","He flipped over and pinned Gu Chacha down, holding the phone in front of her face. \"Take a good look for your husband—what's this?\"","\"Oh! It actually worked!\"","Gu Chacha was thrilled at the sight of the transfer. She knew it should have been fine, but until the money hit the account, she couldn't help worrying.","She'd talked a big game in front of her family, and if this hadn't worked, wouldn't she have become a joke?","The thought of He Huanhuan laughing at her was worse than death.","But thankfully, the money was in. That meant this method was feasible.","If it worked, the guy would keep spending money to promote her.","Then she would definitely become a real pianist, a world-renowned pianist.","At the thought of that possibility, her heart surged with excitement.","She wrapped her arms around the man beneath her, her eyes sparkling as she looked at him. \"Honey, I love you so much!\"","Han Xuan gave a smug smile in response. \"Want to go again already? You're so greedy.\"","The presidential suite briefly came alive with energy once more.","Meanwhile, on the roadside, Han Mo wore a serious expression as he stared at the unfamiliar text message.","[Payment sent. You're in.]","His jet-black pupils seemed to hold countless emotions before returning to calm.","He put away his phone, a faint smile curling at the corner of his mouth. \"How about we head back?\"","He Huanhuan nodded. \"Sure.\"","She genuinely couldn't walk anymore now. After just two hours of walking, her calves were sore.","She had assumed \"heading back\" meant going home, but when the car stopped, she was surprised to find they were back at Flow Gold Hall.","Startled, she turned to look at Han Mo. \"Why are we here?\"","Gu Chacha's recital was over, wasn't it?","A trace of a smile rose in Han Mo's eyes. \"Didn't you say you didn't know my friend? I'm bringing you to meet him.\"","He Huanhuan's heart inexplicably grew nervous, and she clung to the passenger seat, refusing to get out. \"No need for that, is there? I think our relationship is just so-so, not at the stage of meeting friends.\"","But Han Mo didn't give her a chance to back out. He opened the car door directly and bent down into the vehicle.","The cramped passenger seat instantly filled with his presence. He looked at her with deep, steady eyes. \"Then who are you close with? Liang Ye?\"","His low voice sounded in her ear, and He Huanhuan wrinkled her nose. \"Can we not bring up Liang Ye right now?\"","That would really kill the mood, wouldn't it?","The smile in Han Mo's eyes deepened. He reached out, took her hand, and coaxed softly, \"Come on, let's just chat. It'll be fine.\"","The largest hall in Flow Gold Hall was the one where Gu Chacha had just played the piano. Han Mo led her straight back there.","In the center of the audience seats sat a man in a suit.","He was lounging on the stool with his long legs crossed, looking down at them. \"Coming into my territory, why aren't you paying me respect?\"","Han Mo tightened his grip on He Huanhuan's hand and shot him an annoyed glance. \"Possessed again?\"","\"Heh heh!\"","The man jumped up in an instant, dashed over to them, and cheerfully extended a hand to He Huanhuan. \"The True Heiress of the Gu family? Hi, I'm Fu Jingnian, Han Mo's good friend.\"","He Huanhuan was about to shake his hand when Han Mo pulled her back abruptly, swatting Fu Jingnian's hand away. \"Did Gu Chacha and the others leave?\"","Fu Jingnian rubbed the back of his hit hand and gestured with his chin toward him. \"Generous as always—booked the whole day but only used it for two hours. Is the Han family loaded these days? That extravagant?\"","Han Mo let out a sarcastic laugh. \"Probably, but that's not my case.\"","He looked at Fu Jingnian. \"The payment's been made, so I can use this hall, right?\"","Fu Jingnian shot him a disdainful glare. \"You're mooching the hall? That's so stingy.\"","Wasn't the guy supposed to be a trust-fund kid too?","How could he pull such a cheap move?","At least send him a little cash, so he could make some money too!","Han Mo shrugged shamelessly. \"I'm unemployed now, didn't you know?\"","He had no family support and no job to fall back on—why should he pretend?","Han Xuan had already paid, so he might as well take advantage of it.","Hearing this, Fu Jingnian wrinkled his nose, exasperated. \"You, man!\"","It wasn't like he needed that little bit of cash!","He just didn't want to make things easy for him.","Hmph, just you wait!","\"The hall closes at ten. Don't make my staff work overtime.\"","With that, he clapped his hands and left, even thoughtfully turning off the biggest light.","The entire hall suddenly went dark.","He Huanhuan stood bewildered in the darkness. \"What's this all about?\"","Han Mo's voice came from right beside her, almost brushing her ear. \"Didn't you want someone to sponsor you? Now you've got it.\"","He Huanhuan was stunned. \"Han Xuan?\"","That was how you wrangle a sponsorship?","Han Mo let out a helpless laugh. \"How could it be him? It's me.\"","He Huanhuan insisted, \"But it was Han Xuan who paid.\"","His voice came even closer, so near she could feel his breath. \"If he finds out I brought you to mooch his hall, who do you think he'll come after—you or me?\"","He Huanhuan swallowed. \"Definitely you.\"","A low chuckle sounded near her ear. \"So you see, this is my sponsorship to you.\"","He Huanhuan puffed out her cheeks. \"You're really good at saving money.\"","The laughter in her ear grew warmer. \"What can I do? I don't have a job right now...\"","He Huanhuan inexplicably felt he was in an exceptionally good mood—one that seemed tied to reasons beyond her.","She tried hard to see his face in the dark. \"You seem really happy...\"","Before she could ask more, his hand pressed against her back. \"Do you want to perform a scolding act?\"","He Huanhuan quickly shook her head. \"No way!\"","Scolding someone in a big, dark hall would just make her look crazy.","\"Then what do you want to do?\"","He Huanhuan shook her head again. \"I don't know.\"","\"Then let's dance.\"","\"But I can't...\"","\"Doesn't matter—dance however you like. We don't have to worry about angry audiences demanding refunds.\"","His hand pressed firmly against her back, guiding her step by step onto the performance stage.","It was her first time stepping onto such a stage. The soles of her shoes clicked sharply against the expensive floor.","She couldn't help feeling nervous. \"Maybe we should go back down...\"","In the darkness, soft music began to play.","His hand pushed her into the warmth of his embrace, his broad shoulders enveloping her completely as they swayed gently to the melody.","\"See? You dance wonderfully.\"","His low voice, wrapped in the soft music, drifted slowly into her ear through the darkness. He Huanhuan felt as if she were starting to get dizzy."]},{"number":44,"title":"Chapter 44: The company has no money to pay salaries.","paragraphs":["Han Xuan had been busy lately, busy building momentum for Gu Chacha. He needed to push her into the spotlight and make her famous as quickly as possible.","Only then would holding a tour for Gu Chacha later not seem too conspicuous.","He was so occupied with spending money to get Gu Chacha onto projects and competitions that he barely had any mind left for company matters.","That was until Han Changyong called him, his voice brimming with anger on the phone:","\"Why hasn't the company paid wages this month? Employees have been complaining to me about it!\"","Han Xuan replied nonchalantly, \"Oh, really? Let me ask the finance department what's going on.\"","After fobbing off Han Changyong, he called Meng Yu.","As soon as the call connected, he demanded coldly, \"Why haven't the wages been paid this month? I pay you a shitload of money, what the hell do you do all day? Don't you keep an eye on things?\"","Meng Yu was almost speechless: \"I called you, I sent you so many messages, but you didn't reply to me...\"","He had called him over a dozen times in the past two days, and he hadn't answered a single one!","How was he supposed to keep an eye on things?","There wasn't enough money in the company account. Could he magically conjure up cash to pay everyone's salaries?","Han Xuan snapped impatiently, \"What's with the delay in wages? It's gotten back to my dad!\"","Meng Yu replied helplessly, \"Mr. Han, there's no money left in the company account. The finance department reported it last week, and I showed you.\"","Han Xuan flew into a rage: \"Didn't the company have several hundred million in the account? How could there be no money? Did you pocket my money?\"","Meng Yu thought: If I had that kind of skill, would I still be his assistant?","He would have taken the money and emigrated overseas long ago, ha.","He explained bitterly, \"When you first took over the company, didn't you cancel all of Senior Han's projects? All those cancellation penalties had to be paid...\"","Han Xuan jumped to his feet and yelled into the phone, \"Who told you to pay the penalties! Didn't I say to let them sue me?\"","Meng Yu was anguished inside but couldn't say it out loud.","\"I reported it to you. To secure those projects smoothly, the penalty funds were frozen in advance...\"","They didn't even need the company's approval to deduct those penalties—the money was automatically withdrawn on the due date.","You weren't listening carefully back then. Look at the mess now.","There's no money left in the company account!","Let's see what you're going to do!","\"Han Mo!\"","Han Xuan gritted his teeth. It must have been his doing!","No one freezes penalty funds when doing projects. This was a trap Han Mo had set for him on purpose.","He knew that Han Xuan, holding a grudge against him, would cancel all his previous projects as soon as he took over the company.","Rage boiling in his heart, he cursed, \"Useless piece of junk! What do I keep you around for? You're fired! Don't come in tomorrow!\"","Meng Yu exclaimed in delight, \"Really? Am I fired?\"","\"Get lost!\"","The call ended, and Meng Yu rushed straight to HR: \"Quick, quick, quick! Mr. Han wants to fire me. Get the paperwork going! Pay me double what I'm owed under the law!\"","Yang Sheng, the HR manager, rolled his eyes at him: \"Have you lost your mind?\"","Meng Yu quickly pulled up a call recording, where Han Xuan's voice was crystal clear: \"You're fired!\"","He frantically urged Yang Sheng, \"Hurry up! Process my termination! Fire me!\"","He wanted to take the severance pay and sleep for three days at home.","But just as the termination contract was printed, Han Xuan's phone call came in again.","Meng Yu's face fell instantly: \"Mr. Han...\"","Han Xuan barked fiercely, \"Go tell all the employees that wages for this month will be paid together with next month's, and everyone will get an extra five percent late fee.\"","Meng Yu hesitated, \"So... are you still firing me?\"","\"Get back to work, damn it!\"","Damn!","Where was the promised firing?","He just wanted to go home and sleep!","The notice was sent out to the staff. Though they grumbled, at least the company was offering a five percent compensation. They'd wait until next month to see—if the money still didn't come, they'd kick up a fuss then.","Temporarily settling things, he quickly made an overseas call. As soon as it connected, he explained his situation: \"Look, I know this timing isn't ideal, but I really have no other choice...\"","The person on the other end smirked slightly: \"How much do you need, Mr. Han?\"","\"Fifty million.\"","The other sighed: \"That's no small amount, Mr. Han.\"","Han Xuan lowered his voice: \"I know, but I need this money urgently. What do you think...\"","There was a long silence on the line, and Han Xuan's heart immediately jumped into his throat.","\"This month, I need you to hold twenty-five recitals.\"","Han Xuan immediately agreed: \"Deal! I'll make it happen!\"","Hanging up, he immediately called Gu Chacha: \"Get ready. We'll be working nonstop from now on.\"","He laid out the plan to Gu Chacha, who couldn't help frowning: \"So many shows in such a short time? It doesn't feel right.\"","She had only just joined two competitions and hadn't even won any awards yet.","Holding so many recitals in one month would raise suspicion among anyone with a sharp eye.","\"Chacha, if I get kicked out of the company, all our future plans will fall apart.\"","He had taken the company seal and flown off to sign the contracts.","If his father found out about this, he'd be finished.","Without him, Gu Chacha could forget about becoming a pianist.","Gu Chacha hesitated, but finally agreed: \"Alright, you arrange it. Just be careful.\"","\"Don't worry! I'll set everything up perfectly!\"","Over the next month, Gu Chacha seemed like a shooting star appearing out of nowhere. Promotional articles flooded everywhere.","Short videos, media appearances, competitions, variety shows—one after another, nonstop.","Recitals were held back-to-back.","Unaware netizens really thought Jiang City had produced an extraordinary pianist.","In the presidential suite, Han Xuan showed his phone to Gu Chacha: \"Look at this idiot asking—'Who's better, you or Lang Lang?' Hahahaha... What an idiot!\"","Gu Chacha frowned in displeasure: \"What did you say?\"","She knew she couldn't compare to someone like that, but what did he mean by that remark?","Han Xuan pulled her into his arms: \"Baby, don't be mad. I know you've worked hard, honey. How about this—I'll buy you another award, one with more prestige.\"","Gu Chacha sat up: \"Really?\"","If she could buy a prestigious award, she'd have more confidence.","Han Xuan said smugly, \"Of course!\"","With twenty-five recitals in one month, the money he needed was gathered quickly.","He had tasted the thrill of fast money—it was incredibly satisfying.","But the thought that all this money would soon become wages for those employees made him unhappy.","Now that he had a way to make money, he didn't need some employees anymore.","Maybe it was time for their company to undergo a reform.","He started scheming about how to drive out his father's people and grab all his father's shares.","He wanted to sell the company outright and pocket a lump sum.","That way, there would be no more expenses in the future—all income would be pure profit!"]},{"number":45,"title":"Chapter 45: Han Mo, It Is You After All","paragraphs":["Over the next few days, he hired several planners to help him figure out how to smoothly carry out his plan.","But before the planners could deliver their proposals, his father’s thunderous fury arrived first.","“Han Xuan! What have you done?”","Han Changyong’s blood pressure spiked. “Why has the company account been frozen? What did you do to the company??”","“What?”","Han Xuan was caught off guard. “What do you mean the company account was frozen? It wasn’t me. I didn’t do anything.”","He hadn’t done anything, had he?","He hadn’t even gone to the company, and he hadn’t touched any projects. How could it be related to him?","Han Changyong replied furiously, “I just got a call. Someone told me that a sum of eight million deposited into the company account the day before yesterday came from a problematic source! If it wasn’t you, then who was it? What did you do?”","The moment he mentioned the eight million, Han Xuan snapped back to reality.","Damn it. It was that money!","He quickly called the person. The call was answered promptly, and he asked urgently, “Didn’t you say the money was clean? Why did my company account gets frozen?”","The person replied leisurely, “That must have been a subordinate sending it to the wrong account. It’s a minor issue.”","“Minor issue?”","Han Xuan, frantic, yelled, “It’s not minor at all! My dad knows! What’s wrong with your people? How could they be so careless? What am I supposed to do now?”","“Well, I gave you a fair amount of money. Just lie low for a while and keep your head down.”","With those dismissive words, the person hung up.","Han Xuan went absolutely crazy. What did he mean by “lie low for a while and keep your head down”?","Crap!","How could he lie low?","That was his family’s company!","If something happened to the company, he was finished!","His father would kill him!","Han Changyong called again, and Han Xuan was so terrified he threw his phone away.","What to do? What to do?","How could he cover this up?","He frantically called Gu Chacha. “Chacha, it’s bad. That unreliable guy sent a payment to the wrong account...”","After he explained everything, Gu Chacha became even more panicked. “Will I get caught? Will this affect me?”","She had only just started tasting the sweetness of fame and fortune, and she couldn’t bear to lose it.","Han Xuan pressed her anxiously, “Chacha, your father should have connections to fix this. Go and beg your dad.”","Old Mr. Gu has always had decent relationships with those people. It was just a small sum of eight million.","If he put in a word, those people would let it slide.","But Gu Chacha hesitated. “Can’t you figure it out yourself? Dad won’t listen to me.”","She didn’t want to beg Old Mr. Gu either.","If she asked for his help, she would have lost.","Han Xuan immediately launched a tirade of insults. “I goddamn wouldn’t be calling you if I had a solution! Do you still want to be a pianist or not? If you do, go to your dad!”","His harsh scolding caused Gu Chacha to break down. “Han Xuan!”","Han Xuan interrupted her impatiently. “Hurry up! If we’re late, we’re both done for!”","With that, he hung up and ignored Gu Chacha.","After much hesitation, Gu Chacha, unwilling to give up her current fame and fortune, drove back to the Gu family home.","Old Mr. Gu was walking in the garden. She forced a sweet smile and called out, “Dad~”","Seeing her return, Old Mr. Gu was pleasantly surprised. “Chacha, you’re here?”","Ever since she got together with Han Xuan, Gu Chacha had rarely come home.","When Jiang Yulan called her, the calls often went unanswered.","They had asked Gu Jinghan, knowing she had been busy with competitions and performances.","The couple hadn’t disturbed her further.","Children grew up and inevitably had their own lives.","Gu Chacha linked her arm with Gu Chengye’s and acted coyly. “Dad, I’ve been so busy and tired lately~”","Old Mr. Gu gave her a closer look. “You’ve lost weight. If you’re tired, come home and rest. It’s not like our family can’t support you.”","A flicker of emotion crossed Gu Chacha’s eyes, followed by a trace of barely concealed disgust.","Of course, the Gu family could support her, but what about supporting her ambitions?","Why hadn’t they lifted her up?","They had sent her to learn piano as a child, but why hadn’t they supported her to become a pianist when she grew up?","Wasn’t it because she was a daughter, not worth their effort?","What was the difference between how they raised her and how Jiang Yulan kept a pet dog?","They gave her food and shelter, but nothing else.","Bitterness and resentment simmered within her. But today, she had an agenda, so she buried those feelings deep.","Cautiously, she began, “Dad, Han Xuan has been working on some project with others. The company just received a sum of money, and then the account was frozen...”","Old Mr. Gu was surprised. “How did that happen?”","For a company of their scale, company accounts weren’t easily frozen.","Gu Chacha pouted. “Who knows? I asked him, but he won’t tell me. It has me so worried.”","Old Mr. Gu smiled reassuringly. “It means he’s growing up. He’s learning to shield you from trouble.”","“But Dad...”","Gu Chacha leaned her head on his shoulder. “I’m really worried. Can you help him out...”","It had been a long time since she had been this coddling with Old Mr. Gu. Pleased, he nodded. “Alright, let Dad make a call and ask around.”","After calling an old acquaintance, Old Mr. Gu mentioned Han Xuan, and the acquaintance replied directly, “Old Gu, this case involves cross-border fraud. It’s not something I can sway.”","Old Mr. Gu was shocked. “Cross-border fraud?”","Wasn’t Chacha saying that Han Xuan was investing in a project with someone else?","How did it involve cross-border fraud?","The acquaintance’s voice turned grave. “We’ve received a tip-off that Han Xuan has close ties with a cross-border fraud ring...”","After hanging up, Old Mr. Gu’s face darkened significantly.","Gu Chacha asked timidly, “Dad? What’s wrong?”","Old Mr. Gu stared at her sharply. “Chacha, tell Dad the truth. Who exactly was that investor you used to talk about?”","Gu Chacha’s heart skipped a beat. “Dad, why are you asking about that?”","Old Mr. Gu’s face turned cold. “Han Xuan is in deep trouble, do you know that? Someone reported him for involvement in cross-border telecom fraud! Tell me honestly—are you involved too?”","Gu Chacha shook her head in panic. “Dad, what are you talking about? I don’t understand.”","“Why did you suddenly start holding concerts? Who was that person who invested in you? And why did he invest in you? What did you do for him?”","Old Mr. Gu stepped closer, confronting her about the concerts.","Gu Chacha was so flustered she couldn’t even lie. She backed away urgently. “Dad, I—I have to go find Han Xuan. Yes! I need to find Han Xuan first!”","With that, she turned and ran, terrified that Old Mr. Gu might stop her.","She sped off in her car, blowing through three red lights. In the garden, Old Mr. Gu called Gu Jingchen. “Jingchen, your sister has made a huge mistake. See what you can do...”","Han Xuan had a penthouse in the city center. Gu Chacha raced there and rushed into the living room, shouting at him, “Did you know someone reported you! Your secret’s out! You’ve ruined me!”","Han Xuan looked up at her with reddened eyes. “Reported?”","A suspicion crossed his mind, and he immediately called a friend.","Ten minutes later, he was so enraged he smashed his phone.","A blazing murderous intent surged in his eyes, and he gritted his teeth, \"Han Mo! It is you, after all!\""]},{"number":46,"title":"Chapter 46: Slink Away in Defeat","paragraphs":["At this moment, at the Han residence, Han Changyong had made countless phone calls.","After begging left and right, he finally figured out what his company had done wrong.","That idiot son of his had actually gotten involved in money laundering, and stupidly used the company’s account to take the payment!","His vision went dark in waves. How could he, Han Changyong, have fathered such a fool of a son!","That brat wasn’t even worth a single finger of Han Mo’s!","Han Mo?","Right, he still had another son!","He immediately called Han Mo. The phone was picked up quickly, and he said hastily, “Good son, the company is in trouble! Come back quick...”","He urgently explained that the company’s accounts had been frozen, but Han Mo didn’t respond.","“Good son, I know you’re angry with your father. But this company is my life’s work. You can’t just abandon it.”","Han Mo still remained silent, and Han Changyong started to panic.","He knew Han Mo held a grudge against him. But if the boy had been more devoted, would he have treated him this way?","If you really wanted to split the blame, both father and son were equally at fault.","But now was not the time to say that. Gritting his teeth, he finally brought up the past: “It wasn’t easy building this company to where it is today. Back then, your mother ruined her stomach trying to secure the West Yard project...”","As expected, at the mention of Chen Meixin, Han Mo’s emotions instantly boiled over: “So you remember how much Mom sacrificed for this company? And look how you treated her! How dare you even mention her name?”","“I know I failed you and your mother. Hate me if you want. But can you really bear to let Meixin’s hard work go to waste?”","He cut straight to the point, pressing Han Mo: “Can you really bear it?”","He knew Han Mo couldn’t say no.","Back in the early days, when he and Meixin were building their careers, they didn’t have Han Mo until they were nearly thirty.","Meixin had doted on Han Mo — afraid he might fall if she held him in her hands, afraid he might break if she held him in her mouth.","The Han Corporation was an empire Meixin had built brick by brick. Han Mo could never stand by and watch it collapse.","“From now on, Han Xuan has nothing to do with the company’s affairs.”","Han Mo’s voice was ice-cold, utterly devoid of emotion.","But that didn’t matter. Han Changyong knew that Han Mo had a hand in today’s crisis.","The fact that he was willing to lay down terms meant he was backing down.","He quickly nodded: “Fine! In a couple of days, I’ll send him abroad to reflect on his mistakes.”","Once the company stabilized, he’d let him come back.","Of course, he didn’t say that out loud, but in his heart, that was exactly what he planned.","Having received his promise, Han Mo said nothing more and simply hung up.","Han Changyong then called Han Xuan. The phone rang for a long time before it was picked up.","On the other end, Han Xuan was crying like a child: “Dad! I didn’t mean to! I swear! Han Mo set me up! It was Han Mo!”","“So you know it was him who set you up!”","Han Changyong scolded him harshly: “He set a trap, and you walked right into it? Do you have a brain made of pig fat? Can’t you think at all?”","“Wah... Dad, I’m sorry...”","You had to admit, Han Changyong truly doted on his younger son.","That was the only reason Han Xuan could cry to his father like this after making such a huge mistake.","If Han Mo had made the same error, Han Changyong would have handed him over to the authorities long ago.","Hearing the crying on the phone, Han Changyong’s heart softened. He soothed him: “Stop crying. I’ve already made an agreement with Han Mo. He’ll take over the company from now on and clean up this mess.”","“What?”","Han Xuan shouted in fury: “What about me, then?”","The boy had no real skill, but he sure knew how to fight for his share!","Han Changyong snapped at him, \"Do you have the capability to solve the current problem? 'I'll handle it'? You'd better get home right now and explain everything you've done!\"","Click...","The call was quickly hung up. Han Changyong stared at his phone, his anger boiling over.","Hanging up on him?","Who was the one in the wrong here?","He really owed him one!","His fury surged and then quickly dissipated.","The kid hadn't had it easy either—his mother had passed away a few years ago after a painful illness.","Watching his own mother suffer from such pain had hurt the boy deeply. A little indulgence was understandable.","Loved children were like that—they didn't need to do anything to earn their parents' affection and forgiveness.","Han Xuan had made such a huge mistake that the company nearly went under because of him.","Han Changyong's anger didn't even last half an hour before it fizzled out.","Then he dumped this mess on Han Mo to clean up. Once Han Mo sorted it out, he planned to find an excuse to strip Han Mo of his power.","But this time, he miscalculated. He thought Han Xuan would obediently fall in line.","He didn't realize that Han Xuan had tasted the thrill of easy money and that his mindset had already changed.","The feeling of getting something for nothing was too intoxicating. He couldn't let it go, couldn't give it up.","This time, it was his turn to be kicked out of the company in disgrace.","Too humiliating.","But he had no choice. He didn't have any other option.","The company had nearly been ruined because of him, and he needed Han Mo to clean up his mess.","Han Mo moved quickly. No one knew what he did or who he talked to.","The day after Han Mo returned to the company, the corporate account was temporarily unfrozen.","Han Xuan became even more certain that Han Mo was behind everything.","Even Gu Chengye couldn't solve this problem, but Han Mo fixed it in two days?","How was that possible?","He slumped dejectedly on the sofa, his resentment piling up higher and higher.","Until his phone rang, and a long-awaited number flashed on the screen.","He answered impatiently: \"Hey! Why weren't you taking my calls before?\"","He had called that person countless times a few days ago, but they never answered.","He thought he had been discarded. He never expected them to call him on their own.","On the other end of the line, the voice had a hint of exhaustion: \"Didn't you say your company's account was frozen? I was busy figuring out how to help you. So? It's unfrozen now—want to continue the collaboration?\"","\"What do you mean?\"","Han Xuan was stunned: \"Are you saying you came up with that solution? So it wasn't... wasn't our own plan?\"","Hearing this, the person on the other end exploded: \"I haven't even slept, spent millions to pull some strings for you, and now you're trying to weasel out of it?\"","\"No, no...\"","Han Xuan quickly apologized to the person, finally managing to calm them down.","Only then did the person lazily reveal that over the past few days, they had spent several million to bribe the right people.","That was how the company's account was unfrozen.","The person asked him: \"I'll make sure my people are more careful from now on. Are you still in?\"","\"Yes!\"","Han Xuan agreed without hesitation.","After hanging up, he licked his lips in displeasure.","So, Han Mo had learned to reap the benefits without lifting a finger, huh.","Now came the problem: how could he kick Han Mo out of the company again?","He had just made a huge mistake, and the old man was convinced that Han Mo had saved the company.","There was no way the old man would hand the company over to him again anytime soon. But the person on the phone had insisted the money had to go through the company account.","Said it was harder to trace that way, with lower risk.","He couldn’t let the old man find out he was earning this money—the old man would surely scold him to death.","He reached up and touched his chin, thinking about how he could kick Han Mo out."]},{"number":47,"title":"Chapter 47: Brake Danger","paragraphs":["At the Gu residence, Gu Jinghan knocked on He Huanhuan’s door with a gossipy grin: “Sister Huan, hasn’t Han Mo come around to play with you for a few days now?”","He Huanhuan shot him a glare. “Mind your own business.”","She was already in a bad mood!","That damn Han Mo hadn’t come to see her again.","Not only had he stopped showing up, but his WeChat messages had dwindled down to just good morning and good night check-ins.","Who cared what time he went to bed or woke up?","She wasn’t his kindergarten teacher!","Gu Jinghan pushed the door open and slid in beside her, settling in with a sneaky grin. “You wanna know why?”","He Huanhuan looked up. “Why?”","“Because he doesn’t need you anymore!”","Gu Jinghan handed his phone to He Huanhuan. “Look, he’s back at the Han Corporation. See why he was buttering you up before? He was scared his dad would play favorites with Han Xuan, so he came around every day to suck up to the old man!”","He tapped the screen rapidly. “Man... that guy’s a cold-blooded beast.”","For over ten days straight, Han Mo had come by daily, acting like He Huanhuan’s loyal puppy.","Gu Jinghan had to admit he couldn’t have done it himself. Ruthless. Truly ruthless.","He Huanhuan didn’t get the ins and outs of their schemes. She frowned. “So now he doesn’t need to suck up to me? Because Han Xuan’s out of the picture?”","“Exactly!”","Gu Jinghan nodded. “Han Xuan’s too weak. Han Changyong won’t give him a chance to mess things up. The old guy’s getting frail and sick—the company has to go to Han Mo.”","He Huanhuan listened to Gu Jinghan rambling on, and the anger inside her started to boil.","“Do you have nothing better to do?”","“Huh?”","Gu Jinghan was just getting into it. He’d been about to explain how Han Mo would now have to secure his position at the company for real...","Why did she suddenly shut him down?","Weren’t they having a decent chat?","He Huanhuan stood up, grabbed him by the arm, and shoved him toward the door. “You got no work or what? I can’t stand useless rich brats!”","“I’m not a useless brat! I own a hotel, remember? Hey, hey, hey...”","Before he could explain, she forced him out the door.","The door slammed shut with a thud. He Huanhuan plopped back onto the sofa, restless and irritated.","So all that kindness from Han Mo had just been about getting back into the company?","Now that he was back, she was worthless?","She’d been nothing but a tool?","She’d always known Han Mo’s kindness had an ulterior motive, but now that it was real, she still felt pissed.","A line she’d once read online came to mind.","Don’t force your way into circles that aren’t yours.","It really was true. Look at how casually Gu Jinghan talked about it.","He didn’t see a problem at all.","And there was Gu Chacha, hooking up with Han Xuan as if it were nothing...","Money. Power.","That was what mattered to them.","Feelings? They were just useless extras.","He Huanhuan looked around the room and muttered, “So what if I was used? I didn’t lose anything!”","It wasn’t like she’d been the one fawning over Han Mo. She hadn’t lost a thing!","Yeah. That was it.","She flopped onto the bed, fuming, and stayed there until dinnertime. But her chest still felt tight and upset.","The more she thought about it, the more unfair it felt. Why should she just take it?","She grabbed her phone and, without a second thought, deleted Han Mo!","Screw it!","She wasn’t going to play their rich people’s games anymore!","She was just a broke, hot-headed girl. She was done!","Outside her door, Jiang Yulan knocked softly. “Huanhuan, dinner’s ready.”","“Not hungry!”","Jiang Yulan coaxed her. “Come down and eat a little. Skipping dinner is bad for your stomach.”","She rolled over, even more annoyed.","What bad for her stomach? She’d skipped dinner all the time before and been perfectly fine.","Sleeping didn’t require fuel. Why stuff herself?","Saving money for breakfast was the real priority.","Yeah, that was her real life.","Broke. Scraping by.","Cursing people out for a few bucks, then blowing it all on a bowl of spicy hotpot, savoring every bite as the ultimate happiness.","That was her.","She’d stayed in the Gu house too long. Gotten too used to luxury.","So long that she’d forgotten who she used to be—someone with no time or energy for this kind of girlish drama.","She shot up, threw the door open, and bolted downstairs.","Jiang Yulan jumped. “Eating a little later is fine. Your stomach won’t go bad that fast...”","But He Huanhuan ran straight outside and shouted into the yard, “Old Tang! Old Tang!”","Old Tang rode up smoothly on his e-bike. “What is it, miss?”","He Huanhuan snatched the e-bike from him. “Let me ride it!”","She was going to eat spicy hotpot.","She was a streetwise chick, and she needed her street food!","She desperately wanted to escape this lavish estate, to hit the clamoring streets and bury herself in a steaming hotpot joint, scarfing down a messy feast.","Before Old Tang could respond, she twisted the throttle to the max. The e-bike shot off like an arrow!","The wind rushed past her face, and a grin spread across her lips.","This was it.","Riding an e-bike, wind in her hair, racing toward her favorite bowl of spicy goodness.","That was her real happiness.","She found a random hotpot shop, ordered a giant bowl, and sat quietly on a plastic stool, eating.","She ate until dark, the bowl nearly empty.","She patted her stomach. Full.","Just as she stood to leave, a shadow fell over her.","She looked up, stunned.","It was Han Mo.","“What are you doing here?”","Han Mo held a number tag and sat down. “Wait for me. We’ll go together.”","She sat frozen in shock, watching him finish a whole bowl of spicy hotpot.","“You coming? It’s dark out.”","“Coming.”","She got up in a daze and followed him out of the shop.","Outside, parked next to her little e-bike, was that old BYD.","She asked, “Why are you driving this?”","Hadn’t he already gotten what he wanted? Why was he still driving that cheap car?","Why hadn’t he switched back to his luxury ride?","A long pause passed before he replied softly, “It drives pretty well.”","“Good to drive or not, it’s not right for you.”","A strange wave of grievance welled up in her chest. Angrily, she put on her helmet and swung onto her e-bike.","“I’m going home. Don’t contact me anymore.”","Then she added, “And stop driving my car!”","She’d picked this car. It was hers.","He wasn’t allowed to drive it.","With that, her e-bike shot off. The BYD immediately followed.","He Huanhuan accelerated in irritation, but there was no way an e-bike could outrun a car.","She yelled back, “Stop following me!”","Han Mo turned his head toward her. “Pull over first. I have something to say.”","He Huanhuan ignored him. “What’s there to say? Are we that close?”","“Just stop first.”","“None of your business!”","She sped up even more, making Han Mo anxious. “Don’t ride so fast. It’s dangerous.”","A red light was coming up. He was afraid she’d lose control and run straight through it.","Sure enough, she didn’t slow down at all. He turned again and shouted, “Huanhuan, red light. Stop.”","He didn’t see it coming—from his right, a van was hurtling straight toward him, accelerating fast.","“BANG!”"]},{"number":48,"title":"Chapter 48: Don't Call the Police","paragraphs":["The tremendous force sent Han Mo’s car spinning several times through the air before it crashed upside down onto the ground.","A long skid mark was etched into the asphalt, and thick smoke quickly billowed from the wrecked vehicle.","A van pulled up slowly, its door slid open, and a man wearing a hat and mask stepped out.","He walked over to the car, crouched down, and stared hard at Han Mo in the driver’s seat.","“Han Mo, don’t blame me. You brought this on yourself.”","“Han Xuan.”","Blood blurred his vision, but Han Mo still managed to say his name firmly: “Have you lost your mind?”","“I have lost my mind—because you drove me to it!”","Han Xuan lunged forward, grabbing Han Mo by the hair and screaming: “You forced me! Why did you come back to the company? Why?”","“The company account was locked...”","“Liar!”","A wild gleam flared in Han Xuan’s eyes. “You’re lying! You didn’t unlock the company account! You tricked me! And you tricked Dad! You liar!”","Han Mo struggled to open his eyes, caked with blood. Everything was a red haze, and his breathing came in frantic gasps. “I didn’t...”","“You didn’t my ass!”","Han Xuan wouldn’t listen. He cursed bitterly: “You really think I’m stupid? Brother Bao told me everything! He paid off some connections—it had nothing to do with you!”","He looked down at Han Mo, whose face was streaked with blood.","“Han Mo, if you want to blame anyone, blame Dad. Blame him for playing favorites, for cheating on Mom, for having kids he couldn’t raise right.”","With those words, he turned away without hesitation.","Behind him, fuel slowly leaked from the overturned car’s gas tank.","He pulled out a lighter, lit it, and calmly tossed it toward the wreck.","Flames began to rise, and he sat in the van, watching from a distance.","Until the deafening explosion rang out.","“Boom!”","A burst of sky-high sparks erupted. He took off his hat and saluted the flames. “Goodbye, Han Mo.”","The van sped away without a trace of regret.","Han Xuan laughed joyfully in the driver’s seat. From now on, the company would be all his!","Dad had no other choice now—he’d never have to worry about being kicked out again!","Ha ha ha ha!","What he didn’t know was that while he was crouched by the car, threatening Han Mo,","a hand had silently reached out from the bushes behind him.","That hand held a phone, capturing everything on video without moving an inch.","The moment he left, He Huanhuan rolled out from the bushes.","She slipped deftly into the car, unbuckled Han Mo’s seatbelt, and dragged him out.","She wiped his face carelessly, hoisted him onto her back, and carried him along the greenery toward the nearest hospital.","“Cough... cough...”","After walking for over half an hour, Han Mo finally regained some consciousness.","“Are... are you okay?”","He remembered that when the car was hit, it had crushed He Huanhuan’s electric scooter.","“You’re awake?”","He Huanhuan turned her head to look at him. “Hold on. It’s too remote here—I can’t hail a cab. I’ll keep walking until I find a ride, and then we’ll go to the hospital.”","“No hospital.”","Han Mo struggled to get down. “I have to go back... I have to go back...”","He Huanhuan tightened her grip on him. “What are you doing? Stop moving!”","At over six feet tall, Han Mo was heavy for her to carry.","When he struggled, she nearly toppled over.","But Han Mo insisted: “I have to get back...”","He Huanhuan didn’t understand. “Go back for what? That car is completely wrecked—it’s useless.”","“I need the dashcam footage to keep as evidence...”","“You can’t keep it anymore!”","He Huanhuan walked faster: “Han Xuan set the fire, and your car has been blown to ashes. So much for your damn evidence!”","“How dare he!”","Han Mo thought Han Xuan might lose his mind, but he never imagined Han Xuan would go this far.","“Han Mo, don’t blame me. If you want to blame anyone, blame...”","Suddenly, Han Xuan’s voice echoed in his ears. Han Mo looked down in surprise.","On He Huanhuan’s phone, a video was playing of Han Xuan threatening him coldly.","He stared at her in shock: “You filmed it?”","He Huanhuan sneered: “He was so arrogant, how could I not film it?”","She shifted Han Mo’s weight and hoisted him higher: “Don’t worry. I’ve got all the evidence we need. Han Xuan won’t get away with this.”","The most important thing now was to hail a taxi to the hospital.","His face was covered in blood, and he looked terrifying.","But unexpectedly, even with the evidence, Han Mo insisted: “Not the hospital for now.”","“Why now? Do you have a death wish?”","Han Mo struggled to get down: “I’m fine. I can walk.”","He had just checked himself over. He hadn’t sustained any major injuries.","Just a bump on the head, which had split open and bled a little.","It looked scary, but it probably wasn’t serious.","He took He Huanhuan’s hand and led her off the road into the trees by the roadside.","He Huanhuan was stunned: “What are you doing? Do you want to die?”","But Han Mo asked her: “Did you call for help just now?”","His question finally jogged her memory.","He Huanhuan slapped her thigh: “Damn! How did I forget? I could have called 911!”","She must have lost her mind, carrying Han Mo and looking for a taxi.","Why didn’t she just call 911?","She fumbled for her phone, ready to dial.","But Han Mo reached out and covered her phone with his hand: “Don’t call.”","“Huh?”","Han Mo wiped the blood off his face: “Go back. When you get home, don’t tell anyone you saw me tonight, okay?”","“Why?”","The one who broke the law was obviously Han Xuan.","Why did Han Mo have to hide?","He Huanhuan really didn’t understand.","But Han Mo didn’t seem willing to explain, which made He Huanhuan very unhappy.","She clutched her phone tightly: “If you don’t explain it to me clearly, I’ll delete the video!”","What was he playing at?","What was there to hide?","“Don’t delete.”","Han Mo’s pleading eyes fixed on her, which only made her more annoyed.","“Then come clean! Or I swear, I’ll call not just 911, but every emergency number I can think of!”","The two of them stood there, at a standoff.","Until Han Mo let out a soft sigh: “You weren’t supposed to be part of my plan...”","This accident had been in his plan, just not tonight.","The company’s account freeze was only temporary. Within two weeks at most, their company would be fully shut down.","By then, Han Changyong would definitely help Han Xuan pin everything on him.","That wasn’t the outcome he wanted.","He needed to give the company back to Han Xuan, let him go further, far enough that he could never recover.","“I didn’t expect him to come tonight.”","His plan was set for three days later. In three days, he had a business dinner that would run late.","Then, he would let Han Xuan know when his dinner ended and where he would go...","His face darkened: “I’m sorry for dragging you into this.”","He Huanhuan waved her hand: “That’s nothing. But how did Han Xuan know where you were tonight?”","Han Mo’s expression darkened even further. “Chen Yu, we had a plan. We were supposed to make him switch sides.”"]},{"number":49,"title":"Chapter 49: Just Half a Month","paragraphs":["Chen Yu, had he betrayed him?","Or had he simply changed his mind on his own?","He clenched his fists. Chen Yu was his cousin, and from the moment he decided to take revenge for his mother, Chen Yu had always been on his side.","It was hard for him to imagine how he would face Chen Yu if he had indeed betrayed him.","And how would he face his uncle?","He Huanhuan didn’t care about what was going on with Chen Yu; she only cared about one thing:","“So, according to your original plan, after Han Xuan hit you with the car, what were you going to do?”","Han Mo looked up to his left front: “Chen Yu rented an apartment for me. I planned to stay there for half a month, until everything settled down before coming out.”","“What settled down? How would it settle down?”","Even though He Huanhuan didn’t know much about running a company, she knew that involvement in cross-border telecom fraud was a serious crime.","She asked Han Mo, “How were you going to take the company back then?”","“I wasn’t.”","Han Mo forced a smile, a smile uglier than crying: “I never planned to take it back. I’ve already gotten back what belonged to my mother.”","What he wanted was never the company.","Back then, his mother had taken the company public, with a market value of eight hundred million.","He had already taken that money back.","The projects Han Xuan had shut down, the prepaid funds, and the penalties for breach of contract—","He had recovered all of it.","As for the company, and the shares Han Changyong held in his hands, he had never wanted them.","He only wanted the company to go bankrupt quickly. He wanted all of it to disappear from this world.","He Huanhuan looked at him firmly: “So... the fraud involving Han Xuan, and Gu Chacha’s concert—that was also your doing?”","Han Mo nodded lightly: “I just gave them a choice.”","Whether to take it or not was up to them.","Unfortunately, they didn’t hesitate for a second before making their decision.","The consequences of their own choices had nothing to do with him.","He Huanhuan stared at him expressionlessly: “You’re really ruthless.”","“I’m sorry.”","“Why are you apologizing to me?”","Han Mo looked down at her: “You had nothing to do with any of this, but I dragged you into it.”","He Huanhuan kicked him angrily: “You know that!”","With that, she turned and walked away. After a few steps, she stomped back furiously: “You’re definitely not going to that apartment. So what are you going to do now?”","Han Mo shrugged indifferently: “Anything works. Half a month isn’t long.”","He needed to let Han Xuan smoothly enter the company and continue collaborating with that person.","By then, there would be no way for him to escape.","If Han Changyong wanted to bail him out, he’d have to shell out at least half his wealth.","That was Han Mo’s goal—to strip Han Changyong back to his original state.","His mother had worked herself to the bone building that fortune. How could she be hurt to the point of depression, fall ill, and die, while Han Changyong enjoyed everything in peace, playing out a father-son love story with Han Xuan in the house his mother had bought?","Every time he saw that scene, he found it ridiculous and disgusting.","He had to drive them out of that house.","That house was bought by his mother for him. It was his house.","“Alright,” He Huanhuan put her phone away, grabbed Han Mo, and pulled him toward the woods. “Come with me.”","Han Mo was surprised: “Where to?”","He Huanhuan replied matter-of-factly: “To find a place to stay! You want to sleep out in the wild?”","She led Han Mo through the wild woods by the roadside. By the time they found the nearest village, it was already very late.","She walked straight to the end of the village and, sure enough, found an old brick house at the very back.","It had four windows, three of which were broken.","It was obvious no one had lived there for years.","She skillfully slipped up to a broken window, reached in, and opened it from the inside.","“Follow me.”","She placed her hands on the wall and vaulted inside with remarkable agility.","Han Mo was stunned: “Is this okay?”","“Shut up and get in.”","“Fine.”","Han Mo carefully climbed in after her, only to find the house thick with dust, impossible to step in without leaving marks.","He couldn’t help frowning: “We’re staying here?”","He’d rather sleep out in the wild, where at least there wouldn’t be this much dust.","“Where else?”","He Huanhuan glanced at the room and nodded with satisfaction.","It’s just a bit dirty—nothing else wrong with it.","It reminded her of the house she used to live in. Felt familiar.","She went to the main room, dug out a dried-out plastic basin, and handed it to Han Mo: “Go back out, find the kitchen, and get some water.”","Han Mo’s face was full of reluctance: “Is there even water here?”","He felt the house was practically a wreck.","He couldn’t help suggesting, “How about we just leave? I think sleeping outside is fine too.”","He Huanhuan rolled her eyes at him: “You don’t think there’s nothing out there in the wild, do you?”","Snakes, ants, bugs, mice—there’s plenty in the wild.","If you sleep out on the ground at night, you might end up with bugs crawling into your ears.","Having a house and not sleeping in it, but choosing a field—your brain must be broken!","“But this place... it’s too rundown...”","Han Mo had never seen such a dilapidated house in his entire life.","He really couldn’t believe a place like this could be lived in.","He Huanhuan glared at him: “Who are you insulting? I used to live in a house like this! And it was perfectly fine!”","These kinds of houses were built by the villagers themselves, with solid materials.","Seeing Han Mo dawdling and unwilling to cooperate, she rolled her eyes at him, turned around, and jumped out the window herself.","In these old village houses, the tap was always in the kitchen.","She felt her way to the tap in the dark, mustered all her strength, and turned it on.","Gurgle, gurgle...","First came the sound of rust being washed away, then a rush of murky yellow water.","“Is... is this water?”","Han Mo had just followed her out and saw the water from the tap—it looked like coffee.","He was utterly shocked: “Is this what tap water looks like in the countryside?”","He Huanhuan patiently explained: “It’s been unused for too long and the pipes have rusted. Once the rust is flushed out, it’ll be fine.”","Han Mo: ... He had a feeling this wasn’t going to be reliable.","The young master had never lived like the poor. A basin full of coffee-colored tap water had shattered his worldview.","He hesitated, walked over to He Huanhuan, and asked, “Do we really have to use this water?”","He Huanhuan looked up at him: “Do you have anywhere else to go?”","Han Mo shook his head silently.","She raised her phone again: “Can I turn my phone on now?”","Han Mo kept shaking his head.","Earlier on the road, he had made her power off her phone.","He said that leaving it on would allow them to be tracked and found.","He Huanhuan tossed the plastic basin to him: “Wait here. Once the water runs clear, wash the basin, then fill it up.”","She was exhausted and wanted to wipe down a bed and get some sleep.","Han Mo stood stiffly by the tap. He didn’t believe clean water would ever come out of it.","But as the water kept flowing, the coffee color faded more and more, until it turned into clear, cold tap water.","He was completely amazed—it really had just been rust."]},{"number":50,"title":"Chapter 50: Why Are You Taking Advantage of Me","paragraphs":["He rinsed the plastic basin clean, filled it with water, and brought it to the window.","He Huanhuan stood inside, taking the basin of water into the room. She glanced at herself, then at Han Mo.","“You, take off your clothes.”","Han Mo’s suit had been torn when he was hit, and the chest area was stained with a fair amount of blood.","It was unwearable anyway, so she might as well use it as a rag.","She just needed a rag, but Han Mo didn’t know that. Han Mo thought...","Without a word, he took off his suit jacket and handed it to He Huanhuan. As soon as she wet the jacket, her eyes suddenly lit up!","Holy cow!","Abs!","Eight of them!","The hazy moonlight shone by the window, the faintly visible abs right in front of her.","Firm, crisscrossed ridges...","She couldn’t help but purse her lips tightly: “What are you doing?”","Han Mo looked down at her: “Didn’t you tell me to take off my clothes?”","He Huanhuan glanced at his abs again, her face blushing involuntarily: “I told you to take off your jacket. Why are you taking off your shirt?”","“Then I misunderstood.”","His long, slender fingers picked up the shirt and slipped it back on.","One by one, the buttons were fastened over his abs, slowly hiding the beautiful sight away...","He Huanhuan couldn’t tear her gaze away from him at all.","Damn rich guy, his body was so much better than those scrawny little punks!","Every scrawny little punk back then was just a bag of bones, totally unappetizing.","No wonder she never wanted to fall in love before. Who wants to suffer?","She blinked and said to Han Mo, “Um, it’s not cold out. Take off your clothes and rinse yourself with tap water, it’ll be more comfortable.”","She swore she didn’t want to see his abs.","She just thought people should stay clean, really.","“Alright.”","Han Mo turned and walked to the faucet, took off his shirt, soaked it, then balled it up and wiped his body bit by bit.","Water droplets slid down the line of his shoulders, rolled over his sharply defined abs, and slowly disappeared into his pants.","Ah! Those damn pants!","“You can...”","He Huanhuan abruptly shut her mouth. Oh no!","Guiltily, she turned around: “Um, I wasn’t staring at you! I was just trying to talk to you!”","A faint smile lifted the corner of Han Mo’s mouth, and his voice carried a full dose of temptation: “You can look. I don’t mind.”","He Huanhuan blustered: “I didn’t want to look at you. Your body’s just average anyway.”","“Then I’ll work on it more next time.”","He Huanhuan instinctively turned her head: “Don’t overdo it! Light muscle is the most perfect!”","Her gaze was suddenly grabbed, forcefully drawing closer: “You like it?”","He Huanhuan’s eyes darted away frantically. She clenched the suit jacket in her hands: “Um, after you wash up, come in and get to work. I’m already sleepy...”","“Okay.”","Han Mo supported himself with one hand on the windowsill and vaulted into the room. He leaned close to He Huanhuan and asked, “What needs to be done?”","The damp, steamy air clung to his body and washed over He Huanhuan, carrying a rusty, watery scent that made her head feel a little dizzy.","“Wipe the dust off the bed. Tonight, we’ll just make do and sleep... no, wait, tonight we’ll just make do and rest...”","She felt her face grow burning hot, so hot she couldn’t even speak clearly.","Han Mo reached out and took the suit jacket: “I’ll handle it. Do you want to go wash your face and freshen up?”","“Huh? Me?”","He Huanhuan’s face instantly turned crimson. Was he going to look at her?","Wasn’t this moving a bit too fast?","Han Mo reached out and brushed her hair: “Don’t overthink it. There’s dust on your face. Wiping it clean will be better.”","“Oh, right, right...”","He Huanhuan fled out of the room as if escaping. What on earth was she thinking!","She turned on the faucet and looked at the shirt in her hands, hesitating.","It was just a very ordinary white shirt, but...","The cool fabric brushed against the skin on her neck, and she caught a scent of blood that wasn’t hers.","A sweet, coppery smell rushed into her nose, instantly pulling her back to an hour before.","He had been lying on her back, his breaths brushing over her nape again and again.","Carrying that thick, sweet-iron smell.","At the time, she hadn’t felt much of anything. But for some reason, recalling it now sent goosebumps all over her body.","What was wrong? She felt like she was getting sick.","Her whole skin tingled and felt cold.","She was definitely sick.","“Huanhuan, is this clean enough?”","Han Mo’s voice struck like a thunderbolt, instantly breaking through her discomfort.","The cold feeling vanished in a second. She was fine!","Guiltily, she walked over to check. The old wooden bed had been wiped until it shone, and the water in the plastic basin had turned as black as sesame paste.","“That’s enough. It’s not like we’re staying here long.”","When dawn came, they’d go earn some money, then find a cheap motel that didn’t check IDs.","She hung up Han Mo’s shirt to dry, and they both lay down on the bed, ready to sleep.","The old wooden bed wasn’t big, just enough room for two people.","“Are you cold?”","She asked softly.","Han Mo shook his head, but it was too dark for He Huanhuan to see.","She ventured, “Do you want to scoot over closer to me and sleep?”","“Alright.”","A warm body pressed against her back, and hot breaths fell on her hair, making her own breathing feel warmer too.","“Aren’t you cold, then?”","She could feel the heat radiating off his body.","“A little cold.”","“Oh...”","The two silhouettes clung together like this until they slowly fell asleep.","Once she was asleep, He Huanhuan became much bolder. As the temperature dropped in the latter half of the night, she instinctively latched onto the warm source beside her.","She nuzzled her head into his chest, letting out a satisfied sigh.","But poor Han Mo stayed awake with his eyes wide open until the middle of the night.","He couldn’t sleep, and he didn’t dare to.","Just as he was about to close his eyes and doze off, He Huanhuan’s hand wandered over to his abs.","She rubbed them while giggling to herself.","He even wondered if she was actually asleep or not.","But then that mischievous hand started moving further down, and he grabbed her hand immediately: “No can do.”","“Mmm~”","He Huanhuan grumbled unhappily with her eyes closed.","Han Mo had no choice but to keep holding her hand, preventing her from causing mischief.","But even as he held her hand, her leg started acting up.","She threw her left leg over his and wiggled it restlessly.","Han Mo shifted, trying to escape her harassment.","But her leg pinned him down forcefully, and the woman on him mumbled vaguely: “Don’t move!”","He froze instantly. Her leg was back up in no time, and both hands securely wrapped around him.","One arm hugged his bicep, the other hand kept stroking his abs.","Very clear division of labor.","He sighed quietly. Fine, fine. Let it be.","He stayed awake until dawn, when the village echoed with the shrill crowing of roosters. Only then did He Huanhuan murmur, turn over, and sleep over by the edge of the bed.","Han Mo closed his eyes in resignation, then opened them again a moment later.","If she wasn’t hugging him, how could he fall asleep...","He thought for a moment, then reached out and pulled He Huanhuan into his arms. Finally, closing his eyes, he fell asleep peacefully.","After a few hours of broken sleep, he opened his eyes to find He Huanhuan staring at him with puffed cheeks: “How can you take advantage of me like this!”","......"]},{"number":51,"title":"Chapter 51: Cousin Where are you","paragraphs":["He tried to explain, \"I didn't...\"","He Huanhuan reached out and poked his arm. \"Then why were you holding me?\"","And holding her so tight that even after she woke up, she felt too embarrassed to move and just lay there with her eyes open until he woke up.","Han Mo was exasperated. He really ought to install a surveillance camera in this house so she could see how she tortured him last night!","\"Hurry up and get up. It's getting late,\" she said.","He Huanhuan pushed him, urging him to get out of bed.","They climbed out through the window and washed up quickly.","She dragged him along the village path behind the houses, then slipped out of the village pretending to be morning strollers.","Han Mo was confused. \"Why are we doing this?\"","It felt like sneaking around like thieves.","He Huanhuan shot him a glare. \"Well, aren't we basically thieves? Even if it's an abandoned house, we're still squatting here without permission!\"","\"If the villagers find out and kindly call the police, all the suffering we went through last night would be for nothing.\"","Standing at the village entrance, she glanced toward the city and asked Han Mo, \"Can we really not go into the city?\"","Han Mo shook his head. \"We can't risk being caught on too many surveillance cameras.\"","Otherwise, they’d be easy to track down.","He Huanhuan refused to give up. \"What if I wear a hat? Change my hairstyle, hunch over a little...\"","\"No.\"","Han Mo rejected it flatly. \"Those are useless tricks. Big data scanning can identify you in a second.\"","He Huanhuan was speechless. \"So I can't turn on my phone at all, huh?\"","Han Mo nodded. \"Right.\"","Then what the hell were they supposed to do?","These days, you couldn't do anything without a phone.","Even if you found a part-time job, they’d pay you through online transfers!","He Huanhuan frowned. \"Honestly, I feel like you’re probably not in that much trouble. How about I just go home?\"","She’d finally had a few days of good living—did she really have to suffer through meaningless hardship with him?","Han Mo took her hand and smiled softly. \"Huanhuan, it’s too late. Your father has probably already noticed you’re missing. By now, he’s likely launched a large-scale search.\"","They were stuck together now. If she went home, he’d be found immediately.","He Huanhuan slapped her own forehead. \"Why didn’t I think to call 120!\"","If she had, she’d be sitting at the Gu family’s five-meter-long dining table having breakfast right now!","And she wouldn’t be starving!","\"Growl~\"","Her stomach chose that moment to complain, and she couldn’t help asking again, \"Are you sure your cousin really betrayed you? Could it be that Han Xuan just managed to get information out of him?\"","Han Mo’s face darkened instantly. \"He graduated from a top-three university in the country. You think Han Xuan could trick him into talking?\"","He Huanhuan waved her hand dismissively. \"Fine, fine.\"","So they had no options left. She’d just have to go back to her old rough-and-tumble life with him!","She sighed, grabbed his arm, and dragged him toward an even more remote area. \"Let's go!\"","\"Where?\"","\"To find a job!\"","They avoided the main roads, sticking to country paths, slowly making their way to a remote suburb.","Back at the Chen family home, Chen Yu’s eyes were swollen red from crying as he knelt before Chen Chaoyang, sobbing uncontrollably.","Chen Chaoyang’s face was dark as thunder as he swung his belt fiercely, striking Chen Yu. \"Tell me the truth! Was this your idea or Han Mo’s?\"","Chen Yu winced in pain. \"My cousin and I planned it together...\"","Chen Chaoyang was furious. Those two brats had incredible nerve!","Risking their lives like this!","Did they think they were lead characters in a TV drama, unkillable?","Every year, how many people died in car accidents in this country? Hadn’t they ever looked at the statistics?","Thinking about this, he kicked his son hard. \"Where is he now?\"","Tears streamed down Chen Yu’s face. \"I don’t know, sob sob sob... My cousin and I originally planned to do it the day after tomorrow. I went to his apartment last night—it was empty, sob sob sob...\"","What were they going to do?","Never mind Han Mo—but now Miss Gu was missing too!","They had completely botched this!","Chen Chaoyang wished he could beat some sense into this idiot son.","\"You already got the money back—why did you have to stir up more trouble?\"","Chen Yu cried even harder. \"We had to make the company collapse! That company was started by Auntie—why should that lecherous old man Han Changyong get to keep it?\"","\"You—!\"","Chen Chaoyang wanted to scold him, but the words got stuck in his throat.","How could he not feel hatred?","Meixin was his only sister.","She had been like a little ray of sunshine, and in the end, she weighed barely over sixty pounds.","Whenever he thought of it, he couldn’t help but tear up.","He turned away, wiped the corner of his eye, and choked out, \"But you can’t just follow Han Mo on these reckless schemes. He’s your aunt’s only child. If anything happens to him, how are you going to explain it to her?\"","Chen Yu shrunk back, explaining guiltily, \"I had the car reinforced. It wouldn’t have killed anyone...\"","Chen Chaoyang raised his belt again. \"Then where is he now?\"","Chen Yu let out a wail. \"I don’t know! I went to the apartment—there was no one there!\"","He really couldn’t figure out how Han Xuan had found his cousin.","Going to find He Huanhuan had been a spur-of-the-moment decision. They were about to head home after work when his cousin suddenly realized she had deleted him and immediately drove off to see her.","He had tried to talk him out of it.","He said, \"You won her over just so Uncle Gu wouldn’t pick Han Xuan, right? Now that your goal is achieved, there’s no more need for you two to stay in touch.\"","He remembered his cousin giving him a cold look, not saying a word, and driving away.","Damn love—truly destructive!","Cousin! If you don’t show up soon, he’s going to get beaten to death!","But unfortunately, Han Mo couldn’t hear his cries at all.","Right now, he and He Huanhuan were strolling through the fields.","Well, no—they were looking for work.","As for what kind of work, he had no idea.","After walking along the small path for over an hour, a brand-new residential complex appeared ahead.","He Huanhuan smiled and pointed at the complex. \"I saw online that they’re hiring actors. Let’s go try out.\"","Han Mo was puzzled. \"Actors?\"","He Huanhuan shot him a knowing look. \"Pretending you don’t know? Isn’t this the typical capitalist trick?\"","When a new housing project launches, you bring in a bunch of people to pretend to be house-hunters, pretending to buy, and fighting over units.","They’d even get into fights, yelling curses at each other’s ancestors.","All to fool the real, unsuspecting buyers.","When they saw the chaos, they’d think, \"Wow, people are literally fighting over these units!\" and rush to buy.","Then, when they asked the salesperson, wouldn’t you know it—just one unit happened to open up.","The floor plan was bad, the floor was bad too, but since no one knew about it, the salesperson would sign them on the spot!","Once contracts were signed and deposits paid, guess what?","They’d realize they were the only real buyer in the whole place. Everyone else was just part of the atmosphere squad.","Han Mo was stunned. He knew sales departments had their tactics.","But the specifics—like getting people to fight and swear—would never show up in the performance reports.","The reports he received only listed how many units were sold that month, marketing expenses, revenue, and actual collections.","The breakdown of expenses? He’d never seen it.","He Huanhuan clapped her hands like an old pro. \"Today, big sister is going to show you how the real world works!\""]},{"number":52,"title":"Chapter 52: Old Acquaintance","paragraphs":["On a workday, the sales hall was deathly quiet.","Wang Qiang leaned against the doorway in boredom, counting his fingers. He suspected he was the jinx of the sales world.","He used to sell health supplements but hadn't made a single sale before the company got raided.","Luckily, he hadn't closed any deals, so after an investigation, they let him go.","He figured health supplements were sketchy, so he needed to sell something reliable.","He went to work at a 4S dealership selling cars. Three months in, he'd sold exactly one vehicle.","It was the cheapest Qin series, and his commission was just two hundred bucks.","He didn't mind the measly two hundred, but the store manager minded that he couldn't close deals and fired him.","After getting canned, he thought it over—selling cars still wasn't the way.","The unit price was too low; one sale wouldn't even cover two days of meals.","He had to sell houses. If he could move just one property, the commission would feed him for a whole year!","So he came to the real estate sales office. After a month on the job, he hadn't sold a single unit...","At least this time, he wasn't the only one striking out—everyone was in the same boat.","That was some consolation.","He was daydreaming, kicking at the floor: \"Come on, someone come look at a house. Even if you don't buy, just browsing would be nice...\"","\"Hey! Little Fatty, has your project opened for sales yet?\"","He looked up excitedly: \"It's open! It's open! You want to... wait, it's you two?\"","Seeing He Huanhuan and Han Mo, he was a bit taken aback: \"You two want to buy a house?\"","He still remembered how He Huanhuan had demanded a gift from him last time—she was even fiercer than the aunties scrambling for discounted groceries.","He Huanhuan glanced at him: \"Do I know you?\"","Wang Qiang stepped forward: \"You don't remember me? Last time you bought a BYD, I was the one who helped you!\"","He Huanhuan tried to recall. There seemed to be some chubby guy, but he wasn't this fat...","\"Did you gain more weight?\"","Wang Qiang scratched his head sheepishly: \"Sales pressure is high, so I eat a lot...\"","He hadn't sold many cars, but he'd packed on several pounds.","He stole a glance at Han Mo. He remembered this guy was loaded.","He always used a black card.","Wang Qiang looked at them with eager anticipation: \"Are you two here to buy a house?\"","Was he finally going to close a deal?","He'd already calculated—even the smallest floor plan.","If he could sell just one, his commission would be twenty thousand!","Hehehe...","With twenty thousand, he'd treat himself to a 350-buck buffet...","And buy a new electric scooter, and...","He hadn't even earned the money yet, but he'd already planned how to spend it.","Unfortunately, he was destined to be disappointed today.","He Huanhuan shook her head bluntly: \"No, I'm not buying. I just want to ask if you need any actors to pose as house viewers.\"","\"Huh?\"","Wang Qiang was crushed: \"Not today.\"","The economy had been bad the last couple of years, and the real estate market was sluggish.","Their sales office only arranged fake viewers every few days. Without real buyers, what was the point?","He Huanhuan asked matter-of-factly: \"Why not arrange any? What's wrong with your company?\"","She even made Wang Qiang feel nervous. He explained awkwardly: \"The economy is bad. Houses aren't selling, so there are no real buyers coming...\"","Wait, why was he the one feeling awkward?","It wasn't his fault, was it?","Before he could muster any confidence, He Huanhuan asked again: \"So when do you need them? I want to do this job.\"","Wang Qiang counted on his fingers: \"The day after tomorrow. A newlywed couple has scheduled a viewing for a wedding house.\"","The team leader had mentioned that morning they needed to hire a few fake viewers to stir up the couple's interest.","He asked He Huanhuan: \"You want to come? If so, I'll let the team leader know.\"","He Huanhuan nodded eagerly: \"Yes! Both of us will come. We'll play any role.\"","Wang Qiang led them to the team leader's office. With their good looks, the leader decided on the spot: \"You two it is. The day after tomorrow, 9:30 sharp. One hundred each, and you'll play a newlywed couple too.\"","He Huanhuan agreed without hesitation: \"Deal! We'll be there on time!\"","As they left the sales hall, Han Mo looked worried.","They had work set for the day after tomorrow, but what about today and tomorrow?","He'd never in his life worried about a meal before.","No ID, no phone, and they couldn't be caught on large-scale surveillance.","For the first time, he really had no idea how to earn money.","\"Huanhuan, how are we—\"","Before he could finish, He Huanhuan had already gone back to Wang Qiang: \"Little Fatty, can you lend me some money?\"","Wang Qiang was stunned: \"You're asking me to lend you money?\"","He Huanhuan nodded: \"Yeah.\"","Wang Qiang stepped back: \"But I don't even know you!\"","He Huanhuan took a big step closer: \"I bought a car from you! How can you say you don't know me?\"","Wang Qiang clutched his phone tightly: \"But I only made two hundred in commission from that sale!\"","\"I'm only borrowing two hundred.\"","......","Wang Qiang grimaced: \"Can I not lend it?\"","He'd only been at the sales office for a month and hadn't gotten his salary yet.","He didn't have much money on him either.","He Huanhuan leaned in and asked: \"Have you made a sale yet?\"","Wang Qiang shook his head: \"It's not that easy. The economy's bad. Who buys a house for no reason?\"","He Huanhuan looked at him sincerely: \"How about this: you lend me two hundred, and next month I'll have him buy a house from you. Deal?\"","Wang Qiang glanced at her: \"Do you think that sounds believable?\"","If she needed to borrow two hundred, how was she going to buy a house?","He Huanhuan turned his head toward Han Mo: \"Don't look at me. Look at him.\"","Compared to the day they bought the car, Han Mo looked much more ragged.","His white shirt was wrinkled and unironed, hanging loosely on him.","But with his narrow waist and broad shoulders, he somehow made the wrinkled shirt look effortlessly stylish.","Wang Qiang looked at Han Mo, then at He Huanhuan, then back at Han Mo.","Then he gritted his teeth and said: \"I can lend it to him, but not to you.\"","He Huanhuan was speechless: \"You're judging by looks, you know that? Don't I look trustworthy?\"","Wang Qiang shook his head: \"No.\"","He Huanhuan: ......","Whatever. At least he was willing to lend.","Wang Qiang pulled out his phone and looked at Han Mo: \"Give me your payment QR code, and I'll transfer it to you.\"","Han Mo: \"I don't have a phone.\"","His phone had been thrown from the car in the crash, and He Huanhuan hadn't thought to look for it.","But even if they found it, it wouldn't matter—they couldn't use phones anyway.","They still couldn't receive the money.","Wang Qiang frowned: \"I'm starting to not want to lend to you, okay?\"","No phone? This felt even more unreliable!","\"Of course not!\"","He Huanhuan jumped up and threw her arm around his neck: \"We're old friends! You can't do this to a friend!\"","\"Friends?\"","Wang Qiang asked in a daze: \"Are we friends?\"","Han Mo stepped forward in an instant, rescuing Wang Qiang. He frowned disapprovingly: \"Don't bully him.\"","Then he stood between the two, blocking He Huanhuan's little antics.","He looked down at Wang Qiang: \"Sorry, we've run into some trouble lately. I know you're not well-off either...\"","Wang Qiang thought he was about to say they wouldn't borrow the money, but then he paused and continued: \"But today, we really have to borrow this money. I'm truly sorry.\"","....","He was surprisingly polite."]},{"number":53,"title":"Chapter 53: Delivering Takeout","paragraphs":["“I’ll lend it to you.”","Wang Qiang said firmly. He was definitely going to lend this money.","He Huanhuan said they were friends.","After junior high school, he had been wandering around working odd jobs. How long had it been since he had a friend?","So long he couldn’t even remember.","Every day after work, he went back to his rented room—cramped, narrow, and silent.","No one talked to him, and he had no one to talk to.","He could only lie quietly in his rented room, eating takeout. He hadn’t saved a single cent, but he had eaten himself into a fat mess...","Boo hoo...","He couldn’t think about it. If he kept thinking, he’d cry.","“Wait for me a moment.”","He jogged into the sales office, swapped with a coworker for two hundred in cash, then jogged back out and handed the money to He Huanhuan: “Friend, here’s your money.”","He Huanhuan took the money solemnly: “Thank you, friend. We’ll definitely pay you back!”","Wang Qiang nodded even more solemnly: “If you don’t pay me back, the day after tomorrow I won’t let the team leader settle your pay.”","......","“Deal!”","With the two hundred yuan in hand, their steps felt much lighter.","He Huanhuan asked with a smile, “Han Mo, what should we do?”","Han Mo rubbed his stomach: “Let’s eat first.”","They hadn’t eaten anything since last night. They were really hungry.","“Okay!”","The two walked back along the small path and returned to the village they’d been in earlier.","They strolled along the village road, wandering until they reached the village entrance. By the main road, there was a row of shop-front houses with a few small restaurants.","They picked a noodle shop, went in, and each ordered a bowl of beef noodles, spending thirty yuan total.","When they handed over cash, the boss seemed a bit taken aback.","The boss pointed at the QR code on the wall: “Just scan to pay.”","These days, hardly anyone used cash anymore.","He Huanhuan clutched the money and laughed: “Boss, I don’t have a phone. Just take the cash, okay?”","She said this with her multi-colored hair, and the boss immediately became wary.","He took the money, inspected it front and back, then held it up to the sun for a closer look.","He Huanhuan was speechless. Did he think she was trying to pass off fake money?","Luckily, the money her coworker had swapped was real.","After confirming it was genuine, the boss pocketed the cash.","He turned around to prepare their beef noodles.","He Huanhuan sat down with a huff and asked Han Mo, “Do I look that unreliable?”","She thought she looked perfectly approachable!","What was wrong with their judgment?","Han Mo glanced at her hair: “Do you think someone with hair like that looks approachable? Friendly?”","Her hair looked way too outrageous, and outrageous often meant unfriendly and unapproachable.","He Huanhuan pouted unhappily: “If I hadn’t dyed my hair, those people would look down on me and shove me into the bathroom to beat me up...”","“Who?”","Han Mo’s eyes darkened instantly: “Who bullied you? Why did they hit you?”","He Huanhuan waved her hand: “That’s all in the past. It’s long over.”","It was just something from junior high school, and she had fought back like crazy too.","Even though she hadn’t won...","But she wasn’t the type to just take it. She quickly found a chance to get to know Qi Meili, who ran with the gangs, and became her friend.","Later, when those people tried to bully her again, she immediately reported it to Qi Meili.","Qi Meili brought seven or eight guys with tattoos to the school and gave those bullies a serious warning.","It was absolutely awesome!","Even now, thinking about it, she felt Qi Meili was a total hero!","But Han Mo pressed on in a low voice: “Did you get beaten up often back then?”","He couldn’t bear to imagine what a little girl like her had suffered in the past.","Thinking about her love for street-side stalls... had she not even been able to afford that kind of food before?","This was a life he simply couldn’t fathom.","How could anyone not afford something as cheap as spicy hot pot?","He had thought that the poorest person could still at least afford a house and a car.","If He Huanhuan knew what he was thinking, she’d jump up and hit him.","What, were you some kind of expert?","“Young people wanting to increase their income should just buy more houses and rent them out...”","She was just a kid—where was she supposed to get money to buy spicy hot pot?","She shot Han Mo an annoyed look: “Didn’t I tell you not to ask?”","There was no way she was going to tell him that later she became a punk girl.","If anyone dared to mess with her, she’d jump up and curse out their ancestors for eighteen generations, right?","After finishing the beef noodles, the two didn’t know what to do next.","They wandered around until they ended up back at that neighborhood.","Wang Qiang was still standing at the entrance. When he saw them coming, he immediately clutched his phone tight: “I really have no money left!”","He wouldn’t get paid until next week, and he only had three hundred left—he needed that to eat.","He Huanhuan waved her hand: “We’re not borrowing money. We’re just bored and wandering around.”","They couldn’t go to that dumpy house during the day.","If someone saw them, they might easily mistake them for burglars.","They had to wait until dark to sneak over and sleep.","But Wang Qiang didn’t know that. He gave them a disdainful look: “You two are this broke and you’re not thinking about making money? Why are you just wandering around?”","You had to borrow two hundred yuan, so why weren’t you earning some?","He Huanhuan touched her phone—she had hundreds of thousands in there!","Han Mo had transferred it to her.","But she couldn’t use it!","She sighed helplessly: “How are we supposed to earn? Isn’t your company only hiring the day after tomorrow?”","They couldn’t go into the city. There were too many cameras there—they’d be spotted too easily.","They couldn’t take buses or the subway either, since they had no phones to scan the QR codes.","Wang Qiang frowned at her question: “Deliver food! You get paid per delivery!”","Sometimes when he was off work and too bored at home, he would deliver food and earn a little bit here and there.","Hearing this, He Huanhuan’s eyes lit up: “You have a delivery driver account?”","Her eyes sparkled as she looked at Wang Qiang, making him shrink back instinctively.","Why did it feel like trouble was coming?","Sure enough, He Huanhuan immediately said, “Lend us your account!”","“Can’t you register your own?”","Wang Qiang couldn’t understand why she’d want to borrow his.","Anyone could register for one.","Was she planning to do something bad with his account?","He grew suspicious. He’d heard stories about people renting delivery driver accounts for high prices, using them to traffic drugs.","By the time the police came knocking, you couldn’t even explain yourself.","He looked at He Huanhuan, then at Han Mo, then back at He Huanhuan.","Friend, you’re looking pretty suspicious.","His suspicion was totally baseless—she had to borrow two hundred yuan from him; there was no way she could afford to rent his account!","She was borrowing it for free.","She leaned in mysteriously close to Wang Qiang and asked, “What do you think Han Mo looks like?”","Wang Qiang thought for a moment: “He looks rich.”","Really, really rich.","He Huanhuan nodded: “You’re right. We’re actually rich, but we’ve run into some trouble. You know how it is with rich families—there’s always some drama...”","She winked at Wang Qiang, who instantly started imagining all sorts of soap opera plots.","He ventured a guess: “Are you guys from ‘The Prince Who Turns Into a Frog’ or ‘Destined to Love You’?”","He Huanhuan blinked: “Whatever you think fits. Long story short, we’re in a tight spot right now. Just lend us your delivery driver account!”","Wang Qiang agreed without a second thought. \"Alright, you can take my electric scooter too, but you have to bring it back before I get off work tonight.\"","He still needed to ride it home to charge.","He even lent them his spare phone for food delivery, and as he watched the two of them ride away, he started daydreaming happily.","When they finally turn their lives around, will they take him along too?","When that day comes, would he be able to climb up the social ladder and become a phoenix?","Wow!","Then maybe he should start losing some weight?"]},{"number":54,"title":"Chapter 54: Come and stay with us","paragraphs":["When lunch break came, a colleague came over to call Wang Qiang to go eat together.","Wang Qiang touched his soft, pudgy belly and firmly refused: \"I'm not eating. I'm starting my diet from today.\"","He couldn't afford to get any fatter. He had to work hard, he had to rise to the top and become a phoenix.","What if he got too heavy and broke the branch he was perching on?","His colleague was shocked: \"What's gotten into you? Why do you suddenly want to lose weight? Chubby guys are adorable!\"","Wang Qiang shook his head: \"You don't get it. The opportunity of a lifetime has come for me! I have to seize it!\"","His colleague became instantly curious: \"What's up? Are you falling in love? Does she not like chubby guys?\"","Wang Qiang sneered. Falling in love? How boring!","He vaguely boasted to his colleague that he had made some really awesome friends and would soon become awesome himself.","His colleague couldn't help frowning: \"You're not talking about those two who just borrowed two hundred bucks from you, are you?\"","He had just asked his colleague to exchange some money, and the colleague casually asked about it.","He didn't hide it and told his colleague he was helping out a friend in need.","Now, as soon as he mentioned it, his colleague immediately connected it to those two hundred bucks.","Wang Qiang hesitated and nodded: \"Yeah, why?\"","His colleague said with disappointment: \"Are you stupid? Someone who can't even scrape together two hundred bucks—what kind of future do they have? You've been scammed!\"","\"Really? That can't be...\"","Wang Qiang couldn't believe it. Last time, Han Mo and the others had flashed a black card when buying a BYD car!","His colleague sneered: \"A black card to buy a BYD? Use your brain—does that make any sense?\"","It didn't seem quite right...","\"You've definitely been scammed!\"","His colleague quickly asked him: \"You didn't lend them anything else, did you? Forget the two hundred—they didn't take your phone or anything, did they?\"","Wang Qiang's tears nearly fell: \"I lent them my phone, I lent them my e-bike, I even lent them my food delivery account...\"","His colleague was speechless: \"Did a donkey kick your head? You lend all that to people you don't even know? Since when are you this generous with me?\"","Wang Qiang said aggrievedly: \"But she said we're friends... She wouldn't trick me, would she?\"","Never mind He Huanhuan—Han Mo looked so trustworthy. He wouldn't deceive him, would he?","Would he?","An e-bike cost over four thousand—he couldn't afford to lose that!","His colleague was exasperated: \"These days, only scammers make friends with strangers. Get a clue!\"","After his colleague's warning, Wang Qiang grew extremely anxious.","The spare phone and the e-bike together were worth over four thousand!","That was almost two months of his salary. His base pay was only three thousand, and that was before taxes...","The whole afternoon, he couldn't do a thing.","He stood at the doorway, staring longingly into the distance, hoping to see his beloved e-bike being brought back.","But nothing. By the time it got dark and his shift was over, he still hadn't seen anyone.","His colleague got on his own e-bike and said helplessly: \"Want me to give you a ride? After payday, you can buy a used e-bike from someone.\"","Wang Qiang stubbornly shook his head: \"I'll wait a bit longer. You go ahead.\"","His colleague was speechless: \"Your place is a two-hour walk from here! Don't you have work tomorrow?\"","The area where they lived was remote, and there were no buses at this hour.","What was he even waiting for? Those two were definitely scammers!","What part-time job? As far as he was concerned, it was all nonsense.","Two people that good-looking needed to work part-time?","With their looks, they could make money any way they wanted.","They were scammers!","But no matter how much he tried to persuade him, Wang Qiang insisted on waiting there.","His colleague stayed with him for an hour and then had no choice but to leave.","His girlfriend was waiting for him at home!","Once his colleague was gone, Wang Qiang was left alone.","The pitiful little Fatty crouched on the ground, motionless, muttering to himself: \"You've got to come back. Please don't trick me...\"","He had never been this kind to anyone in his whole life. He hoped they wouldn't let him down.","But as time passed, his heart grew heavier and heavier.","Until...","\"Little Fatty! Are you still there?\"","He Huanhuan's loud voice suddenly rang out in the night. Wang Qiang jumped up excitedly: \"I'm here! I'm here! I've been waiting for you all along!\"","Then came He Huanhuan's annoyed voice: \"Why didn't you say your e-bike was out of juice?! I pushed it the whole damn way!\"","Uh...","Wang Qiang felt embarrassed: \"I bought it secondhand... The battery really isn't that great anymore...\"","\"Why didn't you say so!\"","She and Han Mo had never delivered food before. They spent the better part of an hour just figuring out how to take orders and make deliveries.","They completed one order first and earned five bucks.","Then they took another order that was farther away, earning twelve bucks.","After that, the e-bike ran out of battery. When they checked their phones, they found it was a three-hour walk away...","She tried to quick-charge the bike, but the charging station only took mobile payments.","Wang Qiang's spare phone had zero balance.","So the two of them had to push the bike all the way back, huffing and puffing. By the time it got dark, they were still halfway there.","He Huanhuan jumped up and smacked Wang Qiang on the head: \"Why didn't you charge the e-bike!\"","Wang Qiang scratched his head guiltily: \"I forgot...\"","He only rode it to and from work every day, so it never occurred to him to charge it daily.","He had planned to charge it after work today, but when He Huanhuan suddenly asked to borrow it, he got so excited that he forgot.","Now, with the e-bike completely dead, he had no way to get home.","He Huanhuan asked him: \"Where do you live? How far is it from here?\"","Wang Qiang: \"Not too far—just a two-hour walk.\"","He Huanhuan looked at the pitch-black night and waved her hand: \"It's too far for that. You're coming home with us for the night.\"","Han Mo frowned. Their place—did they have the conditions to host someone?","Oh, they did!","You just wipe down the concrete floor, and that's good enough to sleep on!","Wang Qiang had no idea that \"coming home\" meant sleeping on concrete. He asked He Huanhuan excitedly: \"Really? Can I?\"","They had just met—was it okay to crash at their place already?","They hadn't even talked much, hadn't discussed their families or their heartbreaks.","Wasn't this moving a little too fast?","He Huanhuan rolled her eyes at him: \"What, are you dating or something? Hurry up and park the bike. We're going home!\"","\"Okay!\"","Wang Qiang scurried off to park his e-bike.","Han Mo leaned in close and asked her: \"Is our place really suitable for him?\"","He Huanhuan blinked her big, innocent eyes: \"Why wouldn't it be?\"","It was just one night—what was the big deal?","She could tell just by looking at Wang Qiang that the little Fatty was like her—a kid from a poor family.","Clothes that didn't fit, a phone that cost a few hundred bucks.","So young but already changing jobs countless times.","People who didn't know him might think he was unreliable, never sticking with one job for long.","But the truth was, he was so young his brain hadn't fully developed yet before he had to start working to support his family.","This was what happened to kids without families to fall back on. Most of the time, they were completely muddleheaded.","Because they had no time to think, no time to learn.","They just had to earn money—money earned through hard, grueling work."]},{"number":55,"title":"Chapter 55: Going to Buy You Clothes","paragraphs":["Standing by the broken window, Wang Qiang really wanted to say, why not let him go home; his rented place was much better than this.","It was only a two-hour walk, wasn't it? He could manage it!","Just treat it as exercise.","\"Are you going in? What are you spacing out for? Aren't you tired?\"","He Huanhuan pushed the window open with one hand and vaulted in nimbly.","Then she handed a plastic basin to Han Mo: \"Get some water, I'm going to wipe the floor for Xiaoqiang.\"","Wang Qiang stared at the floor He Huanhuan was referring to in disbelief: \"When you say Xiaoqiang, you don't mean me, do you?\"","And the floor she mentioned—surely not that cement floor?","He Huanhuan nodded, her eyes sparkling: \"That's right! Tonight, you'll sleep in the same room as us! How about it?\"","No way.","Wang Qiang wanted to go home. Even though his rental was small, he had a one-and-a-half-meter bed all to himself.","He didn't want to sleep on cement.","No way.","Han Mo also wanted Wang Qiang to go home. He didn't like others intruding on his life.","He and He Huanhuan were fine on their own, and he didn't want to be disturbed.","But Wang Qiang had lent them money, as well as his electric scooter and food delivery account.","He couldn't bring himself to tell him to go home.","He should have said it—if he'd just said the word, Wang Qiang would have gone home without a second thought.","Two hours for a comfortable night's sleep—it was worth it!","But he didn't speak, and Wang Qiang didn't speak either.","And so things went according to He Huanhuan's plan.","She cheerfully wiped the floor clean, then showed it off to Wang Qiang: \"Ta-da! Clean, right?\"","Wang Qiang forced a grim smile and nodded: \"Looks clean... heh heh...\"","He Huanhuan enthusiastically invited him: \"Then go wash up under the faucet. Once you're clean, get some sleep! We've got money to make tomorrow!\"","Though the old house was dilapidated, the water and electricity were still connected.","They found a power strip and ran an extension cord outside to charge the scooter.","Early the next morning, they could start delivering food.","That afternoon, she'd asked a seasoned delivery driver, and he said if you worked hard, making two hundred yuan a day was no sweat!","Her goal was to earn two hundred yuan with Han Mo tomorrow!","That would be enough to repay Wang Qiang.","Wang Qiang looked at the faucet and swallowed: \"Taking a bath here?\"","Han Mo nodded seriously: \"It's not cold out. Just wipe down with some water.\"","With that, he took off his shirt, soaked it, and began wiping himself down.","Wang Qiang was stunned by how effortlessly he did it: \"How many days have you been staying here?\"","How could anyone live like this?","He had a vivid impression of Han Mo. Back at the 4S shop, Han Mo had exuded a unique aura from the moment he appeared.","Maybe it was because his clothes fit so perfectly, or because the black card he pulled out was so flashy.","Either way, the moment he stood there, he seemed on a whole different level from everyone around him.","He radiated the air of a rich man.","But now, that man with the CEO vibe was washing himself with tap water using his own shirt.","It was absurd.","\"We just got here yesterday.\"","Yesterday?","Wang Qiang immediately pulled out his phone. He remembered scrolling past a video earlier that day?","He hadn't paid attention then and had swiped right past it.","He searched the keywords: Jiangcheng, rich second generation, disappearance.","Sure enough, he found the video. A horrific car crash had occurred last night in the outskirts of Jiangcheng. A BYD car had been hit by an unknown vehicle, sent flying, and burned to a frame...","Because the accident site was remote and surveillance was incomplete, the Han Group's general manager and the Gu heiress had vanished from the scene...","Wang Qiang's eyes widened as he read the caption, and he swallowed again.","At the end of the video, it clearly stated: \"Anyone with information about these two is urged to come forward. Upon verification, the Gu family will immediately offer a reward of 200,000 yuan.\"","His voice trembled: \"That's not you two, is it?\"","He knew Han Mo was someone special, but he never imagined He Huanhuan was the Gu heiress!","Good heavens!","His own company was a real estate subsidiary of the Gu Group!","Han Mo glanced at the phone screen and frowned: \"Are you going to claim that 200,000?\"","Wang Qiang shook his head frantically: \"I won't say a thing! You two must have a reason for staying hidden. We're friends, I won't betray you!\"","To prove his loyalty, he immediately stripped off his shirt and followed suit, wiping himself with water: \"See? I really won't tell anyone.\"","Han Mo frowned. What did one thing have to do with the other?","It did. The kid was showing his allegiance!","He could wash with tap water and sleep on cement.","He wasn't tempted by that 200,000...","Really!","He wouldn't blab.","Han Mo nodded: \"Once this is all over, I'll give you that money myself.\"","He wouldn't let him go unrewarded.","Wang Qiang struggled to suppress a grin: \"Well... I really don't need the money. You don't have to give it...\"","\"Then I won't!\" He Huanhuan leaned by the window. \"We're friends—money is so tacky! Since you said no, then no!\"","\"Ah?\"","Overdid it!","Wang Qiang frowned: \"You really won't? Actually, I could use some money...\"","\"Hahahaha...\" He Huanhuan burst out laughing. \"Don't worry, he'll give it to you!\"","\"Han Mo is the most generous person!\"","Han Mo's lips curled slightly involuntarily: \"She says I'll give it, so I'll give it.\"","Wang Qiang furrowed his brow. Something about the vibe felt off.","It was getting late, so the three of them washed up quickly and got ready to sleep.","Wang Qiang never expected that the biggest hardship wouldn't be sleeping on cement, but climbing back in through the window!","He'd just watched He Huanhuan vault over with one hand, so light and easy.","How come when it was his turn, it was so hard?","He planted both hands on the windowsill, his legs flailing in the air, but he couldn't get himself up no matter how he tried.","He Huanhuan coached from the side: \"Don't use both hands, just one. Then lift your body and spring up... That's it... Push! Spring!\"","Wang Qiang pushed up with one hand and hopped in place...","He Huanhuan: \"Why didn't you spring?\"","Wang Qiang looked innocent: \"I did spring, just not very obviously...\"","Han Mo stepped in to teach him: \"You're heavy. First, get your butt onto the windowsill, then wiggle over.\"","Wang Qiang was puzzled: \"But how do I get my butt up there?\"","Han Mo: ......","In the end, Han Mo had to grab him under the armpits and lift him up, and only then did Wang Qiang manage to get over.","Han Mo looked at his hands and sighed helplessly.","He hadn't even carried He Huanhuan like that.","Lying on the bed, He Huanhuan was so sleepy she could barely keep her eyes open.","She squinted, leaning against Han Mo: \"Sleep now. When we wake up tomorrow, we'll make money. I'll buy you a new shirt—yours is so wrinkled it's unwatchable...\"","Even half-asleep, she was still thinking about buying him new clothes.","Han Mo's eyes instantly softened. He reached out, stroked her eyes, then her face, soothing her like a child.","\"Okay, we'll buy it tomorrow.\"","From the floor, Wang Qiang quietly raised his hand: \"I actually have a few spare shirts. You can wear mine...\"","\"Shut up.\"","\"Okay...\""]},{"number":56,"title":"Chapter 56: Was I Wrong","paragraphs":["The three of them slept like logs in that rundown house, completely unaware that the Han and Gu families had already turned the world upside down.","Han Changyong pointed at Han Xuan in fury and demanded, \"Tell me the truth—did you do this or not?\"","Han Xuan curled his lip. \"Why would I hit him? I'm not stupid.\"","\"I think you're damned stupid!\"","Han Changyong was shaking with rage. \"The police have already reviewed all the surveillance footage. It won't take them more than a couple of days to trace where that van ended up.\"","But Han Xuan wasn't scared at all. He stretched lazily and sank into the sofa. \"Dad, you'd better worry about the company. It's leaderless right now.\"","The company's bank accounts had just been unfrozen, and morale was already shaky.","He ought to think about how to keep the employees in line first.","Han Changyong’s vision went dark. \"You did this just to take over the company? He’s your brother, after all.\"","Han Xuan let out a scornful laugh. \"Who was it that told me when I was a kid that I was the only son? I don't have a brother.\"","\"You!\"","Han Changyong choked on his words. \"Aren't you afraid they'll trace it back to you? You'll go to prison!\"","Han Xuan sat on the sofa, laughing without restraint. \"Don't worry, Dad. They won't find anything.\"","He wasn't the least bit afraid of Han Changyong knowing the truth. He just hated Han Mo's guts.","He'd hated him for a long time. His only regret was that he hadn't hit him sooner.","A flood of emotions surged in Han Changyong's heart. Though he didn't like Han Mo, the boy was still his son.","When he was born, he'd felt genuine joy.","But...","Never mind. He sighed helplessly. \"Do you know there was no body at the scene? He's not dead yet. Aren't you afraid—\"","Han Xuan stared coldly at Han Changyong. \"Dad, he's dead.\"","It was his own fault for not being thorough enough to confirm Han Mo's death.","But that didn't mean Han Mo would ever get a chance to turn things around.","In a few days, once the accident was officially closed, he'd go file for Han Mo's death certificate.","By then, whether he was alive or dead, Han Mo would be dead.","The company would be his, and his alone.","He fixed his gaze on Han Changyong. \"Dad, let me take over the company. I'll do a good job.\"","Han Changyong ignored him. \"What can you possibly do? Last time I handed the company over to you, you nearly ruined it.\"","He picked up his phone to make a call, but Han Xuan lunged at him from behind and shoved him down the stairs!","\"Han Xuan!\"","The cry of shock faded into the air. Han Changyong hit the ground with a heavy thud.","After a long pause, Han Xuan strolled downstairs, crouched beside Han Changyong, and said softly, \"Don't worry, Dad. You won't die. I'll make sure the hospital takes good care of you.\"","Han Changyong was ill, so the story went—overcome with grief from his eldest son's car accident, he had fallen into a coma and wouldn't wake up.","Luckily, the Han family had money. Han Xuan arranged a quiet sanatorium for his father and assigned a dedicated caregiver to look after him.","Surely, he'd get better soon.","Meanwhile, the Gu family was in an uproar. Gu Jinghan was throwing a fit at home: \"Dad! Can't you take this seriously? Huanhuan has gone missing!\"","Gu Chengye rubbed his aching head. \"I've already contacted everyone I can, and I've put up a reward. What more do you want me to do?\"","Gu Jinghan was furious. \"You only offered two hundred thousand—nobody's going to take that seriously! Raise it. Raise it to a million! No—two million!\"","Gu Chengye glared at him in exasperation. \"Nothing's been decided yet. We don't even know what happened to Huanhuan. What's the rush?\"","\"How can I not be in a rush?\"","Gu Jinghan was fuming, stomping his feet: \"Is she even your daughter or not?! She's been missing for two days! If someone had killed her, she'd be stinking by now!\"","At the thought, his eyes turned red: \"She's already suffered so much before, and since coming back, she hasn't had a single good day. That fake Gu Chacha has been going after her like crazy...\"","\"Jinghan!\"","Gu Chengye called him sharply, his voice full of warning.","He wouldn't allow him to speak of Gu Chacha like that, wouldn't allow him to dig up the family's unsightly truths.","He, Gu Chengye, had struggled half a lifetime without cheating or visiting prostitutes.","He had three children, all well-behaved and obedient.","His life was perfect.","His family was equally perfect.","His face darkened, and he shot Gu Jinghan a warning glare: \"Don't drag Chacha into this nonsense. Remember, she's your sister too.\"","Gu Jinghan completely lost it: \"Sister my ass! She's not! He Huanhuan is my sister!\"","\"No—He Huanhuan isn't my sister. You don't even treat her like a daughter. You know she gets carsick, but she's been back this long, and you still haven't bought a BYD. You haven't given her any spending money either. You just don't care about her at all!\"","He demanded angrily, \"If you weren't planning to raise her properly, why did you bring her back in the first place?! Are you crazy?!\"","\"Slap!\"","A heavy palm struck his face. Gu Chengye's face was black enough to drip ink: \"Stop this nonsense!\"","Gu Jinghan turned and walked away—screw his dad!","He'd find her himself!","Once he found her, he wasn't bringing her back. He'd let Huanhuan stay at his hotel!","His dad didn't want this daughter anyway—fine, his dad wouldn't have her, but he would!","He'd be Huanhuan's dad!","He'd definitely raise her well!","Great plan in theory, but bro, did you ask He Huanhuan?","It didn't matter. He stormed off to the garage, ran to the very back, and got into his newly bought BYD.","He'd bought the car a while ago but never found a chance to take He Huanhuan out.","Either he was busy, or Han Mo had already picked her up.","He sat in the car, feeling pitiful: \"I only just got a sister...\"","Ever since he was little, he'd never gotten along with Gu Chacha—the moment he saw her, he disliked her.","He'd always thought he just wasn't a good brother, which was why he didn't like this sister.","He never guessed that Gu Chacha wasn't even his real sister!","The first time he saw He Huanhuan, he liked her instantly.","She looked so much like him—one look and you could tell they were real siblings.","She had such a good personality too, not getting angry even when she was targeted.","When their parents made her stay in the guest room, she was happy about how nice it was.","So silly.","His sister was so silly.","He wiped his eyes fiercely: \"Fine, I'll find her myself!\"","The car sped out of the house like lightning, racing through the entire city, searching inch by inch...","Gu Chengye watched Gu Jinghan leave and couldn't help asking, \"Yulan, was I wrong?\"","Had he really not cared enough about Huanhuan?","He'd put out a reward, asked several acquaintances in positions of authority to put pressure on their people, and made sure they'd find her.","Wasn't that enough?","Jiang Yulan said nothing. She didn't know if Old Gu was wrong, and she didn't know if she herself was wrong.","All she knew was that when Huanhuan first came back, she had wanted to make it up to her.","But He Huanhuan was like a wild weed—she adapted to life in the house so quickly, without any awkwardness.","And so, those feelings of guilt and the urge to make amends quietly faded away.","Were they wrong?","Probably not.","She shook her head firmly. \"Old Gu, you're not in the wrong. Jinghan just has too fiery a temper. I'll talk to him about it later.\"","\"Mm.\""]},{"number":57,"title":"Chapter 57: Baby, We Are One","paragraphs":["Gu Jinghan searched street by street, but he couldn't find her—not a single trace of He Huanhuan anywhere.","He drove back to the scene of the car accident and crouched down, examining it carefully.","But he wasn't a professional detective, and he couldn't make heads or tails of anything.","\"Second Young Master Gu, what are you doing here?\"","A young voice suddenly sounded from behind him. Gu Jinghan turned around.","The man looked somewhat familiar—wasn't he Han Mo's special assistant?","He couldn't help but frown. \"What are you doing here?\"","If it hadn't been for Han Mo, Huanhuan would never have been in trouble.","Who knows if she's already gone bad by now?","Waaah...","Not gone bad. She was nestled in Han Mo's neck, fast asleep and snoring softly.","Chen Yu's eyes reddened as he asked again, \"Why are you here, sir?\"","Gu Jinghan said impatiently, \"Why do you think I'm here? If it weren't for Han Mo, would I be here? What else could it be? My sister is missing!\"","He angrily picked up a clump of mud and hurled it at Chen Yu. \"Get out of my sight! Just seeing you pisses me off!\"","But Chen Yu stood there and let him throw it. \"My brother—he didn't do it on purpose... he didn't know Han Xuan would suddenly...\"","Gu Jinghan froze mid-motion. \"Han Xuan? How do you know it was Han Xuan who hit him?\"","Chen Yu shut his mouth and said nothing. Gu Jinghan grew even angrier, charging forward and landing a punch on him. \"Talk!\"","Chen Yu had already taken quite a few beatings from his father over the past couple of days, and his body still ached.","Gu Jinghan's punch was fierce, so Chen Yu immediately caved. \"My brother was planning to...\"","He spilled their plan, omitting the key details, and sobbed with tearful eyes, \"My brother's gone missing too...\"","\"Is Han Mo insane or what?\"","Gu Jinghan didn't understand. Why would he pull a stunt like that for no reason?","Chen Yu didn't tell him about Han Xuan's involvement in fraud.","And since he'd always had a strained relationship with Gu Chacha, Gu Jinghan's father naturally hadn't told him about any of that either.","So he knew absolutely nothing about the little scheme between Gu Chacha and Han Xuan.","From his perspective, he just thought Han Mo was nuts.","Why would you deliberately lure Han Xuan into scheming against you?","Just to get him locked up?","What a waste of time!","And he'd dragged Huanhuan into suffering along with him!","But at least he had some idea now—he could be fairly certain that He Huanhuan was still alive.","She wouldn't have gone bad.","\"Han Xuan?\"","He released Chen Yu and stood up straight. \"You're absolutely sure it was him?\"","Chen Yu nodded firmly. \"Definitely him. There's no one else.\"","\"Good.\"","Gu Jinghan got into his car with a dark face and drove off, heading back to the Gu residence to grab the listening device he'd bought.","To hell with morality!","It was his hotel—so what if he bugged it?","Sue him if they dared!","At the hotel, he headed straight for the presidential suite.","The manager chased after him, asking cautiously, \"Boss, what are you planning to do?\"","He glanced at the manager. \"Are you going to interfere in my business now? Am I the boss, or are you?\"","The manager quickly stepped back. \"I was just asking, just asking...\"","\"Wait outside! Don't come in!\"","He laid down the order and entered the presidential suite alone.","Thinking about Han Xuan's brevity in bed, he decided to install the bug under the bed.","Given how little time he lasted, there was no way he'd have much time for pillow talk beforehand.","He crouched down, then shouted toward the door, \"Hey! Get in here!\"","The manager rushed in. \"Boss, what's wrong?\"","Gu Jinghan: \"How do I install this thing?\"","He didn't know how...","The manager's face went pale. \"Boss, this is illegal!\"","Gu Jinghan jumped up and clamped his hand over the manager's mouth. \"I know! Keep your voice down! I'll only listen once, and then I'll take it out!\"","The manager frowned. Their hotel wasn't in the best location, so the presidential suite rarely got booked.","Recently, only the Second Young Master Han and the boss's sister had stayed there.","He looked at Gu Jinghan. \"Boss, you're a real pervert.\"","Gu Jinghan's face darkened. \"Shut up and install it. I'll transfer you two thousand after.\"","The manager quickly crouched down. \"Alright, boss. My lips are sealed!\"","The moment the bug was installed, the manager's earpiece picked up the front desk's voice: \"Manager, manager, a guest wants to book the presidential suite. Is it ready?\"","\"It's ready, it's ready. Send them up!\"","The manager grabbed Gu Jinghan and scrambled out to hide. He said, as if seeking praise, \"Boss, the guests are here!\"","Transfer me the money, quick, and make it plenty.","Gu Jinghan transferred him five thousand without a second thought. The manager's eyes squinted happily.","So what if the boss was a pervert? He could handle it!","As long as the boss didn't get perverted with him.","The two of them hid in the fire escape stairwell and watched Han Xuan bring Gu Chacha into the room with their own eyes.","Gu Jinghan immediately went back to the garage, got into his car, and turned on the listening device.","Thud.","The car door opened and closed, and the manager climbed in.","Gu Jinghan gave him a confused look. \"What are you doing in here?\"","The manager said matter-of-factly, \"Boss, I'm afraid you might do something shady and drag me down with you. I have to keep an eye on you.\"","......","\"Get out, get out, get out...\"","But before he could shoo him away, noise started coming from the suite.","Moaning and groaning instantly filled the car, echoing in both their ears.","The manager picked his nose. \"Boss, you really are a pervert.\"","Gu Jinghan: ...Fired! He was going to fire this guy!","The noise from the suite came to a quick end, and the manager summarized quietly, \"He looks young, but his stamina's not great.\"","Gu Jinghan's face darkened. \"Shut up!\"","The manager secretly covered his mouth—he'd been talking about the Second Young Master Han, but the boss had gotten all embarrassed and angry...","My God, he'd just discovered another one of the boss's little secrets!","Inside the suite, Han Xuan lay on the bed with his arm around Gu Chacha. \"Chacha, the company's back in my hands. Your performances can resume now.\"","Gu Chacha said uneasily, \"Nothing like last time will happen again, right?\"","Han Xuan kissed her forehead. \"Don't worry, I'll keep a close eye on things. I won't let them screw up.\"","He took her hand. \"Next, it's your time to shine. Once we've made enough money, how about we emigrate to New Zealand? We can buy a ranch there and start a farm...\"","As for the Han Corporation, he'd already planned it out.","Once he made enough money, he'd sell the company for cheap.","Then he'd head abroad in style and live his best, carefree life.","Gu Chacha frowned. \"What about my piano?\"","She'd done all this not just for money.","She wanted both fame and fortune.","She was still young—there was no way she was going to emigrate and retire so early!","Han Xuan kissed her hand again. \"Chacha, you have to come with me. You have to understand—Han Mo isn't dead. If he comes back, do you think he won't investigate who ran him over?\"","Gu Chacha pulled her hand back. \"What do you mean? You're the one who hit him. That has nothing to do with me!\"","A smile curled at the corner of Han Xuan's mouth. \"But how would I have known where he was? Chacha, don't forget—you went back to the Gu residence that day.\"","Gu Chacha sat up abruptly. \"Are you threatening me?\"","Han Xuan's smile widened. \"How is that a threat? I'm just reminding you, darling. We're in this together.\""]},{"number":58,"title":"Chapter 58: Where Did This Countryside Big Shot Come From","paragraphs":["\"Boss!!\"","The manager excitedly slapped Gu Jinghan on the shoulder. \"Boss! This is gold! Pure gold!\"","Gu Jinghan rubbed his shoulder. \"I know. Why do you think I was eavesdropping in the first place?\"","Did he really think he was some kind of creep?","The manager urged him on. \"Boss, quick! Copy that recording and let's go blackmail Second Young Master Han!\"","Gu Jinghan cursed at him. \"You're obsessed with money. I didn't do all this just to—\"","He stopped mid-sentence, his face going pale.","The manager asked nervously, \"Boss, what's wrong? Did we get caught? Hey, this has nothing to do with me...\"","Gu Jinghan almost burst into tears. \"Where's the copy button?\"","He couldn't find it!","The manager peeked over and nearly rolled his eyes out of his head. \"Boss! Could you just spend a little money for once? The one you bought can only listen—it can't copy!\"","Gu Jinghan felt wronged. How was he supposed to know?","It wasn't like he had a hobby of eavesdropping!","\"So what do I do now? Buy another one?\"","The manager shot him a look. \"With Han Mo's stamina, who knows when he'll next book a room!\"","Gu Jinghan's face fell even further. \"Then what do I do? I still haven't found my sister!\"","The manager pushed the door open and got out in disgust. \"Keep looking, I guess. You've got nothing else to do all day anyway.\"","Sigh. Why did he have to end up with such a stupid boss?","Well, whatever. If the boss weren't stupid, he wouldn't have become a manager. With his skills, he'd be working as a waiter at any other hotel.","Gu Jinghan sat in the car feeling utterly pitiful. His morals! Gone for nothing!","He pulled out his phone and called his older brother. The moment it connected, he let out a wail. \"Bro! I'm so wronged! My morals are gone! And I didn't even save the evidence! I don't want to live anymore!\"","Gu Jingchen sat in his office, frowning at the phone. \"What are you even talking about?\"","Gu Jinghan cried even harder, his words jumbling together. \"Like... setting up Han Mo to get back at Han Xuan... and it dragged Huanhuan into it... it was Xuan who told Han Xuan... it's all—\"","\"Get your emotions in check, then call me back.\"","The line went dead with a click. Gu Jinghan broke down. \"This family is so cold! Why am I even part of this family? I'm running away from home!\"","He and Huanhuan were both unloved children, sob sob...","In the office, Gu Jingchen stared at his computer screen, frowning deeply.","In the surveillance footage, a man in a baseball cap stepped out of a van.","He zoomed in on the frame, bit by bit, until the cap filled the entire screen.","If he wasn't mistaken, that cap was one bought at a roadside shop in the Maldives last year, when they'd gone on vacation as a family, the one Chacha had picked out.","He remembered clearly, because Jinghan and Chacha had fought over that cap.","Chacha had fallen in love with it at first sight, and Jinghan had said it was an ugly cap on an ugly head, double ugly.","It made Chacha cry, and their parents had scolded him harshly.","Jinghan had gotten angry, dragged Chacha aside, fought with her on the street, and then flown back to China by himself.","That day, Jinghan had been extraordinarily hot-tempered for some reason.","That's why he remembered the cap so vividly.","A light blue cap, with white wing embroidery on the front...","He squinted at the cap in the surveillance feed.","The arsonist was Han Xuan.","In the footage, Han Xuan drove off after setting the fire.","Which meant Han Mo's and Huanhuan's disappearance had nothing to do with him.","Of course, he didn't have the brains for it anyway.","Han Mo's BYD had rolled out of the surveillance range, so there was no way to know if he'd crawled out of the car himself or if someone had helped him.","Had Huanhuan gotten him out?","But then why hadn't they come back?","Why were they hiding?","Gu Jingchen sat frowning at his desk for a long moment, then made a call. \"Can you do me a favor? Can you look into the Han Corporation's financial transactions...\"","\"I know it's not exactly standard procedure, that's why I'm asking you... please...\"","\"Alright, I'll wait for your news.\"","To find Huanhuan, he first needed to understand Han Mo's motives.","The two brothers were each doing their part. What they didn't know was that He Huanhuan was just as hard at work...","Haggling, that is.","He Huanhuan held up the school uniform. \"Can you give me a discount? This is obviously last season's style. Nobody wears this anymore!\"","The shop owner sat on his little stool and waved his hand. \"Best I can do is fifty. If you don't want it, fine!\"","He Huanhuan: \"Final offer, thirty!\"","The owner glared at her. \"At thirty, I'm not making any money!\"","He Huanhuan glared back harder. \"At thirty, you're definitely still making money!\"","The owner ignored her. \"It's fifty, not a cent less!\"","He Huanhuan tossed the uniform back on the stall. \"Then I don't want it.\"","She plopped back onto her electric scooter, twisted the throttle, and started riding away... slowly. Very, very slowly.","Slower than an eighty-year-old grandma with a cane.","Han Mo was puzzled. \"Aren't we leaving?\"","He Huanhuan gritted her teeth. \"Shut up!\"","She was playing the bargaining game with the owner!","Sure enough, after the scooter glided another two meters, the owner called out grudgingly, \"Fine! Thirty! It's yours!\"","\"Deal!\"","He Huanhuan abandoned the scooter and ran back happily, handed over thirty yuan, and bought the old-style school uniform.","She shoved it into Han Mo's hands. \"Here, you've got new clothes now.\"","Han Mo looked at the uniform, his face nearly cracking. \"For me?\"","He Huanhuan grinned and nodded. \"Of course!\"","Han Mo frowned slightly. \"Maybe you should wear it instead. You don't have anything to change into either.\"","He really didn't want to wear it.","To his surprise, He Huanhuan waved her hand dismissively. \"I'm not wearing a school uniform! I'm going to buy a dress!\"","Han Mo glanced at the uniform, then nodded seriously. \"Alright, let's go buy a dress then.\"","Wearing the school uniform was fine. He'd buy her two pretty dresses.","Han Mo stood at the doorway of the shop, completely speechless.","He never expected that the dress He Huanhuan wanted to buy was... this kind of dress.","He looked at the store full of big rose-print dresses, big begonia-print dresses...","His eyes were exhausted.","He reached out and grabbed He Huanhuan, who was itching to dart inside. \"Do we really have to buy this?\"","He still had a bit over a hundred yuan left from the two hundred he'd borrowed from Wang Qiang yesterday, and they'd made over fifty this morning too.","They weren't that broke.","He Huanhuan reached out and touched the fabric, the smooth, cool material familiar against her fingers, stirring a hollow ache deep in her chest.","\"This one's great. My grandma used to love wearing this.\"","The grief flickered across her face, there and gone in an instant, as if it had never existed at all.","But Han Mo caught it.","He said nothing, just stepped forward, took her hand, and looked at her. \"If you like it, buy two. You can rotate them.\"","The shop owner sat inside rolling his eyes so hard they nearly fell out of his head. Where did this countryside CEO come from? Even the cheapest dresses were fifteen yuan each, and he's pretending to spoil her with two. With the two-for-discount, it's only twenty-five for both. What kind of flex is that?!","Some people, honestly!"]},{"number":59,"title":"Chapter 59: The cake is really sweet and delicious.","paragraphs":["The two of them walked into the shop, and Han Mo glanced down at the owner. “Two dresses. Wrap them up.”","The owner finally couldn’t hold back a snort of laughter. “Wrap~them~up~ Where’s this punk from? Coming to my shop to scam a young girl! Get lost! I’m not doing business with you!”","A twenty-odd yuan sale wasn’t worth the trouble anyway.","Nothing disgusted her more than a man fooling a young girl.","She gave Han Mo’s wrinkled shirt and dress pants a once-over, then looked at He Huanhuan’s cartoon T-shirt and her flashy, colorful hair.","She sized up the situation in an instant: a rebellious girl falling for a con man!","She yanked He Huanhuan over to her side and lectured her earnestly, “Little miss, a man’s mouth is a ghost’s lie. This guy here doesn’t look reliable at all—don’t you dare believe him, you hear?”","He Huanhuan tried hard to suppress a smile. “He does lie to me a lot. He said he’d take me out every day, but after two days he stopped.”","The owner glared at Han Mo, indignation burning in her eyes. “Men are all the same! All talk, no action whatsoever!”","Han Mo had nothing to say for himself. He really had broken his promise for a few days.","But those few days...","“I’m sorry.”","He apologized sincerely. His original intentions had indeed not been pure—there was no denying that.","He Huanhuan tilted her head up, the corners of her mouth curling involuntarily. “Which one are you apologizing for?”","Before Han Mo could answer, the owner exploded. “There’s more than one?! Good grief! That’s exactly what I said—men are useless! Little sister, don’t you dare stay with him! A good-looking man is good for nothing...”","He Huanhuan nodded with a pleased grin. “He is pretty good-looking.”","Han Mo’s frustration vanished in an instant, a smile rising unbidden in his eyes.","The owner saw it and felt the world go dark. A lovesick fool—hopeless.","She rolled her eyes at Han Mo. “Do you still want the dresses or not?”","Since she couldn’t talk sense into the girl, she might as well just do business.","Twenty-five yuan was twenty-five yuan.","Han Mo nodded. “Yes, please. Thank you.”","The owner pursed her lips. Handsome and polite—no wonder the girl was head over heels.","Back in her younger days, she wouldn’t have been able to resist either.","Sigh. Fate!","It was destined that she would end up selling middle-aged women’s clothing!","He Huanhuan carefully picked out two terribly frumpy floral dresses—one rust-red, one bronze.","When she was little, she never understood why her grandmother wore those dresses every summer.","When she got older, she realized: because they were cheap and wouldn’t wash out.","Twenty or thirty yuan could cover an entire summer.","Her grandmother’s summer was dresses for twenty or thirty yuan, bruised apples, a fan she was too stingy to run.","And a son who never stopped owing money.","She looked at the dresses in her hands and suddenly felt less drawn to the world she had left.","The grandmother who loved her most was already gone. Back home, there was only a drunkard father who gambled like his life depended on it.","And a pile of gambling debts dumped on her head.","Aside from Qi Meili, that world had treated her terribly.","She blinked, then asked the owner, “Can I change clothes here?”","The girl, who had been all smiles a moment ago, suddenly drooped, her face crumpling as if she was about to cry.","The owner nodded without a second thought. “Change, go ahead and change. No one else is in the shop anyway.”","The roadside shop had no fitting room, so the owner held up a piece of cloth to screen off a corner. He Huanhuan stripped off her T-shirt and pants and slipped into the rust-red rose-print dress.","The dress had no shape to it, hanging loose and baggy on her body.","She asked Han Mo, “Do I look good?”","Han Mo nodded seriously. “You look good. Beautiful, like a flower.”","“I think so too.”","He Huanhuan smiled lightly. “Han Mo, buy me a cake. I want to eat cake.”","“Okay.”","Han Mo changed into the school uniform as well, and the two of them asked the owner for a bag, stuffed their dirty clothes inside, and headed out to buy a cake.","The owner watched their departing figures and couldn’t help but sigh. “If you’re going to have kids, raise them right! Such a pretty girl—she’s got to be out of her mind!”","People online always said that spoiling a daughter too much, never letting her face hardships, would make her run off with some punk.","But the truth was, the girls who got taken in by bad boys were the ones who never got love at home.","Love is the foundation of a person’s growth.","Only a child who never received love at home would be moved by the slightest bit of kindness and charge headfirst into a wall.","And a child who grew up with plenty of love at home wouldn’t even bother to look twice at that kind of gesture.","The electric scooter sped down the road, a gentle breeze brushing He Huanhuan’s skirt.","And stirring her heartstrings.","Grandma, I’m free!","She thought she had been so stupid, even wanting to go back—back to work, back to paying off debts.","Those debts could never be paid off!","“Hahaha...”","She laughed out loud. “Han Mo, I’m so happy!”","She didn’t explain why she was happy. She just laughed freely. “Hahaha... I was so dumb! I’ve been free this whole time!”","The moment she had been pulled into the world of the book, she was free!","She no longer had to be trapped by that man, no longer had to be cornered by debt collectors, stuck at home with no food and no way out.","She no longer had to count down the days until she turned eighteen so she could go work in a factory and pay off his debts.","She no longer had to cling stubbornly to her grandparents’ old house, refusing to let go.","She was truly, genuinely free!","“Hahaha...”","The tears at the corners of her eyes were blown away by the wind, landing on the back of Han Mo’s hand.","He instinctively clenched his fist.","Why was she crying?","Was it because of her grandmother?","What did she mean by freedom?","Sitting on the back of the scooter, he reached out and patted her shoulder. “You will always be free.”","“Mm!”","They rode to the cake shop, where He Huanhuan rushed in, bought a small cake, and asked the clerk for two candles.","Out on the street, she couldn’t wait to open the cake and stick the two candles in.","Han Mo held the cake in his hands and stared at the number 18 on the candles, unable to stop himself from reminding her, “Huanhuan, you’re twenty this year.”","He Huanhuan ignored him. She lit the candles without looking away, then blew them out with focus.","“Han Mo, I’m an adult now!”","Han Mo stressed, “You became an adult two years ago.”","Uncle Gu wasn’t a monster—he would never arrange a betrothal for a minor.","He Huanhuan beamed. “Not my body. My spirit. My soul. I’ve become an adult for real, completely and utterly.”","The words seemed to come out of nowhere, but she didn’t explain further. She leaned in and took a big, greedy bite of the cake.","Cream smeared across her face, and she squinted in pure bliss. “Han Mo, do you know? This is the first birthday cake I’ve ever had that was truly mine in my whole life.”","Even the rebellious girls—Qi Meili and the others—had lived better lives than she had.","Their parents were unreliable too, sure, but at least they just ignored them.","Qi Meili could still squeeze some pocket money out of her folks now and then.","Only she had nothing.","Oh, wait—she had a mountain of debt waiting for her to repay.","She had never eaten a birthday cake. Not once, ever.","Grandpa and Grandma loved her, but they were too old, too old to know that kids nowadays ate cake for their birthdays.","They would only cook her a bowl of long-life noodles and add two poached eggs on top.","When Qi Meili and the others had their birthdays, she never touched their cakes.","Every time, she would shake her leg and act all high and mighty, claiming she didn't like cake.","The birthday cake was the inferiority and pain she hid deep inside.","She licked the cream at the corner of her mouth and smiled with relief: \"It's really sweet, really delicious.\""]},{"number":60,"title":"Chapter 60: Passing by Chen Yu","paragraphs":["She hadn't said a word, but Han Mo felt his heart ache.","She must have had such a hard life before, right?","He couldn't help but pull her into his arms: \"It's over. Everything will pass.\"","His pain, He Huanhuan's pain—it would all pass.","He Huanhuan nodded seriously: \"I know.\"","The two of them squatted by the roadside sharing a piece of cake, taking turns taking bites, utterly carefree.","Near the end, she shoved him away in disgust: \"It's not even that big to begin with, and you've eaten this much!\"","But Han Mo stubbornly held out his spoon: \"This is your coming-of-age cake. We have to share it together.\"","\"No way!\"","The two of them wrestled over it right there on the street, oblivious to everyone around them. He Huanhuan still had her helmet on and, without a second thought, bonked him right on the head with it!","Neither of them noticed that, just ahead of them, Chen Yu's car slowly drove past.","It had been less than three days since the accident, but Chen Yu looked completely worn out.","His dark circles were so deep he could cosplay as a panda, and stubble had grown in thick and fine—he simply didn't have the heart to shave.","He drove slowly through the streets, searching aimlessly.","He knew it was like looking for a needle in a haystack, but he had no other choice.","He couldn't just sit at home waiting for news from the police, could he?","That would be pure torture.","And he couldn't go home either—if he did, he'd get beaten.","His father's belt was practically wearing out against his back...","So better to come out and search. At least it gave him something to do, and it kept his mind a little lighter.","As his car passed the cake shop, he even glanced at He Huanhuan and Han Mo fighting over the cake.","The kid wiped his tears with his hand: \"I'm so worried about my cousin that I'm starting to see things...\"","Even a mother and son playing by the roadside looked familiar—he thought he glimpsed his cousin's and He Huanhuan's faces.","He really needed to rest. If he didn't, he was going to go crazy.","He didn't see that in the rearview mirror, the \"mother and son\" he thought he saw stood up, and both their faces were fully exposed.","It was He Huanhuan and Han Mo!","He Huanhuan adjusted her helmet: \"The e-bike's almost out of battery. Let's ride it home and charge it.\"","Wang Qiang's company was too stingy—employees weren't allowed to charge e-bikes at work. If they got caught, it was a two-hundred-yuan fine.","The two of them couldn't even earn two hundred yuan from delivering food all day, so they had to ride the e-bike back to the rundown house to charge it.","They rode into the village, and when they got near the rundown house, they noticed a bunch of villagers gathered by the roadside.","He Huanhuan curiously went up to ask: \"What's going on? Why's everyone gathered here?\"","\"That old house of Old Li's was taken over by a homeless person! So they're installing surveillance cameras on it now!\"","He Huanhuan was shocked: \"There are homeless people these days?\"","\"You bet! Isn't that something!\"","He Huanhuan took another look—oh my goodness! That was her and Han Mo's home!","Wait, no—wasn't that the rundown house they were temporarily staying in?","So the \"homeless person\" was them!","She awkwardly turned her head and exchanged a silent look with Han Mo.","She blinked: Our home is gone.","Han Mo gave a bitter smile: I can see that.","She blinked again: So what do we do now?","Han Mo raised an eyebrow: Let's go. Don't get caught by the owner.","Just as they were about to leave, the villager who had just spoken suddenly turned around!","Six eyes met. The villager grinned: \"Picking up your son from school?\"","Han Mo stared at the villager, pupils shaking. Him? Her son?","He Huanhuan? Her mother?","When did this man go blind?","But He Huanhuan instantly nodded with familiarity: \"Yeah, picking him up for lunch.\"","The villager glanced at Han Mo: \"Doesn't the school provide lunch? Why bring him home to eat?\"","Han Mo kept his face straight and said nothing. He Huanhuan immediately elbowed him: \"When your uncle's talking to you, why don't you answer? Kid, you're such a disappointment!\"","Han Mo's face instantly darkened: \"The food's bad.\"","The villager instantly started rambling: \"This kid's pretty big, but so picky! That's not good. You should learn from your parents. Your dad never used to be picky when he was little...\"","Han Mo's head was about to explode. His dad? Not picky when he was little?","What nonsense was this man talking?","Did he even know his dad?","He Huanhuan kept nodding: \"Tell me about it. Raising a kid is so exhausting. They won't eat this, won't eat that. Ugh, so stressful!\"","...","Han Mo couldn't take it anymore. He shoved He Huanhuan: \"Let's go home.\"","But He Huanhuan was getting into her role. She turned and glared at him: \"Mom's talking to someone here. All you know is 'go home, go home.' Such an ill-mannered kid!\"","Han Mo glared at her, face dark: \"We're leaving.\"","\"Ugh, there's just no dealing with you!\"","He Huanhuan still remembered to wave at the villager: \"We'll get going now...\"","The villager earnestly saw her off: \"Alright, alright... come over for a meal sometime...\"","\"Sure, sure...\"","Han Mo's head was spinning even more: \"You're actually going to eat at his house?\"","He Huanhuan laughed: \"Haven't you ever chatted with people before? This is just small talk!\"","...","They rode the e-bike out of the village, then squatted by the roadside, silent and staring at each other.","He Huanhuan sighed: \"We had a piece of cake, and now our home's gone.\"","The e-bike was also completely dead by then, so they had no choice but to push it.","Han Mo stood up and started pushing: \"Let's go to the sales office first and return the bike to Wang Qiang.\"","He Huanhuan followed behind, feeling regretful: \"Honestly, our home wasn't that bad. That bed was sturdier than the one I used to sleep on...\"","Han Mo paused, then asked casually: \"What kind of bed did you used to sleep on?\"","He Huanhuan replied offhandedly: \"I didn't have a bed. I used to sleep with my grandpa and grandma. That old wooden bed was sold by my dad for money.\"","Han Mo frowned in disbelief: \"You had no bed? How did you sleep?\"","\"Three wooden planks on two old benches—that was enough to sleep on.\"","...","A wordless emotion churned in his chest. He already knew she had suffered a lot before.","But when that suffering became specific—when it settled into those tiny details of everyday life—it suddenly became vivid and concrete.","He felt his heart ache in waves. What kind of life had she been living before?","He opened his mouth and finally forced the question out: \"What about your mom?\"","She'd only ever mentioned her loving grandparents and her worthless dad.","But her mother—she'd never mentioned her.","He Huanhuan blinked and said casually: \"Don't even bring her up. My dad was into drinking, gambling, whoring, and everything else. My mom got beaten away by him more than ten years ago.\"","Han Mo couldn't help but ask: \"Why didn't she take you with her?\"","If her mom had taken her away, wouldn't she have been spared all this suffering?","\"Forget it.\"","He Huanhuan stood behind the e-bike, pushing from the back: \"It wasn't easy for her just to escape. How would she have managed with me in tow? My dad's crazy. If she'd taken me, and he went off the deep end looking for her, what then?\"","Her dad was a total scumbag. Getting as far away from him as possible was a good thing.","She was genuinely happy for her mom.","Han Mo walked ahead, saying nothing for a long time.","The mood suddenly turned heavy. He Huanhuan reached out and patted him: \"Why aren't you saying anything?\"","\"Did he ever hit you?\"","He Huanhuan shook her head: \"No. He never had the guts for that.\"","When she was little, her grandparents protected her, so he couldn't get to her.","By the time her grandparents died, she was already grown and had gotten mixed into the punk scene.","If he dared so much as curse at her, she'd buy two packs of spicy chips and drag a whole house full of dyed-haired thugs back with her. She'd beat him senseless!"]},{"number":61,"title":"Chapter 61: No Subletting for Group Rentals","paragraphs":["Han Mo was a little displeased: \"Does Uncle Gu know about all the hardships you've endured?\"","He had been to the Gu family many times, but he had never seen a trace of heartache or guilt toward He Huanhuan in Mr. and Mrs. Gu Chengye.","Their biological daughter had suffered so much in the village, while Gu Chacha lived a life of luxury and wealth right beside them.","Didn't they feel any pain at all?","Unexpectedly, He Huanhuan gave a sly smile: \"Let me tell you a secret—I'm not actually the Gu family's daughter.\"","Han Mo was completely stunned: \"What did you say?\"","The Gu family had already made this kind of mistake once—how could they make it a second time?","That was absurd!","He Huanhuan put away her smile and looked at him seriously: \"Have you ever read Strange Tales from a Chinese Studio? There's a story in it called Xiaoxie. Have you read it?\"","Han Mo nodded. He had read it with his parents when he was a child.","He Huanhuan touched her face: \"I'm that Xiaoxie, just living inside this body.\"","Her expression was grave, nothing like someone joking around.","Han Mo hesitated for a moment, then chose to believe her: \"Then who were you before?\"","He Huanhuan touched her face again: \"Amazing, right? I used to look like this too! It's just that all the tattoos I paid for are gone now. I had tattoos all over my body—cost a small fortune!\"","\"Tattoos?\"","Han Mo couldn't quite imagine her covered in tattoos.","It was probably a stereotype, but a body full of tattoos inevitably made people think of danger, aggression, and impulsiveness.","He Huanhuan sighed: \"Tell me about it! My tattoos!\"","She reached for her right arm: \"Here I had a Doraemon tattooed, bright blue, it was gorgeous!\"","Then she touched her left arm: \"And here I had a SpongeBob. Those two took a ton of ink—it hurt like hell getting them done!\"","Han Mo looked at her now-clean arms: \"Why did you get those two?\"","He Huanhuan said enviously: \"Doraemon has that magic pouch—how awesome is that?\"","\"And SpongeBob?\"","He Huanhuan laughed: \"That was a buy-one-get-one-free deal. It was free, so why wouldn't I get a tattoo that uses tons of ink?\"","When it came to getting a bargain, looking good didn't matter—what mattered most was getting your money's worth!","Han Mo smiled helplessly: \"So are you going to get tattoos again now?\"","He Huanhuan shook her head: \"Forget it. That stuff hurts like crazy. I don't want to suffer through that again!\"","At first, she got tattoos to scare people off—to look fierce and intimidating so no one would dare bully her.","Later, she got tattoos to fit in with her circle. Everyone had them—how could she not?","That scene didn't tolerate nonconformists. You had to do everything the same way.","Now she wasn't afraid of bullies anymore, and she didn't need to please anyone else either.","Why the hell would she get more tattoos?","They hurt like hell!","When she said she wouldn't get any more, Han Mo secretly breathed a sigh of relief.","A body full of tattoos—he still couldn't appreciate that.","Besides, tattoos faded over time.","An image involuntarily flashed through his mind: the two of them in their forties or fifties, lying in bed, searching each other's bodies piece by piece—which one had faded, which one was half-faded...","Hmm, that didn't sound so bad either.","A faint smile tugged at his lips, and he couldn't help feeling a bit curious about He Huanhuan's past: \"So... your soul, I mean, the original you—where did you live? Do you want to go back and take a look?\"","He Huanhuan quickly reached out and covered his mouth: \"Pfft, pfft, pfft... I just decided to stay here for good, and you want to send me back?\"","\"You can't go back?\"","His eyes flickered. Was her father really as easy to handle as she'd said?","Or was she actually...","\"How can I go back when it's not even the same world?\"","The very thought of it frustrated He Huanhuan. If she had to be transmigrated into a book, couldn't they have brought Qi Meili along with her?","Her parents weren't that good to her anyway. It would've been great to have her come into the book and become a rich heiress with her.","In the modern world, the person she missed the most was Qi Meili.","With her gone, would Qi Meili still be able to out-argue those people?","\"Ugh...\"","She let out a deep sigh, then kicked Han Mo: \"No more questions. You're so annoying!\"","They pushed the scooter to the sales office. Wang Qiang, as the new guy, was still stationed at the entrance.","Seeing the two of them pushing the scooter toward him, Wang Qiang hurried over: \"What are you two doing here? The scooter's out of battery? Why didn't you take it back to charge?\"","The sales office didn't allow employees to charge personal scooters there. He'd told them that before.","\"What are you talking about! We got busted!\"","\"Huh?\"","Wang Qiang didn't understand. What did \"got busted\" mean?","Han Mo parked the scooter to the side and explained: \"That house has an owner, and they live in the village. The owner thought some homeless person had taken over the place, so today they installed surveillance cameras.\"","They couldn't stay there anymore.","\"Ah? Then what are you going to do?\"","Wang Qiang was worried for them: \"So where are you two going to sleep tonight?\"","He Huanhuan sighed: \"Under a bridge, I guess. It's not like we have any other options—we're both down on our luck...\"","Han Mo lowered his gaze despondently: \"I'm sorry I've put you through all this. I...\"","The two of them looked so miserable that Wang Qiang's heart ached for them.","While sneaking peeks on his phone at work this morning, he'd searched their stories. These two rich kids were worse off than an ordinary guy like him.","He Huanhuan was the real daughter who'd been switched at birth, only brought back home not long ago.","As for Han Mo, his mother had been driven to death by his father's mistress and illegitimate son, and then he was shipped off abroad and only returned after several years.","Whatever had happened, the two of them were now reduced to hiding out in a run-down house.","They couldn't use their phones, and they couldn't spend a single cent.","How pitiful!","He couldn't help but pull out the key to his rental room: \"How about you two crash at my place for now? It's small, but the three of us can manage if we squeeze in.\"","Han Mo looked up in a flash: \"Deal.\"","Huh?","Before he could react, He Huanhuan hopped over to Wang Qiang, snatched the key, and stuffed it into the pocket of Han Mo's school uniform.","Then, grinning, she patted Wang Qiang on the shoulder: \"Sis knew it—you're the best, Xiaoqiang!\"","Something felt off.","Wang Qiang scratched his head: \"Wait... were you two just putting on a show for me?\"","He Huanhuan smiled innocently: \"Xiaoqiang, what are you talking about? When would we ever trick you!\"","Han Mo nodded seriously: \"Right.\"","\"Really?\"","Wang Qiang looked at them suspiciously: \"So you didn't have your eye on my place from the very start?\"","He Huanhuan raised her hand as if swearing an oath: \"If I'm lying to you, then let Han Mo have no place to sleep tonight!\"","Han Mo: ...That doesn't sound great?","Wang Qiang still had work to do, so after they got the exact location of his rental from him, the two pushed the scooter and left.","He rented a room in a residential building too, about ten kilometers from the sales office.","They pushed the scooter for over two hours before finding the three-story building he'd mentioned.","Wang Qiang's single room was on the second floor. They had just carried the battery up and plugged it in to charge when a loud knock pounded on the door!","\"Open up! Now!\"","Han Mo went to open the door. Standing outside was a middle-aged man in his forties, with a thin, gaunt face that looked somewhat mean-spirited.","He scanned the two of them and asked in a hostile tone: \"Who are you to Wang Qiang?\"","Han Mo replied: \"Friends.\"","He asked again: \"Where's Wang Qiang?\"","Han Mo continued: \"He hasn't gotten off work yet. We brought his scooter back to charge.\"","He gave them another once-over: \"I don't do group rentals for this house. You two aren't staying here tonight, are you?\"","......"]},{"number":62,"title":"Chapter 62: Hey Huanhuan Han Mo Stop right there","paragraphs":["The two of them were dead silent, their eyes darting away nervously.","The man's face immediately turned sour: \"What's the matter?! You think three people can squeeze into this piss-small room?\"","Han Mo braced one hand against the doorframe, blocking the man from coming in: \"Are you the landlord?\"","The man shot him a look: \"Who else would I be?\"","Han Mo kept his expression calm: \"We're just here to charge his e-bike. We're not staying the night.\"","The landlord eyed him suspiciously: \"Really?\"","Han Mo nodded: \"As you said, this room is too small for three people anyway.\"","Only then did the landlord turn and head downstairs, but he left the first-floor door cracked open.","Seeing him leave, He Huanhuan grimaced and smacked herself: \"I was just shooting my mouth off, and now we actually got ourselves kicked out of a place to sleep!\"","Han Mo was about to comfort her when she added: \"And why does the punishment have to be collective? It'd be fine if just Han Mo had no place to sleep!\"","Forget comforting her. Might as well go wander the streets together.","Wang Qiang's rental was tiny. Against the wall sat a single bed. A nightstand beside the bed, a small wardrobe at the foot — that was it.","So small, a kid couldn't even fill the room.","Two pairs of shoes sat behind the door, and the wardrobe held maybe a dozen pieces of clothing covering all four seasons.","He Huanhuan sat on the bed and didn't even need to stand to take in the whole room.","\"He's had it rough too.\"","Han Mo nodded: \"Once this mess is over, I'll take care of him.\"","He Huanhuan looked up: \"How exactly do you plan to do that?\"","Han Mo thought for a moment: \"Get him a driver's license. He can start as my driver.\"","Let him stick around and get used to things first, then see if there's a better path for him later.","After all, this guy helped him when he was in trouble. He couldn't just watch him keep living such a hard life.","The moment he finished speaking, a sneering voice drifted from outside the door: \"Oh ho, look who we have here — a big-shot boss from the countryside! Got his own driver and everything! Just too bad he's mooching off my crummy place!\"","...","How did this guy move so quietly?","Before they could react, the landlord called out again from the hall: \"Big boss, is the e-bike charged yet? Want me to call your driver to pick you up?\"","Well, looks like they weren't staying here tonight.","Han Mo glanced at the battery — it was over half charged, enough for Wang Qiang to ride back on.","He bent down, unplugged the charger, and hoisted the battery out.","\"Let's go.\"","He Huanhuan shot up: \"Fine.\"","It was just some run-down house anyway! If they didn't let them stay, so be it!","When they opened the door, sure enough, the landlord was standing right there, staring at them with pure mockery: \"Big boss, battery charged? Driver called? Want me to dial someone up for you?\"","Han Mo ignored him, walking off with the battery in hand.","Down on the first floor, he put the battery back into the e-bike.","He Huanhuan put on her helmet, sat on the bike, and pressed the horn.","\"Beep beep!\"","She shouted: \"Old Geezer!\"","The landlord actually poked his head out from upstairs, and He Huanhuan flipped him off into the air: \"I'm his driver, you hear me?!\"","With that, she gunned the throttle and sped off with Han Mo on the back.","The landlord spat angrily at their tails: \"Pfft! You think I can't find someone? I just don't want to!\"","He was still young — no advantage yet.","Wait until he hit sixty: pension in his pocket, rent rolling in every month.","Then the advantage kicks in!","They rode back to the sales office, and Wang Qiang was still standing outside.","Seeing them, he looked baffled: \"Why are you two back?\"","He Huanhuan got off the bike with a huff: \"Your psycho landlord wouldn't let us stay! And he made fun of Han Mo! Who does he think he is?!\"","Wang Qiang leaned in: \"He's got a sharp mouth, sure. What exactly did he say?\"","The corner of Han Mo's mouth twitched slightly upward: \"Nothing much. He overheard us talking and got it in his head that I was pretending to be rich, so he threw a few snide remarks my way.\"","He parked the e-bike to the side and told Wang Qiang: \"Didn't charge it much. Go straight home after work. Don't wander off.\"","Wang Qiang nodded: \"Got it.\"","After parking, the two were ready to head out, and Wang Qiang couldn't help asking: \"Where are you two going?\"","Their hideout had cameras, and they couldn't use their phones or IDs. Where could they even go?","He Huanhuan waved at him coolly: \"Just do your job. See you tomorrow!\"","They had another two hundred yuan to earn tomorrow.","Watching them leave, Wang Qiang stood at the entrance, feeling miserable and with no idea what to do.","He'd worked a lot of jobs, but he never finished high school and was only nineteen years old.","A not-very-bright nineteen-year-old couldn't come up with a solid plan that fast.","A coworker saw him out there with his head down, all gloomy.","He came out and asked: \"What's with the long face? Got dumped?\"","Wang Qiang grimaced at him: \"How do you jump straight to romance?\"","The coworker widened his eyes dramatically: \"What else is life for if not love? Working a job? Then I might as well be dead!\"","He nudged Wang Qiang: \"So what's going on? Spill.\"","Wang Qiang told him about the landlord refusing to let more people stay: \"What are they supposed to do tonight? Really sleep under a bridge?\"","The coworker stared at him like he was an idiot: \"They can't use their IDs. But yours works fine, right? Just use your ID to book them a hotel room tonight.\"","...","\"Right!\"","Wang Qiang lit up: \"You're so smart!\"","The coworker rolled his eyes: \"I can tell you've never been in a relationship. You don't even know how to book a hotel!\"","Wang Qiang grinned sheepishly: \"Then I'll tell them right now!\"","He pulled out his phone and froze: \"They don't have phones. How am I supposed to tell them?\"","The coworker was speechless: \"Don't tell me they're the same two con artists from yesterday. You actually made friends with them?\"","Wang Qiang insisted: \"Don't talk about them like that. They're really not bad people.\"","The coworker couldn't be bothered to argue. Whatever — the kid had no money anyway, so if he got scammed, so be it.","These days, everyone gets scammed eventually.","If not by friends, then by love.","A couple of lessons and he'd wise up.","Besides, the kid was so dense he couldn't even think of booking a hotel room. What was there to scam from him?","And even funnier — those two \"con artists\" hadn't thought of it either.","Clearly, they weren't very sharp con artists.","The coworker went back inside, satisfied.","He'd get a good look at those two con artists tomorrow when the homeowner showed up for a viewing.","Meanwhile, the two not-so-bright con artists had already walked past the village where they'd first crashed and reached a second village.","This one looked a lot richer than the last. From the edge of the village, all you could see were neat three-story houses or four-to-five-story villas.","As they walked down the village road, they found it was paved with asphalt, with tidy little flower beds lining both sides.","He Huanhuan sighed: \"I feel like there's no house for us in this village...\"","This one clearly had no run-down buildings.","Han Mo nodded: \"If there's nothing here, we go to the next village. We'll find ourselves a home.\"","They strolled from one end of the village to the other, and sure enough, not a single broken-down house in sight.","They were about to leave when a loud, certain voice rang out from behind them: \"He Huanhuan! Han Mo! Stop right there!\""]},{"number":63,"title":"Chapter 63: So that's what he meant","paragraphs":["Suddenly being called out by name, both of them tensed up and stopped in their tracks.","He Huanhuan nudged Han Mo with her elbow: \"Should we run?\"","Han Mo hesitated: \"Don't you think that voice sounds a little familiar?\"","It seemed their home had come to find them.","He Huanhuan tried to recall: \"Familiar? I don't think so?\"","Before she could remember, the person was already sprinting toward them: \"He Huanhuan! You're alive! Wuwuwu... thank goodness!\"","The voice reached them in a flash, and He Huanhuan finally recognized him: \"Liang Ye? What are you doing here?\"","Wasn't he working at the neighborhood committee?","She remembered that the big heart she'd sent him last time didn't say this village on it.","\"He Huanhuan! I knew you weren't dead! Wuwuwu...\"","Liang Ye had no interest in answering her question. He spread his arms wide, ready to wrap He Huanhuan up in a good cry.","Han Mo saw his outstretched arms and couldn't help but frown.","He quickly sidestepped, blocking himself in front of He Huanhuan.","Liang Ye was crying with his eyes closed and hadn't noticed the movement at all, so he hugged him directly: \"Wuwuwu... Huh?\"","Since when was He Huanhuan this tall?","Opening his eyes, he instantly let go: \"Han Mo! Why aren't you dead?\"","Han Mo looked down at him: \"Sorry to disappoint you.\"","\"Hmph!\"","Liang Ye glanced at him, then at He Huanhuan.","His brother was right — the two of them really had disappeared together.","He looked at He Huanhuan with a wounded expression: \"Why did you disappear with Han Mo? His family's mess has nothing to do with you!\"","\"How is it nothing to do with me? We're...\"","Mid-sentence, He Huanhuan snapped her mouth shut, her eyes darting away.","Liang Ye blinked his innocent little eyes and asked: \"You're what? What?\"","No wonder he never succeeded in all those blind dates — he had zero situational awareness!","He Huanhuan flushed with embarrassment and anger, hopping up to punch him: \"Ask again and I'll beat you up!\"","Liang Ye clutched his aching arm with a silly grin: \"That punch actually hurt, hehe...\"","...","That made He Huanhuan unable to throw another punch — wasn't that just rewarding him?","She said to him in a huffy tone: \"Don't tell anyone you saw us, got it?\"","Liang Ye nodded: \"Got it.\"","Hearing that, He Huanhuan made to leave.","But before she could lift her foot, she saw Liang Ye pull out his phone and start sending a voice message: \"Bro, guess who I saw today...\"","He Huanhuan snatched the phone away: \"Didn't you just promise not to tell anyone?\"","Liang Ye nodded: \"But that's my brother.\"","...","\"Not even your brother!\"","Liang Ye frowned: \"Then I might not be able to control myself...\"","He never kept secrets from his brother.","Brother would say: That's because you have no secrets. I still have mine.","He Huanhuan glared at him: \"You have to control it even if you can't!\"","Liang Ye's little eyes darted around, then he said as if casually: \"Unless you keep an eye on me, I definitely won't be able to hold it in...\"","He Huanhuan took the bait: \"Fine, I'll watch you!\"","She and Han Mo had already held out for two days. Only thirteen more days to go — they had to tough it out!","Wasn't it just watching Liang Ye?","Wasn't it just...","Hmm?","Her eyes suddenly lit up. Oh, wow!","They'd been stuck with no place to stay!","This was the perfect chance to stay at Liang Ye's house!","Hahahaha...","What was this called?","You search high and low for something, only to find it right in front of you with no effort at all!","She tried to suppress the smile tugging at her lips and nudged Han Mo with her elbow: \"We have to go watch him, right?\"","Han Mo nodded: \"Right.\"","He Huanhuan struggled to keep her mouth straight: \"Then let's stay at his place and watch him around the clock.\"","A faint smile curved Han Mo's lips: \"Sounds good.\"","Liang Ye's smile was even harder to suppress: \"Then come on over!\"","Han Mo watched the two of them and gave a helpless chuckle.","Those two were basically a mutual match made in heaven.","Liang Ye checked the time — it wasn't quitting time yet, but he was afraid they'd run off, so he quickly said to them: \"You two wait for me. I'll go request leave, and once that's done, we'll go home together!\"","He sprinted off toward the village committee office, shouting back as he ran: \"Make sure you wait for me!\"","He was overthinking it — even if hail were falling from the sky right now, those two wouldn't leave.","They'd finally found a place to stay; there was no way they'd give that up.","By the time Liang Ye finished requesting leave and ran back out, they were indeed still waiting right where he'd left them.","He jogged over to He Huanhuan cheerfully: \"Come on, follow me home!\"","The two fell in step behind him, but Liang Ye scowled at Han Mo: \"Why are you following me?\"","Han Mo smiled: \"We're together.\"","Liang Ye's face soured even more: \"You're not welcome in my house.\"","The smile in Han Mo's eyes deepened: \"Fine.\"","He reached out, took He Huanhuan's hand, and turned to leave.","He hadn't taken two steps before a desperate shout rang out behind him: \"Stop!\"","\"No, let go of her first!\"","Liang Ye stomped over and separated the two of them. He shot Han Mo a glare: \"You're coming home with me too!\"","Dammit, he'd actually let his rival stay under his roof.","He was tainted now!","At the parking lot at the edge of the village, he pointed at the electric scooter parked farthest in and showed off: \"See? I bought my own scooter!\"","He Huanhuan didn't get it. What was he bragging about?","Was he a rich second-generation kid or something? Why show off over an electric scooter?","What Liang Ye wanted to say was that he used to be so naive, thinking taking a taxi was already the thriftiest way to get around.","If it hadn't been for He Huanhuan, he'd never have learned just how much money a scooter could save.","That was all her doing.","He looked down at He Huanhuan: \"If it weren't for you, I'd never have gotten on an electric scooter...\"","He Huanhuan rolled her eyes at him: \"Are you trying to insult me?\"","Liang Ye rushed to explain: \"No, no! I mean, if it weren't for hitching rides on your scooter, I'd never have known a person could be that shameless about bumming rides...\"","...Was that even a compliment?","Han Mo's lips twitched upward. What a pitifully weak rival.","Han Mo cut off his clumsy rambling: \"If not for you, his world wouldn't have so many options.\"","Liang Ye hurriedly nodded: \"Right, right, right! That's exactly what I meant!\"","Han Mo continued: \"You've shown us a different world, Huanhuan. That's all your doing.\"","Liang Ye nodded frantically: \"Yes, yes! That's what I meant!\"","He Huanhuan looked at Han Mo with a smile: \"Really? You're not lying to me?\"","Han Mo nodded: \"Really.\"","He Huanhuan wrinkled her nose: \"Hmph! I don't believe you!\"","Liang Ye stood at the side, frowning. Something felt off here, right?","Wasn't that his line?","Why was He Huanhuan humming at Han Mo?","That wasn't right!","He tried his best to squeeze between the two of them: \"Hey, Huanhuan, I meant that too. Really, I meant the same thing...\"","He Huanhuan gave a perfunctory nod: \"Mm-hmm, I know. Let's go. Time to head home.\"","The two of them walked over to his scooter in perfect sync, leaving him looking as unnecessary as a bystander.","No wait — those had been his words!"]},{"number":64,"title":"Chapter 64: Don't rush her to shower tomorrow.","paragraphs":["Liang Ye's home was in the city proper, about a half-hour's ride from the village by electric scooter.","One scooter couldn't fit three people at all, but he couldn't bear to spend money on a taxi. He sat on the scooter and gestured to the other two: \"You both sit behind me. The three of us can squeeze.\"","Han Mo frowned: \"Isn't that unsafe?\"","Liang Ye shot him a look: \"You've already been hit by a car, and you're still worried about safety?\"","Han Mo said helplessly: \"It's precisely because I've been hit by a car that I need to worry more, right?\"","Liang Ye scooted his hips forward: \"Don't worry, I've got great riding skills. Very steady.\"","A taxi from here to his place would cost over fifty yuan. Might as well kill him.","\"Huanhuan, hurry up and get on. You sit behind me. Han Mo sits behind you. It'll work.\"","A smile crept up at the corner of his mouth. This way, he'd get to sit right next to He Huanhuan. Hehehe...","But to his surprise, He Huanhuan yanked him off the scooter: \"I'll drive.\"","He'd only ridden an electric scooter a few times. How could he compare to her experience?","She was a bona fide poor person, after all!","She plopped herself onto the seat and looked at Han Mo: \"You sit behind me.\"","Liang Ye tried to grab the spot: \"I want to sit!\"","But Han Mo, quick-eyed and fast-legged, stepped forward and sat right down behind He Huanhuan. Then he smiled at him: \"Come on, I left a spot for you.\"","Seeing them pressed together made Liang Ye furious: \"Move back! I'm very skinny, I don't need that much space!\"","Han Mo nodded: \"Fine.\"","He scooted back a bit, and the scooter suddenly had no room left at all.","......","Liang Ye sat down behind him in a huff, immediately squashing Han Mo against He Huanhuan.","Liang Ye was angry: \"Move away from her!\"","Stuck in the middle, Han Mo asked him: \"How exactly do you expect me to move?\"","Liang Ye hugged him tightly, pulling him toward himself: \"Don't take advantage of Huanhuan! She's mine!\"","He Huanhuan gripped the handlebars tightly: \"Shut up! Don't move around! The scooter's going to tip over!\"","Actually, she hadn't ridden an electric scooter very many times either. In the past, she'd always gotten around on foot. Where would she have gotten the money for a scooter?","One scooter carrying three people, and the two behind her wouldn't behave. What should have been a half-hour ride took He Huanhuan nearly an hour to finish.","Once they entered the city area, the two behind her, afraid of being caught on camera, kept their heads down in unison.","Liang Ye hugged Han Mo tightly and ducked his head carefully along with him: \"What exactly are we doing?\"","Han Mo pushed his hands away: \"You don't need to lower your head.\"","In the next second, Liang Ye hugged him again: \"Why not?\"","Han Mo was speechless: \"You figure it out yourself.\"","Besides, he wasn't a missing person. Why would he need to hide his face?","And also, \"Put your hands down.\"","Why did he keep hugging him?","Were they even that close?","Liang Ye ignored him and hugged him even tighter: \"What, do you want to sit pressed up against He Huanhuan? Let me tell you, no way!\"","He shouldn't have settled for that little bit of contact. He might as well have gone to sleep under a bridge.","As the scooter drove into the neighborhood, the two finally relaxed.","The neighborhood Liang Ye lived in had been built almost thirty years ago, and it was very old.","The people living there were basically all retirees.","His home was on the third floor of the first building on the right as you entered, which counted as a prime floor.","Once inside the apartment, He Huanhuan was speechless: \"Your place only has one room?\"","She never would have guessed that Liang Ye had bought himself a studio!","Liang Ye nodded proudly: \"Of course just one room. If there were extra rooms, wouldn't that just invite some clueless people to come visit?\"","If they came to visit, he'd have to spend money hosting them, and he couldn't bear that!","The two clueless people stayed silent: Who exactly are you mocking?","Liang Ye didn't realize at all what he'd said. He beamed and called out to He Huanhuan: \"Huanhuan, come here. Let me show you around my place...\"","He Huanhuan glanced at Han Mo: \"Is he deliberately being passive-aggressive at me?\"","Han Mo shook his head without hesitation: \"He's just stupid.\"","That was true. His buddy never thought of He Huanhuan as just a visitor. She was his future lady of the house, okay?","There wasn't much to see in a place of under forty square meters anyway. To the left of the entrance was the bathroom and kitchen. On the right was a small living room, past the living room was the bedroom, and outside the bedroom was a small balcony.","Everything was very small, after all, it was barely over thirty square meters.","They took it all in with two glances.","But at least there was a proper sofa. He Huanhuan plopped herself down on it: \"I'm starving. Let's order takeout.\"","The two looked at Liang Ye. Their phones weren't usable, so they could only order through Liang Ye's account.","Liang Ye pursed his lips, his face full of hesitation: \"I can order, but you two have to split the cost with me.\"","......","\"Split!\"","Liang Ye held out his hand: \"Let's split it upfront. I'm afraid you two won't pay me back.\"","......","Han Mo counted out thirty-five yuan in cash and handed it to him. Only then did Liang Ye open his food delivery app and order from a place he usually got rice bowls from.","After paying, he sneakily glanced at the two. Seeing that neither was paying attention to him, he breathed a sigh of relief and grinned inwardly.","He'd used a big coupon. All three meals together only cost thirty-two yuan.","He'd made three yuan in profit, hehe......","He quietly slipped his phone into his pocket. Once money entered his pocket, there was no way he was giving it back.","Good thing neither of them had any intention of asking how much he'd actually spent. They were worn out from the day and only wanted to finish eating quickly and wash up properly so they could sleep.","For the past couple of days in that crappy house, they could only make do with a wipe-down wash. Unbearable!","The takeout arrived quickly. The three of them didn't talk and just ate in silence.","After eating, He Huanhuan rushed to the bathroom first, giving her hair a good long wash and taking a proper shower to loosen up.","Twenty minutes under the hot water, and she finally felt alive again.","The bathroom door was knocked on, and Liang Ye felt his heart bleed: \"Haven't you had enough, Huanhuan? How long are you going to wash? Wasting water is wrong.\"","......","This guy really... No wonder he couldn't find a girlfriend!","He Huanhuan silently turned off the water, dried off, and stepped out.","Outside the door, Liang Ye lectured Han Mo with righteous indignation: \"You only get to shower for ten minutes. If you go over, I'm charging you for water and gas.\"","Han Mo said: \"Deal.\"","The moment Han Mo went in, Liang Ye pulled out his phone and started a timer.","Two minutes, five minutes, eight minutes, nine minutes thirty seconds...","A smile tugged at the corner of Liang Ye's lips. Another bit of income was coming his way!","Nine minutes, fifty-seven seconds. Nine minutes, fifty-eight seconds...","The sound of the water suddenly stopped. Han Mo opened the door and stepped out: \"I'm done.\"","Damn!","So close. Just a little more, just a little bit more, and he could have charged him money!","\"Oh, by the way.\"","Han Mo turned back and asked him: \"How much did that takeout just now cost? Let me see the order.\"","Damn!","His heart ached. His three yuan!","No, his 13.6666...","He pulled out his phone with a grimace: \"I just forgot to settle the bill with you. Three meals for thirty-two yuan, so I still owe you thirteen...\"","Han Mo smiled: \"It's thirteen yuan and sixty-six cents. Give me thirteen fifty.\"","Liang Ye's heart ached as if bleeding: \"My heart hurts. Can I just not pay?\"","Han Mo stated his condition: \"Tomorrow when Huanhuan showers, don't rush her.\"","Liang Ye nodded eagerly: \"Deal! I definitely won't rush her!\""]},{"number":65,"title":"Chapter 65: Perhaps You Know He Huanhuan","paragraphs":["There was only one room, and Liang Ye naturally gave it to He Huanhuan.","When money wasn't involved, the guy could still be a gentleman.","He gave He Huanhuan a concerned look. \"The room's yours. I haven't seen you in a few days, and you look worn out...\"","He Huanhuan held out her hand to him. \"Then give me some cash to spend.\"","The guy tilted his head up at a forty-five degree angle and gazed at the sky. \"Wow, the moon is so round tonight! Aiya~ I really need to go admire the moon~\"","He Huanhuan smirked slyly. She knew he'd do exactly that.","She glanced at Han Mo. \"How are you sleeping tonight?\"","Han Mo pointed at the sofa. \"He bought a sofa bed. He and I will just crash on that.\"","\"Alright.\"","He Huanhuan turned and went back into the room, lying down on the bed. She almost let out a moan of comfort.","Liang Ye might be cheap, but he didn't treat himself badly.","The mattress was soft and springy — clearly not a cheap buy.","Liang Ye said it was a gift from his brother. If he'd had to buy it himself, he definitely wouldn't have splurged.","Lying on that incredibly comfortable bed, she fell asleep as soon as her head hit the pillow.","In her dream, she was back in the real world, right after she'd been cracked over the head with a beer bottle.","She'd passed out on the spot and never woken up again.","The person who hit her came from a poor family and only paid her family a little over twenty thousand yuan in compensation.","Her dad took the money and went off to drink and party, not giving a damn about her.","In the dream, Qi Meili was crouched by her bedside with a bruised eye, crying:","\"Sister Huan, I couldn't beat up your dad. He took all the money, wuwuwu... But don't worry, I'll earn money to treat you...\"","Then Qi Meili went off to work, taking double shifts at a factory, night after night.","She was the laziest person when it came to work, yet she stuck with it without missing a single day.","When her first month's paycheck came in, Qi Meili threw herself over He Huanhuan and wailed: \"Sister Huan! Work is so exhausting! How about we just die together, wuwuwu...\"","He Huanhuan's eyes turned red despite herself. \"Just leave me alone, wuwuwu...\"","A painful sob jolted her awake. He Huanhuan sat up, sniffling, and realized it was only a dream.","It was too real. How could a dream be that real?","She could even remember the feeling of Qi Meili's tears landing on her hand — cool, and heartbreaking.","She sat on the bed, staring at the moon outside the window, and couldn't stop feeling a wave of sadness.","If that dream was real, how much pain would Qi Meili be in?","\"God, please don't do that to Qi Meili. I beg you.\"","Qi Meili was the last person who could endure hardship. Back when they used to go out and hit the streets, after just two hours of walking, Qi Meili would already be complaining that her feet hurt.","Qi Meili's parents divorced when she was in elementary school, and later each remarried and had their own kids.","They occasionally gave Qi Meili a little money, but she didn't have parents anymore.","They had become other people's parents.","So Qi Meili dropped out of middle school and started drifting through the streets. She hated working more than anything.","She'd said it herself: as long as she wasn't literally starving to death, she would never get a job.","And yet, for her, she went and took double shifts at a factory.","Double shifts meant twelve hours straight...","Thinking about it, He Huanhuan wanted to cry again.","Anyway, her parents didn't want her, and she had no attachments left in that world.","Better to be sent into the world of this book, so the two of them could stay together forever.","Right!","Give Qi Meili to her!","He Huanhuan sat up and desperately kowtowed at the moon. \"Send Qi Meili to me! I'll take good care of her!\"","In the living room, Liang Ye was hugging Han Mo and snoring like crazy, pounding his head with noise.","Half-asleep, Han Mo heard a faint, muffled crying coming from the room.","He got up, walked to the door, and wanted to knock to ask if something was wrong.","But he hesitated, pulled his hand back, and went to the kitchen to pour a glass of water instead.","He set it on the cabinet by the door and went back to sleep.","He Huanhuan had a good long cry, then got up to wash her face.","When she opened the door and saw the glass of water on the cabinet, she froze for a moment before looking over at the sofa.","On the sofa, Liang Ye was sprawled over Han Mo like an octopus, snoring away, while Han Mo's brows were tightly furrowed — clearly not sleeping well.","She dried her tears, drank the water in one go, and turned back into the room to sleep.","The next morning, Liang Ye got up early and shoved Han Mo awake. \"How can you be so lazy? Look at the time, and you're still not up!\"","Han Mo sat up with dark circles under his eyes, his head throbbing. Liang Ye's sleeping habits were truly terrible!","Breakfast was made from discounted eggs Liang Ye had bought before, and discounted toast frozen in the fridge.","The toast was heated up in the air fryer, and each of them got two fried eggs.","Total cost for the two of them: five yuan.","Yes, Liang Ye even charged for breakfast, but he didn't dare overcharge — he only asked for what he'd paid.","After breakfast, they again hitched a ride on Liang Ye's electric scooter to the village.","They dropped Liang Ye off at the village committee office, then planned to take his scooter to the sales office.","Liang Ye endured it as long as he could, then finally blurted out: \"You two aren't going to steal my baby, are you?\"","Han Mo sighed helplessly. \"Do you really think I would?\"","It wasn't like Liang Ye didn't know them. They were just temporarily down on their luck, not actually broke.","Liang Ye lowered his head guiltily. \"Your dad's collapsed and in the hospital, and your family's company is completely in your brother's hands now. Who knows if you still have any money...\"","\"Relax, I still have plenty of money. I won't steal your scooter.\"","The two promised to return it before noon, and only then did Liang Ye reluctantly agree to lend it to them.","Worried about his scooter, he was distracted all morning at work.","He waited until lunch break, but the scooter still hadn't come back.","He was so anxious he couldn't even eat. He borrowed an electric scooter from a coworker and set off to find them. That was his precious ride! Brand new!","The shortest route to the sales office was a quiet little road with barely any people, so Liang Ye boldly sped up quite a bit.","He was sure there hadn't been anyone ahead, but in the blink of an eye, an electric scooter suddenly appeared right in front of him!","He had no time to brake and slammed straight into it!","\"BANG!\"","He felt the world spin, then a blinding flash of red.","Oh no! His eyes must be bleeding!","\"Hey! You dead or not?\"","A highly impatient voice sounded in his ear. He looked over, dazed.","Oh!","Turns out that blinding red was just the person's red hair!","His eyes were fine!","Hahaha...","He scrambled to his feet, overjoyed, and looked at the person.","She was a young girl, around twenty years old, with a shockingly bright red dye job.","She was chewing gum, had a vivid blue Doraemon tattooed on her right arm, and a bright yellow SpongeBob on her left.","She looked completely shady at first glance.","He instinctively shuffled a couple of steps toward his scooter, and the girl immediately glared at him viciously. \"What? Hit someone and now you're trying to run?\"","He quickly waved his hands. \"No, no, it's not that...\"","\"SMACK!\"","Without even letting him explain, the girl slapped him right across the face. \"You son of a bitch! You hit me and try to run?! I'll beat you to death!\"","Slaps and curses rained down on his head, leaving him dizzy and disoriented.","But deep down, a strange flicker of familiarity stirred in him. \"Um... do you know He Huanhuan?\"","The beating and scolding abruptly stopped as the red-haired girl fixed him with a fierce glare. \"How do you know my Sister Huan? Who the hell are you?\""]},{"number":66,"title":"Chapter 66: Qi Meili","paragraphs":["Liang Ye was overjoyed. \"You really know He Huanhuan?\"","Oh my god!","He didn't have to pay damages after all!","But the girl grabbed his ear. \"I'm asking who you are! Why aren't you answering? Looking for death, huh!\"","\"It hurts, it hurts, it hurts...\"","Liang Ye yelped in pain. \"I was just about to go find He Huanhuan!\"","\"You're looking for Sister Huan?\"","The girl gave him a very strange look. \"How exactly are you going to find her?\"","Liang Ye was confused. \"She's at the sales office, isn't she? Isn't she supposed to be buying a house today?\"","He hadn't gotten it wrong, had he? Weren't they headed to the sales office to pretend to buy a house?","And she'd borrowed his electric scooter, which was exactly why he'd been in such a hurry that he'd accidentally bumped into someone...","\"Buying a house?\"","The girl's expression turned even weirder. \"She said she was buying a house?\"","Liang Ye nodded. \"You didn't know?\"","Did she even actually know He Huanhuan?","But with that head of red hair and that fierce way she carried herself, she really did remind him of He Huanhuan!","Qi Meili couldn't quite process it. She'd been working the long night shift today.","The factory was behind schedule, and she'd volunteered to work extra hours on top of that, not getting off until noon.","On her way home she was so exhausted she could barely keep her eyes open.","Just now, in a daze, she'd nodded off while riding.","When she came back to her senses, she realized her surroundings didn't look right.","She'd been riding the route from the factory to her home for over a month—she knew exactly what was on every stretch of road and what it looked like. It was etched into her memory.","She was absolutely certain that the scene in front of her didn't belong to any part of that route.","She couldn't help but panic. She'd heard that if you worked too much overtime, you started hallucinating, and then you lost your mind.","She knew she shouldn't have gone to work!","Boohoo...","She had to hold it together. Even if she died, she was dragging He Huanhuan down with her!","She was still so young. She didn't want to die!","She'd never even dated a hot guy!","Tears started streaming down her face, blurring her vision.","And then...","\"BAM!\"","She was knocked flying.","The person who hit her actually knew He Huanhuan? And said He Huanhuan was at the sales office buying a house?","She started to suspect she'd already lost her mind. Wasn't He Huanhuan in a vegetative state?","Were they talking about the same He Huanhuan?","She pulled out her phone and found a picture of her and He Huanhuan together to show Liang Ye. \"The He Huanhuan you're talking about—is it her?\"","Liang Ye looked at her phone and was stunned.","In the photo, He Huanhuan's head of bright blue hair nearly blinded him through the screen.","Both arms were completely covered in tattoos, and she was rolling her eyes at the camera.","God!","Where did this punk chick come from?!","He swallowed hard. \"It looks like her—same face. But her hair isn't blue. It's rainbow-colored. And she doesn't have any tattoos...\"","\"No tattoos?\"","Qi Meili's brow furrowed deeply. \"Not a single one?\"","Liang Ye nodded. \"Well, at least when I saw her, she didn't have any.\"","Qi Meili understood immediately. This guy had to be He Huanhuan's ex-boyfriend!","That little sneak had been dating behind her back!","She'd probably covered up her tattoos with foundation because she was afraid he'd think less of her.","She gave Liang Ye a disdainful once-over. What was so great about this ugly duckling?","Her stingy little friend actually spent money on foundation for him—with that many tattoos, it would take a whole lot of foundation to cover them all!","But what did he mean by saying He Huanhuan was buying a house?","Was He Huanhuan pretending to be rich for this guy or something?","When did that happen?","He Huanhuan had been lying in a hospital bed for over a month now. Didn't he know that?","Her not-so-bright brain spun wildly, unable to make sense of the timeline.","She grabbed Liang Ye and hauled him up. \"Ugly piece of trash, when exactly did He Huanhuan tell you she was buying a house? How long has it been since you two talked?\"","\"What did you call me ugly for?\"","Liang Ye had never been called ugly to his face before. He couldn't believe it.","Was he ugly?","Where was he ugly?","He just wasn't obviously handsome, that was all!","\"SMACK!\"","Qi Meili slapped him on the head. \"Talk!\"","Liang Ye held his head and confessed. \"She told me this morning! She was going to the sales office to put on an act and pretend to buy a house, a hundred bucks a day. She and her friend also borrowed my electric scooter. They said they'd bring it back by noon, but they haven't...\"","Qi Meili's eyes went wide instantly. \"Morning? You said morning? Which morning? This morning?\"","Liang Ye was puzzled. \"Of course this morning...\"","It wasn't yesterday morning—he hadn't even met them then.","\"Hold on, wait...\"","Qi Meili couldn't piece it together. She'd gone to the hospital to see He Huanhuan yesterday after work, and she was definitely lying in that hospital bed.","But this ugly idiot was saying he'd talked to He Huanhuan this morning, and that He Huanhuan was going to the sales office today to put on an act?","No, no, no...","No, no, no...","\"SMACK!\"","She slapped herself hard. \"This is what you get for not studying hard back in school. Can't figure it out now, can you!\"","Fine. She had to go see for herself. She absolutely had to—otherwise she'd never be able to close her eyes in peace, even in death.","\"You!\"","She pointed at Liang Ye. \"Take me to He Huanhuan right now.\"","Liang Ye whined. \"I was going to go find her anyway. She still hasn't returned my electric scooter...\"","\"Shut up! Start driving!\"","\"Okay...\"","Meanwhile, in the sales office, He Huanhuan was busy playing the part of a shy little bride-to-be, completely unaware of the huge surprise heading her way.","Today's customers were a young couple preparing for their wedding, looking to buy a marital home.","There were only two customers, but twenty actors.","He Huanhuan and Han Mo had been assigned the same role—also a sweet young couple preparing to get married.","The two of them had deliberately worn the same proper outfits they'd had on the day they went missing. He Huanhuan sweetly hooked her arm through Han Mo's and carefully examined the model display.","She squinted and smiled. \"Honey, we absolutely have to get a house today! I want to marry you beautifully~\"","Han Mo: \"Mm.\"","He Huanhuan secretly pinched him and whispered in his ear, \"Get into character!\"","Han Mo frowned. \"This is a little awkward.\"","Just then, the customer couple walked up beside them and started looking at the same small unit on the model display.","A salesperson rushed over and introduced it. \"This small unit is specially designed for young couples... This is the last one remaining in the entire complex...\"","\"Oh! The last one?\"","He Huanhuan covered her mouth dramatically. \"Then we'll take it!\"","The female customer frowned in displeasure and shot He Huanhuan a look. \"We're looking at it right now!\"","He Huanhuan pouted. \"We're looking at it too! But you didn't say you wanted it. I said it first.\"","The female customer gave her a once-over. \"You're saying you want it without even looking at it?\"","Could she be a plant?","He Huanhuan immediately leaned into Han Mo and acted coquettish. \"My husband's rich! Anything I fancy, he'll buy for me~ Right, honey?\"","She blinked up at Han Mo, who was dying inside. He couldn't bring himself to say the word \"right.\"","He Huanhuan pinched him. \"Honey? Honey? Say something!\"","Just as the act was about to fall apart, the old man standing behind them quickly chimed in. \"Oh, I think this unit suits retirement living quite well!\"","The old man shoved He Huanhuan aside and smiled at the salesperson. \"Does this layout have any mid-floor options? I'm looking to buy for retirement. I don't like high floors.\"","The salesperson immediately nodded. \"There's one left—it's on the sixth floor, right in the middle.\"","The old man nodded approvingly. \"Six for good luck. Very nice. Why don't you show me the model room?\"","\"Sure!\"","The salesperson immediately agreed, and the young couple grew anxious: \"We saw it first!\"","He Huanhuan was even more frantic: \"We saw it first!\"","The girlfriend gave her a dismissive look: \"You should sort things out with your husband before you say that! I can tell he's not really interested in buying it for you!\""]},{"number":67,"title":"Chapter 67: How Dare You Insult My Sister You're Asking for Death","paragraphs":["He Huanhuan glared at her: \"You're talking nonsense! My husband loves me so much!\"","She reached her hand behind her back and gave Han Mo a three-sixty-degree vicious pinch, one that nearly made Han Mo collapse. He instantly transformed into a big-spending tycoon: \"Anything my wife wants, we'll take it all.\"","He was wearing the same outfit from the car accident today, carefully ironed before he left the house that morning.","The deep gray bespoke suit made him stand tall and look extraordinary.","The effect of saying this in that outfit was far more convincing than yesterday's school uniform.","The girlfriend over there immediately grew anxious: \"We saw this first! It's just a small unit—why are you competing with us for it?\"","Han Mo's lips curled slightly: \"She likes it. I have to give it to her.\"","\"You!\"","The girlfriend's eyes reddened from anger, and her boyfriend curled his lip smugly: \"What's this 'she likes it, he buys it'? Buying it for his mistress, right? They don't even look like a proper married couple!\"","\"What nonsense are you spewing?!\"","Before He Huanhuan could respond, the girlfriend got angry first.","The girl's eyes reddened: \"Why are you slandering them?\"","Her boyfriend pointed at He Huanhuan: \"Look at the way she looks! All seductive and cheap—clearly not a decent woman. This guy here is obviously keeping a mistress!\"","Half jealous, half envious, he shot Han Mo a glance: \"Keeping a mistress and not even willing to buy her a big house—clearly a poser!\"","If he had the money for a mistress, why not buy the mistress a big house?","Why compete with them over a small unit?","But his girlfriend was even angrier: \"Are you insane? We're here to buy a house, and you're making up lies about people?!\"","The man didn't think anything was wrong with what he said, completely self-righteous: \"How am I lying? She looks like a mistress...\"","\"Shut up!\"","The girl's eyes were now wet: \"Just because she's pretty, she's a mistress? Why are you talking so nastily today? You weren't like this before!\"","They had met through a matchmaking setup and had been together for less than two months.","That's how matchmaking worked—as long as neither party found the other repulsive, both sets of parents would push you forward.","First they'd push for an engagement, then after the engagement, they'd push for marriage. They wouldn't leave you any time to really get to know each other.","They'd met the month before last, and last month they were already pushed into getting engaged.","She felt it was too fast, but her parents said they were both from well-known, reliable families, so there was no problem.","These past two days, Chen Feng's family had been pushing her to go look at houses together, which made her parents even happier.","They said, \"He's already planning to buy a house for you—isn't that proof enough that he values you?\"","She was twenty-nine this year, already feeling somewhat anxious.","After these two months with Chen Feng, things had felt decent.","Their conversations weren't much, but when they went out on dates, he'd buy her flowers and actively pick up the tab.","She thought he was at least a decent man. Yes, all she wanted was for her future husband to be a decent person.","But she never expected that he would casually slander a girl like that.","That was truly despicable!","With red eyes, she said to Chen Feng: \"You need to apologize to her.\"","He Huanhuan awkwardly stepped back. Damn it—this deal looked like it was about to fall through...","She snuck a glance at her team leader, whose face was dark as coal.","But this wasn't her fault, was it?","Who told that man to have such a foul mouth?","A pretty woman is automatically a mistress? Then what's a handsome man? A gigolo?","With so many people staring at him, Chen Feng felt embarrassed. He scolded her impatiently: \"What are you crying about? I didn't say you were a mistress. Ruan Yuanyuan, can you stop throwing a tantrum?\"","\"I'm throwing a tantrum?\"","Ruan Yuanyuan laughed bitterly at him: \"How am I throwing a tantrum? You're the one who started slandering people out of nowhere. It's your fault, and you should apologize to her!\"","Chen Feng completely snapped. The two months of faking it had been driving him crazy anyway—he'd been out of patience for ages!","\"The hell I'll apologize! Can you get it through your head? They're competing with us for a house! They're our rivals. What are you doing preaching morals at a time like this?\"","Ruan Yuanyuan stared at him in disbelief. In the two months they'd been together, he had never once cursed.","He'd even talked to her about the struggles women face, saying how hard life was for them...","She'd actually thought he was different.","She couldn't help but step back: \"I'm not buying it. I'm not buying this house. And I'm not marrying you. We're done here.\"","She turned to leave, but Chen Feng grabbed her arm: \"Are you crazy?! My parents already told all our relatives we're getting married! You can't just call it off! What did I do? I didn't cheat!\"","\"Let go, let me go...\"","Ruan Yuanyuan struggled, trying to break free, but she couldn't.","\"Let her go!\"","He Huanhuan charged forward and kicked Chen Feng away, pulling Ruan Yuanyuan behind her: \"She told you to let go—didn't you hear?\"","Chen Feng scrambled up furiously and lunged at He Huanhuan: \"You sneaky mistress! You dare hit me?!\"","He swung his arm toward her, his palm carrying a vicious force.","The slap flew toward He Huanhuan's face but was caught mid-air by a large hand with distinct knuckles.","Han Mo's face darkened to the extreme, his eyes fixed on Chen Feng: \"You dare hit someone?\"","\"She hit me first!\"","Chen Feng struggled like a wild man, but Han Mo looked lean yet was startlingly strong.","He pinned Chen Feng firmly in place, completely unable to break free!","Frantic, Chen Feng spat: \"What? Got your eye on Ruan Yuanyuan? What kind of taste is that? She's not even pretty!\"","Ruan Yuanyuan's tears fell uncontrollably: \"Chen Feng! Shut up!\"","This was so humiliating. She'd spent two months with someone like this, nearly married him.","So humiliating!","He Huanhuan squeezed her hand tightly: \"Sister, don't be upset. You're beautiful.\"","Then, after a pause, she added: \"Just the hair is a bit plain. When we're done here, I'll give you a tube of hair dye.\"","\"Huh?\"","Ruan Yuanyuan's tears were still at the corners of her eyes, but that one sentence made them stop instantly.","She glanced at He Huanhuan's rainbow-colored hair and shook her head: \"Maybe not, thanks?\"","She thought black hair was quite pretty.","Seeing the two of them chatting like that, Chen Feng grew even more furious: \"Ruan Yuanyuan! Get over here now!\"","\"Don't go.\"","He Huanhuan held her back: \"This guy's bad news. Don't stick with him.\"","Han Mo nodded: \"He's got violent tendencies. Not a good fit.\"","Ruan Yuanyuan sniffled and looked at Chen Feng: \"Chen Feng, I'll tell my parents exactly what happened today. This is the end for us.\"","\"In your dreams!\"","Chen Feng cursed viciously: \"You gold digger! You've spent all this money of mine and now you want to break up?! If you don't marry me, I'll come make a scene at your house!\"","Ruan Yuanyuan looked at him in disbelief: \"When did I ever spend your money?\"","In two months they'd gone on about eight or nine dates. She'd paid three times, and Chen Feng had paid five or six.","Chen Feng had bought her a gold necklace, and she'd bought him a new phone.","All told, they'd spent about the same amount.","When did she ever spend his money?","How was she a gold digger?","Chen Feng pointed at her neck: \"I bought you that gold necklace!\"","Ruan Yuanyuan shot back furiously: \"And I bought you that phone! The phone cost more than the necklace!\"","Chen Feng wouldn't acknowledge it. He just kept at her, cursing: \"Gold digger!\"","\"You—!\"","Ruan Yuanyuan was beside herself with rage, wanting nothing more than to rip the necklace off and throw it back at him!","At this moment, at the entrance of the sales center, Qi Meili stumbled in, dazed and lightheaded, and immediately spotted the lively and vigorous He Huanhuan.","Tears streamed down uncontrollably—it really was Sister Huan!","Then she saw the ugly man standing across from He Huanhuan hurl an insult at her: \"Gold digger!\"","Damn!","How dare he curse her sister!","She charged over like the wind: \"You're asking for it!\"","\"Smack!\"","\"Ahh!\""]},{"number":68,"title":"Chapter 68: You Killed Her","paragraphs":["Before Chen Feng could even see what was happening, a heavy slap landed right across his face!","The force was so strong it brought tears to his eyes.","But the person didn't give him a single second to cry—she leapt right onto him and started whaling on him like crazy: \"How dare you talk trash about my girl? You looking to die?!\"","\"Who the hell are you?\"","SMACK!","\"Who's your girl?!\"","SMACK!","\"I wasn't—\"","SMACK!","Three slaps in, and Chen Feng's head was spinning, stars flashing before his eyes. He could barely stand.","\"Get off me!\"","He used every ounce of strength he had to shove her off his body.","Qi Meili had been working a twelve-hour shift, and her body was already at its limit. That burst of energy she'd just spent was pure adrenaline.","Once the adrenaline burned out, she couldn't hold herself up anymore either—she stumbled backward, about to topple over.","Chen Feng saw her stagger, a glint of viciousness flashing in his eyes, and kicked her square in the gut: \"Get lost!\"","Everything happened too fast. Nobody in the room had time to react.","THUD!","The heavy kick landed right on Qi Meili's stomach. Her eyes rolled back, and she crashed to the ground.","\"Meili?\"","\"MEILI!\"","He Huanhuan was stunned for a split second before she recognized who it was—Qi Meili had suddenly charged out of nowhere!","Before she could even say a word, Qi Meili had collapsed right in front of her.","She lunged forward and scooped Qi Meili into her arms: \"Meili? Meili?\"","There was no response from the person in her arms. She completely broke down: \"Han Mo! Beat him to a pulp!\"","Chen Feng blustered out of guilt: \"You wouldn't dare! Hitting someone is against the law!\"","THUD!","Han Mo slammed his fist into him without a moment's hesitation. Chen Feng's eye instantly turned a bruised purple: \"That's assault! I'm calling the cops!\"","Ruan Yuanyuan crouched beside He Huanhuan and angrily shouted at Chen Feng: \"You beat a girl up like this and you have the nerve to talk about calling the cops?\"","Chen Feng tried to scramble away: \"She hit me first!\"","He Huanhuan felt the body in her arms twitch slightly. She quickly leaned down and called out: \"Meili? You okay?\"","\"Snore... snore...\"","Two faint snores drifted into her ears. Qi Meili sniffled, found a comfy spot in He Huanhuan's arms, and went right back to snoozing.","???","He Huanhuan looked at Qi Meili, then at Chen Feng, who was now a bruised and battered mess courtesy of Han Mo.","She quietly reached up and covered Qi Meili's face, muffling those snores.","\"Meili! You died so tragically!\"","A theatrical wail suddenly boomed through the entire sales lobby. He Huanhuan's tears streamed down her face: \"Oh, my Meili! Beaten to death just like that! And what about your paralyzed dad and stroke-stricken mom? The whole family counts on you to bring in the money!\"","Ruan Yuanyuan's face went white when she heard that: \"Chen Feng! You killed her!\"","Panic surged through Chen Feng: \"Impossible! I only gave her one kick, and I didn't even put my back into it! No way!\"","That woman had jumped on top of him and pummeled him senseless. He'd barely put any force into that kick. How could it have killed her?","\"Oh, Meili! You died so wrongly! I'm calling the cops right now—\"","He Huanhuan wailed even harder, and Chen Feng's panic grew. He turned and bolted out of the lobby.","\"Chen Feng! Stop right there!\"","Ruan Yuanyuan started to chase after him, but He Huanhuan grabbed her arm: \"Let him run.\"","Ruan Yuanyuan was frantic: \"But he—\"","Before she could finish, a gigantic snore erupted from He Huanhuan's arms!","Qi Meili smacked her lips, shifted positions, and settled her head against He Huanhuan's shoulder, continuing to sleep.","......","Ruan Yuanyuan was baffled: \"Did she just... snore?\"","He Huanhuan smiled: \"Yep.\"","\"But—\"","He Huanhuan patted her arm: \"Just scaring that scumbag, that's all. Girl, you need to go home and call off that engagement.\"","\"Huh?\"","Ruan Yuanyuan was confused. What did that have to do with her?","He Huanhuan shot her a look: \"You still want to marry him?\"","Ruan Yuanyuan shook her head frantically: \"No way!\"","\"Then get home and tell your parents right now. Don't waste any time!\"","\"Oh... okay...\"","Ruan Yuanyuan got up in a daze and walked out of the sales lobby.","Even after she got into a taxi, she was still in a fog.","What a dramatic day today had been!","God! Could this be the universe trying to warn her?","She thought to herself: she had to seize this chance fate had given her. There was absolutely no way she was marrying Chen Feng.","What she didn't know was that Chen Feng had already fled back home.","He'd gone inside, packed a bag without saying a word, ignored his parents' questions, and hopped in his car and driven out of the province.","Not a peep from him again—not until Ruan Yuanyuan met her true match, got married, and had kids, let alone any news of him coming back.","But that's all beside the point. Back to the present.","In the sales lobby, once the drama was over, the hired extras collected their pay and headed out.","He Huanhuan hoisted Qi Meili onto her back. Han Mo tried to offer help, but she firmly refused: \"My girl, I carry her myself.\"","She had to keep her eyes on Qi Meili—what if the woman vanished the second she looked away?","She carried Qi Meili over to the sales team leader to ask for her pay. The leader's eyes bulged: \"You have the nerve to ask me for money? You ruined our sale today, and I haven't even settled the score with you! Now you want your pay?!\"","He Huanhuan didn't back down: \"That guy was scum. What does that have to do with me?\"","Even without her, they probably weren't buying today anyway.","Buying a house is a huge decision—people look at multiple developments, don't they? No way they'd lock in on the first one they see.","But the team leader insisted on blaming her anyway, huffing and puffing, telling her to get lost: \"Leave now, or I'm calling security! What kind of people are you? Turning our sales lobby into a circus!\"","Secretly, though, he was already planning which restaurant to treat himself to with that 200 yuan he was pocketing tonight.","Wang Qiang couldn't bear to watch. He timidly spoke up: \"Team leader, just give them the money. They really need it.\"","They still owed him 200 yuan, after all.","If the team leader refused to pay them, how were they going to pay him back?","\"Not paying, huh?\"","He Huanhuan didn't argue. She carefully set Qi Meili down, then let out a shriek and threw herself onto Qi Meili's body:","\"Everyone, come look! Yijing Gardens is ripping people off! My sister's lying in bed, paralyzed, waiting for money for treatment, and they're heartlessly cheating us!\"","Zero hesitation, pure performance on demand.","The team leader was instantly flustered: \"Hey! Don't talk nonsense! We didn't cheat you! And besides, she's just asleep—\"","But his voice was no match for a true professional. He Huanhuan had three years of experience wailing at funerals!","\"Oh, Meili! Our lives are so miserable! Cheated till we can't even survive, over a lousy 200 yuan!\"","\"Stop wailing! STOP! I'll give you the money! Here!\"","The team leader frantically shoved the 200 yuan at her and waved her away: \"Just go! Please, just leave!\"","He Huanhuan pocketed the cash in a second, flashed a grin, and gave him a mock salute: \"Thanks, boss!\""]},{"number":69,"title":"Chapter 69: Sisters Reunited","paragraphs":["After walking out of the sales center, He Huanhuan shoved two hundred yuan at Wang Qiang. \"Here, paying you back.\"","Wang Qiang felt embarrassed. \"You guys are struggling right now too. Why don't you wait until things ease up before paying me back?\"","He glanced at their clean, tidy clothes and couldn't help asking, \"Where did you two sleep last night? You didn't end up on the streets, did you?\"","He Huanhuan pointed at Liang Ye, who was curled up on the electric scooter. \"Don't worry, we found ourselves a temporary sucker.\"","She shoved the money directly into Wang Qiang's hands. \"Take it. You're not well-off either.\"","Wang Qiang blushed and accepted the money. Payday was still several days away, and he really was running low on cash...","He Huanhuan patted him on the shoulder. \"Hurry back to work. Your team leader is staring at you.\"","Wang Qiang turned around—sure enough! The team leader's tiny bean-like eyes were fixed dead on him.","No wait, fixed on the two hundred yuan in his hand.","He quickly stuffed the money into his pocket and walked back into the sales center.","The sales team leader watched him with burning eyes. \"How did that money end up in your hands?\"","That was supposed to be his meal.","Wang Qiang clenched his palm. \"They borrowed two hundred from me before. They just paid it back.\"","The team leader didn't buy it. \"Really?\"","What were the odds that they happened to owe him exactly two hundred?","Wang Qiang nodded firmly. \"Really. I got that two hundred from Brother Li in exchange. Ask him if you don't believe me.\"","The team leader waved his hand. \"Of course I believe you.\"","But inside, he couldn't help developing a grudge against Wang Qiang. Hmph, this snot-nosed kid had no sense!","He'd practically hinted at it, and the kid still hadn't offered the money to him.","If he still didn't close a deal next month, hmph...","Outside the hall, He Huanhuan hugged the sleeping Qi Meili, struggling to prop her onto the electric scooter.","She ordered Han Mo, \"You sit in the back and hold her up.\"","She and Han Mo sandwiched Qi Meili between them. Qi Meili's head lolled backward uncontrollably, and Han Mo had to constantly prop her up.","He couldn't help asking, \"Should we just take a taxi? This feels a bit dangerous.\"","He Huanhuan shot him a glance. \"Do you have money or do I?\"","Remembering the little money they had left, Han Mo silently reached out and held Qi Meili's head steady.","Liang Ye stared at the two electric scooters in front of him, worried. \"If you two leave, what am I supposed to do? I can't ride two scooters by myself.\"","He Huanhuan pointed at the sales office. \"Go inside and ask someone to help you.\"","Liang Ye hesitated. \"What if they don't want to?\"","He Huanhuan gunned the throttle, and the scooter zoomed off. \"If they won't, then beg them!\"","\"What if they still won't after I beg?\"","\"Then die!\"","\"That doesn't seem right...\"","...","Liang Ye looked at the scooter, then at the sales office. Everyone silently averted their gaze.","He thought it over, then flopped to the ground in desperation. \"If nobody helps me ride it back, I'm dead...\"","\"I'm dead...\"","\"I'm dead...\"","\"Snore...\"","Three hours later, a colleague at the village committee checked his phone. \"It's this late already. Why hasn't Xiao Liang come back yet?\"","In the old neighborhood, He Huanhuan rested her chin on both hands, staring intently at the sleeping figure on the bed.","\"How did Meili get here?\" she wondered.","Han Mo crouched beside her, also staring. \"Who is she exactly?\"","He Huanhuan reached out and touched the tattoo on Qi Meili's arm. \"See this tattoo? Buy one get one free—we got them together.\"","Han Mo nodded. \"I see it.\"","He remembered clearly—He Huanhuan had told him about her arm tattoo before. A blue Doraemon and a yellow SpongeBob.","Exactly the same as the ones on Qi Meili's arm. He'd noticed it right away.","It was way too noticeable.","He glanced at He Huanhuan. \"She's your friend?\"","He Huanhuan nodded. \"My best friend. She's the one who got me into dyeing my hair and getting tattoos.\"","Han Mo was speechless. \"...She never got you into anything else?\"","He Huanhuan thought for a moment. \"She told me to date. I wasn't really into it, so I didn't.\"","Han Mo's expression shifted slightly. \"...Good thing you didn't.\"","He Huanhuan added, \"She also taught me how to curse.\"","Han Mo asked, \"You didn't learn that either?\"","He Huanhuan smiled mysteriously. \"Oh, I learned that really well. I surpassed my teacher—Meili can't even out-cuss me now.\"","Han Mo was at a loss for words. \"...Alright then.\"","The two of them sat quietly by the bed, watching Qi Meili sleep, until they too drifted off, slumped over the bedside.","Time passed quietly. Outside, the sky gradually darkened. The person on the bed slowly opened her eyes.","Qi Meili smacked her lips. \"Mm... I had such a good dream.\"","She dreamed of Huanhuan—the lively, energetic Huanhuan.","How wonderful.","She rubbed her eyes and got up, ready to go to work.","As her hand touched the edge of the bed, she felt a hand with well-defined knuckles.","Startled, she looked over—a strikingly handsome face with sharp features was resting by the bedside.","She was stunned, and without hesitation reached out: \"SLAP!\"","Han Mo jolted upright, staring at her in confusion.","Qi Meili asked him, \"Does your face hurt?\"","Han Mo nodded. \"A little.\"","Qi Meili was shocked. \"Holy shit! A wild gorgeous guy!\"","Qi Meili swore this was the handsomest man she'd seen in the past two years!","She immediately asked, \"Hey handsome, got a girlfriend? Wanna give us a try?\"","Han Mo didn't say anything, but silently scooted backward.","As he sat up straight, Qi Meili suddenly noticed a lump of a person sleeping across his lap.","That person was curled up in a ball, face turned toward her direction.","\"HE HUANHUAN!!\"","He Huanhuan frowned. \"Who's that? Don't be so loud...\"","Qi Meili grabbed her and hauled her up. \"Oh my god! Sister Huan! Yesterday when I went to the hospital, you were still a vegetable! When did you wake up?\"","She had a loud voice, and her string of shouts startled He Huanhuan fully awake.","He Huanhuan groggily opened her eyes, meeting Qi Meili's gaze.","\"Meili!\"","\"Huanhuan!\"","The two let out a cry and hugged each other, wailing.","He Huanhuan's tears came pouring down. \"Meili, I missed you so much!\"","Qi Meili cried even harder. \"Huanhuan! I've been working so hard!\"","He Huanhuan nodded frantically. \"I saw that! I even wanted to tell you to quit—I wasn't in that body anymore, wuwuwu... But you couldn't hear me...\"","Qi Meili sobbed. \"Silly child, what are you even saying? I didn't understand a word, wuwuwu...\"","He Huanhuan peeled her off and rolled up her smooth arm for her to see. \"Meili, don't you notice anything different about me?\"","Qi Meili frowned in disgust. \"Yeah, I noticed. You romantic fool! You covered up your sister's tattoo for a man. I'm ashamed of you.\"","He Huanhuan: \"...My tattoos are gone!\"","She grabbed Qi Meili's hand and rubbed it frantically over her own arm. Nothing came off.","Qi Meili marveled. \"Where did you get your tattoos removed? That's incredible!\"","...Seriously, people really should read more books."]},{"number":70,"title":"Chapter 70: We Crossed Over","paragraphs":["\"Beautiful, it's like this...\"","He Huanhuan then gave a rough rundown of her transmigration into the novel: \"I don't know why you're here, but this isn't the world we were in...\"","Before she could finish, Qi Meili reached out and touched her head. \"You don't have a fever, so why are you talking nonsense?\"","He Huanhuan: ...She'd said it before—Meili was an idiot!","\"It's transmigration! Transmigration!\"","He Huanhuan was speechless: \"Then how else do you explain that yesterday I was lying in a hospital bed as a vegetable, and today I'm alive and kicking, squatting here talking to you!\"","Qi Meili stared back with her big innocent eyes: \"So what? Vegetables can't wake up? Haven't you ever watched TV?\"","...","He Huanhuan's head was about to explode. Why couldn't she get through to her?","Han Mo sat to the side, a slight smile tugging at his lips. Finally, someone who could give her a taste of her own medicine.","It had been a long time coming.","He Huanhuan snatched her phone, entered the password to unlock it, and searched up the news coverage from when the Gu family had first found her.","\"Look, is this me or not? Now check the date on this news. And think about when I got my head cracked open.\"","\"Wait, hold on... give me a second to think...\"","Qi Meili stared at the date on the news, her brain struggling to catch up.","The article had a photo with six people in it.","She didn't recognize the other five, but the He Huanhuan on the side was way too familiar.","\"This is you?\"","He Huanhuan nodded: \"That's me!\"","Qi Meili's appreciative gaze couldn't help but drift toward the two handsome guys in the photo: \"Who are these two hunks? They got girlfriends or what?\"","This woman's inability to focus on the main point—she really hadn't changed one bit!","He Huanhuan wanted to jump up and punch her: \"Focus! Say the important stuff first!\"","\"Oh oh oh, right! Focus!\"","Qi Meili tried to yank her thoughts back, but she couldn't. With two gorgeous men right in front of her, it was impossible!","She shoved the phone away. Out of sight, out of mind.","She and He Huanhuan had never left their small county town their whole lives, and there was no way their little county had any rich and powerful families like this.","\"So, we really did transmigrate?\"","She still found it absurd: \"But how come our transmigration methods are different?\"","He Huanhuan's soul had entered the body of the real heiress, which at least made some sense—that's how TV dramas did it.","But she just rode her e-bike home. How did riding a bike get her here?","He Huanhuan shook her head: \"I don't know. If I could figure it out, I'd go be a scientist.\"","Qi Meili agreed: \"Yeah, that gig's not easy.\"","She had no lingering attachments back in the modern world, so she accepted it pretty quickly.","Chin propped on her hand as she sat on the bed, her gaze suddenly landed on Han Mo, who had been quietly listening by the bedside.","She let out a shriek: \"Damn! When did you get here? How dare you eavesdrop on our conversation!\"","Han Mo: \"...I've been here the whole time. You talked to me first when you woke up.\"","\"Then you still can't listen to top-secret stuff like this!\"","Qi Meili took one look at his handsome face and decided to make a concession: \"Tell you what, if you don't have a girlfriend, I could lower my standards and be with you for a few days.\"","...","He Huanhuan tugged at Qi Meili: \"Meili, he's mine.\"","\"Yours?\"","Qi Meili frowned in displeasure: \"Since when did you start dating people? When did you pick up such bad habits?\"","She gave Han Mo a once-over, her eyes instantly filling with disdain: \"Did you seduce my Huanhuan?\"","Han Mo wanted to deny it, but He Huanhuan was staring at him with burning intensity. He really couldn't deny it.","It was true—he'd been the one making moves on her all along...","He gave a slight nod: \"You could say that.\"","\"Could say that? I'll strangle you!\"","Qi Meili lunged at him, reaching for his neck: \"My Huanhuan is a pure, innocent jasmine flower! You ugly freak, stay away from her!\"","Han Mo sidestepped to dodge: \"You just called me handsome a second ago. How am I an ugly freak now?\"","He Huanhuan quickly grabbed her: \"Meili, calm down, calm down...\"","Qi Meili shot Han Mo a furious glare: \"Your face is barely passable. Someone like you is about my level, but going after my Huanhuan? That's just shameless.\"","Han Mo found it almost funny: \"You really love Huanhuan, huh.\"","\"Damn right!\"","Qi Meili said triumphantly: \"We're the best sisters in the whole wide world!\"","She cupped He Huanhuan's face and lectured her seriously: \"Handsome men are fun to play with for a couple days, but don't ever get invested, got it?\"","He Huanhuan nodded eagerly: \"I won't play, and I won't get invested.\"","Han Mo: ...A girlfriend's best friend really is the most terrifying thing in existence.","Oh wait, he wasn't even the boyfriend yet. He was just some guy who was neither played with nor invested in.","Seeing the two of them diving back into their chatter, Han Mo couldn't help but interrupt: \"You guys hungry? How about we order some takeout?\"","It was already dark, and they hadn't even had dinner yet.","Not to mention Qi Meili—she hadn't had a single grain of rice since last night.","She was past the point of hunger.","The moment he asked, their stomachs started growling like crazy.","Both of them nodded in unison: \"Hungry! Let's eat!\"","\"Alright, then—\"","Han Mo suddenly stopped mid-sentence: \"Where's Liang Ye? Why isn't he back yet?\"","The village committee didn't do overtime. He should've been home ages ago. Why wasn't he here?","Liang Ye was lying on the ground at the corner of the sales office's outer wall, sleeping like a baby.","Wang Qiang crouched beside him, shaking him frantically: \"Hey, stop sleeping! Wake up! We're off work now! I can take your e-bike back for you! Wake up!\"","But he was out cold—nothing was waking him up.","Poor colleague. Wang Qiang had waited until the end of the workday, and Liang Ye never showed up.","He'd called over ten times, no answer. With no other option, the colleague hitched a ride home with someone else.","No wonder this guy had been seconded to the village committee. Clearly, he'd been squeezed out of his original position for being useless!","Wang Qiang crouched beside him for over half an hour. When he couldn't wake him no matter what, he gave up.","He couldn't get in touch with He Huanhuan and the others either, so he found a poster to cover Liang Ye with, then rode off home on his bike.","Meanwhile, He Huanhuan and the others waited at home for a while longer, but still no sign of him.","So the three of them rode out on their e-bikes to look for him. They went to the village committee first—naturally, no one there.","Feeling uneasy, they went to the sales office as well. The entrance was completely empty—nobody.","Wang Qiang was a thoughtful kid. Worried that the e-bike might get stolen if left by the door, he'd specially dragged it into a shed in the corner.","And Liang Ye was skinny. Huddled under that poster, he was completely unnoticeable.","None of the three spotted him.","He Huanhuan was puzzled: \"Where could a grown man have gone?\"","Han Mo guessed: \"Maybe he went home?\"","He Huanhuan nodded: \"Could be. And this guy—he could've at least told us if he was going home!\"","Han Mo: \"Maybe his family called him back suddenly, and he couldn't get in touch with us either.\"","Qi Meili urged them from the bike: \"Then let's just go back! He's not a kid. Ugly as he is, he's not going to be in danger!\"","The e-bike whizzed off. The next second, a thunderous snore echoed from under the poster.","Liang Ye sat up groggily: \"Where is this?\"","A moment later, a wail erupted out of nowhere: \"Wait... where's my bike???\""]},{"number":71,"title":"Chapter 71: Damn, Liang Ye, you're this handsome","paragraphs":["On the way home, He Huanhuan suggested, \"Liang Ye isn't home, so we can't order takeout. Let's find a place to eat out before heading back.\"","Qi Meili was puzzled. \"Why can't you order takeout?\"","He Huanhuan sighed. \"My phone doesn't work.\"","\"Why?\"","He Huanhuan then gave her a brief rundown of what had happened over the past few days, which made Qi Meili frown deeply. \"He Huanhuan, are you stupid? Why would you give up a good life to go wandering around with some random guy?\"","He Huanhuan felt a twinge of guilt. \"I'm not wandering. We do have a place to stay.\"","\"Could it be as nice as a big villa?\"","Qi Meili was this close to pulling over and flicking her on the forehead. \"Back when I told you to date, you acted like it would kill you! You never listened!\"","\"And now you've gone and gotten all tangled up with some old guy! What a mess!\"","The \"old guy\" in question, Han Mo, tried to explain. \"It'll all be fine in a couple of days. It won't take too long.\"","Qi Meili shot him a glare. \"You say it's fine and it's fine? Who made you God? You think everything goes your way? If you're so great, why are you two still stuck here?\"","Good question.","He Huanhuan subtly poked Qi Meili. \"Meili, he's actually been through a lot.\"","And then, right in front of Han Mo, she started telling Qi Meili about all the terrible things that had happened in his family.","\"...Think about it—his mother was literally infuriated to death. Can you imagine how devastated he was back then? Let's not give him a hard time, okay?\"","These were things Han Mo hadn't heard mentioned in years.","Of course, no ordinary person would ever walk up to him and say, \"Hey, your dad drove your mom to an early grave, right? And your brother's a bastard your dad had during the marriage? Man, your life is tragic...\"","Who in their right mind would say something like that?","Oh, right. The two women in front of him would.","Qi Meili was stunned. \"His dad is that much of a monster?\"","He Huanhuan nodded. \"A real villain! And his brother is disgusting too—he even tried to get fresh with me!\"","\"No way! You didn't beat him to a pulp?\"","\"I did hit him, but now he's hooking up with that fake heiress from the Gu family.\"","\"What the hell! She's got some messed-up taste!\"","The car stopped in front of a beef noodle shop. Qi Meili got out, glanced at Han Mo, and said, \"Dude, you've had it rough.\"","Han Mo nodded. \"It's okay.\"","Qi Meili agreed. \"Yeah, it could be worse. At least you've got money. Me and Huanhuan are pretty unlucky too, but we're broke on top of that.\"","Han Mo tentatively offered, \"Once this is all over, I could send you some money?\"","Qi Meili's eyes lit up. \"Send a lot! Otherwise, I won't approve of you two!\"","Han Mo smiled and nodded. \"Deal.\"","Watching the two of them walking hand in hand into the noodle shop, a smile tugged at Han Mo's lips.","They were pretty similar in personality. That was good—they'd get along well.","He Huanhuan wouldn't be bored from now on.","Inside, they ordered three bowls of beef noodles. Suddenly, He Huanhuan thought of something. \"Meili, do you think your phone can pay for this here?\"","That was a phone from their world. Would it even work here?","Qi Meili immediately perked up, eager to try. \"Let me test it.\"","Thirty-six yuan transferred instantly. He Huanhuan was ecstatic. \"It works! Quick, let me see how much money you have!\"","She opened the balance: five thousand seven hundred and eighty-something.","He Huanhuan was shocked. \"Whoa! Meili, you're loaded!\"","At this rate, who needed to run around for takeout? They could just lie back and wait for time to pass!","But Qi Meili seriously put her phone away. \"No, I can't spend this money recklessly. What if I suddenly get sent back in a couple of days? And you're still lying in the hospital. This money needs to go toward your hospital bills.\"","Five thousand sounded like a lot, but He Huanhuan's hospital fees were nearly four thousand a month.","That four thousand was absolutely off-limits.","He Huanhuan looked at Qi Meili with teary eyes. \"Meili... why are you so good to me? From now on, I'll do whatever you say~\"","Qi Meili smiled. \"Then stop hanging out with Han Mo.\"","Han Mo, who'd been silent but was now getting stabbed out of nowhere: ...He'd figured it out. The heavens had sent Qi Meili here on purpose.","Just to mess with him.","He turned to Qi Meili. \"Actually, I—\"","Qi Meili glared at him. \"Shut up.\"","Han Mo: \"...Fine.\"","He Huanhuan hesitated. \"Meili, actually I—\"","Qi Meili glared at her too. \"You be quiet too.\"","He Huanhuan: \"...Okay.\"","The bowl of noodles was eaten in near-perfect silence, the three of them each lost in their own thoughts.","Han Mo was calculating. Han Xuan should already be past the point of no return by now. Maybe it was time to go see Chen Yu.","He Huanhuan, meanwhile, was racking her brain: Why did Meili's phone work here?","Could she get her own body back?","Actually, she didn't really want to be the Gu family's daughter. Sure, they had money, but it never felt comfortable.","Qi Meili was wolfing down her food, screaming internally: Oh my god! This is amazing! Eating with your bestie is the best feeling ever!","The three of them were each lost in their own world, not one of them sparing a thought for Liang Ye.","Out on the village road, Liang Ye was using his phone's flashlight to stumble home in the dark.","After walking for over ten minutes, he was exhausted.","He gritted his teeth and decided to hail a cab. But when he opened his phone, the late-night surcharge brought the fare up to over seventy yuan.","He couldn't bear to part with that money!","But he really couldn't walk any further. It was pitch black all around, and fear was creeping in.","Finally, he couldn't take it anymore and called his brother. \"Bro, can you send a car to pick me up? I'm scared, wahhh...\"","Liang Zheng was already asleep when he suddenly got a call from his little brother. The moment he picked up, sobbing came through the line: \"...My e-bike is gone, I can't find it anywhere, and I tried to walk home, but it's so dark and there's no one around...\"","His brother quickly sat up. \"Call a cab right now and come home.\"","Liang Ye sniffled. \"The late-night surcharge, it's over seventy bucks. I can't bear it, wahhh...\"","His brother frowned. \"Where are you right now?\"","Liang Ye sobbed. \"I'm in the village...\"","\"Why the hell are you there?\"","His brother had no idea Liang Ye had been temporarily reassigned. He thought his brother was still working at the neighborhood committee near his apartment.","\"I got sent here for a temporary assignment...\"","His brother pulled out his phone and searched for Liang Ye's location. Sure enough—it was as remote as remote gets.","No wonder he couldn't bring himself to pay for a cab.","\"I'll book one for you... Actually, forget it, I'll just drive over and get you myself.\"","That way his brother wouldn't have to fret about the money.","He quickly got up, headed downstairs, and got in the car. When he finally found Liang Ye, the guy had dozed off squatting on the ground...","He patted him. \"Xiao Ye, I'm here. Let's go home.\"","\"Zzz...\"","His only response was a long, drawn-out snore.","Liang Zheng let out a helpless chuckle. How could anyone fall asleep squatting by the roadside?","He heaved Liang Ye into the car, originally planning to take him back to the family home.","But then he thought about the morning—when Liang Ye would wake up and start picking everything apart: Why do we have to live this far out in the sticks? It burns so much gas just getting anywhere!","And bro, you never eat anything—can you tell the kitchen not to make so much food?","Wasteful! Wasteful! You guys are so wasteful!","So he pointed the car straight back toward the city instead. Better to drop him off at his little apartment.","The car pulled up to the building, and his brother carried Liang Ye upstairs.","He'd just slid the key into the lock when the door swung open on its own, revealing a shock of flashy red hair. \"Holy crap! Half a day without seeing you, and you got this handsome all of a sudden, Liang Ye?\""]},{"number":72,"title":"Chapter 72: Hey Bro, Do You Have a Significant Other","paragraphs":["Liang Zheng hesitated for a second. \"Who are you?\"","His little brother had that kind of charm, enough to invite a girl over to the house?","He glanced at the night outside. And she'd stayed this late?","Qi Meili gave a shy smile. \"Didn't you bump into me at noon? How come you don't recognize me after just one afternoon~\"","\"Bump into?\"","Liang Zheng shifted to the side, showing Liang Ye's face to Qi Meili. \"Are you talking about my brother running into you?\"","\"Whoa! You're not Liang Ye!\"","Only then did Qi Meili catch on. She shoved Liang Ye's face aside. \"God! Don't scare me with that ugly face at night!\"","She blinked and stared at Liang Zheng. \"So, handsome, who are you?\"","Liang Zheng frowned. \"I'm his older brother.\"","\"Oh~ big brother~ No wonder you're so hot! I just love... ah!\"","She was mid-flirt when she suddenly let out a scream and slammed the door shut!","\"Shit shit shit!\"","She crouched down and stuffed the extra shoes into the shoe cabinet, then dashed over to the two people chatting in the room, grabbing them and pushing them toward the bathroom.","\"Get in there! Liang Zheng's big brother is here! You two aren't supposed to be sneaking off together, right? Hide!\"","Han Mo tried to explain: \"It's not eloping, I—\"","\"Shut up!\"","Qi Meili slammed the bathroom door shut, dusted off her hands with a look of disgust, \"Old geezers are so long-winded.\"","Then, smiling sweetly, she opened the front door again. Liang Zheng stood there looking baffled. \"May I come in now?\"","His brother was pretty heavy, too.","Once Liang Ye was on the bed, Liang Zheng just stood up. Qi Meili shot out a hand like lightning and pressed it straight onto Liang Zheng's back. \"Brother~ you tired~?\"","Liang Zheng immediately backed away. \"Miss, what are you doing?\"","Qi Meili squinted with a grin. \"I was worried you might be exhausted. Just giving you a steadying hand.\"","God, such a slim waist. Firm to the touch, too. Heh heh heh...","Liang Zheng's brows knitted tightly. Where did Xiao Ye meet this girl? She doesn't exactly seem like a proper person?","He eyed her warily, then turned and headed for the bathroom.","\"Whoa!\"","Qi Meili zipped over and blocked the bathroom door. \"No!\"","Liang Zheng frowned even deeper. \"I just want to wash my hands. Is that not allowed?\"","Qi Meili: \"Wash them in the kitchen.\"","Liang Zheng's gaze slid toward the bathroom. \"Why not in there?\"","Qi Meili bit her lip and blinked. \"I've got my underwear drying in there. I was afraid you'd see it and fall in love with me.\"",".....","Liang Zheng turned around without hesitation. \"I'm leaving now.\"","He even considered taking Liang Ye with him, but then he remembered Qi Meili's assessment of Liang Ye's looks and felt reassured.","At the door, he paused, then turned back. \"You said my brother bumped into you. What happened?\"","Qi Meili just wanted him gone, so she said quickly: \"At noon I got off work, and he hit me with his electric scooter.\"","\"So you came home with him because of that?\"","Liang Zheng's mind immediately conjured an image: the girl asking Xiao Ye for compensation, Xiao Ye being too cheap to pay, and the girl camping out at the house demanding her money.","Qi Meili nodded. \"Yeah, yeah, that's it. You can go now.\"","Liang Zheng thought for a moment, pulled out his phone. \"Give me your payment code. I'll pay you back for him.\"","Qi Meili's eyes lit up. Wait, this is a thing?","People really are more generous when they're good-looking.","She whipped out her phone and showed him her payment QR code.","Her phone buzzed. Qi Meili glanced at the notification and nearly keeled over. \"No no no, I'm feeling dizzy...\"","Liang Zheng hurriedly reached out to steady her. \"What's wrong? Did Xiao Ye's accident do this to you?\"","It was the money knocking her out!","Fifty thousand!","He'd just transferred her fifty thousand without a second thought!","Dear God, she'd have to work a whole year to make that much.","That's a full year of Sister Huan's hospital bills covered!","She could take a whole year off work!","She went limp against Liang Zheng's shoulder. Bliss. Pure bliss.","Money AND a hot guy she could cop a feel on.","Her smile just wouldn't come down. \"Handsome, you got a girlfriend?\"","Liang Zheng nodded. \"Yes, I do.\"","\"Shit! Why didn't you say so!\"","Qi Meili straightened up in a second, body stiff as a board. \"I'm fine. You go, go, goodbye!\"","A smile tugged at Liang Zheng's lips. \"Alright. See you.\"","Downstairs, back in his car, he lit a cigarette and sat there.","He remembered Xiao Ye mentioning that the daughter the Gu family had found was quite unconventional.","Dyed flashy hair, saying rebellious things.","The image of that scarlet red hair flashed through his mind, along with her wandering hands.","He couldn't help but smile. Looks like Xiao Ye was doomed to be heartbroken.","A girl that vibrant wouldn't put up with Xiao Ye.","Upstairs in the bathroom, He Huanhuan whispered to Han Mo: \"Is Liang Ye's big brother impressive?\"","Han Mo nodded. \"Smart, decisive, very resourceful.\"","He Huanhuan pressed her eye to the crack in the door. \"And good-looking, too.\"","She heard Meili take advantage of the guy, so he had to be handsome.","Let her see. Two sons from the same mother, how different could they be?","The gap was too small. She squinted but still couldn't see anything outside.","\"What does he look—\"","Suddenly, a big hand reached out and blocked her view. \"He's just okay. Nothing to look at.\"","He Huanhuan turned her head to look at him. \"You jealous?\"","Han Mo's gaze flickered away. He pulled her back from the door. \"Don't let him find out.\"","He Huanhuan grinned with certainty. \"You're definitely jealous. Tsk tsk tsk...\"","The bathroom door was yanked open. Qi Meili stood at the entrance, staring at them. \"You two, why are you so close together?\"","He Huanhuan immediately tattled: \"Meili, I was just trying to peek at Liang Ye's brother, and he's jealous!\"","Han Mo: \"......\"","Qi Meili shot Han Mo a look. \"No sense of male virtue? Dismissed!\"","He Huanhuan giggled in agreement: \"Fine! But hey, is Liang Ye's brother actually hot?\"","Qi Meili sighed in regret. \"Hot my ass. He's taken.\"","Han Mo looked puzzled. \"I don't remember that. He was engaged a few years ago, but I recall it was called off the year before last.\"","\"What?\"","Qi Meili was full of remorse. \"Why didn't you say so earlier! If I'd known, I would've leaned on his arm a while longer! He's gorgeous!\"","This only made He Huanhuan more curious. \"How gorgeous, exactly?\"","\"Like Erlang Shen from the legends!\"","Specifically the scorching-hot version played by Jiao Enjun. Handsome, tough, athletic build...","He Huanhuan thought for a moment, then asked Han Mo: \"Between you and him, who do you think is better looking?\"","Han Mo sighed. \"How am I supposed to answer that?\"","He Huanhuan grinned slyly. \"Come on, be confident. You're a certified hottie too, Meili said so.\"","Han Mo thought seriously. \"We've never stood side by side to compare. Brother Zheng is a few years older, and he carries a certain commanding presence.\"","\"Mm... different strokes, I guess.\"","Qi Meili shot him a disdainful glare. \"Different strokes, my foot! He's way better looking than you!\"","She never certified anything. She was just groggy when she first saw Han Mo, her eyes playing tricks on her.","Yes, that was exactly it.","Nobody thinks their best friend's boyfriend is good-looking, anyway. She absolutely refuses to admit that the first time she laid eyes on Han Mo, she was blown away by his face."]},{"number":73,"title":"Chapter 73: The villain has always been only you.","paragraphs":["After washing up quickly, the three of them were about to go to sleep.","But the bed had been taken over by Liang Ye. Once that guy fell asleep, he was heavier than a stone slab.","Han Mo tried to move him onto the sofa, but almost got beaten to death by his flailing fists: \"Mm-hmm... Don't touch me! So annoying!\"","With no other choice, they let him sleep there.","The three of them sat down on the sofa bed, which wasn't very big. Han Mo got up and went into the room to grab an old mattress pad: \"You two take the bed. I'll just sleep on the floor.\"","\"Fine.\"","He Huanhuan was just about to lie down on the edge of the bed when Qi Meili shoved her aside with her butt: \"Why are you getting so close? Don't you know to keep some distance?\"","She stared at He Huanhuan with a very serious expression: \"How old are you this year?\"","He Huanhuan: \"Eighteen.\"","Qi Meili nodded: \"Kids aren't allowed to date, got it?\"","He Huanhuan couldn't help but fight back: \"But you're only twenty this year, and you were dating two years ago. And when you were seventeen, you—\"","Her mouth was instantly covered. Qi Meili refused to admit a thing: \"Nonsense! I've never dated anyone in my life!\"","She raised her SpongeBob-patterned arm and threatened Han Mo: \"Our Huanhuan has had a tough life before. She's not allowed to date until she's twenty, you hear me?\"","Han Mo wanted to say that logic didn't quite hold up, but when he met Qi Meili's serious gaze, he earnestly nodded: \"Twenty's fine, twenty-five's fine too. Whatever works.\"","Qi Meili curled her lip: \"Let's skip twenty-five. Don't want you breaking up later and people saying our Huanhuan wasted your time and turned you into an old geezer.\"","Han Mo: \"...I'm not that old.\"","Liang Zheng was two years older than him, anyway.","Qi Meili: \"Oh my god, dude! You're not old? You're already an old geezer!\"","That sounded familiar. He Huanhuan had said something like that before...","The Old Geezer silently lay down on the floor. Sleep, just sleep. Not sleeping well would only age him faster.","The three of them lay quietly. Qi Meili couldn't sleep, and she didn't want to either.","Today had been way too intense. She was afraid that if she woke up, she'd find it was all a dream.","He Huanhuan was still lying in the hospital, and she herself would have to go back to work at the factory.","\"Oh right, Huanhuan, guess what? Liang Zheng just paid me fifty thousand yuan in compensation.\"","She faced He Huanhuan and whispered: \"Fifty thousand. That's so much. We don't even have to work anymore.\"","He Huanhuan smiled and leaned in close to whisper back: \"There's a few hundred thousand in my phone, you know~\"","In a few days, she'd bring Meili back to the Gu family estate.","Show her what the rich life was like. Let her know what it felt like to have come to the right place.","Qi Meili's eyes were wide as saucers: \"Where did you get that much money? Did that cheap dad of yours give it to you?\"","That cheap dad was way better than her real dad. Her real dad had taken every last bit of her compensation money!","He Huanhuan shook her head: \"Part of it was from Han Mo, part of it was from my two cheap brothers.\"","As for Old Man Gu (her father), he hadn't even seemed to think about it.","But He Huanhuan didn't really care. After all, he wasn't her biological dad.","Whether Old Man Gu had some genuine feelings for her didn't matter much to her.","Qi Meili let out a soft sigh: \"That old geezer Han Mo isn't such a bad guy after all.\"","He Huanhuan nodded: \"Setting everything else aside, he's still pretty generous.\"","\"Those two brothers of yours are decent too.\"","He Huanhuan nodded again: \"The eldest brother is pretty cold and distant, and you rarely see him around. The second brother is a bit of an idiot, but he's not a bad person.\"","Qi Meili couldn't help but ask: \"And what about Han Mo and you going missing like this? Are your brothers even looking for you?\"","He Huanhuan shook her head: \"No idea. Probably not much? I haven't been back that long anyway. There's not that much of a bond yet.\"","Growing up, aside from her grandparents, she'd only ever felt love from Meili.","When it came to love, she didn't feel she deserved much of it.","Especially since she wasn't even the real daughter of the Gu family. She couldn't imagine those two brothers loving her all that much.","They'd been nice to her. Really, they had.","But they probably wouldn't worry about her that much, right?","Probably... right?","——","In the hotel parking garage, Gu Jinghan was sleeping in his car, completely miserable.","Ever since that fight with his dad, he hadn't gone back home.","He'd been staying at the hotel directly, staking out around the clock for Gu Chacha and Han Xuan.","He refused to believe he couldn't catch them!","\"Hey, hey, boss, boss, do you copy? Your sister and Second Young Master Han are back for another room!\"","The manager's voice crackled through the earpiece, and Gu Jinghan shot upright in his seat!","He didn't even bother wiping the sleep crust from his eyes. He immediately activated his wiretap equipment and hit record the second it was on.","This time, he was going to succeed for sure!","As usual, there were two minutes of foreplay sounds at the start. After that came over ten minutes of dead silence.","Gu Jinghan tapped the equipment in confusion. What's wrong? Did it break?","Or had Han Xuan knocked himself out from exhaustion?","Two minutes? That couldn't be it, right?","\"Chacha, I'm planning to sell the company. When that's done, come with me.\"","Han Xuan's voice suddenly cut through. Gu Jinghan straightened up and listened closely.","Gu Chacha let out a cold laugh: \"Come with you? Go where?\"","Han Xuan leaned against the bed, smoking a cigarette: \"How about New Zealand?\"","Gu Chacha nodded: \"Sure, that's nice. I'll come visit you when I get the chance.\"","\"You're not coming?\"","Gu Chacha stood in front of the mirror, reaching up to touch her face: \"Han Xuan, I'm only twenty. I'm still so young. My career is just taking off. How could I retire now?\"","Retire? That was something for people in their seventies or eighties.","She was still so young. Why on earth would she retire?","Her life, her career, was just getting started!","Han Xuan narrowed his eyes, barely containing the fury in them: \"You're trying to dump me?\"","\"How is that dumping you?\"","Gu Chacha gave a brilliant smile: \"I'll come to New Zealand to see you. When I do, remember to buy me some fresh milk, okay?\"","The anger could no longer be held back. Han Xuan shot up from the bed, charged over to her, and grabbed her face in his hand: \"Gu Chacha, you don't actually think you're some kind of real pianist, do you? You know exactly what's behind your concerts, don't you?\"","They'd laundered so much money out of the company. If they didn't leave now, they'd stay in the country and wait to get caught?","Gu Chacha's lips curled up slightly: \"Han Xuan, I'm not afraid.\"","She wasn't afraid?","Han Xuan's eyes narrowed dangerously as he tightened his grip: \"Have you been in contact with Brother Bao?\"","Gu Chacha's eyes flickered: \"What are you talking about? I don't understand.\"","\"You slept with him?\"","\"Han Xuan!\"","Gu Chacha frowned in displeasure: \"Watch your words. What do you take me for? I'm—\"","\"What are you? The eldest daughter of the Gu family, or a renowned pianist?\"","Han Xuan's lips twisted in sneering mockery: \"Gu Chacha, it's all fake. There's no Gu blood in your veins, and you don't have a pianist's calluses on your hands. You're just a fraud. How much longer do you think you can keep this up?\"","His fingers dug deep into her cheeks as he stared at her with contempt: \"You have no choice but to come with me. Don't forget — why did Han Mo get into that car crash? Who was it that tipped me off?\"","Gu Chacha struggled to open her phone. On the screen, a recording played: Han Xuan's furious voice — \"Han Mo! I want him dead! I swear I'll kill him! Where is he? I'm going to run him over!\"","Followed by Gu Chacha's timid voice: \"Han Xuan, calm down. Don't rush. Your father will let you back into the company... \"","\"I don't have time to wait! I want him dead NOW!\"","Gu Chacha carefully tried to persuade him: \"He just came to your place looking for your sister and didn’t find her. I can tell you’re not that fond of him anyway—maybe Dad won’t give the project to him...\"","\"He went to your house?\"","The recording came to an abrupt end, and Gu Chacha stared straight at Han Xuan:","\"Han Xuan, you heard it—I kept trying to talk you out of it. The bad guy was always only you.\""]},{"number":74,"title":"Chapter 74: Recording","paragraphs":["\"Gu Chacha!\"","His fingers pressed harder, pinching her cheek until it turned red. Han Xuan gritted his teeth as he stared at her: \"Do you really think you can shake me off? You think they can't trace you from the top? Your awards, the concert revenue—you think you can hide all that?\"","A gentle smile bloomed at the corner of her lips under his grip: \"That's my business. None of yours.\"","\"Fine, fine, fine...\"","Han Xuan shoved her away in fury: \"Then let's see! Just how far you, Gu Chacha, can go!\"","Gu Chacha staggered back several steps from the shove. She straightened her clothes and replied with a smile: \"When I go to New Zealand for my concert, I'll send you a ticket.\"","With that, she turned without hesitation. When she reached the door of the room, she paused slightly: \"Han Xuan, go to your New Zealand. Don't ever come back.\"","Han Xuan grew even more enraged. He grabbed the nearest pillow and hurled it at her with all his might: \"I don't need you to meddle in my business! Get lost!\"","The pillow cut through the air and slammed against the door!","The door closed behind her, and the sound of things smashing and crashing rang out from inside the room.","Gu Chacha listened to the noise, her gaze turning cold.","She had done everything she could. What happened next was up to fate.","Her phone vibrated twice. She answered: \"Hello.\"","A forceful, commanding voice came through the line: \"Come pick me up at the airport.\"","Gu Chacha nodded: \"Okay.\"","Just as she was about to hang up, she hesitated for a moment: \"Han Xuan, he...\"","\"Heh.\"","A contemptuous laugh came through the phone: \"What, someone that pathetic—you actually developed feelings for him?\"","Gu Chacha shook her head quickly, as if the person on the other end could see her: \"No, I just want to know—what's going to happen to him?\"","\"Don't worry, he won't die. Just telecom fraud. A few years in prison and he's out.\"","As for exactly how many years—that, she didn't need to know.","Gu Chacha nodded: \"I understand. I'll come pick you up now.\"","In the airport lounge, a dark-skinned man's eyes flashed with a hint of ruthlessness. He made a call.","\"The scapegoat is about to run. Tell them to make their move now.\"","After hanging up, he sprawled back in his chair with his legs spread, relaxed, waiting for Gu Chacha to come get him.","Outside the window, the roar of airplanes sounded. A group of people arrived here; another group left here.","Jiangcheng. A good place.","He glanced at his bank account—a string of cold zeros glittering on his phone screen.","From now on, he was Chen Jiarong, a Malaysian businessman.","Meanwhile, in the hotel's underground parking garage, Gu Jinghan was so excited he jumped up on the spot!","Then he smacked his head right into the car roof.","\"Ow, ow, ow...\"","That hurt!","\"Boss, who are you trying to bang?\"","The manager's gossipy, lecherous face suddenly appeared outside the car window, startling Gu Jinghan so badly he forgot all about the pain on his head!","He snapped irritably: \"What the hell is wrong with you?! I just hit my head!\"","God, where on earth had he even hired this weirdo from?","The manager plopped into the car: \"So? How's the equipment I bought? Did the recording save?\"","Gu Jinghan nodded eagerly: \"You're actually good at something! It recorded crystal clear!\"","He pressed play, and moaning sounds suddenly filled the car. The manager frowned: \"Boss, do we really have to be this awkward? Can you fast-forward a bit?\"","Gu Jinghan fumbled with the device: \"Give me a sec; I can't find the fast-forward button...\"","A minute later.","\"Found it!\"","The manager said flatly: \"It's already over.\"","......","Gu Jinghan gave an awkward laugh: \"What if I said I didn't mean to do that? Would you believe me?\"","The manager nodded: \"Boss, I know. You've always been a dumb pretty boy.\"","Gu Jinghan: \"Take out the 'pretty boy.'\"","The manager smiled: \"Fine. Dumb.\"","\"Get lost!\"","The manager waved his phone: \"Boss, reimburse me for the wiretap.\"","Gu Jinghan opened the transfer page and asked the manager: \"How much?\"","\"One hundred eighty thousand.\"","Gu Jinghan paused: \"You really think I'm an idiot?\"","The manager chuckled awkwardly: \"Maybe that was a bit greedy. How about eight thousand? Eight thousand works.\"","Eight thousand was transferred, and Gu Jinghan glared at him: \"I pay you a decent salary, don't I? Why are you still so greedy?\"","The manager put on an ingratiating smile: \"Just kidding~\"","Gu Jinghan waved him off impatiently: \"Scram, scram, scram...\"","Just looking at him was annoying.","The manager hurried out of the car, but as he turned, his phone screen flashed in front of Gu Jinghan's eyes.","An obvious Pinduoduo order stared right at him: 28.99.","\"Cheng Huaiyu!\"","\"Oops~ It slipped out! Bye, boss!\"","The manager slammed the car door shut, turned, and bolted without a moment's hesitation.","Gu Jinghan angrily opened his phone and texted him: [Quarterly bonus cancelled!]","A bright red exclamation mark popped up instantly: [Message sent, but has been rejected by the recipient.]","\"Cheng Huaiyu! I'm going to destroy you one day!\"","A second later, his phone buzzed again.","He picked it up and his face darkened.","Cheng Huaiyu: [That's too intimate! Let's not do this!]","......","Fine. He'd leave.","He was going to find his big brother!","He needed to let his brother know what Gu Chacha was really like. She was bad news, and they couldn't hang out with her anymore.","He drove to the company building and went straight up to the top-floor office.","\"Bro! I've got something to show you!\"","Pushing open the door, Gu Jingchen was on the phone, his expression extremely serious.","Seeing him come in, Gu Jingchen pressed a hand down in the air to signal him to sit quietly.","\"Mm, please keep an eye on it for me. Mm, I know it's not easy for you. Mm hm... thanks, appreciate it.\"","The call ended, and Gu Jingchen glanced at Gu Jinghan: \"Barging in like that without even knocking.\"","\"Oh, come on! Since when do we stand on ceremony with each other?\"","Gu Jinghan placed the wiretap device in front of him: \"Bro, I want you to listen to something.\"","Gu Jingchen nodded, only to watch Gu Jinghan fiddle with it for ages with nothing coming out.","He asked in exasperation: \"What are you up to now?\"","Gu Jinghan, focused on finding the fast-forward button, muttered: \"The beginning's too awkward. Won't play that part for you.\"","Gu Jingchen frowned: \"What on earth...\"","\"Don't forget—why did Han Mo get into that car accident? Who gave me the tip?\"","\"Han Mo! I want him dead!\"","\"...\"","\"He just came by the house, didn't find my sister...\"","\"He went to your place?\"","\"...\"","Gu Jinghan pressed pause, his eyes burning as he looked at Gu Jingchen: \"Big bro! Did you hear that? It was Han Xuan who ran down Han Mo—and Gu Chacha who gave him the location!\"","Such explosive news—he expected Gu Jingchen to be shocked.","But instead, his brother frowned slightly and asked him: \"Where did you get this recording?\"","He blurted out: \"The two of them hooked up at the hotel I own...\"","Gu Jingchen's frown deepened: \"You wiretapped them? Do you know that's illegal?\"","\"I only did it once...\"","Gu Jinghan said guiltily: \"Anyway, that's not the point! The point is what's on the recording! I've always said Gu Chacha is no good! Even when we were kids, she was like this—always so good at pretending! Bro, you can't let her fool you anymore...\"","Huanhuan was their real sister. Their blood sister."]},{"number":75,"title":"Chapter 75: Big Brother's Arrangement","paragraphs":["He went on and on, talking about how Gu Chacha had a black heart, and had always liked to mess with him back in the day.","After Huanhuan came to the house, she kept picking on Huanhuan nonstop.","But he could talk until his throat went dry, and Gu Jingchen didn't react at all.","\"Bro!\"","He slapped the table in annoyance: \"Are you even listening to me? Don't tell me you're still on Gu Chacha's side? Are you stupid or what?\"","Gu Jingchen sat behind his desk, his fingertips tapping lightly twice on the surface: \"I already know everything you've said. Is there anything else you'd like to add?\"","Gu Jinghan stared with wide eyes: \"You know? When did you find out? Really? Are you serious? Are you just messing with me?\"","Gu Jingchen glanced at his brother, who had that foolish look on his face, and let out a silent sigh.","He turned the computer screen around to face him and pulled up the surveillance video of the car accident scene.","He paused the video right as the person got out of the car, and clicked to stop: \"Notice anything off?\"","Gu Jinghan stared hard at the screen, then stared even harder: \"That hat of his is pretty stylish.\"","...","His brother wanted to sigh again: \"That's the hat we got on our trip to the Maldives last year, the one that made you and Chacha fight.\"","Last year he'd insisted it was ugly, called it double ugly, and now suddenly it was stylish.","Gu Jinghan's eyes went wide at that: \"Really? No wonder it looks so ugly!\"","...","His brother turned the computer back around. Forget it, even if he showed him, he wouldn't get it.","He waved his hand: \"You don't need to worry about this. I've got it handled.\"","Then, after a moment of thought, he carefully added: \"Your hotel has a lot of employees too. Don't go causing unnecessary trouble.\"","The hotel wasn't a big deal to Jinghan—it was just a small startup project from his college days.","But a stable job was everything to ordinary people. The monthly paycheck was what gave them the confidence to live their lives properly.","Don't let employees pay the price for your own whims.","Gu Jinghan nodded: \"I know. I only risked eavesdropping because I was worried about Huanhuan.\"","Otherwise, why would he eavesdrop on Gu Chacha's hotel room? He wasn't some pervert.","A faint smile tugged at the corner of Gu Jingchen's mouth: \"She's doing fine right now. She's staying over at Liang Ye's place.\"","\"What?\"","Gu Jinghan jumped straight up: \"How do you know where she is? Did she contact you?\"","He immediately felt wronged: \"But I treat her so much better! Why didn't she contact me?\"","\"Sit down properly and act your age.\"","Gu Jingchen scolded him, exasperated: \"Liang Zheng told me. Huanhuan and Han Mo are both staying at Liang Ye's place.\"","Gu Jinghan couldn't quite wrap his head around the three of them: \"How are the three of them living together? That relationship dynamic is a bit messy, isn't it?\"","\"Liang Zheng said there's another girl staying with Huanhuan and the others. She looks...\" Gu Jingchen wasn't sure how to repeat Liang Zheng's description: \"like a delinquent girl—tattoos, dyed hair, mooching off men. Apparently she's Huanhuan's friend.\"","Tattoos, dyed hair, mooching off men...","So she was Huanhuan's wild version?","Gu Jinghan clicked his tongue in amazement: \"Huanhuan's already such an amazing person, and there's a wilder version of her? I've gotta go see this!\"","He got up to leave but was stopped by Gu Jingchen: \"Don't go.\"","\"Why not?\"","He didn't understand. Now that they knew where Huanhuan was, shouldn't he go check on her?","Gu Jingchen picked up his phone: \"She wasn't very happy at home. Let her have some fun outside.\"","Their parents weren't exactly attentive to her, and she could feel it.","Let her stay out there and enjoy herself with her friends. She could come back once everything was settled.","Gu Jinghan wrinkled his nose: \"Fine.\"","He agreed verbally, but as soon as he got downstairs, he got in his car and drove into the city.","Fine, he wouldn't meet her. But he could at least sneak a peek, right?","Huanhuan had disappeared for days. He needed to confirm she was okay before he could feel at ease.","He parked the car across from the neighborhood and planned to stake out the place to catch sight of He Huanhuan.","On the third floor, Liang Ye was scrambling into his clothes: \"Why didn't you guys wake me up! I'm late!\"","He Huanhuan spread her hands: \"We did wake you. You almost threw a punch at me.\"","No idea how the guy did it, but his sleep was so deep that no amount of calling could wake him up!","And the moment you tried to shove him, a fist came flying!","Liang Ye glared at Han Mo: \"It's your fault for sleeping so badly the night before last and ruining my sleep. Otherwise I wouldn't have passed out right outside the sales hall!\"","He hadn't even returned his coworker's scooter yet!","He'd only been transferred to this position about half a month ago and didn't know his colleagues well yet. How embarrassing!","Han Mo was speechless. The guy had snored all night long, and he had the nerve to say he didn't sleep well?","But his buddy looked like he was about to cry. He'd never been late to work in all his years of working!","Last night, Han Mo had briefly mentioned Liang Ye's family background, and Qi Meili was genuinely confused: \"Did you rack up gambling debts behind your family's back?\"","Liang Ye's eyes went wide in horror: \"Don't say that! Gambling is bad! I don't gamble!\"","Qi Meili was even more confused: \"Then you don't owe any money. Why are you working?\"","Liang Ye: \"How can a person not work? If you don't work, you'll lose touch with society, get left behind by others, and—\"","\"Shut up!\" Qi Meili's head was spinning: \"It's just a lousy job. What's the big deal? Who the hell is chasing you anyway?\"","He Huanhuan nodded: \"Whoever's so eager to chase you, maybe you should just get together with her.\"","Liang Ye was speechless: \"My grandpa said that only people who work hard have value to society!\"","...","Times have changed, kid. In your grandparents' generation, society was developing at lightning speed and everyone was a pillar of the community.","Now, we're just ordinary workhorses.","But these beliefs were already deeply rooted in Liang Ye's soul. He was panicking: \"My scooter is still at the sales hall! How am I supposed to get to work?\"","Qi Meili couldn't stand to see him all whiny. She waved a hand grandly: \"Stop crying! I'll drive you!\"","He Huanhuan suggested: \"How about I take him instead?\"","She knew the area better and it would be more convenient.","Qi Meili was this close to flicking her on the forehead: \"If you go drop him off, then I'm stuck at home with Han Laodeng. Do you want me dead or do you want him dead?\"","Han Mo said that it would probably be him who dies.","Qi Meili grabbed her keys and headed out, dropping Liang Ye off at the village committee office.","Then he dragged her back and forth to the sales department twice to retrieve both scooters, and only then did Liang Ye let her go with a grin.","\"I swear, how is there such a meek rich kid? If you can't handle it, let me do it!\"","Qi Meili grumbled the whole way as she rode the scooter, until she made it back to the entrance of the neighborhood.","Her sharp eyes immediately spotted a car parked across the street, and inside sat a gorgeous, stunningly handsome guy!","Without a second thought, she turned around and rode over, tapping her slender fingers on the car window.","Gu Jinghan had just parked when the window was knocked on. His heart tightened instantly.","No way? Found out already?","He turned his head to look—bright red, amber yellow, vivid blue...","A thought flashed through his mind. As the window rolled down slowly, a rogue smile appeared under a head of crimson hair: \"Hey handsome, got a girlfriend? If not, how about we date for a couple days?\""]},{"number":76,"title":"Chapter 76: Something's Off","paragraphs":["Gu Jinghan shot a glance at her hair, then another at the tattoo peeking out from under her sleeve, and took in her flippant attitude.","Damn! Busted on the first try!","Qi Meili leaned against the car window: \"Hey handsome? Dazzled by me? Want to add a friend~\"","The window shot up in a hurry. Gu Jinghan didn't dare say a word, hit the gas, and peeled out!","Qi Meili watched him go, savoring the moment: \"What a cold, handsome flower boy. That's my kind of love!\"","Though... didn’t that guy look a little familiar?","Ah well! Being familiar is normal. Pretty faces always have something in common — unlike ugly people, who are ugly in a thousand bizarre and distinct ways.","She rode her bike back in high spirits, only to find He Huanhuan and Han Mo sitting obediently in the living room waiting for her.","Kids go quiet, they're up to something.","Sitting that still? Definitely suspicious.","She eyed them with suspicion: \"You two look like you're cooking up something no good.\"","He Huanhuan smiled sweetly: \"Meili, I want to eat something good.\"","She and Han Mo had just over thirty yuan left between them, and their phones were useless. They could only wait for Meili to throw them a bone.","After all, Meili had just come into a windfall of fifty thousand.","Hearing that, Qi Meili rolled her eyes: \"That's all? Come on! Whatever you want, your big sister will buy it for you!\"","She'd always been free with her money — it's just that she used to be too broke to show it.","A twenty-yuan insult fee had to be haggled down to 13.52.","But not anymore. She was rich now. Supporting her besties was a piece of cake!","She grabbed He Huanhuan and linked arms with her: \"What do you want? Beef noodles or lamb soup noodles? I'll get you both!\"","Old habits die hard when you've just come into money — she was all in billionaire mode, but her brain could only conjure cheap carbs.","He Huanhuan, on the other hand, had been a rich kid for a while and knew exactly how to spend money.","She crossed her arms, all smug: \"Who eats that stuff? That's peasant food! I want Wenxiang!\"","Now, malatang may sound humble and down-to-earth, but it's anything but cheap.","Potatoes that go for two yuan a pound, sliced thin and soaked in water, sell for one-fifty per slice.","Grab a few veggies, and your bowl easily hits thirty-plus.","More profitable than running with the mob!","But Qi Meili wrinkled her nose in disgust: \"Wenxiang? That place got exposed!\"","He Huanhuan was stunned: \"When did that happen? How did I not hear about it?\"","That was her favorite spot!","Qi Meili pulled out her phone and showed her. A video played with a stern news anchor reporting on Wenxiang's hygiene violations.","Qi Meili scoffed: \"That's what you get for being such a lovestruck fool. You don't even have a phone to play with now. All you've got to look forward to is digging wild greens!\"","He Huanhuan: ..........","It had only been a few days!","Had she already fallen off the face of the earth?","And her beloved Wenxiang had gotten shut down?","Qi Meili draped an arm around her and pulled her along: \"Come on, let's go get some beef noodles. I'll spring for extra meat for you.\"","They found a small place on the roadside and each ordered a bowl of beef noodles.","Qi Meili asked Han Mo: \"How long are you planning to crash here?\"","Han Mo grabbed chopsticks for them: \"Just a couple more days.\"","He Huanhuan gave him a puzzled look: \"How do you know it's just a couple of days?\"","They'd been together every day. He had no phone and no internet. How could he know that?","Han Mo smiled faintly: \"Just a feeling.\"","So pretentious.","Inside the top-floor office of the Gu Corporation building, Gu Jingchen was on a call, his expression serious.","\"You guessed right. Han Xuan is indeed transferring money out of the company accounts.\"","Gu Jingchen sat up straight: \"Help me hold him off.\"","The voice on the other end shot up in pitch: \"How can you ask that? If they find out, I'll get chewed out! That Diao Mao guy is...\"","\"Xu You seems to be coming back in the next few days, though I don't know the exact flight...\"","The voice immediately sighed in defeat: \"Diao Mao can chew me out all he wants! Helping a friend is what counts!\"","The corner of Gu Jingchen's mouth lifted: \"Thanks.\"","\"Say, when's she getting back?\"","\"We'll talk about that later.\"","Five minutes later, the phone rang again.","Qi Ming, utterly confused, was on the other end: \"Didn't you already finish blocking him? What do you still need from me?\"","Gu Jingchen shot upright: \"What are you talking about?\"","Qi Ming stared at the status in his system, amazed: \"Old Gu, you've got some skills. You actually got Diao Mao to bend the rules for you? How'd you manage that?\"","He glanced at the office diagonally across from his, where a gleaming bald head sat calmly.","Diao Mao was notoriously hard to deal with. Old Gu really was a cunning fox. Impressive!","But Gu Jingchen didn't feel like explaining: \"If there's nothing else, I'll hang up.\"","\"Hey, hey, hey...\"","Qi Ming quickly called out: \"Uh, when's Xu You coming back? Which flight?\"","Gu Jingchen's voice was full of surprise: \"Who said she's coming back? News to me.\"","......","\"Gu Jingchen! You son of a —\"","After hanging up, Gu Jingchen sat in a grim silence.","He'd planned to give Han Mo a hand, only to find out Han Mo had already handled it himself.","So why wasn't he showing up yet?","What was he scheming?","He thought it over, then called a friend of his at the Land and Resources Bureau.","After some small talk, he cut straight to the point and asked what he wanted to know.","The friend gave him an answer quickly.","After the call ended, Gu Jingchen sat in his chair for a long time without speaking.","His long fingers tapped his knee again and again. Then he let out a light chuckle: \"This Han Mo, seriously...\"","Ah well. It wasn't a bad thing in the end. He'd let them play it out themselves.","Down on the third floor, the three of them were sitting on the living room sofa watching TV.","It was an awkward time of the afternoon — lots of ads, not much actual programming.","They flipped through channels endlessly until, somehow, they ended up watching local news.","Qi Meili leaned against He Huanhuan's shoulder and let out a long yawn: \"This is so boring. How about we go tear up the town?\"","Man, people are such jerks. Back when she didn't have to work, every day was a blast.","Now that she'd gotten that factory job, suddenly having time off didn't feel right anymore.","Serves her right!","She blinked, then clung to He Huanhuan's arm: \"Come on, let's go out for a walk. I'm dying of boredom.\"","He Huanhuan also felt a bit too idle, so she nodded in agreement: \"Alright.\"","She turned to Han Mo: \"You coming with us?\"","But Han Mo shook his head to refuse: \"I'll watch some TV at home. You two go on without me.\"","Something was off.","Very off.","He Huanhuan followed Qi Meili out the door, then turned back in a flash and peeked through the peephole.","\"What are you doing?\"","Startled by her sudden move, Qi Meili leaned in and whispered.","He Huanhuan wished she could flatten herself against the door: \"Don't you think Han Mo's acting weird today?\"","Qi Meili was confused: \"Weird how?\"","Didn't he seem normal?","He Huanhuan gritted her teeth: \"He won't come tear up the town with us.\"","......","Hopeless romantic.","Qi Meili grabbed her and dragged her away: \"Let's go get some sun. I'm not letting you back inside until this lovesick nonsense is cured.\"","\"No, really. Something's off about him...\"","He Huanhuan tried to explain, but Qi Meili wasn't having it.","You hear about young people losing their minds, but you never hear about old geezers going wild. The man was ancient — what business did he have tearing up the town, anyway?"]},{"number":77,"title":"Chapter 77: That handsome guy looks a bit familiar.","paragraphs":["Dragging He Huanhuan out of the apartment complex, Qi Meili gave her a sharp flick on the forehead, clearly annoyed:","\"How many times have I told you? Romance is just the seasoning in life. You can dip your toes in, but don't get too invested. And what happens if you do?\"","He Huanhuan obediently chimed in: \"You get hurt by men. You get your heart broken.\"","\"Exactly!\"","Qi Meili, like a patient kindergarten teacher, stared at her and asked again: \"So what do we do about it?\"","He Huanhuan blinked. \"I don't know.\"","\"Cure your lovesick brain!\"","And how do you cure a lovesick brain? You hit the streets.","You just walk. You walk for three or four hours straight, until your legs ache and your feet throb, and the moment your head hits the pillow, you're out cold.","No time or energy left for lovesickness.","So, naturally, Qi Meili dragged He Huanhuan on a relentless power walk through the streets.","From the blazing afternoon sun all the way to dusk.","Until He Huanhuan was waving her hands in surrender: \"Okay, seriously, that's enough. I swear I'm not lovesick anymore. I swear.\"","She couldn't take another single step.","If Han Mo dropped dead right in front of her at this point, all she'd offer him was a \"good dog doesn't block the road, kindly go die on the curb.\"","Qi Meili raised a hand and made an OK sign.","Not because she was being cold—she was too exhausted to speak.","She pulled out her phone to book a ride-share home.","The moment she entered their destination, she nearly choked. The two of them had walked the equivalent of sixty bucks' worth of distance that afternoon.","No wonder they were dead on their feet!","She tapped the screen, hesitating. She couldn't quite bring herself to spend the money.","But walking back? Absolutely not. She had no strength left for that.","Just as she was wavering, her eye caught a striking figure across the street.","A face of intense beauty. Sharp brows, piercing eyes—an absolute heartthrob.","Qi Meili's spirits instantly soared: \"Huanhuan! Wait right there! I'll find you a ride!\"","She vanished in a flash, so fast He Huanhuan couldn't even react: \"Where are you going? Are you coming back?\"","Across the road, a cold, gleaming black SUV sat parked.","The window was half open. A man pulled out a cigarette and put it between his lips. The lighter flickered to life with a cool blue flame, which he brought up to light the cigarette.","The moment it was lit, a slender white hand suddenly reached through the window and snatched the cigarette right out of his mouth.","His brow instantly furrowed.","\"Hey, handsome. Got a partner? If not, want to date me for a couple days?\"","His gaze shifted to the window in disbelief, and there it was—that red hair he'd seen just last night.","And beneath the red hair, that flippant smile.","Liang Zheng looked at Qi Meili. \"What did you just say to me?\"","Qi Meili beamed radiantly: \"Handsome, where are you headed? Mind giving me a lift?\"","\"You don't recognize me?\"","Liang Zheng could hardly believe it. She'd touched his lower back just last night, and now here she was, acting like she'd never seen him before.","Qi Meili held the cigarette between her fingers, brought it to her lips, and took a deep drag. White smoke swirled between them, blurring his vision.","A second later, the cigarette was shoved back into his mouth.","Carrying a faint, barely perceptible trace of moisture.","\"Of course I recognize you—you're my future husband, aren't you?\"","Qi Meili's voice dripped with carefree flippancy: \"Hubby, how about we add each other?\"","\"Ha.\"","Liang Zheng nearly laughed out loud. He'd never thought he'd see the day someone forgot him the moment they turned around.","He put the cigarette to his lips and took a drag: \"I'm Liang Ye—\"","\"Holy crap! In one day, Liang Ye, you got this handsome?\"","Liang Zheng burst out laughing. \"Haha... You already said that yesterday, Miss Qi.\"","Qi Meili's eyes flew wide: \"Yesterday? You're Liang Zheng???\"","\"Meili, did you book the ride yet?\"","He Huanhuan's voice suddenly came from behind. Qi Meili spun around: \"Um! Bye, bro!\"","She grabbed He Huanhuan and bolted. He Huanhuan had no idea what was going on, but the two of them had years of tacit understanding—she didn't ask questions, she just ran.","But no matter how fast two legs can go, can they outrun four wheels?","The SUV shot forward and cut in front of them. Liang Zheng's gaze locked onto Qi Meili. \"Weren't you going to add me? Why are you leaving?\"","Qi Meili gave an awkward laugh: \"Ah, my husband doesn't let me fool around these days. Maybe some other time.\"","...","Liang Zheng's smile only grew. \"Not taking that ride anymore?\"","Qi Meili's smile turned even more strained: \"I'll pass. My husband's still waiting for me at home. Next time he's not around, I'll take you up on that ride.\"","Liang Zheng nodded with a smile. \"Fine.\"","But the car didn't move.","He Huanhuan leaned in and whispered to Qi Meili: \"Meili, what's going on?\"","Qi Meili gritted her teeth: \"That's Liang Ye's older brother.\"","Damn!","They had to run!","But whether they ran fast, or ran faster, or just gave up and trudged along—","The gleaming black SUV followed every step of the way without fail.","The man inside didn't say a word to them, just tailed them with an oppressive silence.","It went on until Qi Meili's temper finally flared. She charged up to the car: \"Why the hell are you following us? Are you some kind of creep?\"","Liang Zheng glanced at her. \"I'm curious what your husband looks like. Is it a crime to follow and see?\"","Qi Meili spouted nonsense without missing a beat: \"My husband has social anxiety. Don't you dare scare him!\"","\"Funny. I'm very outgoing. I specialize in curing social anxiety.\"","...","He was dressed in a black suit, sitting in that big off-road vehicle. With his intense features, he looked like a mob boss.","He's outgoing?","Who would believe that?!","Qi Meili shot him a dirty look, then grabbed He Huanhuan and plopped herself into his car.","\"Drive!\"","If he wanted to give them a ride so badly, fine. Let him.","A smile flickered instantly in Liang Zheng's eyes: \"Not going to pick up your husband too?\"","\"Shut up and drive.\"","\"Okay.\"","The car sped off toward the apartment complex. He Huanhuan shrank into the back seat, trying to make herself as small as possible.","But her luck didn't hold. Liang Zheng glanced at the rearview mirror and asked with a smile:","\"I remember Xiao Ye mentioning that Huanhuan was a very lively girl. Why so quiet today?\"","...","He Huanhuan was stunned: \"You know me?\"","She'd never met Liang Zheng before, and she'd been secretly hoping she'd go unnoticed if she stayed quiet.","Liang Zheng pointed at her hair. \"Very distinctive.\"","Then his gaze slid to Qi Meili's red hair. \"Also very distinctive.\"","He Huanhuan was speechless. So this was how she got caught.","All that suffering over the past few days was for nothing!","Unbelievable!","She pouted: \"Bro, can you not tell anyone about this?\"","Liang Zheng shook his head: \"Too late. Your brother-in-law already found out last night.\"","\"What?\"","Both of them were shocked: \"Last night?\"","Hadn't they hidden themselves last night? How did he know?","Liang Zheng gave Qi Meili a helpless smile: \"You didn't close your shoe cabinet door properly.\"","And besides—Liang Ye was petty. He'd bought the cheapest glass door for the bathroom.","He Huanhuan and Han Mo's figures were reflected crystal clear through it.","As long as he wasn't blind, he'd see them at a glance.","Huh?","He Huanhuan almost fainted: \"Meili, how did you not see that?\"","Qi Meili said matter-of-factly: \"He was so good-looking, I was staring at him the whole time. When would I have had a chance to look at the door?\"","Who's the real lovesick one here?","She'd like to know!"]},{"number":78,"title":"Chapter 78: She Belongs to Herself","paragraphs":["The car pulled up at the entrance of the residential complex. He Huanhuan shot out of the car in a flash—she needed to find Han Mo immediately.","Qi Meili turned to follow, only to discover the car door had been locked in an instant!","She turned around in annoyance and glared at Liang Zheng: \"What are you doing? I need to go home.\"","\"Going home?\"","Liang Zheng looked at her with an unreadable expression: \"What? Does your socially anxious husband live there too?\"","Qi Meili patted him on the shoulder: \"Bro, a man who clings too hard loses his appeal, you know that?\"","Their gazes met. Liang Zheng could clearly see nothing but careless frivolity in her eyes.","He couldn't help but laugh. He really was too used to being pursued and adored—that was why he cared so much about why this strange girl didn't remember him.","He unlocked the car: \"Go on, then.\"","Qi Meili jumped out without a second thought, sprinting away without looking back.","A clingy man was a definite no-go. If you gave them an inch, you'd never shake them off.","Liang Zheng sat in the car, watching her flee as if escaping from something, then couldn't help glancing at himself in the rearview mirror.","Clean features, nothing wrong with his face.","Didn't she say he was good-looking? Why was she so desperate to get away from him?","She was like a completely different person from the one who had brazenly taken advantage of him last night.","He lit another cigarette. This time, no one suddenly snatched it from him, and no one took a drag and shoved it back into his mouth.","He sat in the car and smoked the whole cigarette, but his brow never relaxed.","Flicking the butt into the trash can by the roadside, he figured he really wasn't getting any younger—it was time to arrange a blind date for himself.","The SUV quickly disappeared from in front of the complex.","\"Hey, isn't that my brother's car?\"","Liang Ye rode by on his electric scooter, curious, but then decided it couldn't be. His brother didn't like noisy places, and this apartment had been bought for five or six years now. His brother had visited maybe a handful of times.","Definitely a case of mistaken identity.","He rode his scooter into the complex, carrying a bag of Nanjing roast duck, and happily climbed up to the third floor.","Opening the door, he shouted with excitement: \"I bought roast duck! Who wants some!\"","No one answered him.","He was rarely this generous, yet he didn't get the reaction he wanted. He felt let down: \"I'm not charging you!\"","The duck vanished in an instant. He Huanhuan appeared with a grin, carrying the duck to the dining table: \"Got a promotion or a raise? Since when are you this generous?\"","Mind you, he'd even ask them to chip in for discounted eggs.","Liang Ye happily sat down across from her: \"I was craving roast duck today, but I couldn't bring myself to buy one.\"","Yeah, that's him.","\"I just stood there at the duck shop entrance looking at it. The owner thought I was a beggar and gave me half.\"","...","He Huanhuan looked up at him: \"How long did you stand there?\"","Liang Ye grinned: \"Not long. Just two hours.\"","Two hours and he still couldn't bring himself to buy half a duck?","Qi Meili sat down next to He Huanhuan to look at the duck: \"It's not gone bad from not selling, is it?\"","Liang Ye glared at her: \"Don't go suspecting the owner like that! He's a kind-hearted man, okay?\"","Sure, he was a bit rude about it and told him to take it and scram...","But he gave him roast duck, right? What a nice guy!","He Huanhuan looked at the plastic container of duck: \"Well, this can count as our farewell meal.\"","\"What? Farewell meal?\" Liang Ye's head shot up, staring at He Huanhuan.","Han Mo walked over and sat beside him, explaining: \"It's time for us to go back. Thank you for having us these past couple of days.\"","\"What... what do you mean, going back so soon?\"","Liang Ye felt a lump in his throat, unable to speak.","Weren't they supposed to stay at his place for seven or eight days?","It had only been three days. Why were they suddenly leaving?","His face fell, twisting in misery: \"You're really going back?\"","Han Mo nodded: \"Yes.\"","Liang Ye couldn't help rambling: \"But your dad's in the hospital, and your company's been taken over by your brother. Going back won't change anything...\"","\"And another thing—why would someone deliberately crash into your car? Someone must be out to get you. Going back like this is so dangerous...\"","He blinked rapidly, desperately searching for arguments to convince them, but the ones who had made up their minds refused to be swayed.","Han Mo patted him on the shoulder: \"We're friends. We can grab a meal together sometime.\"","Liang Ye burst into loud sobs: \"Who wants to have meals with you! It's Huanhuan I can't bear to part with. Huanhuan, can't you stay? I can sleep on the couch every day, I swear, waaaah...\"","He Huanhuan declined: \"I'm not living in a cramped thirty-square-meter dump.\"","She was taking Meili back to her own three-hundred-square-meter penthouse!","Liang Ye's tears wouldn't stop: \"Huanhuan, waaaah...\"","He really couldn't stand to lose her...","He Huanhuan poured the braising sauce over the roast duck: \"You're that sad to see me go? Then I'll have the drumstick.\"","Liang Ye sniffled and cried: \"No, there's only one drumstick, and I can't part with it. How about the wing tip instead?\"","...","Buddy, you're never going to win a girl over with that attitude.","The four of them sat around the table and shared the half duck. In the end, Liang Ye's mood improved quite a bit.","He sniffled and asked them: \"When are you leaving?\"","Han Mo: \"Tomorrow morning.\"","He Huanhuan had the evidence in her phone of Han Xuan ramming his car. Tomorrow morning, they'd go straight to the police station to file a report and catch Han Xuan completely off guard.","That night, as they lay down to sleep, Liang Ye turned to face Han Mo: \"Han Mo, you know, you've really been through a lot.\"","\"It's fine.\"","Han Mo lay flat, trying to lull himself to sleep. He needed to fall asleep before Liang Ye did, or he wouldn't get any sleep tonight.","\"But honestly, your situation isn't that bad. Sure, your dad had an affair, but he's also bedridden sick now—that's karma! And my brother says your company is about to go under because of your brother—that's karma too!\"","He got himself all worked up and excited. What a satisfying thought!","But Han Mo showed little reaction, just a faint \"Mm.\"","\"So...\"","Liang Ye probed cautiously: \"Since you're not pitiful anymore, how about you let me have Huanhuan?\"","...","So that's where he was going with this.","Han Mo opened his eyes and shot him a glance: \"How am I supposed to 'let' you have her?\"","\"Just, you know, don't contact Huanhuan anymore. And stop transferring her so much money. The way you do it, I can't even compete. I really can't bear to let go...\"","Ten thousand after ten thousand—who could handle that!","Han Mo asked him: \"You think that if I stop sending her money and we stop contacting each other, she'll end up with you?\"","Liang Ye nodded vigorously: \"Of course! I like her that much!\"","Han Mo let out a light laugh: \"Liang Ye, I don't see your love. You say you like her, but what have you actually done? You wouldn't even give her the drumstick.\"","Liang Ye explained guiltily: \"I'd been craving that drumstick all day long...\"","If there had been two drumsticks, he would definitely have given her one.","Han Mo smiled: \"You'd only share if you had extra. That's not love.\"","Liang Ye was unhappy and fired back: \"And how much do you love her? I don't see your love either!\"","Unexpectedly, Han Mo nodded in agreement: \"You're right. When I first got involved with her, I had ulterior motives. So I'm no better.\"","Liang Ye glared at him: \"Then why are you criticizing me!\"","He, on the other hand, hadn't had any hidden agenda at all.","Han Mo closed his eyes again, trying to coax himself back to sleep. “So it’s not that I gave her up to you. It’s that whoever she chooses is the one she ends up with. She doesn’t belong to anyone. She belongs to herself.”"]},{"number":79,"title":"Chapter 79: I’m Going to Kill You","paragraphs":["With things weighing on his mind, Liang Ye woke up just as dawn broke the next day.","He trailed sullenly behind He Huanhuan: \"Huanhuan, are you really going too? This doesn't really have anything to do with you, so maybe you should sit this one out?\"","He Huanhuan shot him a look: \"I'm an eyewitness, and I'm the one who filmed the evidence. Why wouldn't I go?\"","Liang Ye thought for a moment, then turned to Qi Meili: \"Why don't you go? Just say you filmed it—you're Han Mo's girlfriend...\"","Qi Meili clenched her fist: \"Are you asking for a beating?\"","Did he think the police were idiots?","Besides, she probably wasn't even in the police station's household registry—they'd have to figure out who she was first before anything else.","Liang Ye looked pitiful: \"But I really don't want to leave you... what if...\"","He was mid-sentence when the alarm clock by the bed suddenly started beeping.","Liang Ye turned off the alarm and walked off. He Huanhuan was baffled: \"Where are you going?\"","He hadn't even finished talking!","Liang Ye put on a serious face: \"I've got to get to work—I was late yesterday, and I can't be late again today.\"","......","Was there really such a thing as a workaholic obsessed with clocking in?","The door slammed shut, and from outside came Liang Ye's faint reminder: \"Huanhuan, I'll come find you when I'm off work!\"","The three left inside stared at each other. Qi Meili scratched her forehead in confusion: \"Did he get, like, bound to some system? Does he get electrocuted if he doesn't work?\"","He Huanhuan nodded: \"Probably.\"","Qi Meili sighed: \"Poor kid—he must've gotten zapped so hard that he ended up so thunderously ugly.\"","If he were as handsome as his brother, then his stinginess would be called thriftiness, and his love for work would be called diligence.","Handsome, thrifty, and hardworking—how charming would that be?","Too bad heaven didn't give him a good face. That's just fate.","After tidying up and locking the door, they set off for the police station.","On the way, He Huanhuan asked curiously: \"How did you even find out the news?\"","Last night, the moment she pushed the door open, Han Mo had told her they could go back.","He said Han Xuan had transferred all his dirty money out, and now it was all frozen by the banks.","It was time to send him a big \"gift\" and make him sink into the mire, never to rise again.","But the question was: How did he know all this?","He'd been at home alone, with no phone to contact anyone!","He Huanhuan had racked her brain all night without figuring it out, and now she finally couldn't help but ask: \"So how do you know all that?\"","Han Mo gave a sly smile: \"I guessed.\"","That only made He Huanhuan frantic as she chased after him: \"No way! You must have a way to contact people!\"","\"Come on, just tell me at this point!\"","\"Tell me—hey, tell me...\"","After badgering him all the way, Han Mo finally laughed and told her: \"It was the livestream.\"","It was the age of the internet, and TV stations, desperate to ride the trend, had started their own livestreams.","Every day in the afternoon, they broadcast live for two hours on a fixed schedule.","The news he wanted was relayed to him through those livestreams.","As for the exact method, there was no need to go into details.","He Huanhuan didn't press further—she knew he always had a way.","But...","She couldn't help but think of Chen Yu: \"What about your cousin? Did he actually betray you?\"","Han Mo shook his head: \"He wouldn't do that. He's not that kind of person.\"","Wait a second...","He Huanhuan suddenly realized something: \"You trust him that much?\"","Han Mo nodded: \"We grew up together. I know him.\"","He Huanhuan was exasperated: \"But then why didn't we stay in the place you guys had arranged if he was fine?\"","Han Mo smiled faintly: \"He's too impulsive. This is a good chance to teach him a lesson—so he'll be a bit more steady in the future.\"","......","He Huanhuan: \"Are you teaching him a lesson or teaching me?\"","She was the one stuck living in that run-down place with him, not Chen Yu!","Han Mo looked at her softly: \"Don't you think these past few days have been special? When we're old and look back on this time, we'll treasure the memories.\"","Treasure what?","What was there for her to treasure?","She'd lived like that every single day before—what was there to cherish?","God!","She just couldn't see eye to eye with those rich people!","\"Get out of here!\"","He Huanhuan wanted nothing more than to kick him flying.","She angrily linked arms with Qi Meili: \"If it weren't for meeting you by wandering around with him, Meili, I'd totally kick him to death.\"","Qi Meili smiled: \"Go on, kick him dead. Don't hold back on my account.\"","......","\"Meili!\"","Qi Meili curled her lip in disgust. Sweet talk was gross.","When they walked into the police station, they didn't even need to report anything—the moment they reached the entrance, they were recognized.","Finding missing persons was usually the drudgery handed to new recruits.","A rookie officer with two big dark circles under his eyes came sprinting at them: \"Hey! You two! Don't run!\"","Uninformed bystanders thought the two of them had committed a crime, and cleared the space in a flash for the police to do their thing.","The young officer shouted excitedly: \"Chief! Found them! I found them!\"","......","Found them? They came to you on their own.","The rest of the process was simple. He Huanhuan's video hadn't just captured Han Xuan's harsh words—it had also directly caught his face.","With both witnesses and physical evidence in hand, the police immediately sent people to the Han residence to bring him in for detention and interrogation.","At the Han residence, Han Xuan paced anxiously in the living room, making call after call, growing more and more agitated.","After more than a dozen attempts, the phone finally got through: \"Brother Bao! My money's been frozen by the bank! Can you...\"","\"Mr. Han, Brother Bao is on vacation these days. Call back another time.\"","Han Xuan urgently pressed on: \"Where is he now? Do you have his number? Give me his number—I need to talk to him...\"","\"Beep, beep, beep...\"","\"Damn it!\"","He hurled his phone at the floor like a madman!","\"Damn your ancestors!\"","He took a few deep breaths, then picked the phone back up. His finger swiped wildly across the screen, scrambling to find someone—anyone—who could help.","\"Ding-dong~\"","The doorbell rang. Han Xuan irritably kicked the rug: \"Didn't I already pay you all? Get lost!\"","He'd dismissed all the maids and servants earlier that morning, thinking this was just some stubborn one trying to beg him to stay.","\"Get out!\"","But the doorbell kept ringing, one chime after another, fueling his rage. He stormed to the door and yanked it open: \"I told you all to get...\"","\"Han Xuan, you are suspected of intentional injury. In accordance with the relevant provisions of the Criminal Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China, we hereby decide to place you under criminal detention.\"","Over a dozen police officers stood at the door, staring at him sternly: \" Please come with us.\"","He froze. How could this be? How...","But his gaze suddenly landed on a familiar figure behind the crowd.","\"Han Mo! It's you! You did this to me!\"","He lunged forward like a madman, trying to grab Han Mo and demand an answer—why was he doing this? Why ruin him?","But he was pinned to the ground instantly, followed by a stern warning: \"Don't resist unnecessarily. Resisting law enforcement will only add to your charges! Cooperate, or we will be forced to take measures in accordance with the law!\"","\"Let me go! Let me go! Han Mo! I'll kill you!\""]},{"number":80,"title":"Chapter 80: What a show-off you are","paragraphs":["He was seething with hatred, hating that Han Mo hadn't died, hating himself for not being more careful back then!","Hating his mother for being a mistress, and hating Han Changyong even more for having two sons!","He was so full of hate!","He had already decided to leave!","Just a few more days, only a few days. Once he sold the company and transferred all the money out, all of this would be over!","Han Mo looked down at him. He was sprawled on the ground in a sorry state, utterly unable to struggle.","A mocking smile curled at the corner of his mouth: \"Han Xuan, you brought all of this on yourself.\"","Han Xuan roared like a trapped beast: \"I'll kill you!!\"","\"Whack!\"","A solid slap landed on his head, and the police officer pressing him down scolded him sternly:","\"Behave yourself! Don't you know murder is against the law? Yelling about killing someone right in front of law enforcement? What do you take us for?\"","Han Xuan shut his mouth resentfully, but his eyes burned with indignation. It was just hitting someone with a car, hardly a big deal.","Intentional injury, minor injury could only get him three years at most.","Han Mo was perfectly fine, so he'd get three years at most. Later, he'd spend some money to grease some palms and get parole directly.","So he wasn't all that scared. In fact, his attitude was still cocky.","\"I didn't hit him. That video is AI-generated.\"","\"Fine, I hit him, but he begged me to. I had no choice, I had to agree.\"","\"We were acting, the camera was right behind the lens. Didn't you see it on the surveillance footage?\"","\"Actually, I was possessed. I'm a Martian, I'm here to save the Earth.\"","\"...\"","He spouted nonsense crazily, and the officer interrogating him furrowed his brows deeply: \"Confess properly! Stop talking nonsense! We have witnesses and physical evidence, you can't deny it!\"","Han Xuan shrugged shamelessly: \"Fine, I'll confess. Actually, I'm time-traveled from another world. Do you know about parallel universes? I'm Han Xuan from a parallel universe. My family was poor, my father was a drunk...\"","If He Huanhuan had heard him say that, she'd have called it plagiarism. He was basically describing her life story.","The officer's expression darkened even more: \"You really think we can't do anything to you?\"","Han Xuan grinned and raised an eyebrow: \"I want to see my lawyer.\"","He wanted to get his story straight with the lawyer. He could pay. As long as he didn't go to jail, he'd pay any amount.","Little did he know, his plans were doomed to fail.","No sooner had he been brought in for questioning than the police station received an anonymous email.","It contained a detailed record of all the evidence of Han Xuan's fraud and money laundering, including his contract with Brother Bao and all the transaction records.","Before nightfall, the police station had submitted all this physical evidence to the higher authorities.","Han Xuan didn't get his lawyer; instead, he got transferred to a higher-level department first.","He shouted uneasily: \"I want to see my lawyer! I want to see my lawyer!\"","The man who came shoved him into the car: \"Don't worry, you'll have plenty of chances to see him soon.\"","In front of the police car, an extended Lincoln slowly drove by.","Chen Jiarong sat in the back seat with his arm around Gu Chacha, watching Han Xuan being taken away.","Gu Chacha looked worried: \"Brother Bao, what will happen to him?\"","Chen Jiarong's tone was unreadable: \"What? Are you worried about him?\"","\"No...\" Gu Chacha shook her head: \"I'm afraid he'll drag us down with him. If he rats us out, we'll be in trouble...\"","She felt a nagging worry inside. After all, she was the one who had told Han Xuan about Han Mo's whereabouts. She feared that Han Xuan might throw caution to the wind and take everyone down with him.","A rough hand slid down from her shoulder: \"Don't worry, we have people above us. He won't say a word.\"","Gu Chacha leaned into him softly: \"I trust you...\"","Chen Jiarong kissed her ear: \"I remember your father is in real estate, right?\"","Gu Chacha nodded: \"Yes.\"","\"How about taking me to meet your father in a few days?\"","Gu Chacha hesitated: \"Han Xuan was just arrested, it doesn't feel right to bring you home so soon, does it?\"","She couldn't even imagine how her parents and older brother would see her if she brought him back.","They'd definitely think she was frivolous and had no self-respect.","She didn't want to go back. Not at all.","The big hand caressed her face with an undeniable pushiness: \"Just say I'm pursuing you. Be good, I have something to discuss with your father.\"","\"But...\"","The rest of her words were swallowed up as she saw the impatience in his eyes.","She obediently nodded: \"Then I'll go back and tell Mom and Dad, so they can prepare.\"","\"Good girl. Isn't that international piano competition in China coming up soon? I'll find a way to get you an award. How about that?\"","Gu Chacha's eyes immediately lit up: \"Really? Can you do that?\"","That was the most prestigious piano competition in the country. If she could win the championship, then she'd have truly made it!","She looked at Chen Jiarong with gleaming eyes: \"I'll go back tomorrow and tell my parents!\"","Chen Jiarong patted her head: \"As long as you're obedient, anything you want, I can give you.\"","The car sped through the city, drawing envious stares from the roadside.","\"Holy shit, an extended Lincoln!\"","A passerby was so envious he was almost drooling: \"If I could afford a car like that, I'd be picking up eight girls a month!\"","Liang Ye sighed: \"I have this car, but I still can't get a girl to date me.\"","The passerby rolled his eyes at him: \"You're such a poser!\"","His scooter wasn't even as new as his. How was he this full of it?","Liang Ye explained seriously: \"I'm not posing, I really do have one. My dad has one, and my brother has one too. But my dad's is old, a bit dated, doesn't look great...\"","The guy nearly rolled his eyes out of his head: \"If your family's that loaded, why are you riding a scooter? Drive the Lincoln over and show me!\"","Liang Ye thought seriously: \"My dad's probably playing mahjong right now, he definitely doesn't have time. My brother's probably about to get off work. If you want to see it, I'll call him over.\"","His earnest expression made the guy doubt himself. Could this dude actually own an extended Lincoln?","\"Uh, call your brother, I'll wait right here!\"","He was going to see whether or not Liang Ye actually had an extended Lincoln.","Liang Ye pulled out his phone and called his brother: \"Bro, what are you doing? Off work yet?\"","Liang Zheng sat at his desk preparing for a video conference: \"Not yet. What's up?\"","Liang Ye sighed: \"Bro, can you come see me? I'm feeling a bit down.\"","These past two days, the four of them had been squeezed into a tiny thirty-square-meter place, and it had been lively.","But just thinking about going home to an empty house, all alone, made him not want to go back.","He whined: \"Bro, come stay with me tonight, okay? Please?\"","He needed some love and care.","In the office, Liang Zheng's brows immediately furrowed. He stood up and strode out: \"What's wrong? What happened? Did someone bully you?\"","Liang Ye shook his head: \"Huanhuan and the others went back. I'm so lonely. I'm going to miss them...\"","The anxious figure suddenly stopped in his tracks: \"Went back? They all went back?\"","Liang Ye choked up: \"They all left. I'm home all by myself, boohoo...\"","His brother turned and walked back into the office: \"I've got a meeting to go to. You're an adult now. Stop being so childish.\"","\"Beep beep beep...\"","The phone was hung up instantly, and Liang Ye felt even more wronged: \"Wuwuwu... my brother isn't coming to pick me up...\"","The young guy's face twitched again and again. Damn, to show off to that extent—he had to admit, that was impressive!","Next time, he'd show off the same way!"]},{"number":81,"title":"Chapter 81: Bringing Beauty Home","paragraphs":["By the time the two of them finished giving their detailed statements with the police, it was already dark outside.","No sooner had they walked out of the police station than two figures came charging at them, sobbing uncontrollably.","Chen Yu was crying so hard he was hiccuping: \"Bro! Where the hell have you been these past few days?! I searched everywhere for you!\"","It really hurt—his dad had nearly beaten him to death!","Gu Jinghan, tears streaming down his face, lunged at He Huanhuan to hug her: \"Huanhuan! We don't have a home anymore! Mom and Dad have lost their minds, they don't care about you at all. From now on, I'll be your dad...\"","He Huanhuan shoved him away: \"Are you trying to pull one over on me?\"","What was this, suddenly moving up a generation?!","Gu Jinghan had a chest full of grievances he'd had nowhere to vent, and today he'd finally found his outlet. He clung to He Huanhuan and wailed:","\"Huanhuan, we're just unloved kids. When we were little, Mom and Dad were always biased—they only ever believed what Gu Chacha said. Anything I said was 'nonsense' or 'lying'... we're just pitiful, that's all...\"","That wail of \"pitiful\" was so tragic and loud it threw Chen Yu's sobbing completely off its rhythm.","Offended, Chen Yu sniffled: \"Second Young Master, it's my turn to cry now. Hold on a sec.\"","Gu Jinghan ignored him and cried even louder: \"Huanhuan! Let's run away from home! Let's make them never find us!\"","Chen Yu: This is provocation! Outright provocation! He could not lose!","He let out a howl at maximum volume: \"COUSIN!!!\"","Han Mo reached out and clamped a hand over his mouth: \"Stop singing mountain songs. Too noisy.\"","The stage instantly became Gu Jinghan's solo showcase: \"When Gu Chacha turned eighteen, Dad gave her ten million! When I turned eighteen, I only got five million! He's biased!\"","\"When Gu Chacha went to France, Dad said 'have fun!' When I went to France, Dad said I was out there running wild every day!\"","\"When Gu Chacha went to Antarctica to watch whales, Dad hired bodyguards to follow her. When I went to Antarctica to watch whales, Dad just booked me a spot on a national team group tour. I've suffered so much~~~\"","What exactly was so suffering about that?","Daggers of murderous glares shot at him from all directions, and He Huanhuan quietly took a step back. She'd never been to any of those places—don't drag her into this.","Gu Jinghan didn't notice the crowd's fury at all: \"When Gu Chacha went to Africa to see the Great Migration, Dad transferred her a million. When I went to Africa to see the Great Migration, he only gave me five hundred thousand! That trip I was so broke! So humiliated!\"","......","Forget the passersby—even He Huanhuan wanted to hit him now.","Five hundred thousand and he calls it \"broke\"? What about the middle-class people who start planning a year in advance and manage Africa's Great Migration with an average budget of thirty thousand per person? How are they supposed to live?","What about her, someone who stretches a two-hour walk just to go to the county seat? How is she supposed to survive that comparison?","Brother's grievance was taller than the sky, deeper than the sea: \"When Gu Chacha went to Egypt...\"","\"Why does everything Gu Chacha does, you have to do too? Are you a copycat?\"","A flash of bright red hair came storming across the road from the opposite side!","Qi Meili hadn't wanted to come over at first—she was afraid since she was technically an unregistered resident, she might draw trouble if the police noticed her.","But she absolutely couldn't listen to another word from Gu Jinghan!","Damn rich kid, she was going to fight him!","She zoomed up to Gu Jinghan, slapped him so hard he staggered aside, and said: \"Shut up, you rich—\"","\"Oh my god! Baby, are you okay? Does your head hurt? Want me to blow on it?\"","Gu Jinghan hadn't even steadied himself when she pulled him back over.","Qi Meili gently stroked his head: \"Baby, I was way too rough just now~ Go on, tell me slowly. How is your dad biased? That nasty old man, how could he be so mean? Want me to go hit him for you later?\"","Gu Jinghan suddenly felt goosebumps all over. Why did he feel a chill down his back?","He instinctively turned to look—whoa! When had his big brother shown up?!","His brother stood at the intersection with a grim face, staring at him with heavy eyes.","Also looking black as thunder beside his brother—was that Liang Zheng?","Liang Ye's older brother? Why was HE here?","Gu Jinghan shrank his neck and timidly called out: \"Brother...\"","Gu Jingchen didn't even look at him. With long strides, he walked straight up to He Huanhuan and asked: \"All done? Tired?\"","He Huanhuan nodded: \"All done. Not tired.\"","Gu Jingchen patted her head: \"Come home with me. I had the kitchen make your favorite dishes.\"","Standing beside He Huanhuan, Qi Meili nearly fainted from happiness.","So handsome. So attentive. So gentle.","The charm of an older man—who gets it? She gets it!","She was about to speak when a shadow suddenly fell over her, completely engulfing her.","Startled, she looked up to see Liang Zheng glaring at her with a black face: \"So THIS is your 'socially anxious husband'? Since when is Gu the Second married?\"","His gaze swept over Gu Jinghan with a scrutinizing look, and Gu Jinghan inexplicably felt a chill run through his body.","He forced out a smile: \"Brother Zheng, good evening...\"","Damn, the pressure! He was crying about his dad being biased—what did Liang Zheng have to be upset about?","Wait a second... did that mean Liang Ye's stinginess wasn't just his personality, but actually because of family favoritism?","Oh?","Major gossip!","His eyes lit up instantly, but under Liang Zheng's oppressive presence, he sneakily averted his gaze.","Liang Zheng's face darkened further. What was he skulking around smirking about? His shifty eyes kept darting toward Qi Meili like he was up to no good.","He stepped to the side, inserting himself between the two of them, and lowered his head to interrogate Qi Meili: \"Yesterday you said I was your husband. Today it's Gu the Second? Miss Qi, exactly how many husbands do you have?\"","Qi Meili blinked: \"I just called him 'baby,' not 'husband.' You misheard.\"","\"Is there a difference?\"","Qi Meili nodded: \"Of course there's a difference. 'Husband' is too stiff. Calling him 'baby' is more intimate~\"","......","So she was saying he ranked below Gu the Second?","Liang Zheng was so angry he almost laughed out loud. In all his life, he'd never felt this defeated.","But Qi Meili wasn't paying attention to him at all. The girl was staring blissfully at Gu Jingchen: \"Big Brother is really so gentle, I love it~\"","Liang Zheng: ...Why was she dragging Gu Jingchen into this too? Exactly how many men did she love?","Well, uncountably many, of course—as long as they were handsome, they were all her loves.","His face was at rock-bottom gloom, and Qi Meili paid it zero attention. She just patted him: \"Move aside, you're blocking my view.\"","......","Now he truly understood what \"out with the new, in with the old\" felt like. He shot a glance at Gu Jingchen. Gentle? It was just average.","He tried to soften his expression: \"Where do you live? I'll—\"","Before he could finish, He Huanhuan yanked Qi Meili in front of Gu Jingchen: \"Big Brother! This is my best friend Meili! I can bring her home with me, right?\"","Gu Jingchen smiled and nodded: \"Of course.\"","A warm smile curved at the corners of his lips as he looked at Qi Meili: \"Meili, is it? Huanhuan lived through a lot of hardship before. Thank you for taking care of her. I hope you'll give us the chance to host you properly.\"","Qi Meili's voice instantly softened: \"Of course. Thank you, gege~\"","She tried to hold back her grin, but it was a total failure.","The gentle type—in all her years in the wild club scene, she'd never met one!","Jackpot. Absolute jackpot."]},{"number":82,"title":"Chapter 82: You Favor Sons Over Daughters","paragraphs":["Gu Jingchen turned to look at Han Mo and said, \"We're going back first. Come to our place for dinner tomorrow. We'll have a welcome feast for you.\"","Han Mo looked at him in surprise. Gu Jingchen had always been rather lukewarm towards him, so this was quite unusual.","Their gazes met in the air. The next second, they exchanged a knowing smile.","Han Mo nodded. \"See you tomorrow.\"","\"Okay.\"","Gu Jingchen then looked at Liang Zheng. \"Is your matter difficult? Do you need any help?\"","They had met by chance on the way. Liang Zheng said he happened to be coming to handle some business, so they came together.","As for what business Liang Zheng was going to handle, Gu Jingchen didn't ask.","The relationship between their two families was just so - so. It would be better not to talk too much.","Now it was a good opportunity to ask. If there was anything he could help with, the relationship could be improved.","But little did he know that his plan was doomed to fail.","Liang Zheng actually had nothing to do. He didn't know what was wrong with him; he just drove here uncontrollably.","It was only now that his rationality finally returned.","What on earth was he doing?","Was he acting like a mindless fool and accusing someone of something?","He quietly took a half - step back and put on a polite smile on his face. \"It's a small matter. I can handle it myself.\"","After saying that, he stepped into the police station without the slightest hesitation.","Failing to build a better relationship, Gu Jingchen wasn't discouraged. He looked at He Huanhuan and Qi Meili gently. \"Let's go home. The food is almost ready.\"","He Huanhuan pulled Meili and started walking. \"Meili, you'll sleep with me tonight. My room on the third floor is so big that you can even run laps in it...\"","The two girls walked away so briskly that they didn't even remember to say goodbye to Han Mo.","Chen Yu walked up to Han Mo in a teasing way. \"Brother, you two don't seem to be making any progress. Well, it's your own fault. You had impure motives at the beginning. It's normal that she ignores you... Hey, brother! Where are you going?\"","Han Mo sneered. \"I'm going home to let Uncle beat you up.\"","\"Please no? Brother? Brother?\"","...","At the Gu family's place, Gu Chengye and Jiang Yulan were sitting in the living room calmly.","Jiang Yulan looked worried. \"I wonder if Huanhuan has suffered any hardships outside these days?\"","Gu Chengye smiled and patted her hand. \"Don't worry. That Han Mo knows what he's doing. He won't let Huanhuan suffer.\"","Jiang Yulan couldn't help but let out a snort. \"You think highly of him, but I don't think he's that good.\"","Han Mo came from a complicated family. He had too many things on his mind, which was not good.","She would prefer Huanhuan to find a boy from a simpler family with a purer mind.","She thought the second son of the Liang family was quite good, but he was really stingy.","These days, when chasing a girl, you either have to be sincere or be willing to spend money.","You have to have at least one of these qualities.","He was so stingy that he brought a big love - shaped object given for free by the neighborhood committee when he came to visit. It was so shabby. It would have been better if he didn't bring anything at all.","Involuntarily thinking of Han Mo's generosity, Jiang Yulan sighed. Why couldn't the two of them combine their good points?","Of course, that was impossible. There are rarely perfect things in the world. If you have all the good qualities, what about others?","But whether it was Han Mo or Liang Ye, they were both better than Han Xuan.","Thinking of Han Xuan and Chacha, Jiang Yulan felt like she wanted to let out ten long sighs. She wondered what was wrong with Chacha. Why did she fall for Han Xuan?","That boy didn't have a single merit even if you peeled off his skin.","While her thoughts were still wandering, Gu Chengye, with his sharp eyes, noticed the movement outside. He quickly pulled her up. \"They're back, they're back...\"","The two of them went out to greet them. Two eye - catching heads popped out of the car one after another.","One was colorful, and the other was a bright red.","Gu Chengye was a little dazed for a moment. Why did this scene seem so familiar?","\"Damn! Princess little sister! Huanhuan, you're like the princess in that drama!\"","Qi Meili was completely stunned when she saw the huge manor in front of her. She had thought the Gu family was rich, but her poor imagination could only picture a big flat in the city center.","A manor?","It was so high - class!","This was what it was like to be a princess!","He Huanhuan nodded wildly. \"Scary, right? Five people live in such a big house. If someone got killed here, they might stink before anyone knew!\"","Qi Meili said, \"I know! I saw it in a short drama! The stupid parents were biased towards the fake daughter, and the real daughter starved to death in her own room and maggots grew on her body. They still thought she was just being angry! Damn! It made me so mad when I watched it!\"","Gu Chengye thought to himself: Is she hinting at something about me?","Without a doubt, Qi Meili's gaze had already swept towards him. The girl greeted them very politely, \"Hello, uncle and aunt.\"","Her politeness made Gu Chengye and his wife feel a little flattered. Remembering that when He Huanhuan first came to their home, she had even called them \"old folks\".","\"Yeah, yeah... Hello, hello.\"","The couple was very respectful of her red hair and tattoos. They replied very politely.","Sure enough, Qi Meili then asked, \"Your family is so rich. How could you have mixed up your children? Are you being biased against girls?\"","...","Gu Chengye's lips twitched. \"How could that be? Our family has always treated all the children equally.\"","\"Tsk.\"","Qi Meili curled her lips. \"You're just kidding. If you treated the children equally, why did you let your son manage the company instead of your daughter? You're just biased against girls.\"","Gu Chengye's face changed slightly. After hesitating for a second, he explained gently, \"Girls should be pampered. Our family has enough money. As long as she's happy, that's enough.\"","\"Tsk.\"","Qi Meili let out another cold snort. \"Then why don't you let the eldest brother be happy?\"","It was still because of the bias against girls!","The two older sons weren't even married yet, so why was the girl already being arranged for a marriage alliance?","As long as she's happy? It was all nonsense.","Happiness wasn't just about spending money. It also meant cultivating her hobbies and abilities and planning her future.","In this regard, not to mention He Huanhuan, even Gu Chacha hadn't received such treatment.","Gu Chengye's face turned even darker. \"Girl, you...\"","Before he could finish speaking, Gu Jingchen immediately stepped forward and looked at Meili with a smile. \"It's getting late. Let's go in and have dinner.\"","Meili instantly squinted her eyes happily. \"Okay, okay~\"","The smile on Gu Jingchen's lips deepened. He had noticed before that Huanhuan's friend, although very sharp - tongued, was actually a real face - control person.","She was quite easy to handle.","He led them into the dining room and deliberately arranged for Qi Meili to sit next to Jinghan. He wanted her to focus on looking at the handsome faces and talk less.","It had to be said that his arrangement was quite ingenious. He sat right across from Meili, and Gu Jinghan sat between Meili and their parents.","Every time Meili wanted to say something, when she looked up and saw his smiling face, she would immediately be in a daze.","When she remembered again and turned her head, she saw Gu Jinghan's perfect side - profile, and she would be in a daze again.","She was in a daze throughout the meal. Before she knew it, she had already reached the third floor.","She flopped down on the sofa and slapped her thigh hard. \"It's the beauty trap! Your eldest brother set a beauty trap for me!\"","He Huanhuan laughed at her. \"You just realized it?\"","Qi Meili said happily, \"He was so thoughtful. I love him even more.\"","From now on, she wouldn't hang out in the so - called cool crowd anymore. She only loved gentle and elite men.","The quality was so high!"]},{"number":83,"title":"Chapter 83: I'm Bringing a Friend Along","paragraphs":["He Huanhuan flopped down beside her and asked curiously, \"But why did you suddenly bring up favoring boys over girls?\"","Qi Meili reached out and tapped her on the head. \"Idiot, because that's exactly what he's doing—favoring boys over girls!\"","She sat up straight and asked He Huanhuan seriously, \"Think about it—aren't your two brothers older than you? And neither of them is married yet.\"","He Huanhuan nodded. \"Right.\"","\"That's exactly the problem!\" Qi Meili snapped her fingers with a look of great wisdom. \"Compared to you, aren't they way better suited for a marriage alliance? Their ages are right too—you're only twenty!\"","\"This is textbook favoritism toward boys, because marriage alliance is the only use you have to them.\"","Qi Meili snorted coldly. \"That old geezer is rotten to the core!\"","He Huanhuan nodded. \"I know.\"","It was just that at first, she thought she wouldn't stay in this world for long. She thought she'd still go back, so she didn't make a big deal out of it.","\"But things are different now.\"","She looked at Qi Meili with total seriousness. \"Meili, now that you're here, everything's changed.\"","She could feel it—they probably couldn't go back so easily anymore. She wasn't just drifting through this world in a daze anymore; she might have to live here with Meili for a very, very long time.","So she needed to plan properly for herself.","She leaned against Qi Meili's shoulder. \"Meili, I'm so glad you're here.\"","She wasn't alone anymore, and that was wonderful.","Qi Meili wrapped an arm around her and pulled her close. \"Don't worry, I'm always here!\"","They were best friends, and no matter what ghosts and monsters or scheming rich girls came their way, they'd face them together!","Early the next morning, Gu Chacha drove straight back to the Gu family estate.","She sat demurely beside Jiang Yulan, listening to her question: \"I heard from Jingchen that Han Mo's car accident this time was caused by Han Xuan?\"","Gu Chacha nodded, her expression downcast. \"It was him. He was too impulsive, so...\"","\"Chacha.\" Jiang Yulan frowned deeply and grabbed her hand. \"If he can go that far against his own brother, that kind of man is no good. You can't stay with him!\"","Gu Chacha blinked, and tears streamed down her face instantly. \"Mom, he tricked me. But he's been taken away now—I won't pay him any more attention...\"","Seeing her cry so pitifully, Jiang Yulan quickly pulled her into a hug to soothe her. \"Silly child, I'm glad you're willing to listen. I was worried you'd be angry with me.\"","\"Of course not, Mom. I know you truly care about me.\"","Gu Chacha looked up at Jiang Yulan between sobs. \"Mom, since sister is back, shouldn't we throw her a welcome dinner?\"","Jiang Yulan nodded. \"Your eldest brother has already arranged it. We're going to Junyue Ting at noon to welcome Huanhuan and Han Mo.\"","Gu Chacha leaned obediently against Jiang Yulan's shoulder. \"Mom, can I bring a friend along?\"","Jiang Yulan smiled and nodded. \"Of course! Huanhuan's friend is staying at the house too. One more pair of chopsticks won't make a difference.\"","She assumed the friend Gu Chacha mentioned was some girl she was close to. She never imagined that the moment Han Xuan was locked up, Gu Chacha would already have someone new.","Gu Chacha didn't say anything more, because she feared her parents wouldn't approve. She planned to have Brother Bao show up directly at Junyue Ting at noon. By then, with so many people around, her parents would have no choice but to go along with it even if they weren't happy.","For now, though, her attention had drifted to He Huanhuan. \"Sister's friend? When did sister make a new friend?\"","Jiang Yulan smiled. \"She's an old friend from Huanhuan's hometown. She used to look after Huanhuan a lot.\"","Gu Chacha's eyes flickered. \"Is she staying at the house now?\"","Jiang Yulan nodded. \"The two of them are very close. Huanhuan said no need to prepare a separate room—they'll share a bed.\"","Gu Chacha bit her lip and said nothing more.","But the envy in her heart couldn't help but sprout. That third floor used to be hers. Even He Huanhuan's friend could stay there now, yet she herself had been completely cut off from it.","She forced the bitterness back down deep inside. She told herself none of that mattered anymore.","She had already moved forward. She was living a bigger, bolder life now.","Meanwhile, He Huanhuan was just like her old self—obediently under the family's thumb, a pawn in a marriage alliance.","Get married, have kids, lead a completely ordinary life.","That was the kind of life she wouldn't live for even one more day.","Everything she wanted, she would get on her own.","She pulled out her phone and sent Brother Bao the address for Junyue Ting. A reply came back almost instantly: an OK.","She lowered her eyes, listening to Jiang Yulan chatter on about mundane family matters.","On her phone screen, Brother Bao's WeChat was pinned to the very top.","International piano competition—she was going to win that prize.","She would become a world-renowned artist, living her whole life under the spotlight, basking in admiring and envious gazes.","She let out a quiet sigh. Thank you, Han Xuan.","If he hadn't taken her to Southeast Asia, she'd never have found this path.","It was dangerous, sure, but it was glamorous.","She loved the feeling of the spotlight on her. She, the center of all eyes, would shine like this forever.","The elevator made a mechanical hum, and a smile instantly bloomed on her face as she turned with Jiang Yulan to look.","In the elevator, He Huanhuan and Qi Meili stepped out, laughing.","Gu Chacha rose gracefully. \"Sister, is this your friend? How...\"","The compliment she'd prepared died in her throat the moment she saw Qi Meili.","As He Huanhuan's spiritual guide, Qi Meili's aesthetic truly leaned into punk rebellion.","Her body was covered in dazzling tattoos that nearly blinded Gu Chacha.","So much yellow, so much blue, so much red...","How could one person have so many colors on them?","Was she a dye vat reincarnated?","Qi Meili grinned and waved at her. \"Hey there, fake heiress.\"","Gu Chacha's face stiffened, and then she caught sight of the big peony tattoo on Qi Meili's hand, and froze again.","\"Um, miss...\" She tried to say something, but her eyes kept darting around Qi Meili's tattoos, completely unable to focus.","There were just too many focal points on her body!","Qi Meili plopped herself down right next to the two of them, looking supremely relaxed, and asked, \"When do we eat?\"","Last night she and He Huanhuan had gotten so excited chatting that they'd talked until the wee hours, and they'd slept straight through until now. She was starving.","Jiang Yulan tried her best to sit up straight, like a student called on by the teacher. \"I had the maid save you both some breakfast. Why don't you have a little something to tie you over, and then we'll head straight to Junyue Ting, alright?\"","She sat stiffly, not daring to even glance at Qi Meili.","Last night it had been dark, so she hadn't noticed Qi Meili's tattoos at all.","Now in the light—lord, it was terrifying!","The two of them went into the dining room and found Gu Jinghan sitting at the table in silence, eating his meal.","Seeing them, he raised an eyebrow quickly. \"See that? That nuisance is back again.\"","He couldn't stand talking to Gu Chacha, so he'd come straight to the dining room after getting up.","And when he'd heard Gu Chacha was heading to Junyue Ting, he'd almost decided not to go at all.","If it weren't for...","His eyes rolled around slyly, and he leaned in, gossip written all over his face. \"Guess what I just overheard? Gu Chacha's bringing a friend to lunch at Junyue Ting.\"","Definitely not any real friend, he thought. He had to go and see the show for himself!"]},{"number":84,"title":"Chapter 84: A Family Cannot Have Two Daughters","paragraphs":["The three of them dawdled in the dining room for over an hour, until Jiang Yulan came to hurry them along: \"Why are you eating so slowly? It's time to head to Junyue Court.\"","Only then did they get up and head out, directly boarding Gu Jinghan's BYD without saying a single word to Gu Chacha.","Gu Chacha didn't mind, though. She and Gu Jinghan had never gotten along since childhood—they never spoke when they met.","Only...","She glanced at the car, a mocking smirk curling at the corner of her mouth.","To please He Huanhuan, Gu Jinghan had actually gone and bought a cheap car. How tacky.","When the car arrived at Junyue Court, Brother Bao was already waiting at the main entrance.","He carried two gift boxes in his hands, a fervent smile plastered on his face.","The moment Old Mr. Gu stepped out of the car, Brother Bao strode over and enthusiastically shook his hand: \"Hello, Uncle. I've admired you for a long time. Truly an honor to finally meet you today.\"","Gu Chengye was taken aback: \"And you are?\"","Today was a family dinner—no one else had been told. How did this man know to wait here?","Brother Bao let out a hearty laugh: \"Hello, Uncle. I'm Chacha's friend, Chen Jiarong.\"","\"Friend?\"","Gu Chengye frowned and gave him a once-over. Dark skin, slightly protruding cheekbones—a typical Southeast Asian look.","He knitted his brows and glanced at Gu Chacha: \"Chacha, this is your friend?\"","This Mr. Chen looked to be about thirty-five or thirty-six. How could he be Chacha's friend?","Gu Chacha stepped forward, linking her arm through Gu Chengye's in a cajoling manner: \"Dad, Jiarong is Malaysian. He recently came to Jiangcheng to expand his business.\"","Gu Chengye's expression shifted slightly, clearly displeased.","He stared at Gu Chacha with a heavy gaze: \"Your friend?\"","The accusatory tone was unmistakable. Gu Chacha blinked, looking aggrieved and timid: \"Dad, what's wrong?\"","She didn't answer Gu Chengye's question directly, just wanted to play the victim and muddle through.","But Chen Jiarong didn't give her that chance. He walked over to her with a smile: \"Uncle, I'm currently pursuing Chacha. I hope we can become family in the future.\"","Whoa. The moment he said that, three pairs of eyes instantly locked onto him.","Gu Jinghan's eyes were like an infrared scanner, sweeping over him twice in three seconds.","Then he gave a satisfied shake of his head and muttered to He Huanhuan: \"Ugly, old, but rich.\"","The watch on his wrist could buy a decent three-bedroom apartment in Jiangcheng.","He Huanhuan and Qi Meili stared wide-eyed: \"That watch costs that much? Must be a few hundred thousand, right?\"","Gu Jinghan held up two fingers: \"Over two million.\"","Qi Meili's eyes nearly popped out: \"Jiangcheng real estate is that expensive?!\"","He Huanhuan immediately pulled out her phone to check—her total savings were around five hundred thousand. They'd been transferred to her by Han Mo and her two older brothers, and since she had nowhere to spend them, she'd just saved it all.","Originally, she and Meili had planned to buy an apartment in the city center and move out on their own.","Two small-town girls who only frequented fancy circles in their county had no idea how much a place in Jiangcheng actually cost.","Five hundred thousand could buy an old three-bedroom in a small county town.","In Jiangcheng, it couldn't even make them Liang Ye's neighbor.","His run-down place was over nine hundred thousand.","The two exchanged a bitter look. No matter how grand the manor was, it wasn't the same as having their own place!","Gu Chacha was in worse shape than both of them at the moment. Gu Chengye's face had gone sour to the extreme—almost black.","What friend!","This was her new boyfriend!","So old, and so...","Gu Chengye gave Chen Jiarong a blunt once-over: triangular eyes, sclera showing beneath the pupils—a textbook villain's face.","The viciousness in his gaze was unmistakable. He couldn't just be an ordinary businessman.","He said coldly to Chen Jiarong: \"Today is a family dinner, so we won't—\"","But before he could finish, Chen Jiarong cut him off with a genial smile: \"I know—the welcome dinner for Sister Chacha, right? I specially brought a gift for her.\"","With that, he walked straight up to He Huanhuan: \"I heard you went missing for a few days. You must have suffered a lot. A small token of appreciation—please don't think less of it.\"","He held the small gift bag out to He Huanhuan, and Gu Jinghan's eyes immediately lit up. A Patek Philippe 7118—that's over seven hundred thousand!","He couldn't help but lean in and whisper to He Huanhuan: \"Can I borrow it later?\"","Luxury cars and fancy watches—the playthings of the rich.","The family had luxury cars; Gu Jinghan could drive them anytime.","But he didn't have nearly as many fancy watches.","He was unreliable, so Old Mr. Gu didn't let him touch the company.","He could only collect a monthly allowance from the family. The amount wasn't small, but his spending habits were even bigger.","A decent watch easily cost hundreds of thousands, even millions. He hadn't reached that level of extravagance yet.","He stared at Chen Jiarong with longing. If Chen Jiarong gave him a watch too, he'd happily package Gu Chacha up and hand her over.","He didn't have the authority to make that call, but damn it, he'd make it anyway!","Right now, this instant—take that watch off and give it to him!","While he was still being greedy, He Huanhuan shoved the watch back: \"I don't like wearing watches. Too tight.\"","Chen Jiarong looked at her and smiled: \"Chacha told me you had a rough life before. Consider this my, or rather Chacha's, apology to you. Keep it.\"","Gu Chengye's face went instantly black. How dare an outsider meddle in his family's affairs?","His lips twitched downward hard. He stepped forward to intervene.","But He Huanhuan refused, righteous and firm: \"Who even are you? What's a crappy watch supposed to compensate? Our old man here is way more generous than you!\"","She then turned to Gu Chengye with a beaming smile: \"Right, old man?\"","Gu Chengye's eyes instantly filled with warmth: \"Of course. Dad will transfer you the money when we get back.\"","He Huanhuan's eyes sparkled: \"Then I want five hundred thousand!\"","Gu Chengye nodded with a chuckle: \"Deal.\"","Gu Jinghan panicked and quickly whispered in her ear: \"You little idiot! The watch he's giving you is worth over seven hundred thousand!\"","Ask Dad for more!","And while you're at it, get some for me too—I want to buy a Patek Philippe to play around with.","He Huanhuan immediately changed her tune: \"Then I want seven hundred thousand!\"","Gu Chengye laughed indulgently: \"Alright, alright... Even a million, Dad would still give it to you.\"","Gu Jinghan flashed a sycophantic smile: \"Dad, I want a million too~\"","Gu Chengye shot him a glare: \"You're not young anymore. All you know is how to spend money—what else?\"","......","Whether she was the real daughter or fake, he was the fake son, wasn't he? Huh?","The mood eased considerably. The family laughed and chatted as they headed toward their private room.","Chen Jiarong followed behind them firmly, holding the watch, with Gu Chacha timidly by his side: \"Brother Bao, I'm sorry...\"","Chen Jiarong wrapped an arm around her shoulder: \"Remember, in Jiangcheng, my name is Chen Jiarong.\"","Gu Chacha nodded obediently: \"Yes, Jiarong.\"","Chen Jiarong leaned in and murmured: \"A little cold shoulder is nothing.\"","Gu Chacha couldn't help but tear up: \"It's all because I'm not the Gu family's real daughter, making you suffer all this cold treatment...\"","\"Heh heh...\"","A flash of ruthlessness crossed Chen Jiarong's eyes: \"Chacha, you've hit the nail on the head. The Gu family can't have two daughters.\""]},{"number":85,"title":"Chapter 85: You Two Definitely Slept Together","paragraphs":["He said it lightly, but Gu Chacha's heart jolted with alarm.","She knew he wasn't joking.","Back when Han Xuan had taken her to Southeast Asia, on the second floor of that compound, she had seen what happened to those people.","Human life meant less than ants to him.","She hesitated for a moment. \"There's no need, right?\"","It wasn't that she liked He Huanhuan. She had been the little princess of the Gu family for twenty years, and then suddenly she was the outsider.","Everything that had belonged to her—her parents' love, her eldest brother's care—had suddenly turned to foam.","Naturally, she felt bitter, and she didn't like He Huanhuan.","She wished He Huanhuan had never appeared, but she had never wanted He Huanhuan dead.","She clenched her hands. Murder was against the law. Any move would leave evidence behind.","It was too dangerous!","What she regretted most these past few days was giving Han Xuan information about Han Mo that day.","She shouldn't have put herself in such danger.","The money laundering had always been handled by Han Xuan, and those funds had never passed through her hands.","Even if Han Xuan later implicated her, she wouldn't qualify as an accomplice.","She had only accepted his sponsorship and organized many concerts.","She had never known what he was up to. She was innocent.","But killing someone was different—criminal cases are never closed. She didn't want to carry the shadow of murder on her conscience forever.","It was too terrifying.","\"Don't be afraid. She won't die in the country.\"","Chen Jiarong pulled her closer. \"You know where my territory is. I'll take her out and kill her.\"","Gu Chacha frowned at him. \"You mean...\"","Take He Huanhuan abroad to be killed?","A smile curled at the corner of Chen Jiarong's mouth. \"I still want to do good business in Jiangcheng. How could I do something so heinous here?\"","Gu Chacha was uneasy. \"But how are you going to get her out of the country?\"","He Huanhuan was a living person, not a puppet to be pushed around. Sending her abroad wasn't something you could just order in passing.","Chen Jiarong led her through the door of the private room. \"Don't worry. I have my ways.\"","Inside the private room, Gu Jingchen and Han Mo had already arrived. The two were sitting on separate sofas, talking quietly.","When they saw the newcomers enter, they quickly stood up.","\"Hello, Auntie and Uncle.\"","Han Mo stepped forward to greet each of them, and when his eyes swept over Chen Jiarong, who had entered behind them, his gaze trembled violently.","Gu Chengye smiled and asked him, \"Xiao Han, why are you here so early?\"","Han Mo forced a smile. \"Nothing much to do at home, so I came on ahead.\"","Then, as naturally as could be, he walked over to He Huanhuan's side and gave Chen Jiarong a puzzled look before asking, \"And this is?\"","Gu Jinghan grinned and helped introduce him. \"Chacha's new friend.\"","Han Mo nodded at Chen Jiarong. \"Hello.\"","Chen Jiarong's face broke into a warm smile. \"Hello!\"","Han Mo quickly averted his gaze and didn't engage further.","After the greetings, everyone took their seats.","Qi Meili sat down next to He Huanhuan, and beside her sat Chen Jiarong.","Chen Jiarong smiled at her. \"I didn't get the chance to ask earlier—who are you?\"","Qi Meili glanced at him. \"I'm Huanhuan's good friend. The best kind.\"","Chen Jiarong nodded. \"That's clear to see.\"","His appraising gaze swept over Qi Meili's face, then over He Huanhuan's.","He felt satisfied deep down—young and pretty. He could take them back to the compound to make money for him.","A plan quickly formed in his mind, and his smile grew even wider.","But then he heard Qi Meili's disdainful voice: \"Why are you grinning like such a lecher? I don't like ugly people.\"","......","Chen Jiarong's smile vanished. \"You might be misunderstanding. I didn't mean anything—\"","Qi Meili snorted. \"Are you kidding me? You think I'm some fresh rookie? You reek of filth and dogs, it's disgusting!\"","Gu Chacha frowned. \"Sister Meili, how can you talk about Brother Jiarong like that? He was just being kind...\"","\"Pfft.\"","Qi Meili rolled her eyes. \"You've slept with him, so of course you can't smell the filth on him.\"","Gu Chacha's face changed dramatically. \"Sister Meili! What nonsense are you talking about!\"","In front of her parents and her eldest brother, she had always been the obedient good girl. How could it be possible that the moment Han Xuan got locked up, she'd already be in bed with another man?","Her eyes instantly reddened. \"Sister Meili, this is misogyny—\"","Qi Meili pursed her lips. \"Misogyny my ass! One whiff and I can tell you two definitely slept together last night!\"","Her tears dried instantly. Gu Chacha stared at Qi Meili in terror. \"You can actually smell that???\"","She and Chen Jiarong had indeed slept together last night, but how on earth could something like that be smelled?!","She wasn't a dog!","Her terrified reaction said everything, and Qi Meili giggled. \"I was just guessing, sweetie. I've got a sharp tongue—don't hold it against big sis, yeah?\"","\"You!\"","Gu Chacha's face flushed crimson in an instant. She had been tricked!","She guiltily turned to look at Gu Chengye and his wife, and both their faces were extremely sour.","Especially Gu Chengye—his face was dark enough to drip ink.","He cast a heavy glance at Gu Chacha. \"You said before that you had performances and it was inconvenient to live at home, so you insisted on moving out...\"","\"Dad...\"","Gu Chacha explained in a wronged tone, \"Most of the performances are in the city center. It really is inconvenient.\"","Gu Jinghan sneered. \"We have drivers at home. How is anywhere inconvenient? You don't even get carsick. Stop pretending!\"","\"Second Brother!\"","A tear slid down the corner of her eye. \"You don't have a job, so of course you wouldn't know how exhausting an extra half-hour of commuting is. I have to rehearse every day, I have to go over performance schedules... I just want to spend less time on the road every day. Is that wrong?\"","She had always been good at playing the victim. With her tearful, rain-and-willow act, she instantly softened the hearts of both elders.","Jiang Yulan's face was full of concern. \"Oh, alright, alright—stop crying. Living in the city center is indeed more convenient...\"","Jiang Yulan had spoken up for her, and Gu Chengye didn't want to go against her, so he didn't press further.","But a knot of anger was stuck in his chest, and he couldn't let it out easily.","Out of the corner of his eye, he caught sight of Gu Jinghan, whose eyes were bulging with indignation, and the old man's fury finally found its outlet:","\"And you! Bumming around all day, what kind of example is that?! Your little sister's private matters are none of your business to gossip about! Keep running your mouth, and don't ever ask me for money again!\"","......","Gu Jinghan: Wait, what the hell does this have to do with him?","And besides, when had he ever gossiped about Gu Chacha's private affairs?","He was quick-tempered, so he leapt up immediately. \"When the hell did I gossip?! Her and Han Xuan at my—\"","\"Jinghan!\"","Gu Jingchen suddenly cut in, interrupting his outburst. \"Sit down and eat.\"","\"Brother! I clearly—\"","Gu Jinghan was furious. Gu Chacha was constantly booking hotel rooms with Han Xuan, and they were at the hotel he owned, no less!","Gu Jingchen shot him a warning look. \"Sit down. Eat.\"","Only then did he realize—he'd almost blurted out that he'd been eavesdropping on Gu Chacha's hotel room visits.","If that got out, this meal would be ruined for sure.","And besides, based on past experience—","If the truth came out, whether Gu Chacha would suffer was still up in the air, but he was definitely getting his allowance cut off!","But he'd already built up the momentum to explode, and he couldn't just deflate so pathetically, could he?","That would be such a loss of face!","He didn't know whether to stand or sit, and in the end, he shot Gu Chacha a furious glare. \"You've got a thing for ugly! I despise you!\""]},{"number":86,"title":"Chapter 86: She Has Only Beauty and Sex","paragraphs":["A perfectly good meal turned deeply uncomfortable — though that discomfort certainly didn't include He Huanhuan and Qi Meili.","“Meili, this crab is expensive, let's eat more of this.”","“Oh wow! It's super sweet!”","“Well, that's why it's pricey!”","The two chatted away, heads together, taking turns feeding each other bites, eating with pure, unbridled joy.","At the side, Chen Jiarong watched them devour their food, his mind racing with calculations.","These two clearly haven't seen much of the world or spent big money. People like that love little bargains.","All I have to do is dangle something tempting, and getting them out of the country is a matter of minutes.","At the thought, a faint, barely noticeable smile tugged at the corner of his mouth.","His ancestral home was in the south; his grandfather had moved overseas, and the family had always been in a trade that wasn't exactly respectable but was highly profitable.","But the last few years had been hard on the business. Domestic crackdowns were relentless, and they'd teamed up with foreign authorities to bust several of their operations.","Every year, the bribes he paid out grew larger while the profits shrank.","He needed to find himself a new path.","The Gu family had three generations of deep roots in Jiangcheng, and they'd always maintained good relations with those in power.","If he could get in with the Gu family, he could plant himself firmly on domestic soil.","Once his domestic ventures took off, he could cut all ties with the overseas operations.","Then he could become, completely and utterly, Chen Jiarong the respectable Malaysian businessman, with no trace of his past left to haunt him.","But Gu Chacha wasn't the Gu family's biological daughter, and that was a problem.","Blood was a strange and powerful thing. With He Huanhuan around, the Gu family wasn't necessarily willing to accept him.","If they lost what they'd just recovered, the grief and love would all be redirected onto Gu Chacha.","That would work in his favor.","He cast another glance at He Huanhuan, still buried in her food. When we meet again at the compound, I'll apologize to her properly.","Beside He Huanhuan, Han Mo's face was grim.","He was certain: Chen Jiarong had looked at Huanhuan several times, and there was something deeply wrong in his eyes.","What was he planning?","After the meal, Gu Chengye and his wife went for a stroll in the hotel garden to digest. Gu Jinghan stuck to his brother's side, grumbling and complaining in a low voice.","Han Mo shot one look at Chen Jiarong, then turned and walked out.","He waited in the corridor for half a minute before Chen Jiarong pushed the door open as expected: “Master Han, we finally meet.”","Han Mo's face was cold: “Do I know you?”","Chen Jiarong smirked teasingly: “If you didn't know me, why would you be waiting for me here?”","Han Mo's expression grew even colder: “You're on domestic soil now. Keep your dirty tricks to yourself. If you so much as lay a finger on He Huanhuan, I'll make you regret it.”","Chen Jiarong blinked, his tone turning suggestive: “Didn't you just say you don't know me? Then how do you know about my tricks?”","Han Mo turned to look out at the courtyard, his voice full of warning: “If you want to stay in this country and live well, behave yourself.”","Chen Jiarong smiled: “Don't worry. She's going to be my future sister-in-law.”","Han Mo shot him a cold glare: “You'd better keep your word.”","“Han Mo!”","He Huanhuan stood at the doorway, eyes bright, calling him: “What are you doing standing out there? Get over here!”","The coldness in Han Mo's eyes vanished instantly. He nodded: “Alright.”","After firing one last warning look at Chen Jiarong, he left without hesitation and stepped back into the private room.","He Huanhuan frowned at him: “Why were you talking to Chen Jiarong? Do you two know each other?”","She didn't like this Chen Jiarong. He gave her a worse feeling than Han Xuan.","There was something about his eyes — murky and sinister. He didn't seem like a good person.","Han Mo shook his head: “Just bumped into him in the corridor. Exchanged a few words.”","He didn't want to elaborate, so he changed the subject and asked Qi Meili: “How did you think to bluff Gu Chacha like that?”","The trick was dirty, but it certainly did the job.","For the rest of the meal, Gu Chacha sat quietly, eating her food without causing a single scene.","Qi Meili frowned: “I wasn't bluffing. He really does have that smell on him.”","The smell of someone who'd slept around and hadn't bothered to shower. She'd grown up smelling it. It only disappeared from her life after she moved out at fifteen.","The moment Chen Jiarong got near her, she caught that disgusting odor.","Too familiar, too nauseating. There was no mistaking it.","Han Mo: ... Why did I even ask? How am I supposed to respond to this topic?","Luckily, Old Mr. Gu finished his walk and pushed the door open just in time: “Everyone rested enough? Shall we head back?”","Han Mo immediately turned around: “Sure.”","Behind him, Qi Meili leaned over to He Huanhuan: “Is he embarrassed?”","He Huanhuan nodded: “Definitely. Guys his age can't talk about this kind of stuff.”","Han Mo: ...","Gu Chacha had planned to leave with Chen Jiarong, but Gu Jingchen suddenly called out: “Chacha, do you have anything planned for the afternoon?”","Gu Chacha shook her head: “No.”","Gu Jingchen: “Come to the company with me then. I have something to say to you.”","His tone was stern, his attitude cold and hard. No need to guess — whatever it was, it wouldn't be pleasant.","But Gu Chacha couldn't refuse. Since childhood, her eldest brother had spoiled her the most, and she could never say no to him.","She nodded obediently: “Okay.”","Once in the car, the siblings sat in silence, like a wordless battle of wills.","Finally, Gu Jingchen let out a sigh: “What's the deal with this Chen Jiarong?”","Gu Chacha glanced at the rearview mirror. Gu Jingchen's expression wasn't especially harsh, so she said, “He's a friend I recently met. He treats me well...”","“How, exactly?”","Gu Chacha lowered her eyes: “He supports my career. He'll help me put on a concert.”","Gu Jingchen's eyes darkened instantly: “And for that, you...”","He didn't finish the sentence, but Gu Chacha knew what he meant. Tears slid down her lashes and fell one by one onto her skirt: “Brother, is that what you think of me?”","Gu Jingchen didn't look at her. He'd watched her grow up; how could he not know her nature?","She was a master at playing innocent and crying pitifully.","A few blinks and tears would stream down her face, tugging at everyone's heartstrings.","If it were a small matter, she'd cry a little and he'd let it go.","But matters of the heart weren't a game. He couldn't just let her cry a few tears and move on.","His voice grew colder: “It's not about what I think of you. It's about whether you even know what you're doing.”","Gu Chacha choked back sobs: “Of course I know. He likes me, and he's willing to treat me well, so I like him.”","Gu Jingchen's brows knitted tightly: “Look me in the eye and tell me you truly like him.”","But Gu Chacha couldn't lift her head. Her tears fell harder, and she felt her heart clench: “Brother, stop pushing me, please?”","Gu Jingchen's eyes were filled with barely restrained anger: “Am I the one pushing you? You're pushing yourself. You can't even look me in the eye and say you like him. How could you... how could you sleep with him...”","Sleeping with him wasn't love. It was a transaction.","The words struck Gu Chacha's heart like heavy fists, battering her with grief and resentment.","She wanted things her family refused to give her. What else could she do?","There was nothing else.","The only things she had were her beauty and her body.","If she didn't use them to trade, what did she have left to exchange?"]},{"number":87,"title":"Chapter 87: Luxury Seven-Day Tour for Two","paragraphs":["Intense resentment and bitterness crashed wildly in her chest, surging so fiercely that she could no longer hold it in and screamed out loud: \"Yes! I slept with him! As long as he's willing to spend money to help me, I can sleep with him! What about it?\"","These words had been bottled up inside her for a long time. Ever since she was little, she had loved the feeling of standing under the spotlight.","All eyes on her, stars shining bright—that feeling drove her crazy with obsession.","But her parents wouldn't allow it. They said the entertainment industry was too chaotic. A family like theirs had no need to send their child into that mess.","If the industry was chaotic, then they should have shielded her from it!","Why did they have to so arbitrarily crush her dream?","She sobbed until she fell apart: \"Why do you have to come question me? Why do you have to force me to admit these things?\"","Gu Jingchen looked at her crumbling, unable to speak for a long time.","\"If you want to walk the path of piano, the family will support you.\"","When she was little and learning piano, the family had always hired prestigious teachers for her—just the lesson fees alone had cost several million.","She was the youngest child in the family, and the only girl. How could her parents not love her?","\"That's not what I want! What use are those things!\"","Gu Chacha had completely thrown caution to the wind: \"I want to be a pianist! I want to hold concert after concert! Can you guys pay for that?\"","Gu Jingchen stayed silent. Of course they couldn't.","Not to mention their parents wouldn't agree—he wouldn't agree either.","If she just wanted to hold one concert for fun, he would arrange it without a second word.","But pouring money into pushing her to become a pianist—that wasn't a matter of ten or twenty million.","Chacha had no real talent for piano. To push her forward, they'd first have to buy awards. Prestigious ones, and not-so-prestigious ones—all of them had to be bought.","And the concerts she wanted, the world tour?","That wasn't something that could be settled with a few tens of millions.","If Chacha had talent, throwing money at it would be one thing. But her talent was truly mediocre—what difference would that money make compared to tossing it into the water?","He looked helplessly at the tear-streaked Gu Chacha: \"Do you really have to walk this path that doesn't suit you?\"","Gu Chacha's eyes were red: \"How do I know it doesn't suit me without trying? I'm not asking you all to pay for it—I found my own way! Even if it doesn't suit me, it's not your money being wasted! It's none of your business!\"","\"Stop the car!\"","She ordered Gu Jingchen furiously. She was done pretending to be the obedient, well-behaved little sister!","She had plenty of grievances. She was very unhappy. She didn't want to give them a good face anymore!","The car pulled over to the side of the road, and she pushed open the door without hesitation and walked away.","\"Chacha.\"","Gu Jingchen's voice was full of helplessness: \"Have you ever thought about whether your beauty and your body are really worth that much money to Mr. Chen?\"","Beauty might be a scarce resource, but the world has never been short of top-tier beauties.","The entertainment industry is full of beauties. Compared to them, Gu Chacha was nothing special.","Could her beauty and her body really buy her a worldwide concert tour?","Had she ever stopped to think about what Chen Jiarong was really after? Could she even afford to pay it?","Gu Chacha froze for a moment, her palms clenching unconsciously. She knew Gu Jingchen was right.","Chen Jiarong was willing to push her now because she was useful—she could help him launder money.","But once his business in the country took off, and he no longer needed her for that?","What would her trump card be then?","The Gu family.","A hidden madness ignited in her eyes. Yes, Chen Jiarong had said it right—the Gu family could only have one daughter.","And that one daughter was her.","Only if He Huanhuan were gone could Mom and Dad pour more love onto her.","Only then could she hold more leverage over him and never be abandoned.","“What I do is none of your business.”","With those words, she turned and walked away without a trace of hesitation.","The seed of sin grew wildly in the depths of her heart, and this time, she didn’t push it down—she let it slowly consume her, piece by piece.","Two days later.","He Huanhuan and Qi Meili rode their e-bike out early in the morning.","The one million that Old Mr. Gu had promised as compensation had hit her card yesterday, and she was now a little rich girl with one and a half million in her pocket.","They could hardly contain their excitement. Before dawn, they had already set off for the city to look at houses and scope out the second-hand real estate market in Jiangcheng.","Yeah, they kept their feet on the ground—they were only planning to buy a used apartment.","Shabby property management? Fine. A less-than-great neighborhood? Also fine. The key things were size, space, and natural light throughout.","All their lives, the two of them had never lived in a decent house, so this first home of theirs had to be big, bright, and comfortable to live in.","All morning, they followed an agent and saw ten apartments, but not one of them satisfied them.","Three-bedroom places under one and a half million either had bad layouts or interiors so outdated they couldn’t move in right away.","After looking around, they finally found one that ticked all the boxes.","Great layout, newly renovated, a lively neighborhood, and right outside the door were spots for spicy malatang and beef noodles.","But that place cost two and a half million, and the owner had dug in his heels on the price.","They were short by a whole million!","The agent gave a gentle suggestion: “You could go with a mortgage—one million over thirty years would be just over eight grand a month.”","The two of them shrieked: “How much?!”","The agent jumped with a start: “Eight... grand—”","You two already have cash in hand of one and a half million. Is eight grand a month really that much?","Of course, it was. That one and a half million came to them free of charge; who knew if there would ever be another windfall like this one?","He Huanhuan always felt that she wasn’t the true heiress, so she didn’t feel comfortable asking her family for money.","If they gave, she’d take it.","If they didn’t, she wouldn’t ask.","What if Old Mr. Gu gave that million once and then forgot?","Eight grand a month—where were the two of them supposed to earn that kind of dough?","Forget it, forget it. They’d save this money for now, and worry about it when they got to two and a half million.","After checking a few more places, they wandered down the street. He Huanhuan sighed: “That jerk Han Mo! He used to be so generous, wiring me a hundred grand every other day. Why hasn’t he sent a single payment these last few days?”","Seriously, once your expectations are raised to a certain level, you just can’t lower them without a serious letdown!","What she didn’t know was that Han Mo had been slammed lately.","The company was in total chaos, with every single thing waiting on him.","And he had to squeeze in time to keep tabs on Han Xuan’s legal case, making sure he had no chance of getting out.","Forget wiring her money—he and Chen Yu barely had time to eat.","Qi Meili patted her on the shoulder: “It’s fine, we’re in no rush. We’ll take our time, and one day we’ll find the best home.”","He Huanhuan nodded: “Mhm mhm!”","If worse came to worst, they could compromise and just buy a smaller one.","The only downside was that they wouldn’t have an extra room for practicing their hand-twirling dance moves. Sigh!","“Ladies! Would you like to try a raffle? We’ve just opened a new beauty shop, and the winning chance is super high! The grand prize is a luxurious 7-day trip for two to Sawo Country!”","A girl’s crisp voice suddenly stopped them in their tracks. They looked up and saw that a new beauty salon had opened on the street. The cute store assistant smiled brightly as she held up a prize-drawing box, looking at them expectantly.","He Huanhuan waved her hand and refused: \"I don't have money, and I don't need beauty treatments.\"","She knew all the tricks of these beauty salons. A new store opening would invite you to draw a prize, and the grand prizes were always so tempting.","Things like a few days' trip to Southeast Asia, dozens of grams of gold, or a brand-new electric scooter to ride away for free.","It would make your heart itch with desire. You'd step up and draw—and bam! A coupon for nine thousand off three thousand!","Dear customer! Come and top up your account now!"]},{"number":88,"title":"Chapter 88: Jackpot","paragraphs":["The shop assistant followed them with a sweet smile. \"Ladies, our store is a big chain brand—no force-buying here, I promise. Just think of it as a fun little draw, okay? The grand prize is a luxury seven-day trip for two to Sava Country!\"","She had a sweet face, and her voice was just as sweet.","She was holding a huge box as she trailed behind He Huanhuan and Qi Meili, looking like she was struggling under its weight.","The two women couldn't help but soften. \"Alright, alright, stop following us. We'll draw.\"","\"Thank you so much for supporting my work!\"","The shop assistant immediately thrust the box in front of He Huanhuan and gave her a knowing wink. \"Reach for the bottom, okay? That's where all the surprises are hiding.\"","Inside the box were rows of solid colored plastic balls. He Huanhuan reached down to the bottom, grabbed at random, and pulled out a red one.","The shop assistant beamed at Qi Meili. \"It matches your hair color, miss! This is bound to bring you good luck.\"","Man, was that girl smooth with her words. Even the two women's patience grew just a little bit more patient because of her charm.","Qi Meili laughed. \"Then go ahead and open it for me—let's see if I won anything.\"","\"You got it.\"","The shop assistant cracked open the plastic ball. Inside, a blurry QR code was printed on the ball's inner surface, and her voice immediately shot up with excitement. \"It's a QR code! A QR code means you won!\"","He Huanhuan's guard went up instantly. Could this be some kind of QR code scam?","She tightened her grip on her phone and frowned. \"Wait—you're not going to make me scan this QR code, are you?\"","There was 1.5 million yuan sitting in her phone. She'd sooner turn into Second Fool—no wait, she'd sooner turn into Liang Ye—than scan that thing.","But to her surprise, the shop assistant just gave a sweet little smile. \"Why would I ask you to scan it? That's our company's verification code. We have to use our own special scanner to confirm what prize you've won.\"","That sounded pretty legit. He Huanhuan relaxed and asked the shop assistant, \"So what kind of prizes do people usually get?\"","The assistant leaned in closer and whispered, \"Honestly, it's mostly consolation prizes—these cups that headquarters ordered in bulk. If you like them, I'll toss in an extra one for you later.\"","Both of them nodded eagerly. \"Great, great! Thank you!\"","Why pass up a freebie? And if the cups happened to be ugly, well, they could just give one to Liang Ye.","He wouldn't mind anyway.","Liang Ye, secretly thrilled: Matching cups? So she really does like me!","The shop assistant went behind the counter, grabbed a scanner, and aimed it at the QR code. \"Besides the cups, there's also the third prize, which is a set of toiletries... Oh my god! It's the GRAND PRIZE! Miss, you just won the GRAND PRIZE!!!\"","The assistant's voice shot up so high it nearly ruptured both women's eardrums. \"Store manager! Store manager! We've got a grand prize in our store! An actual GRAND PRIZE!!!\"","Her cheeks flushed bright red with excitement. She completely forgot about attending to He Huanhuan and Qi Meili, clutching the red ball and shrieking like crazy. \"Oh my god! So you really can pull the grand prize! I thought the company was lying to us!\"","She was so loud that the manager and two other employees rushed out. \"What's wrong? What's wrong? What's going on?\"","The assistant held up the red ball and hopped in place. \"Manager! Our store just drew the grand prize!\"","The manager's eyes went wide. \"No way? The grand prize actually exists? HQ wasn't scamming us after all?\"","He Huanhuan: ...Is it really appropriate for them to be trash-talking their own company right in front of their customers?","Actually, yes. It was more than appropriate.","They were just corporate grunts, after all. No love lost between them and their employer.","The store manager and a few staff members scanned the red ball over and over again, confirmed dozens of times that it was the grand prize, and only then did their emotions start to settle down a little.","The store manager looked at He Huanhuan apologetically: \"Miss, I'm really sorry, we got a bit carried away...\"","He Huanhuan: \"A bit? You guys were completely carried away.\"","You'd think they were the ones who won the prize.","The store manager flushed slightly: \"I'm truly sorry, it's just that this grand prize is really rare! It's a luxury travel package that headquarters arranged with a travel agency—first-class round-trip flights, five-star hotel stays, Michelin three-star dining. Top-tier luxury travel package.\"","He Huanhuan was shocked: \"That lavish? Is your company out of its mind?\"","She thought it was one of those cheap 499 or 599 travel deals.","The store manager smiled and nodded: \"That's why we're so excited—the whole seven-day package is worth over a hundred thousand yuan!\"","For context, joining a tour to Sawa Country for seven days only costs two thousand yuan.","A hundred thousand versus two thousand—you can imagine how extravagant it is.","He Huanhuan could hardly believe it: \"But I've never even bought anything from your store. Can I still claim it?\"","The store manager smiled warmly: \"Liwai Spring is a publicly listed company, and all our draws are fair, just, and transparent. Even if you've never made a purchase, this draw is still valid.\"","Qi Meili piped up anxiously: \"Then how do we claim it?\"","With such a big prize on the line, she wouldn't feel at ease until it was secured.","\"One moment, please.\"","The store manager hurried to the back storeroom and, half a minute later, came out carrying a delicate little box.","She handed the box to He Huanhuan: \"Inside the box is the redemption code. The prize is valid until the end of next month. Before you depart, you just need to log onto our official website, click the redemption link, and enter the code—then you can fill in your ID information.\"","Once the ID info was filled in and the travel date selected, this particular prize would be locked in.","The two of them, worried something might go wrong, immediately searched for the official website and redeemed the code on the spot.","Looking at the ID information form on the redemption page, He Huanhuan finally felt a bit more at ease.","She blinked and asked the store manager: \"So later I just fill in my ID and I'm good?\"","The store manager smiled and nodded: \"Yes, and if you're not sure, you can fill it in right now—the ticket will be issued right away.\"","He Huanhuan waved her hand: \"I feel like I'm dreaming. I need to go home and calm down before I fill it in.\"","The store manager didn't rush her, just reminded her with a smile: \"It's valid until the end of next month, so don't forget the deadline. If you miss it, you can't apply again.\"","After the reminder, she cautiously asked He Huanhuan: \"Um, can I take a photo with you?\"","She wanted to post it on her social feed to show off—her store had issued the grand prize! Let the other store managers be jealous!","The request wasn't unreasonable, so He Huanhuan agreed without hesitation.","Meili cheerfully stepped over: \"Buy one, get one free, hehe...\"","After the photos, the two of them left the store and continued strolling.","The staff girl held the draw box and watched them leave until their figures fully disappeared from sight, before she put away her smile and turned back into the store.","A good-looking woman in her forties walked over from the roadside, saw the draw box in the girl's hand, pulled closer and asked: \"Hey, is this a lucky draw? What are the prizes?\"","The girl smiled: \"Sorry, ma'am, the draw event has already ended.\"","The pretty auntie wasn't giving up: \"I come to your shop for facials all the time, just let me draw one~\"","She really was a regular customer, so the young lady behind the counter thought for a moment, then held the box out to her: \"We'll make an exception for you then, but only one draw~\"","The pretty auntie quickly reached in and pulled out a ball, then opened it on the spot: \"Why is it a QR code? What does that mean?\"","The young lady smiled: \"A QR code means 'thank you for your patronage' — you didn't win, sorry~\""]},{"number":89,"title":"Chapter 89: Shall We Go to Sava Country Together","paragraphs":["The auntie wasn't disappointed at not winning. She tossed the little ball back into the raffle box: \"Fine, give me a call next time you have an event. I think I still have over seven hundred bucks left on my card.\"","The young woman at the counter nodded: \"Don't worry, we always notify our members when there's an event.\"","With that, she carried the box back into the store and closed the door behind her.","Behind the counter, the store manager asked her with a serious expression: \"You got that ball back, right?\"","The young woman nodded: \"I watched her put it back.\"","A ball worth a hundred thousand—if that auntie hadn't put it back, she would've asked for it outright.","\"Good. Go out back and burn every single ball in that box. Not one can be left behind, understand?\"","The manager picked up her phone, opened a chat, and sent the group photo: [Prize claimed. It's her, right?]","A reply came quickly: [Correct. Well done. Your store's bonus is doubled this month.]","Manager: [Thank you, boss!]","She put down her phone, thought for a moment, and went to keep an eye on the back door.","Each ball was worth ten thousand yuan. If even one slipped out and someone found it, their bonus wouldn't be enough to cover the loss.","In the alley, little balls were tossed one by one into the flickering flames, sending up brilliant sparks.","In the concert hall's green room, Chen Jiarong reached out and touched Gu Chacha's face: \"They took the bait. By next month at the latest, the Gu family will have only one daughter.\"","And that daughter would only be Gu Chacha.","Gu Chacha looked at herself in the mirror—delicate makeup, soft features.","She pressed her cheek against his large hand: \"Be careful. Don't let anyone notice anything off. We still have a lot to do.\"","He pinched her cheek and chuckled: \"Relax. If I couldn't pull off something this small, I wouldn't bother coming back to China to play in the big leagues.\"","The company was a legitimate publicly traded one, and the raffle was a registered, fully compliant promotion.","No matter who investigated, they wouldn't find anything wrong.","Because there was nothing wrong.","The problem lay in Sava Land, in the hotel they'd be staying at on the first night. His men would get the key card, swipe into their room, and take them straight away.","Two drugged girls, vanishing in a foreign land in the dead of night.","Even if the Gu family had connections reaching to the heavens, they wouldn't find them.","Let alone the fact that they didn't quite have that level of reach anyway.","His fingers traced down her cheek, eventually taking her hand: \"Play well. Earn back every cent I spent on this trip.\"","The travel package was only worth a hundred thousand, but setting this whole plan in motion had cost him a fortune.","Her eyes met her reflection in the mirror, and Gu Chacha gave a slight nod: \"I will.\"","I'm sorry, He Huanhuan. You can only blame your bad luck. Why couldn't you just stay a nobody from the countryside instead of barging into her life and shaking it all up?","Meanwhile, back home, the \"countryside girl\" in question was excitedly rushing through the door.","The two of them charged straight up to the fourth floor, where Gu Jinghan was lying on his bed like a blob of chicken shit, singing: \"Rich mommy~ somebody find me a rich mommy to support me~ I'll bring you foot-washing water~ smelly feet or sweet feet, I'll wash 'em all~\"","...","Why was he so obsessed with landing a sugar mommy?","Bro's take: a man's whole life is about enjoying this mortal body.","So you absolutely cannot overwork yourself.","You've got to eat well, drink well, have fun, and take care of it for a whole lifetime to make it worth it.","And for a stable, lasting life of luxury, he had to find a rich mommy.","She handles the outside, he handles the inside.","She earns the money, he maintains the looks~","Perfect!","He Huanhuan nudged him with her foot: \"You know what we did today?\"","Gu Jinghan lifted his head slightly: \"Found me a rich mommy?\"","He Huanhuan rolled her eyes: \"...I'm leaving if you're not gonna listen.\"","Gu Jinghan sprang up like a fish flipping over: \"I'm listening, I'm listening... what'd you do?\"","He Huanhuan pulled up her prize redemption page: \"We won big today! The grand prize! A luxury seven-day trip for two to Sava Land! Worth over a hundred thousand!\"","Gu Jinghan blinked: \"And then?\"","He didn't see what the big deal was. Last time he went to Sava Land for five days, how much did he spend again?","Three hundred grand? Five hundred grand?","Couldn't remember. Anyway, the cost of living in Sava Land was low, so thirty to fifty grand was more than enough to blow through.","He Huanhuan: \"...How the hell did you spend that much?\"","Didn't everyone say Sava Land was cheap? How do you blow three to five hundred grand in five days? How?","Gu Jinghan tried to recall: \"Just rented out an island, hired some dancers and performers. Meh, they didn't have much going on anyway—same old act after act. Boring.\"","The dancers weren't all that great. None of the guys were nearly as good-looking as him.","The girls were decent looking, but half of them might not have been girls.","And he wasn't into that scene anyway, so he came back after a few days.","...","Holy damn. Renting out a whole island just for fun. The two country bumpkins were stunned.","Qi Meili smacked her lips and asked He Huanhuan: \"So are we still going?\"","\"Of course! Absolutely!\"","Gu Jinghan sat up straight: \"I'm coming with you guys! We'll go check out some strip shows! I heard there's body drumming too—I'll take you girls to see it!\"","After coming back last time, he'd gone online to search things up and realized he hadn't even played it right.","Renting an island in Sava Land was the most boring move. You had to go check out the underground shows to have real fun.","Body drumming—imagine how impressive that'd be.","He Huanhuan was shocked: \"What the hell is body drumming? How do you drum on a person? Won't something snap?\"","\"Who knows? Let's go see for ourselves!\"","Gu Jinghan pulled out his phone and started booking tickets: \"When you wanna go? How about the day after tomorrow? We'll skip the weekend—too crowded. We'll go after the working class goes back to their jobs.\"","Before he even finished speaking, he'd already booked the Monday flight to Sava.","It happened so fast the two of them couldn't react in time. He Huanhuan was dumbfounded: \"That's so sudden?\"","She'd never even left the country in her life—the first time she'd even left the county was when she got transmigrated into this book and came to Jiang City.","She wanted to spend a few days preparing, like looking up how to board a plane, how to check a boarding pass, and whether you're actually allowed to use your phone on a flight...","She had to figure all that out before going, or else she'd embarrass herself.","\"Bah! Sava's super close. If anything happens, we'll just come back!\"","Gu Jinghan urged her: \"Hurry up, put your ID info in and book your ticket. Day after tomorrow, all three of us go! I'll take you girls to a ladyboy's abs!\"","Qi Meili nodded excitedly: \"They must feel amazing to touch!\"","Gu Jinghan recoiled: \"Well, sure, they feel great, but do you have to touch mine?\"","Chastity is a man's best dowry. He needed to stay pure for his future rich mommy wife!"]},{"number":90,"title":"Chapter 90: You're asking me to go","paragraphs":["Gu Jinghan moved fast. He Huanhuan hadn't even finished typing in her ID number before he'd already bought tickets for the underground performances.","\"We'll go see the human drumming first, then the ladyboy show, and after that...\"","This was going to be his and Huanhuan's first sibling trip together, and he wished he could just wrap up the whole country of Sawa and hand it to her as a gift.","Truth be told, when it came to financial resources, he couldn't compete with their eldest brother.","And when it came to generosity, he couldn't outdo Han Mo either.","So he had to play to his strengths. He'd show Huanhuan what it meant to have top-tier taste in fun.","Seeing that he'd already made all the arrangements, He Huanhuan opened the prize redemption page to book their tickets.","She was just about to type in her ID number when her phone suddenly buzzed. Liang Ye, persistent as a ghost, was calling.","\"Huanhuan, it's Friday~ I'm off work~ Can I come over to your place and hang out?\"","He Huanhuan declined: \"No.\"","\"Aw~ How did you know I'm already at your doorstep? Hehe... We're so in sync!\"","He Huanhuan: ......","Five minutes later, sure enough, Liang Ye's voice rang out from downstairs: \"Huanhuan, can I come up to your floor? Would that be too intimate?\"","Before he even finished speaking, heavy footsteps were already thundering up the stairs.","The footsteps reached the third floor, and Liang Ye's voice was brimming with excitement: \"Huanhuan! I'm here!\"","Liang Ye stood at the third-floor landing, his heart racing. Once he walked through that door, he'd officially belong to Huanhuan!","\"Hey! Ugly bastard, we're on the fourth floor!\"","Qi Meili stood on the fourth floor, leaning over the railing to shout down at him.","Liang Ye was annoyed: \"Can you stop calling me ugly bastard? I'm not even ugly.\"","He just wasn't handsome in an obvious way.","Qi Meili beamed: \"Sure thing, ugly bastard.\"","......","This Qi Meili! What a mouth on her!","He trudged up to the fourth floor feeling all wronged, ready to tattle to He Huanhuan. But instead, he saw He Huanhuan and Gu Jinghan sitting together looking at a phone, which was playing some saucy exotic dance.","He leaned in and asked, \"Huanhuan, you like this kind of thing?\"","He Huanhuan waved a hand: \"It's alright, but it'd be worth checking out when we go to Sawa.\"","\"Sawa? You guys are going on a trip?\"","Gu Jinghan nodded: \"Yeah, Huanhuan won a two-person trip to Sawa. I'm tagging along to keep them company for a couple of days.\"","\"A prize? A two-person trip to Sawa?\"","Liang Ye's eyes lit up instantly. He looked at He Huanhuan with hopeful, pleading eyes: \"Huanhuan, are you going to take me?\"","\"Smack!\"","A solid slap landed right on top of his head. Qi Meili glared at him in exasperation: \"Are you asking to die?\"","Her and Huanhuan's overseas trip, and this guy had the nerve to want in?","Liang Ye rubbed his head, annoyed: \"You hit me again! Fine, you hit me. But... you'll give me your spot, right?\"","Qi Meili was speechless: \"Do you have no shame? You're a rich kid! Why are you fighting me for this? Just pay for your own trip!\"","His family was loaded, so why was he being so cheap about everything?","Liang Ye shook his head: \"The plane tickets are so expensive. I can't bear to spend it.\"","When something free was on the table, who wanted to pay?","He was about to keep begging Qi Meili when Gu Jinghan couldn't take it anymore: \"Shut up! Stop bothering her! Go buy your own ticket and send me the payment request. I'll cover it.\"","Liang Ye was thrilled: \"Second Brother, you already approve of me as your brother-in-law this quickly? You're so good to me!\"","......","Gu Jinghan looked up at Qi Meili: \"Go on! Smack him one!\"","\"Smack!\"","Meili, the queen of indulging requests, didn't hesitate for a second and rewarded him with another slap.","He wasn't even mad. He just thought happily to himself: Second Brother only told Meili to hit me, but he didn't deny it~","That's basically approval!","He grinned and pulled out his phone to check flights: \"Aw man, weekend flights to Sawa are so expensive, 1300! Weekdays are only 1100!\"","He Huanhuan: \"Then buy the 1100 one. We'll leave Monday and come back on Sunday.\"","\"What?\"","Liang Ye was shocked: \"Isn't it just two days?\"","Gu Jinghan had said he'd join Huanhuan and the others for two days, so he'd assumed it was go tomorrow, come back the day after!","Gu Jinghan shot him a glance: \"What I meant was, we'll casually play for a couple of days within the trip. Not that the whole trip is only two days.\"","\"Why didn't you say that clearly? What's wrong with you?\"","Gu Jinghan was confused: \"Monday tickets are even cheaper, so that works in your favor, doesn't it? Why are you in such a hurry?\"","Liang Ye whined: \"I have to work on Monday. I can't go.\"","Ah right. He'd forgotten that this guy was a dedicated workhorse.","Qi Meili pushed him: \"Then don't go! We never wanted to bring you anyway!\"","\"But I want to go...\"","\"Then take a day off.\"","\"I can't! If I take a day off, I won't be able to get the Outstanding Employee award!\"","\"Then don't go.\"","\"But I want to go...\"","\"Go die, then!\"","Qi Meili was losing her temper. Was this guy sick? Seriously sick!","After leaving the Gu residence, Liang Ye felt so miserable that he pulled out his phone and called Liang Zheng: \"Bro, I'm so upset...\"","On the other end of the line, his brother was swamped with work: \"Didn't they all move out days ago? Why are you still upset?\"","Liang Ye sniffled: \"Huanhuan won a seven-day two-person trip to Sawa in a lottery draw. She's going with Qi Meili, and I want to go too. Second Brother said he'd reimburse my tickets, wuwuwu...\"","Liang Zheng's eyes paused for a moment: \"They're going to Sawa?\"","Liang Ye nodded: \"Yeah. I thought it was tomorrow, but Huanhuan said they're leaving next Monday, wuwuwu... I can't go because I have work, wuwuwu... Bro, I'm so upset...\"","\"Don't be upset.\"","Liang Ye sniffled: \"Okay, Bro.\"","\"Do your job well tomorrow. Work hard to earn that Outstanding Employee award.\"","Liang Ye said with determination: \"Bro, I definitely will!\"","\"Talk later.\"","\"Okay!\"","Say what you will, but they were brothers after all. The older one knew exactly how to handle the younger one.","Back in the office, Liang Zheng glanced at the report submitted by the marketing department.","It was an application for market development targeting Sawa.","He hesitated for a moment. Three seconds later, the marketing manager's phone rang: \"Next Monday, I'll personally go to Sawa to assess the situation.\"","The marketing manager was stunned: \"For such a small project, you're going personally, sir?\"","Liang Zheng said coldly: \"You think this is a small project?\"","\"N-No, no...\"","The marketing manager quickly shook his head: \"There's no such thing as a small project. As long as we put our hearts into it, every project is a big project!\"","\"Good. See you next Monday.\"","The call ended, and the marketing manager's head was spinning.","There went his fun little Sawa getaway! Gone!","Meanwhile, Liang Zheng's brow still hadn't relaxed.","He thought back to what Liang Ye had said. Gu Jinghan was going too?","The image of Qi Meili shouting \"baby\" at Gu Jinghan flashed through his mind, and before he knew it, his hand had dialed another number: \"Hey? Didn't you mention once that your younger brother runs a hotel? Is that right?\"","Gu Jingchen checked the time, then glanced at his phone.","At this hour, Liang Zheng was calling him to ask about this?","He nodded: \"That's right. Do you have friends you need to host? I can have Jinghan arrange something for you.\"","\"No, just asking.\""]},{"number":91,"title":"Chapter 91: Last-Minute Change of Mind","paragraphs":["Early the next morning, before the two of them were even out of bed, there was a knock at the door.","Gu Jinghan's voice came through, sounding anxious: \"Huanhuan! Meili! I can't make it to Sava!\"","The two of them sat bolt upright and hurried over to open the door.","At the doorstep, Gu Jinghan looked utterly dejected: \"The City Construction Commission and the Fire Department suddenly announced a major inspection of all the hotels in our area. I need to be at the hotel to keep an eye on things over the next few days, so I can't go to Sava.\"","\"Ah?\"","They couldn't help feeling a little disappointed—neither of them had ever been abroad, and they'd been counting on Gu Jinghan to guide them so they could travel with peace of mind.","Gu Jinghan apologized guiltily: \"I'm sorry, Huanhuan. Big brother can't go with you. How about I set you up with a handsome local guide instead?\"","He Huanhuan waved her hand to decline: \"No need, go do what you need to do. Meili and I will be fine.\"","She'd done some online research the night before, and lots of people in Sava spoke Chinese. The two of them should be able to manage on their own just fine.","So Gu Jinghan forwarded her all the tickets he'd bought, telling them to use them however they liked once they got to Sava.","With that, he hopped in his car and drove off in a hurry.","The two women stared at their suitcases on the floor, feeling a little lost.","He Huanhuan couldn't help but suggest: \"Why don't I ask Han Mo?\"","Maybe he'd be free.","Qi Meili shot her a look: \"You just want to go on a date with him! And make me the third wheel!\"","He Huanhuan felt a twinge of guilt: \"I just thought, since we've never been abroad, it'd be more comfortable to have someone else along—\"","\"Pfft.\"","Qi Meili couldn't be bothered to call her out. She nodded in agreement: \"Then go ahead and ask if he's free.\"","Compared to Liang Ye, at least Han Mo was good-looking!","He Huanhuan immediately pulled out her phone and texted Han Mo: [Meili and I are going to Sava next week. Want to come along?]","A reply came quickly: [Been pretty busy lately. Company's a mess right now. Probably can't spare the time.]","The next second—ding—a transfer came through.","One, two, three, four, five zeroes.","[Have fun with Meili. Buy whatever you want, don't worry about the money.]","Damn!","That kind of generosity was dangerously charming.","He Huanhuan's disappointment vanished in an instant. She shoved her phone in front of Qi Meili: \"Meili, our dream three-bedroom just grew by another fifteen square meters!\"","Qi Meili's eyes lit up instantly: \"Han Laodeng's not bad after all! I hereby declare—you two have my blessing to get married!\"","Generosity really was the most captivating virtue.","The two of them stared at the 1.8 million yuan balance on He Huanhuan's phone and giggled like idiots.","They could practically feel the dream apartment waving at them.","At the Ai Luwei boutique, Chen Jiarong sat on the sofa in the VIP room, waiting for Gu Chacha to pick out her goods.","In the quiet private lounge, his phone suddenly buzzed.","He opened it, read the message, and the corners of his mouth curved up involuntarily.","Gu Chacha was hesitating between two handbags. He walked over, wrapped an arm around her, and said: \"Why hesitate? If you like them, just buy them both.\"","Gu Chacha wrinkled her nose: \"They're too similar. Buying both would feel redundant.\"","\"Haha...\"","Chen Jiarong laughed heartily: \"As long as you like something, you can buy two identical ones if you want!\"","He gave the sales associate a nod: \"Wrap up everything she was looking at. Checkout.\"","Gu Chacha looked at him: \"You're in a good mood?\"","Chen Jiarong pulled her closer: \"What? Am I not usually good to you?\"","Gu Chacha shook her head: \"No, it's just that you seem really excited...\"","Could it be...","Just as her thoughts drifted toward that possibility, Chen Jiarong leaned in and whispered in her ear: \"Being able to foot the bill for the only daughter of the Gu family—isn't that worth being happy about?\"","There it was!","Her eyes lit up immediately: \"Really?\"","Chen Jiarong waved his phone: \"The plane tickets just came through. Two of them. Flying to Sava tomorrow.\"","Tomorrow?!","Gu Chacha's heart started pounding. Flying out tomorrow morning?","That meant, by tomorrow night, everything would be settled?","It all felt too easy, leaving her with a nagging sense of unreality.","She thought for a moment, then said to Chen Jiarong: \"I don't want to shop anymore. Can you drop me back at the Gu estate? I want to go see Mom and Dad.\"","She needed to confirm it. She had to see it with her own eyes to feel at ease.","Chen Jiarong, of course, knew what she was thinking. He playfully tapped her nose: \"What? You don't trust me?\"","Gu Chacha gave a coaxing smile: \"I just feel a bit uneasy. I want to go check.\"","\"Of course.\"","Chen Jiarong led her out: \"If you're uneasy, I'll take you to see for yourself. Anything you want, I'll give it to you.\"","The car quickly pulled up to the Gu estate. After greeting Old Mr. Gu, Gu Chacha barely contained herself: \"Where's sister? Why don't I see her?\"","Old Mr. Gu smiled: \"She got lucky—won one of those luxury seven-day tours of Sava. Right now she and Meili are upstairs on the third floor packing.\"","Her heart was racing so fast it felt like it might leap out of her mouth. She stood up, forcing herself to stay calm: \"I'll go see her.\"","Gu Chengye waved a hand: \"Go on, go on. If you want to go too, Dad will give you the money. Go have fun with Huanhuan.\"","Gu Chacha shook her head: \"No thanks, Dad. I have a performance in a couple of days. I just want to say hi to sister.\"","She flew upstairs—didn't even think to take the elevator, sprinting up to the third floor.","Gu Chengye sat on the sofa, laughing and sighing: \"That girl. Finally starting to care about her sister.\"","Oh, she cared. Just not in the way he thought.","On the third floor, two huge suitcases lay open, stuffed haphazardly with several tubes of hair dye and over a dozen temporary tattoos.","He Huanhuan had a big black plastic bag over her head, and both arms stuck out with a temporary tattoo on each—not yet peeled off.","Seeing Gu Chacha come up, she looked surprised: \"What are you doing here?\"","Hadn't they gotten to that level of just dropping by each other's rooms?","Gu Chacha stood at the door, watching the two of them bustling around getting ready for their trip.","The frantic racing of her heart finally settled back down. A gentle smile tugged at her lips: \"Dad told me you're going to Sava, sister?\"","He Huanhuan shot her a glance: \"What's it to you?\"","That was from a lottery she'd won herself—it wasn't money from the old man. So don't try to compare!","Gu Chacha smiled: \"I have a lot of haute couture dresses in my room that I've never worn. If you want, sister, I can give you a couple. They'd look great for photos at the beach.\"","He Huanhuan wrinkled her nose in distaste: \"No way. I'd look like a liquor commercial in those! So tacky!\"","Every single one of Gu Chacha's couture gowns looked like it belonged in an ad.","\"Gu Jing\" liquor—China's finest.","Beyond flashy.","\"Well then, sister, have fun on your trip.\"","With that, Gu Chacha turned and walked away quietly, not a single sharp word. It was almost unlike her.","He Huanhuan was baffled: \"Why's she being so docile today?\"","\"Who cares? She's probably green with envy in there!\"","Qi Meili carefully pressed her down and lifted the plastic bag off. He Huanhuan emerged with pineapple-yellow hair and asked: \"Sava enough for you?\"","Qi Meili nodded like crazy: \"Now that is so Sava!\""]},{"number":92,"title":"Chapter 92: Groping into the Room...","paragraphs":["Early Monday morning, He Huanhuan and Qi Meili dragged their suitcases and rode their electric scooter out the door.","At the entrance to the Gu Estate, Gu Chacha and Chen Jiarong sat in a Lincoln, watching the two pass by. \"Ugh! A damn footboard car! That thing is so ugly!\" they scoffed, then sped off without a second glance.","He Huanhuan's pineapple-yellow hair and her two legs flailed in the wind—not because she was being reckless, but because two suitcases were stacked on the footboard, leaving her no room for her feet.","Chen Jiarong watched the scooter disappear from sight, then chuckled and nuzzled Gu Chacha's head: \"See? No need to worry now, right?\"","The anxiety in Gu Chacha's eyes finally melted away, replaced by a sweet smile. \"Yeah, I'm relieved.\"","The award redemption backdrop at Liwei Spring only showed that the booked flights and hotel had been claimed—it didn't reveal the identity of the person who redeemed them.","So she couldn't help but feel uneasy. She always felt like He Huanhuan was her nemesis, the kind that just wouldn't die easily.","Fortunately, everything was going smoothly.","She lowered her gaze, crushing the last shred of guilt in her heart. \"Will she die tonight?\"","A sinister gleam flashed in Chen Jiarong's eyes. \"Silly girl, do you have any idea how much a pretty twenty-year-old can bring us?\"","Gu Chacha's heart lurched. \"You want them to go into prostitution...\"","A hand clamped over her mouth. Chen Jiarong smiled at her. \"Say that out loud and it doesn't sound nice anymore.\"","Gu Chacha's pupils trembled. She clutched tightly at Chen Jiarong's hand. \"Can we not? Just kill her, but don't send her there, okay?\"","Chen Jiarong pinched her cheek, his smile deepening. \"Always talking nonsense.\"","It wasn't just about the mountains of money—money and sex were the only path to power.","Such young, beautiful girls—why would he ever let them close their eyes in the prime of their blossoming youth?","Of course, he'd send them to his home base, let them bloom to their fullest, and serve him well.","His eyes held an unyielding certainty that made Gu Chacha's heart tremble.","In that moment, she suddenly realized just what kind of person she was making a deal with.","Chen Jiarong wasn't Han Xuan. He was born in the muck, his heart had no home—he was a hungry wolf.","She couldn't help but think of herself. What would her fate be?","Would she, young and pretty as she was, one day stand alongside He Huanhuan and the others at some banquet?","She leaned quietly against Chen Jiarong's chest, but her heart pounded like a drum.","She watched the blue sky outside the car window as a plane flew smoothly overhead.","She thought to herself: she'd have to find a way to secure an escape route.","That night, on the seventeenth floor of a five-star hotel, two shadowy figures crept toward room 1721, room card in hand, and swiped it carefully.","\"Click.\"","The lock popped open instantly. The shadows pushed the door open and slipped inside.","Half a minute later: \"Ahh!!\"","The scream vanished into the room, and the hallway fell silent again.","Gu Chacha lay in bed, unable to sleep. When it hit past midnight, she finally couldn't hold back and shook Chen Jiarong awake. \"Has Sawa... succeeded yet?\"","Chen Jiarong, still groggy, pressed her down onto the bed. \"We'll know when we wake up. Stop worrying.\"","\"But...\"","She wanted to say more, but quickly lost the chance to speak.","By the time she was exhausted enough to fall asleep, the string in her heart was still taut.","For a split second, she even hoped He Huanhuan wouldn't get caught.","Then she sneered inwardly: Gu Chacha, Gu Chacha, you've already walked down a road of no return. Who are you trying to fool now?","Didn't you make this choice yourself?","Since you did, stop hesitating.","Hesitation will only push you deeper into the abyss.","With that thought, she finally closed her eyes and drifted off to sleep.","Meanwhile, in room 1721, the two shadows were tied up like boiled prawns, sprawled on the floor, their mouths stuffed with stinky socks that made them roll their eyes in disgust. \"Mmmph mmmph...\"","\"Talk! How did you get into my room?\"","A deep, furious male voice interrogated them harshly.","The two squirmed frantically: \"Mmmph mmmph...\"","The man grew angrier. \"Not talking? Fine, don't blame me for being rough!\"","They squirmed even harder: \"Mmmph mmmph...\"","Take the socks out already!","How were they supposed to talk with those in their mouths?!","\"I swear, how did you even get into the police academy with a brain like that?\"","From the bathroom, another crisp, clear male voice snapped in exasperation: \"Use your pig brain! Their mouths are stuffed with your stinky socks—how can they confess?\"","\"Oh, right!\"","The man quickly got up and yanked the socks out. \"Now talk! Who are you? Why did you sneak into our room? What did you plan to do to us?\"","\"Mai neem tung jai...\"","The two boiled prawns babbled gibberish. The man kicked the one on the right. \"You think I'm blind? You've got 'I'm the Baddest' tattooed on your arm!\"","...","Xiao You quickly hid his arm and kept babbling: \"Sawatdee ka...\"","The man scoffed in disbelief. \"Qi Yuan! Your turn!\"","\"What? The great police officer can't handle such a small task?\"","A man in thin-rimmed glasses stepped out of the bathroom. He looked to be in his mid-twenties, with delicate features and a calm, scholarly air.","He walked to the bed, kicked the stinky socks aside, and said: \"Start talking, while I'm still in a good mood.\"","The two men glanced at Qi Yuan. A bookish guy like him—threats just didn't land.","\"Sawatdee ka ka ba... aghh!!\"","A thin scalpel slammed into Xiao You's arm. Xiao You broke down: \"Why did you stab me? Why not him?\"","Xiao Zuo quietly shrank back. Don't see me, don't see me...","Qi Yuan glanced at him. \"Guess where the next blade goes?\"","Xiao Zuo swallowed hard. \"I don't know anything. We were just hired to do a job.\"","\"Is that so?\"","Another scalpel buried itself in Xiao You's stomach. Xiao You completely lost it: \"Why are you stabbing me again?! And he already talked!\"","Qi Yuan smiled faintly. \"I'm not satisfied with his answer.\"","He tilted his head toward Xiao Zuo. \"Think carefully before you speak... otherwise...\"","Xiao You was beside himself: \"Otherwise what?! I'll talk! I'll talk! Ask me!\"","The blade wasn't sticking in him, so of course he could talk properly!","\"We're just street punks. Someone paid us three thousand baht to come to 1721 and tie up two girls. We'd get another three thousand baht after it was done. That's it!\"","Xiao You spilled everything in one go.","Two girls?","Qi Yuan turned to Qi Jin. \"You said you bought this double room package on what, during the day?\"","Qi Jin blinked innocently. \"Secondhand online. I saw it was a steal, and our vacations lined up, so I grabbed it. Got thirty percent off, too.\""]},{"number":93,"title":"Chapter 93: Vacation","paragraphs":["Qi Yuan asked with certainty, “The seller is a girl?”","Qi Jin nodded. “Pretty good-looking girl, just her hair was a total mess, blinding.”","Qi Yuan frowned. “You looked at her photos?”","“The package came with free show tickets, like seven or eight performances, all free, so of course I had to add her as a friend!”","Qi Yuan was speechless. “What exactly did they teach you at the police academy? Don’t you know to be cautious when buying secondhand?”","Qi Jin looked innocent. “I was cautious! I asked her if she was reliable.”","“She told you she was very reliable, and then you bought it?”","Qi Jin nodded. “Yeah! She looked so young, no way she’d scam me.”","......","Forget it, forget it. He’s my own brother, can’t hit him.","Qi Yuan looked down at Xiao Zuo and Xiao You. “Who hired you? What else did they say?”","Xiao Zuo was still hesitating, but Xiao You immediately spilled the beans. “That’s the local gangster around here, goes by Brother Hu. He’s also from China, out here hustling. Brother Hu said the boss from Mianbei placed the order, to grab two girls and take them to Mianbei for... business...”","Qi Yuan frowned. “Why would this boss want to grab those two girls?”","Xiao You shook his head with a sycophantic grin. “That we really don’t know. Brother Hu didn’t tell us.”","Qi Yuan sat down on the bed, frowning deeply in thought.","The people they were supposed to grab were probably Qi Jin’s seller. For some reason, she’d canceled her trip and sold the package to them, dodging the danger.","Is that it?","Or is this all a lie?","He looked up at Qi Jin. “Did the girl say why she was selling the package?”","“She said she won it in a raffle, and when she was about to buy the tickets, she realized the two of them didn’t have passports.”","......","What a flimsy excuse.","Qi Yuan reached out. “Let me see her moments.”","“Okay.”","The phone was quickly handed to him. What caught his eye was a blinding pineapple yellow and a flashy neon pink.","And two radiant smiles.","The caption: As long as your mindset is good enough, anywhere can be Bali!","Two purely happy faces, filled with transparent foolishness.","Bali is in Indonesia, a good three thousand kilometers away from Sawa.","He tapped the keyboard and commented below: Bali is in Indonesia, not Sawa.","Thirty seconds later, that post was gone.","Another thirty seconds later, the girl posted a new one. Same two radiant smiles, same two wild heads of hair.","Just the caption changed to: As long as your mindset is good enough, anywhere can be Phuket!","The corners of his mouth couldn’t help but turn up. Clearly, these two girls didn’t have enough brains between them to scheme all this up.","He handed the phone back to Qi Jin. “Go stuff your stinky socks back in.”","If they didn’t sleep soon, they wouldn’t be able to enjoy tomorrow.","“Fine.”","The stinky socks were shoved back into both mouths, and Xiao You was sobbing. He needed to go to the hospital, the hospital!","He had no idea that those two stab wounds weren’t even enough to be classified as minor injuries.","Even if you stabbed him a hundred and ten times, as long as Qi Yuan didn’t want it, he wouldn’t suffer serious harm.","Back home in China at that moment, He Huanhuan was lying face down on the big hotel bed, seriously asking AI: What other attractions does Thailand have? Tell me all of them.","She had to post again tomorrow, and she couldn’t pull another Bali mistake.","Qi Meili was rolling around blissfully on the hotel bed. “I think Second Brother’s hotel is more comfortable than Bali!”","“Phuket!”","“Oh right, Phuket!”","The two dragged two beach chairs into the room, turned on the TV, and cast a travel promo video for Sawa.","Lively music quickly filled the room: ~~Curry, bak kut teh, Indonesian lemongrass~~","Living the hotel life, setting the vibe—no different from actually going to Sawa, right?","Qi Meili swayed her body and asked He Huanhuan, “How much did you sell that package for?”","He Huanhuan Pinched her three fingers together, her face brimming with barely contained pride.","“Seventy thousand! That much?”","Qi Meili sat up excitedly. “So you’ve got one hundred and eighty-seven thousand now?”","Adding the fifty-some thousand in her phone, they had one hundred and ninety-two thousand?","The money had come way too easily!","She couldn’t help but remember when He Huanhuan had been hit with a bottle and hospitalized, and she didn’t have the money to pay for He Huanhuan’s stay.","A three-thousand-yuan hospital fee had nearly crushed her.","In the end, she had to throw a fit at her dad’s house just to beg for the money.","Her grip tightened on her phone. “Huanhuan, we’re going to stay here forever, right?”","She didn’t want to go back. Back home, she’d work herself to the bone for a month and only make five thousand.","Working every single day, without even time to spend the money.","He Huanhuan nodded seriously. “Yes, we will.”","Click. The door swung open, and Gu Jinghan stood in the doorway with his arms crossed. “Why do you two look so unhappy?”","Qi Meili vanished instantly and appeared next to him. “Are you going to comfort me?”","Gu Jinghan gave her a speechless look. Her head was pressed firmly against his arm. “Do you even need comforting?”","Qi Meili nodded happily. “Of course I do. There’s still some space here on my head, and it might need a handsome, big hand...”","“Aren’t you greedy!”","Gu Jinghan grudgingly pulled her head close, then reached out to He Huanhuan. “You come too.”","Since he was already getting one, might as well do both. More efficient that way.","Pulling He Huanhuan into the embrace as well, he said in a low voice, “Passports are easy to get. Once I’m done with my work in the next couple of days, I’ll take you both to get them. As soon as they’re ready, I’m taking you to Sawa, and the whole trip’s on me.”","He never imagined they didn’t even have passports.","Which meant they’d never left the country their whole lives?","Then how did they spend every summer and winter break growing up?","Gotta say, this guy was overthinking it.","What “going abroad”? These two had never even left their small county.","How else would two small-town party girls spend their breaks? In summer, they’d walk from one end of the county to the other, then back again. One day gone just like that.","Winter was harder to kill time. It was too cold outside to walk, and their niche talent couldn’t shine.","So they’d just wander up and down the stairs of the county’s single shopping mall.","After enough wandering, the mall employees got to know them, and sometimes even gave them food.","The takoyaki lady on the second floor was especially kind. When she had leftover balls at night that she couldn’t sell, she’d give them away for free.","After eating the balls, they’d help the lady clean up, then head home.","Thinking about that lady, He Huanhuan couldn’t help smacking her lips. “Sister You’s takoyaki was truly terrible. No idea how she kept the shop open.”","Qi Meili added, “She finally shut down last month. Went to work at the same factory as me now.”","......","Gu Jinghan had no idea what to say. What kind of life had these two been living before?","All he could do was pull out his phone. “Takoyaki, right? Your big brother here is ordering you ten portions! Eat as much as you want!”"]},{"number":94,"title":"Chapter 94: The Missing Person","paragraphs":["Before dawn broke, Gu Chacha woke up.","When she opened her eyes, her gaze unexpectedly met Chen Jiarong's, and his eyes were full of impatience.","Her heart jumped suddenly, and she knew something must have gone wrong.","She sat up instantly and quietly asked him, \"What's wrong?\"","Chen Jiarong's face darkened. \"The two guys we sent to grab them... they've disappeared.\"","Gu Chacha was stunned. \"Disappeared? How could they disappear?\"","Didn't they say they'd hired Savar's underworld connections?","Chen Jiarong's lips turned down in annoyance. \"They said they sent two guys, but by morning, neither had come back.\"","Two twenty-something young women—how could they have eaten the guys or something?","That useless Tiger was so cheap, he definitely didn't spend enough to hire the right people.","He took a deep breath and dialed Tiger's number. \"Tell me straight—who exactly did you hire?\"","On the other end of the line, Brother Hu chuckled sheepishly. \"Just... some of my guys...\"","Chen Jiarong's eyes darkened. \"If you don't come clean, we're done cooperating.\"","\"Don't say that! Brother Bao, I'm sorry! I really am sorry!\"","He'd figured since they were just two young women, sending a couple of low-level thugs would be enough, so he hadn't wanted to spend the money.","Chen Jiarong asked him, \"How much did you pay?\"","Brother Hu sounded guilty. \"Three thousand Savar baht, with another three thousand once the job was done...\"","Chen Jiarong laughed in anger. \"I gave you two hundred thousand, and you spent five hundred?\"","Brother Hu weakly emphasized, \"But they'd get another three thousand after the job...\"","\"That's still only a thousand total!\"","How could he do this? He'd taken two hundred thousand and spent a thousand to get the job done.","He'd pocketed a hundred and ninety-nine thousand for himself—did he think Chen Jiarong was a fool?","He gritted his teeth. \"Are you looking for death?\"","Brother Hu quickly begged for mercy. \"I'm sorry, Brother Bao, truly sorry... Tell you what, I'll arrange things right now—we'll get them tonight, no question.\"","Chen Jiarong snorted coldly. \"If you mess this up again, you know what I'll do.\"","If it weren't for that northern tourism grand prize no one wanted to claim, he wouldn't have even used him.","Brother Hu naturally knew he wasn't someone to mess with, and quickly nodded. \"Brother, don't worry. Tonight I'll send two real professionals—we'll definitely bring them back.\"","After hanging up, he furiously called Xiao Zuo and Xiao You. \"Damn it! Where are you!\"","Whether they'd succeeded or not, at least they should have sent word!","They'd taken his five hundred baht!","After calling several times with no answer, he couldn't help but wonder, \"They didn't—they didn't just take my money and run, did they?\"","Beside him, Xiao Qian burst out laughing. \"Brother, what are you thinking? Five hundred baht—where could they even run to? They couldn't even buy a plane ticket home! You're overthinking it!\"","Brother Hu glared at him. \"Then you tell me—where did they go? Tell me!\"","Xiao Qian said confidently, \"They definitely went to go smoke some weed.\"","Brother Hu smacked him on the head. \"Damn it! Who told you to smoke weed? Haven't I said it before—no smoking weed!\"","Xiao Qian wasn't afraid of him at all. \"That stuff is great—what's a couple hits gonna hurt?\"","They were gangsters in Savar, what was a little weed?","Brother Hu said with frustration, \"That stuff is addictive! And it's expensive!\"","A bunch of good-for-nothings!","People who got into this life—who didn't want to go back to their hometown one day, all flashy and loaded, just to show off?","If they didn't save up some money now, how would they show off when they got old?","He didn't want to be a small-time gangster in Savar forever.","But Xiao Qian and the others were only in their teens; young people were always reckless. Being a gangster was so much fun.","Cool, crazy, decadent.","That was their ideal life.","Retire back home? Are you kidding? They weren't even twenty yet!","Brother Hu sighed. \"Damn, saving money is so freaking hard!\"","Even two hundred thousand baht—that wasn't enough to buy himself a few mink coats when he got old. And now he had to split it too. He really hated to part with it.","But there was no choice. If he screwed this up again, he wouldn't be able to operate in this area anymore.","He gritted his teeth, stamped his foot, and finally picked up the phone to make another call. \"Uh, Sang Biao—are you free tonight?\"","Xiao Qian's jaw nearly dropped. \"Wait, bro, are you kidding me? For a job this big, you're calling Sang Biao? What's the difference between Sang Biao and Xiao Zuo or Xiao You?\"","There was a difference. Xiao Zuo and Xiao You together only cost five hundred, while Sang Biao alone cost five hundred.","His fee had literally doubled—what more of a splurge could you ask for?","...","Xiao Qian gave a thumbs-up. \"Bro, still as cheap as ever.\"","His disgusted attitude made Tiger a bit guilty. \"Was I being stingy again?\"","Xiao Qian snorted. \"What do you think? Have you ever been generous?\"","If he hadn't been underage, he wouldn't be following this guy at all.","Man, two years in this life and his monthly earnings had never gone above five thousand.","Unbelievable. He'd earn more working in a factory back home than here.","Brother Hu thought for a moment, then gritted his teeth a little more. \"Then I'll add another five hundred to bring Chunzi along?\"","It really wasn't that he was cheap—it was just tying up two young women. It genuinely didn't call for this much!","He'd seen the girls' photos—both small and thin. Xiao Zuo and Xiao You should have been able to handle them!","Xiao Qian glanced at him. \"Give me a thousand, and tonight I'll go with Sang Biao.\"","He'd take the money and buy some weed tomorrow.","He'd trained in some martial arts as a kid, and he was one of the best fighters among the crew. That was why he could talk so tough.","Brother Hu thought about it for a while, and in the end, he reluctantly shelled out more cash. \"Fine. A thousand it is. Tonight, I need those girls brought in no matter what, or you'll pay the price!\"","Xiao Qian smiled confidently. \"Relax. When have you ever seen me fail?\"","Hearing that, Brother Hu felt a bit more at ease.","He couldn't help but puzzle over where Xiao Zuo and Xiao You had gone off to.","He called around to a few weed-dealing contacts, and none of them had seen the two.","It was really strange—where could they have gone?","They were off being tour companions, of course.","Xiao You huddled in the trunk with tearful eyes: Brother Hu! Save me!","The Qi brothers had rented a sedan, stuffed Xiao Zuo and Xiao You into the trunk, and drove them around Savar for sightseeing.","Xiao Zuo didn't really care, as long as they didn't kill him.","But Xiao You couldn't take it! He'd been stabbed twice! And in the morning, when Qi Yuan stuffed him into the trunk, he'd casually pulled the scalpel out!","Right now, his stomach hurt so much—he was sure his intestines were spilling out. Wuwuwu...","He was only sixteen. He'd never even had a girlfriend. He didn't want to die...","In the driver's seat, Qi Jin didn't understand his brother. \"Why not just take them to the police station?\"","Qi Yuan smiled. \"Aren't you curious? Why are gangsters from Savar targeting girls back home? What's the connection?\"","Qi Jin: \"If you're curious, then go to the police. That's what cops are for.\"","Qi Yuan gave a cold laugh. \"There's a cop sitting right next to me, and has he gotten anything useful out of them?\"","By the time Savar's useless cops figured things out, he'd already be back home.","Qi Jin frowned. \"But last night, you stabbed that Xiao You twice. Isn't it a problem not sending him to the hospital?\"","Qi Yuan gave him a sideways glance. \"Pick up that morality of yours—he's a kidnapper.\"","If it hadn't been for pure luck that they'd bought those two girls' tour package, things would have gone completely differently.","He opened Qi Jin's phone—on social media, Pineapple Huang had posted again: \"Ten portions of takoyaki—who do I owe this lifetime to?\"","His eyes darkened in an instant. If they hadn't had passports, the ones who'd been crept up on last night would have been them."]},{"number":95,"title":"Chapter 95: A Video Flies Over","paragraphs":["He didn't dare to imagine what would have happened last night if the two of them had passports.","He tapped at his phone screen again and again, the smiling face beneath the pineapple-yellow hair beaming like a flower.","He opened the keyboard and commented: \"Do they have takoyaki in Phuket?\"","\"Damn! Does this guy have some kind of problem? I gave him so many free tickets, and he's being passive-aggressive with me!\"","In the hotel room, He Huanhuan was so angry she kicked at the air.","When she'd sold him the grand prize, she'd clearly told him she didn't have a passport, so she couldn't go.","And now he was asking her a question like that—what a jerk!","Meili leaned over to look: \"What's going on?\"","The moment she saw the comment on the Moments post, Meili was furious: \"Holy crap! What a piece of trash! Video-call him, we'll curse him out!\"","The video call went through instantly, and Qi Yuan, sitting in the passenger seat, was completely caught off guard.","She was video-calling him?","He fumbled and shoved the phone back to Qi Jin, who looked totally confused: \"Huh? Why is that little girl video-calling me?\"","Maybe she couldn't come to Sawa, so she wanted to video-call and see what Sawa looked like?","Without a second thought, he hit accept, and the screen exploded with a burst of peach-pink and a deafening: \"You piece of trash!\"","\"Huh?\"","Qi Jin was baffled: \"Why are you cursing at me?\"","Qi Meili pressed her face against the camera, fuming: \"Why did you comment that on our Huanhuan's Moments? Are you proud that we can't go to Sawa?\"","The camera distortion made her eyes look enormous, and Qi Jin couldn't help but click his tongue: \"I didn't comment—my brother was messing with my phone. Probably he commented.\"","The phone was shoved back to Qi Yuan, who came face-to-face with a giant fly-eye on the screen... \"...\"","\"Brother~\"","Qi Meili's face changed instantly: \"Brother, where did you buy your glasses? So classy~\"","Qi Yuan: \"...\"","\"Ooh, a handsome guy? Let me see.\"","The pineapple-yellow hair came barreling into the frame: \"Whoa! A cool guy with glasses, not bad!\"","Qi Yuan: \"...Hi.\"","He Huanhuan asked him: \"Why are you being passive-aggressive with me?\"","Qi Yuan was embarrassed: \"That's not what I meant...\"","\"Then what did you mean?\"","Qi Yuan was at a loss for words: \"...I'm sorry.\"","Commenting once on someone's Moments, and a video call came flying in.","He'd never experienced anything like this before, and it left him a bit overwhelmed.","Qi Jin caught a glimpse of his brother's awkward expression and couldn't help snickering—it was nice to see his big brother finally meet his match.","\"Wow! What's that next to you? Is that a street in Sawa?\"","He Huanhuan screamed in delight: \"Quick! Turn the camera to the side and show me! I want to see the street outside!\"","...","So rude?","He obediently turned the camera outward, and the exotic, foreign-style street was instantly revealed on screen.","The other end erupted in a chorus of \"oohs\" and \"aahs.\"","He Huanhuan: \"Wow! So pretty!\"","Qi Meili: \"Wow! A handsome guy just flashed by! So hot!\"","\"...\"","Ten minutes passed, and the video still hadn't ended. Qi Yuan said: \"We need to go watch the show.\"","So, they could hang up now.","The two faces on screen lit up even brighter: \"Is it the human drumming thing? We want to see that too!\"","Qi Meili the greedy girl laughed: \"Make sure you show me the good stuff—I only watch the good stuff!\"","Qi Yuan: \"...\"","These two—why couldn't they take a hint?","He took them through a ladyboy show too, then looked at the camera: \"We need to go back to the hotel.\"","Now it was really time to hang up.","The two on screen looked even more eager: \"Is it the one with the pool? Take us to see it!\"","Qi Yuan: \"...Fine.\"","When the car pulled into the hotel parking lot, Qi Yuan hesitated for a moment—Little Left and Little Right were still in the trunk...","Before he could overthink it, Qi Jin directly opened the trunk and hauled the two of them out.","Qi Yuan: ...His video call was still connected!","On screen, Qi Meili was stunned: \"Why is your brother escorting them like that?\"","He Huanhuan nodded knowingly: \"His brother is a cop. That's what they call cross-border police work!\"","Qi Meili had an epiphany: \"No wonder they could afford such an expensive travel package—work is reimbursing them, right?\"","That explained it—why their used items sold the second they posted them online.","Turns out, they were spending the company's money.","Qi Yuan smiled helplessly. He didn't even need to come up with an excuse—they'd rationalized it all on their own.","What a pair of innocent souls.","Holding the phone up, he walked back to the room and gave them a thorough tour—the room, the pool, even the bathroom.","Finally satisfied, the two grinned and thanked him: \"You're a sweetheart, hot guy.\"","His lips unconsciously curved up: \"No problem. If you want to see more, I can show you around.\"","He Huanhuan perked up: \"Really? Actually, I'd love to see the hotel lobby!\"","...","He'd just been being polite.","But he got up and headed downstairs to the lobby anyway.","In the first-floor lobby, Liang Zheng sat waiting on the sofa in a sharply tailored black suit.","He'd come straight to the lobby after the meeting ended at four in the afternoon, but still no one had shown up.","He opened Liweiquan's official website once more and clicked the lottery page, which detailed the seven-day ultimate experience for the grand prize.","He clicked on day two's itinerary and confirmed it was indeed this hotel.","He turned off his phone and continued to wait patiently.","He didn't notice that in front of him, a man in gold-rimmed glasses had a phone screen flashing past a peach-pink face—the very face he'd been waiting for all afternoon.","And today's wait was destined to be in vain.","Also waiting anxiously was Han Mo, back at the office.","He'd compensated everyone who needed compensating and reassured everyone who needed reassuring.","At 5:30 in the afternoon, he finally had a moment of peace.","He immediately opened his phone and tapped on He Huanhuan's chat: [Having fun these past couple of days?]","No reply. He thought for a moment, then continued:","[Did you see the show? Was it good?]","[Buy any souvenirs?]","[How's the food? To your taste?]","[Sawa durian is amazing—did you try it?]","...","Over a dozen messages sent, and not a single reply in return.","He opened his phone, then closed it again, completely unable to focus on anything else.","A minute later, he opened his phone once more and transferred some money to her.","Still no reply.","Panic set in. He immediately tried video-calling He Huanhuan, but the line was busy.","Busy?","She was on a video call with someone?","Wasn't she on vacation?","His eyes flickered, and he immediately called Liang Ye.","\"Hey, Han Mo, why are you calling me?\"","Not video-chatting with him after all. Han Mo's expression softened just a fraction: \"Wrong number. Bye.\"","The call was hung up in a second, and Liang Ye was baffled: \"How weird.\"","It wasn't like Han Mo knew he was about to win Employee of the Year and was jealous, right?","Jealousy was useless—his excellence shone bright, and no one could compare!"]},{"number":96,"title":"Chapter 96: Stop Praising the Male Lead's Second","paragraphs":["After checking out the hotel lobby, they went to look at the back garden, the restaurant...","It wasn't until around eight in the evening that this cross-border video call finally drew to a close.","He Huanhuan said with satisfaction, thanking him, \"Thanks so much, handsome. I had a great time today. You're such a nice person.\"","Free good-person card awarded.","Dr. Qi accepted it happily, the corners of his mouth completely unable to come down. \"I'm glad you like it.\"","He Huanhuan nodded earnestly. \"Of course I like it! I love it so much!\"","She was a hype girl at heart — if nothing else, she had to deliver on emotional value, full stop.","Dr. Qi's gaze softened. \"Should I hang up now?\"","\"Mm-hmm!\"","The call finally ended, and Dr. Qi was finally free to head back to his room.","Standing in the elevator, Qi Yuan's heart was beating a little fast.","He thought, it must be because this trip was too special. It had sparked so much new interest in him for this otherwise dull and tedious world.","With a ding, the elevator doors opened, and he walked into the room with an easy, relaxed stride.","In the room, Xiao Zuo and Xiao You were once again tied up like sausages, lying on the floor.","Xiao You, on the other hand, actually felt more comfortable this time — the tight binding around his gut made him feel secure, like a safety hug.","Qi Yuan glanced over. \"Put them on the beds, one each.\"","Qi Jin was confused. \"Then where do I sleep?\"","There were only two beds total. If both of them got one each, where was he supposed to sleep?","This hotel cost five thousand a night normally!","Qi Yuan said, \"If you can't bear to give it up, you can share with one of them. That way you can also take a knife for him in the middle of the night.\"","Xiao You was shocked: Wait, they're going to stab him again tonight? That doesn't seem appropriate, does it?","Qi Jin was even more shocked: \"Are you seriously gonna stab him in the dark? How did you get this messed up?\"","......","Even though they were fraternal twins, was the IQ gap really that wide?","Qi Yuan sighed helplessly. \"They failed to get their hands on them last night and then disappeared. Do you think the people behind them are just going to let this go?\"","During the daytime video call, he had asked them about the details of the prize.","A newly opened cosmetics shop on the side of the road, and she casually drew a grand prize worth a hundred thousand. Possible?","He had searched Liweiquan's official website, and the prize was indeed filed and registered — a perfectly legal and compliant lottery.","But that didn't mean the process of winning it was legal and compliant.","Liweiquan wasn't some no-name small company. Just who could have bought off such connections, used such a perfectly legal lottery to send them to Sava, and then arranged a kidnapping?","Going to all that trouble, what were they after?","Qi Jin couldn't help but ask, \"Bro, why didn't you apply to police academy back then?\"","With that much curiosity, he'd make a better cop than Qi Jin ever could!","Qi Yuan couldn't be bothered to look at him. \"There are plenty of things I'm curious about. How many jobs would I need to have?\"","Fair point.","Qi Jin rubbed his head. \"So, we continuing tonight?\"","Wasn't he supposed to be on vacation? Why did it feel like he was clocking in for work instead?","After moving the two guys onto the beds, Qi Jin suddenly had a moment of brilliance and turned around, asking, \"Hey, are you this invested because you're curious, or because the girl's pretty?\"","The surgical scalpel twirled once around his fingertip, and Qi Yuan gave him a flat look. \"You wanna be an only child?\"","Damn! That was a threat — a blatant threat!","Qi Jin secretly sulked in his head, hoping the girl had a boyfriend so his brother could pine away alone!","But then he hesitated.","Maybe... better not? Pining alone was still pretty miserable...","Thinking this, he pulled out his phone and scrolled through He Huanhuan's Moments, looking for any clues.","Mm...","\"Ten servings of takoyaki — there goes a whole lifetime, I mean it!\"","\"As long as your mindset is good enough, anywhere can be Phuket!\"","\"Hair's gotta be the flashiest, and boyfriend's gotta be the handsomest!\"","\"Delayed broadcast, ladies — I got full-on knocked flying! But no big deal, hahahaha......\"","......","He honestly couldn't believe that Qi Yuan had a thing for such a lively, high-energy girl!","But the photos in her Moments only had her and her pink-haired best friend.","Probably no boyfriend. Probably, right?","At that very moment, right after the video call had ended, He Huanhuan's phone started vibrating like crazy.","She was shocked. \"Whoa, did the Americans actually plant a bomb in my phone or what?\"","Ding ding ding ding...","Han Mo's chat box was firing off messages nonstop: Having fun? Did you eat? Did you buy anything? Transfer sent. Were you on a video call with a friend?... When the call ends, message me back.","\"Why's he sending me so many messages?\"","She immediately accepted the transfer. Heh heh, that's another square meter added to my three-bedroom apartment.","The moment she accepted the money, a video call popped up immediately.","Han Mo sat in the car with a stern face. \"You seem to have been on a video call the whole time. Was it with a friend?\"","He Huanhuan shook her head. \"No, I was on a call with the buyer. They were showing me Sava.\"","Han Mo frowned. \"Buyer? Showing you Sava? Didn't you go to Sava for a trip?\"","He Huanhuan only then remembered that she had forgotten to update him on what had been going on.","She giggled. \"Me and Meili didn't have passports, so we couldn't go. I sold the grand prize at second-hand value. The buyer is a pair of handsome twins — they're so nice! They've been video-calling us to show us around...\"","Here, there followed about twenty thousand words of detailed narration. She didn't notice that the more she talked, the darker Han Mo's face got.","A doctor with gold-rimmed glasses, young and handsome, gentle and considerate, always ready to help...","Wasn't that way too many compliments for this guy?","\"...Later we looked at the garden together. That garden was huge! It had so many flowers! I just didn't recognize any of them...\"","\"...And the elevator was all gold and glittering, super bright. The younger handsome guy looked really good in it — the gold-rimmed glasses totally matched the gold-and-glam vibe...\"","She couldn't wait to tell Han Mo every single detail she saw, but Han Mo's focus wasn't on that. His face darkened as he cut off her gushing:","\"Where are you right now? I'm coming to find you.\"","He couldn't let her keep praising this guy any longer, or he'd get demoted to male lead number two.","\"No need, go do your thing.\"","He Huanhuan rejected him flat-out. \"Me and Meili are hanging out at my second brother's hotel. We're having a blast. Aren't you busy? Go on, mind your own business.\"","Apparently, Han Xuan still hadn't confessed, and his company was in complete chaos.","He Huanhuan thought to herself, she wasn't some lovesick fool.","Personal space and all that? She gave plenty.","......He didn't want it.","Han Mo took a deep breath. Why did he feel like he wasn't needed at all anymore?","That wouldn't do.","\"I've mostly wrapped up the busy work. From here on, I can slow down the pace a bit.\"","\"Eh, then once you're fully—\"","Before she could finish her refusal, Han Mo asked urgently, \"Don't we need to go see Wang Qiang? We promised him. Once we got back, we'd help him level up together.\"","\"Oh right! The little fatty!\"","He Huanhuan shot up from her seat. \"I almost forgot about him!\"","He was her friend through thick and thin — she had to take care of him.","She quickly asked Han Mo, \"When are we going?\"","\"How about tomorrow morning?\"","\"Fine! Then come pick me up tomorrow morning. Don't come tonight.\"","\"......Fine.\""]},{"number":97,"title":"Chapter 97: The Ugly Duckling Isn't Fat","paragraphs":["Inside the property sales lobby, the scolding had been going on for over an hour without stopping.","Wang Qiang brooded with his head down, his thoughts drifting somewhere far away.","The sales team leader shouted at him passionately: “Those people are young masters and ladies, just experiencing the poor life for fun for a few days. You don’t actually think you can turn into a phoenix, do you?”","Wang Qiang muttered: “I didn’t...”","“Hmph, only you know whether you did or not. Ugly ducklings aren’t fat, and fat ducks can’t even fly!”","Wang Qiang’s head almost sank to his chest. He hadn’t wanted to fly up the branch, he just, he just...","They had said they were friends. He thought they really were friends.","“Friends? Are you kidding me? They’re that rich. Who’s going to be friends with someone like you? What are you even worth?”","The sales team leader jabbed his finger hard into Wang Qiang’s chest, his tone dripping with contempt: “Wang Qiang, how long have you been with the company?”","“Two months...”","“How many deals have you closed?”","“No deals...”","“Ha!”","The team leader let out a cold smirk: “You have the nerve to say that! This sales department has monthly performance targets, you know!”","He shot Wang Qiang a sideways glance: “You know what you need to do, right?”","Wang Qiang: “But at the interview, HR said the performance review period was six months...”","It had only been two months. The deadline hadn’t come yet.","They sold houses, not cabbages. The economy had been bad the past two years, and the real estate market was already sluggish.","On top of that, this project’s location was remote, making it even harder to sell.","He wasn’t the only one who hadn’t closed a deal...","The sales team leader sneered: “You still don’t want to leave? Leeching off this company, are you? Want to coast on half a year of base pay? Young people these days really have thick skin...”","“Watch your mouth! Wang Qiang has only been here two months. It’s totally normal not to close a deal yet!”","A coworker couldn’t stand it and stepped in to defend Wang Qiang.","The sales team leader’s face darkened: “Zhang Wei, this has nothing to do with you. Stop sticking your nose where it doesn’t belong!”","Zhang Wei wasn’t afraid of him. Sales work is sales work—he could do it anywhere!","He shot a glare right back: “So what if I do! The kid isn’t even twenty yet! Shame on you, you old geezer!”","“You dare insult me?!”","The sales team leader’s face turned red with anger: “Zhang Wei! Wang Qiang! You’re both fired! Right now, this instant, go process your resignation!”","Zhang Wei laughed coldly: “Fired, huh? Fine! Give me a legitimate reason, or you’ll have to pay me wrongful termination severance.”","He’d been at the company for over two years. Firing him? Not that easy.","“You!”","The team leader was boiling with rage. He didn’t have a legitimate reason!","He...","Oh?","He couldn’t fire Zhang Wei, but he could fire Wang Qiang!","Wang Qiang was still on probation. With poor performance during probation, he could simply decline to continue employing him.","Haha!","He burst into laughter: “When did I say I was firing you? I’m firing Wang Qiang! His probation performance was too poor, he doesn’t meet the company’s standards, so we won’t be keeping him on!”","Zhang Wei immediately panicked: “His six-month probation period hasn’t ended yet! You can’t fire him!”","The sales team leader laughed loudly: “Zhang Wei, are you kidding? His performance was poor, and the company has decided not to continue his employment. What’s wrong with that?”","“Of course there’s...”","Zhang Wei tried to argue, but Wang Qiang tugged at his sleeve to stop him: “Brother Zhang, let it go. I don’t want to stay here anyway. It’s pretty pointless.”","Wang Qiang felt he probably wasn’t cut out for sales. He might as well pack up and find a factory job working rotating shifts.","At most, he could make six or seven thousand a month.","“Then quit! I’m going with you!”","Zhang Wei grabbed his hand and headed straight to HR. Screw this crappy company! He quit too!","Working for someone else—where couldn’t he find work?","They were salespeople, so there wasn’t much to hand over.","Return their employee cards, sign the resignation confirmation, and the process was done.","Leaving the sales office, Zhang Wei cheerfully threw an arm around Wang Qiang’s neck: “I’ve wanted to get rid of that bald geezer for ages! Come on, let’s grab a drink. Later I’ll take you to your sister-in-law’s company. They’re hiring too, we can try together.”","Wang Qiang couldn’t help asking: “What does sister-in-law’s company do?”","“It’s called Amway or something. I heard it makes serious money...”","Just as the electric scooter reached the intersection, a familiar BYD drove straight toward them.","Wang Qiang sighed: “Back when I sold cars, the first deal I closed was...”","“Hey! Chubby Wang Qiang!”","A bright blond head popped out of the rear window, shouting out that loud “Chubby” at him.","Wang Qiang was dumbfounded: “You, you, you...”","He Huanhuan laughed: “What, haven’t seen me in a few days, don’t recognize me?”","From the driver’s seat, Han Mo smiled and asked him: “Isn’t it work hours right now? Where are you headed?”","Wang Qiang’s eyes couldn’t help turning red. He hadn’t been delusional!","They really did remember him. They were friends! They had come back to see him!","“Ah, forget work! That bald geezer team leader was always picking on Wang Qiang. We both got fed up and quit just now.”","Zhang Wei patted Wang Qiang and explained to Han Mo.","Han Mo frowned: “You were being targeted?”","Wang Qiang shook his head: “Well, I already quit, so no worries anymore.”","Han Mo looked at his beat-up electric scooter: “Get in, we’ll take you home to grab your stuff. From now on, you work for me.”","Holy crap! Holy crap!","Zhang Wei instantly forgot about his girlfriend and shamelessly asked: “Um, boss, could you arrange a job for me too? I quit along with Wang Qiang...”","Han Mo nodded in agreement: “Go to the company tomorrow and find Chen Yu. He’ll set you up with something suitable.”","“Thanks, boss! Thanks, boss!”","Zhang Wei was ecstatic. He didn’t even bother saying goodbye—he hopped on his scooter and sped off.","He had to go gossip with his girlfriend about this!","Han Mo took a look at Wang Qiang’s scooter, the same one that never held a charge from before.","He said: “Don’t keep this thing. Just get in. We’ll take you back to pack your things.”","“I can’t just leave it!”","Wang Qiang was reluctant. The scooter was crappy, but he could sell it to a second-hand repair shop for three hundred yuan!","“Forget going back! We’ve got to stand up for Xiaoqiang!”","He Huanhuan shouted across the back seat with her hands on her hips. They dared to bully her friend?","Heh heh... just wait!","Meili nodded: “Right!”","Her heart suddenly burned with excitement. Finally, she could get into another showdown with Huanhuan again!","That nostalgic feeling!","Oh no!","She turned to Wang Qiang: “Take off your helmet and give it to Huanhuan.”","Don’t let her get bonked in the head with a wine bottle again, or she really wouldn’t want to live!","After pulling the BYD over to the side of the road, Han Mo called Chen Yu: “Drive my Porsche over. I’ll send you the location.”","Half an hour later, Chen Yu arrived in the flashy neon-green Porsche: “What’s the rush? I didn’t even get to eat before I came.”","He Huanhuan pinched her nose as she got into the back seat: “Big deal! Time to show off!”"]},{"number":98,"title":"Chapter 98: This Row, This Row, and This Row...","paragraphs":["A dark-green Porsche Panamera pulled up at the entrance of the sales center, and the sales team leader's eyes immediately lit up!","\"It's a Panamera...\"","The pretty female salesperson beside him shot him a look: \"Team leader, you should've gone to dance Zumba ages ago. Look how fat you've gotten—your gut's practically sticking out a mile...\"","\"What Zumba? It's Panamera! PANAMERA!\"","The female salesperson rolled her eyes at him: \"Panamaha or whatever—your belly's way too big. You still got the nerve to talk about Wang Qiang? You could fit three Wang Qiangs in there...\"","She wished she'd just quit with him earlier. Looking at that big gut of his turned her stomach—she couldn't even think about lunch now.","\"Ugh! Can't explain it to you!\"","The sales team leader waddled out on his two stubby legs: \"VIP! VIP incoming... Huh?\"","The car door opened, and out stepped a painfully familiar face—except the rainbow hair had been swapped for a pineapple-style crop...","He Huanhuan beamed: \"Long time no see, Old Fatty.\"","The sales team leader gave an awkward smile: \"S-So you came yourself?\"","Technically speaking, their development was still under the Gu Group's subsidiary.","He Huanhuan's smile widened: \"I'm here to buy a house~ What, not allowed?\"","The sales team leader immediately started bowing and scraping: \"Of course you can! Our development just opened recently—we've got plenty of units available!\"","He Huanhuan and Qi Meili walked hand in hand into the lobby. Glancing at the miniature model in the center of the hall, she casually pointed: \"I want this whole row and this whole row!\"","She turned and wrinkled her nose at Han Mo: \"You'll buy them for me, right?\"","Han Mo smiled indulgently: \"If you want them, I'll buy them.\"","Qi Meili shivered quietly beside them. God, did she used to be this cringe when she was dating?","Hearing \"this row\" and \"that row,\" the team leader's eyes turned red.","God!","If this deal went through, how much commission would he rake in?","Ones, tens, hundreds, thousands, ten thousands, hundred thousands, millions...","His retirement fund was secured!","\"I-I-I...\"","He was so excited he stuttered: \"I—I'll go write up the contract!\"","\"Wait.\"","Han Mo's calm voice cut him off mid-step: \"Put today's deal under Wang Qiang's name.\"","\"Huh?\"","The team leader was dumbfounded, a thin layer of sweat breaking out on his shiny forehead: \"Uh, Wang Qiang's not here today... How about—\"","He Huanhuan's face instantly fell: \"Not here? Then forget it, I'm not buying. We came all this way to show him some support!\"","With that, she turned to leave.","\"Wait, wait! Don't go!\"","The team leader scrambled to call her back: \"He's here! He is! Just wait—I'll get him here right now!\"","He frantically pulled out his phone and tried calling Wang Qiang: \"Sorry, the number you have dialed is temporarily unavailable...\"","\"Sorry, the number you have dialed is temporarily unavailable...\"","Open up the messaging app—the second he typed \"Wang Qiang, come—\" a bright red exclamation mark appeared. Sent, but blocked.","This kid! Why's he got such a short temper!","He Huanhuan stared down at him arrogantly: \"Why hasn't he answered? What's the deal? You and Wang Qiang don't get along or something?\"","\"No, no... just can't get through...\"","Cold sweat dripped down the team leader's face. His heart was racing. He had to get Wang Qiang back here—that was over a million in commission!","Once these spoiled rich kids left, he could just transfer the deal to his own name...","Thinking this, he turned to the female salesperson: \"Lend me your phone, I'll call Wang Qiang.\"","The female salesperson curled her lip: \"No. I just bought this phone case.\"","She didn't want him touching it with his grubby hands.","\"You!\"","The team leader, furious, leaned in and threatened in a low voice: \"You wanna get fired too, huh?\"","The female salesperson looked down at him with a contemptuous glance: \"Oh? You want to fire me?\"","Her sales targets were met every single quarter. Fire her? Was he ready to pay the severance?","She wasn't giving him her phone. He could fire her if he wanted. She'd take the cash and go on vacation!","\"You!\"","The team leader's liver ached with rage, but there was nothing he could do about her.","He Huanhuan stood behind him with arms crossed, watching. It was the first time he'd ever felt time crawl so slowly!","\"Team leader, use mine, use mine...\"","Guo Shan, a veteran salesperson on the team, quickly handed over his phone, going so far as to pull up Wang Qiang's contact page for him.","The call went through—ring, ring, ring...","\"Hello...\"","Wang Qiang's voice came through the phone, and the team leader was so emotional he nearly cried: \"Wang Qiang! Get back here! You're about to hit the jackpot!\"","Wang Qiang: \"I'm too fat to fly.\"","...","The team leader forced a laugh: \"Kid, I was just joking around. Don't be stubborn. Get back to work. Your VIP friends are here.\"","\"What friends?\" asked Wang Qiang flatly.","\"Your lucky friends!\" the team leader nearly shouted. \"They're here to buy a house with your name on the contract!\"","\"But I already quit.\"","\"Nonsense! You're on leave—official leave! Get back here right now. Everyone's waiting for you! Your lucky friends are waiting too! Come back, you hear me?\"","Before Wang Qiang could respond, he hung up.","He didn't believe it—with two big shots hanging around, that kid would come for sure?","Sure enough, two minutes later, Wang Qiang's beat-up electric scooter parked right at the sales hall entrance.","The team leader started to dash out, but Guo Shan grabbed his arm and whispered: \"Team leader, Wang Qiang just got fired by you not long ago. He sees you and he's already feeling sore. Why don't let me go talk to him?\"","\"Right, right, right...\"","The team leader nodded rapidly: \"You go talk to him, make sure he doesn't do anything stupid.\"","Guo Shan turned to him with a sly smile: \"So about that commission—\"","\"You'll get your cut!\"","The team leader shoved him forward, while he himself scurried up to He Huanhuan and the others, fawning: \"So sorry to keep you waiting. Wang Qiang's back—now we can close the deal.\"","In his heart, though, he sneered. This commission? No one was taking it from him.","The second that money hit his account, he was quitting and retiring to his hometown!","He Huanhuan shot him a sideways glance: \"Step further back, Old Fatty. You stink.\"","The team leader's face twitched, but he immediately hunched over and shuffled several steps back: \"Is this far enough?\"","The sheer sycophancy was revolting.","He Huanhuan glanced at Wang Qiang as he walked in, and said cheerfully: \"Xiaoqiang, you're here? I've come to buy a house~ All under your name, okay~\"","His heart pounding, his hands trembling, the team leader fixed his eyes on Wang Qiang. Say yes! Say yes!","\"No. I don't lack money.\"","Wang Qiang kept his hands in his pockets, pinching his own stomach hard beneath the fabric to keep his expression cold and aloof.","\"Huh?\"","He Huanhuan's brows knitted in disappointment: \"But we're so poor that all we've got is money~\"","Wang Qiang pinched his stomach until it turned black and blue: \"I'm not helping you for cash. You should go. I don't need money.\"","\"You do!\"","The team leader nearly passed out on the spot. He scurried over to Wang Qiang's side: \"Kid! What nonsense are you saying? How do you not need money? You need money!\"","With his back to He Huanhuan, he glared at Wang Qiang furiously: \"Over a million in commission. Don't be an idiot!\"","Wang Qiang didn't even look at him. His expression stayed placid: \"Money's all worldly possessions. I'm heading back to my hometown's electronics factory, working double shifts on the line. That's the life meant for me.\"","..."]},{"number":99,"title":"Chapter 99: Better Go Out and Play","paragraphs":["\"You little brat!\"","The sales team leader was sweating profusely: \"Have you lost your mind? Did that electronics factory save your life or something? You're turning down a commission of over a million bucks to go work at an electronics factory?\"","Wang Qiang was thrilled inside, but kept a calm face on purpose: \"You wouldn't understand. The electronics factory is my dream...\"","The sales team leader was itching to drag him over to close the deal: \"Dream my ass! You've just lost your marbles!\"","He turned to He Huanhuan with a pained expression: \"This kid's got a screw loose. How about I open the contract for you instead?\"","\"Eh, forget it.\"","He Huanhuan let out a long sigh: \"Something as noble as a dream shouldn't be corrupted by money. We're too mundane. Let's go...\"","\"Sigh...\"","She sighed again and walked toward the door, looking dejected.","As she passed by Wang Qiang, Qi Meili patted his cheek with a smile: \"A little fatty with some backbone, huh? Let's add each other on socials and grab a date sometime?\"","Wang Qiang said with righteous conviction: \"I only want to work double shifts at the electronics factory. I don't want to date anyone!\"","Qi Meili wiped her eyes dramatically: \"Wahhh, I'm heartbroken...\"","The dark green little Mini cooper disappeared from the front of the sales lobby in a flash. The sales team leader felt his temples throbbing with pain: \"Wang Qiang! Look at what you've done!\"","His one-million commission! Gone!","Wang Qiang shot him a glance: \"Mad, aren't you? I did it on purpose.\"","\"What did you say?!\"","Wang Qiang let out a cold laugh: \"The contract is under my name. Even if there's a loss, it's my loss. Why are you so worked up?\"","\"I...\"","\"Because you wanted to steal my commission! You were planning to transfer the contract from my name to yours the moment they left, weren't you? Team Leader Pan.\"","Wang Qiang stared him down with the question, and the man's round face went pale, then red with embarrassment.","Since the deal was already dead anyway, there was no need to hold back his anger anymore. The sales team leader glared back viciously: \"So what if I was? You're just an untransferred junior salesman. Do you even deserve that much commission? That commission should be mine!\"","\"That commission should be mine!\"","\"Mine...\"","The electronic voice echoed through the hall one after another, and the sales team leader panicked: \"Who?! Come out!\"","\"Why, it's me~ old fatty~\"","The Mini cooper had swung back around. He Huanhuan burst into the hall and pulled a voice recorder out from the model display case.","Recording people? That was her specialty.","She looked at the sales team leader with a grin: \"Old fatty, didn't think you'd be stealing your employees' performance bonuses, huh? Tsk tsk tsk...\"","No wonder he was so ugly. The face reflects the heart!","The sales team leader was furious: \"What do you want?\"","He Huanhuan pulled out her phone and video-called Gu Jingchen: \"Brother, is Wenlan Tianxia our company's property?\"","Gu Jingchen nodded: \"Yes, what's up?\"","He Huanhuan turned the camera toward the sales team leader: \"This old fatty here is bullying the low-level staff and trying to steal an employee's commission. Fire him for me!\"","She hit play on the voice recorder, and the sales team leader's arrogant words played out again:","\"...That commission should be mine!\"","Gu Jingchen's face turned icy cold: \"Sales team leader, is it? Very well.\"","If a sales team leader dared steal a new employee's commission, what about the department manager? The auditors?","What were they all doing?","He suppressed the anger in his chest and said to He Huanhuan: \"I'll have the accounts audited immediately. Every commission he's stolen over the years — he'll have to give it all back.\"","Oh heavens!","Old Pan's vision went black. He nearly fainted!","His retirement money — gone!","\"Good!\"","He Huanhuan nodded contentedly. Out of the corner of her eye, she caught the female saleswoman who had been laughing while watching the drama, and remembered she'd refused to lend her phone to the old fatty.","Without a second thought, she swung the camera toward the female saleswoman: \"Her — do a review of her performance later. Promote her to team leader.\"","The female saleswoman suddenly found herself face-to-face with Gu Jingchen on the video call, and upon hearing He Huanhuan's words, she straightened up immediately, seizing the opportunity:","\"Reporting to the President, my name is Dai Fang. I've been with the company for three years and eight months, and I've hit my sales targets every single month. In my first year, I was the sales champion of the Western District, with sales exceeding one hundred million. In my second year, half of my performance bonus was secretly taken by Director Qian, the Western District sales director. Because of that, I offended him and was transferred to Wenlan Tianxia...\"","She laid everything out with perfect clarity, reporting her entire three-plus-year track record to Gu Jingchen.","Plus every injustice she'd faced during that time — not a single detail was left out.","Gu Jingchen's brows furrowed deeper: \"Come to the headquarters tomorrow and come straight up to the top floor to see me.\"","These people all act so honest and obedient, but under the table, they're working all kinds of schemes!","The female saleswoman immediately acknowledged: \"Yes, President!\"","Finally — her chance had come!","The call ended. Trembling with excitement, she bowed to He Huanhuan: \"Thank you for giving me this opportunity!\"","Director Qian had been doling out her commission little by little every month, just enough to keep her from quitting outright.","Over a year of coasting had nearly drained away her resentment and her ambition — but she used to be a sales champion!","He Huanhuan waved her hands in surprise: \"It was all you. I didn't do anything.\"","The way she gave that report off the cuff just now was already above and beyond impressive.","He Huanhuan put away her phone, and suddenly the thrill of showing off was gone.","Showing off was fun, sure. But thinking about how many low-level employees were being bullied and oppressed by their superiors, she just felt angry.","If it weren't for a lucky coincidence putting her and Han Mo in Wang Qiang's path, he'd be off looking for another job.","Who knew how long Dai Fang's commission would have been dragged out before it finally got paid.","Why were people like this so rotten?!","She huffed and opened her phone, sending a message to Gu Jingchen: [Brother, you have to punish those bad people properly!]","A reply came quickly: [Don't worry. Your brother will handle it.]","With Gu Jingchen's assurance, He Huanhuan shot a venomous glare at Team Leader Pan: \"Just wait for the law to come down on you!\"","She turned without another word, walked out, and got back into the BYD. Han Mo patted her head: \"Don't be angry. Things like this are unavoidable.\"","As long as power exists, oppression and bullying will never fully disappear.","He looked at her gently: \"Do what you can, keep a clear conscience. That's enough.\"","He Huanhuan wrinkled her nose: \"It's all that grand prize's fault! It made me forget about Xiaoqiang so he had to suffer a few more days!\"","The jackpot was so huge that when she got excited, she'd pushed Wang Qiang to the back burner...","Wang Qiang grinned sheepishly: \"I didn't suffer at all. I was just working. Nothing tough about it.\"","If Liang Yeruo heard that, he'd nod fervently: \"Work is the greatest joy in the world! What's there to suffer? Huanhuan, your thinking is flawed!\"","Today's whole scene had been a plot He Huanhuan had designed herself — supposed to be a gloriously satisfying slap-in-the-face moment.","But when the act was over, the great director wasn't happy at all.","Han Mo felt a pang of worry: \"I should have gotten your passports ready earlier. I could have handled this whole thing on my own.\"","She should have been happily traveling in Sava, not grinding her teeth over these troubles.","Good thing she didn't have a passport — otherwise he'd be figuring out how to pull off an international rescue mission right now. Even more of a headache!"]},{"number":100,"title":"Chapter 100: The Old House Is on Fire","paragraphs":["In the Sawar Kingdom, after Qi Yuan hung up the video call, the corners of his mouth wouldn't come down for a long time.","It was enough to make Qi Jin click his tongue involuntarily: \"Looks like this old house of yours is about to catch fire!\"","Given Qi Yuan's usual temperament, if he'd heard that, he would've fired back with all kinds of nasty remarks.","But today, Dr. Qi hesitated for a moment, then asked, \"Am I old?\"","He'd started school two years earlier than most, and after graduating with his medical doctorate at twenty-six, he'd done another two years of residency.","This year he was thirty — still considered a rookie doctor at the hospital.","But thinking of that young face in the video, he did seem a bit old by comparison.","Hearing him ask that, Qi Jin didn't dare joke around anymore.","Damn! The old house really was on fire!","At his age, he was out here trying online dating — did he even know what he was getting into?","Qi Jin grabbed a pillow and headed for the bathroom: \"Old or not, that's one thing — you'd better first find out whether she's got a boyfriend or not, right?\"","Otherwise, if she already had someone, he wouldn't even get a number to stand in line as the side piece.","But there was really no way to tell. He Huanhuan's moments were all silly daily posts, nothing about romance at all.","Qi Yuan scrolled through her feed for ages, getting to know this lively girl through each post.","She loved malatang, loved riding her electric scooter around town, loved colorful hair, loved flashy tattoos.","In every photo, there was a big, beaming smile — clean and pure.","Like a flower carefully raised in a greenhouse, one that had never seen the hardships of the world, which was why she could smile so purely.","But a flower like that had almost been tricked into coming to Sawar to be abducted.","His eyes suddenly darkened, and he turned to Qi Jin: \"You can't even get a few minnows to talk, and you call yourself a cop?\"","Qi Jin was half asleep and completely confused: \"Bro, I'm in economic crime!\"","After graduating, he'd joined the economic crimes unit, which handled capital flow antitrust, anti-money laundering, and telecom fraud.","Criminal interrogation wasn't his specialty at all!","But his brother didn't care. His brother just laid down the law.","And it made him afraid to even close his eyes — what could he do? The guy was born half an hour earlier.","Such was fate!","He sat in the bathroom until around one in the morning, when a click finally came from the door.","Qi Jin snapped back to attention, his whole body tensing up.","The door was pushed open softly, and two figures slipped in.","They made a beeline for the two big beds, pressing the people in them down hard!","Three seconds later, the bedside lamp clicked on, and Sang Biao grinned wide: \"Little Qian, I'm good!\"","He'd always known he was worth more than Xiao Zuo and Xiao You!","Five hundred had its reasons — naturally, because he deserved it.","\"Mmph mmph mmph...\"","Xiao You thrashed beneath him: \"Good my ass! You're pressing down on my stomach! My guts haven't even been stuffed back in yet!\"","The kid had been tied up all day and couldn't see his own injuries. He thought his intestines had been hanging out the whole time, worried sick inside.","But his mouth was stuffed so full he couldn't get out a single coherent word.","Sang Biao was still sitting on the blanket, laughing: \"It's so funny when women get scared, all that mmph mmph mmph... like their mouths are stuffed.\"","The speaker meant nothing by it, but the listener took it to heart. Xiao Qian's face changed drastically. He yanked the blanket open, and Xiao Zuo's pale, starving face was exposed in an instant.","\"Xiao Zuo!\"","Xiao Qian cried out in shock and turned to defend himself — but he was too late!","A massive figure loomed over him!","Ten minutes later, there were two more Captains Kang on the bed.","When the stinky sock was shoved into Sang Biao's mouth, he was gagging from the smell: \"Bro, let's talk this out. Don't do this. I'm not into this, bleh...\"","Qi Yuan asked, \"Who sent you?\"","The stinky sock was right at his lips — as long as he didn't answer properly, it'd be shoved right in.","Without hesitation, he sold out Brother Hu: \"Brother Hu gave me five hundred bucks to come tie up two people.\"","Qi Yuan glanced at Xiao Qian, who was rolling his eyes from the stench: \"And him?\"","Sang Biao answered even faster: \"He's Brother Hu's underling. Real close with Brother Hu. Interrogate him well — he knows a lot!\"","The sock was pulled out of Xiao Qian's mouth, and he cursed Sang Biao in fury: \"Traitor! Brother Hu treated you well!\"","Sang Biao subtly turned his head away: \"Man, you just don't appreciate a good deed. If I hadn't talked, you'd still be eating that sock. What, you into that?\"","\"Traitor!\"","No sooner had he cursed than the sock went back in.","Qi Yuan lay down on the bed: \"Let him cool off for the night.\"","These young punks were the most stubborn. The more you interrogate them, the more their hero complex swells.","Let him suffer a couple of days first.","He'd predicted right — by the middle of the night, Xiao Qian was full of regret.","Damn!","He'd followed Brother Hu and couldn't even make five thousand a month — what loyalty was he trying to prove?","That sock was disgustingly stinky. Hopefully it didn't give him a fungal infection.","If he got a fungal infection, he couldn't even afford to see a doctor...","\"Mmph mmph mmph...\"","He rolled his eyes and tried to yell, hoping to wake Qi Yuan. He was ready to confess — ask him anything, quick!","\"Mmph mmph mmph...\"","\"Shut up!\"","A foot stinkier than the socks stomped onto his face, and his eyes rolled back as he nearly passed out from the odor!","God! He'd never been to Hong Kong, but he'd just experienced a proper Hong Kong foot!","Qi Jin said this little smell was nothing — wait till they got a chance to visit his squad.","Now that was the real deal.","He slept until broad daylight, his eyes rolled back so far he couldn't even blink properly.","Qi Yuan finally rose unhurriedly. He sat on the edge of the bed and looked at the sock in Xiao Qian's mouth: \"Ready to talk?\"","Xiao Qian nodded frantically. Yes! He'd say anything!","Back when he was a kid watching TV, when he saw villains cave under torture, he used to mock them for being spineless.","Who knew that when it happened to him...","It stank. It hurt. It was unbearable!","Seeing him nod without hesitation, Qi Yuan reached out.","His hand approached the mouth, then suddenly stopped. Xiao Qian's heart leapt into his throat.","He wasn't lying, he really was ready to confess — please take it out!","The hand pulled back, and Qi Yuan kicked the neighboring bed: \"Come take your sock off.\"","The sock was too stinky — the brother refused to touch it himself.","Qi Jin casually pulled the sock out, brought it to his nose, and sniffed: \"It's not even that bad. Why does everyone hate it so much?\"","He and Qi Yuan were fraternal twins. Qi Yuan was lean, with a scholarly air.","Qi Jin, on the other hand, was built like a typical North Chinese man — broad shoulders, thick back, sturdy and strong.","Standing there, you could tell he was a man with character.","He nudged Xiao Qian with his foot: \"Are you faking it? It's really not that smelly.\"","The four Captains Kang all widened their eyes — it was practically burning their eyes, and he said it wasn't smelly?!","\"Talk. Who's Brother Hu's buyer?\"","Qi Yuan asked Xiao Qian coldly. Xiao Qian hesitated for a second, and the stench instantly loomed in front of his face. He jolted and came clean: \"It's Brother Bao! Brother Bao runs telecom fraud in Mianbei, and Brother Hu sends people to Mianbei for him every year to work the scams!\"","Telecom fraud?","What would she have to do with telecom fraud?"]}]);
